abhikīrati|abhikiirati|abhikirati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhikiirati</span></p><p>abhikīrati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>pr. 3. sg. scatter over; to sprinkle</p><p>abhikīrati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>pass. pr. 3. sg. is scattered, is dispersed</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhikirati">abhikirati</a>, <a href="bword://abhikirati">abhikirati</a></p>

abhikīḷati|abhikii.lati|abhikilati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhikii.lati</span></p><p>to play (a game), to sport Mil.359 (kīḷaṃ).</p><p>abhi + kìḷati</p>

abhikūjita|abhikuujita|abhikujita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhikuujita</span></p><p>resounding (with the song of birds) Pv.ii.12#3 (cakkavāka˚; so read for kujita). Cp. <em><a href="bword://abhinik%C5%ABjita">abhinikūjita</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + kūjita, pp. of <em>kūj</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinikūjita">abhinikūjita</a></p>

abhilakkhita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>marked out, indicated; characterized; appointed; distinguished.</p>

abhilakkhita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective fixed, designed, inaugurated, marked by auspices Ja.iv.1; DN-a.i.18.</p><p>Sk. abhilakṣita in diff. meaning; pp. of abhi + <em>lakṣ</em></p>

abhilakkhitatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>having signs or marks, being characterised, characteristics Dhs-a.62.</p><p>abstr. fr. abhilakkhita</p>

abhilambati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to hang down over (c. acc.) MN.iii.164 = Ne.179 (+ ajjholambati); Ja.v.70 (papātaṃ), Ja.v.269 (Vetaraṇiṃ)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhilambita">abhilambita</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>abhi + lambati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhilambita">abhilambita</a></p>

abhilambita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective hanging down Ja.v.407 (nīladuma˚).</p><p>pp. of abhilambati</p>

abhilaṅghati|abhila"nghati|abhilanghati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhila"nghati</span></p><p>to ascend, rise, travel or pass over (of the moon traversing the sky) Ja.iii.364; Ja.vi.221.</p><p>abhi + langhati</p>

abhilekheti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to cause to be inscribed Dāvs v.67 (cāritta-lekhaṃ ˚lekhayi).</p><p>Caus. of abhi + <em>likh</em></p>

abhilepana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>plaster; bird-lime.</p>

abhilepana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>“smearing over”, stain, pollution Snp.1032, Snp.1033 = Ne.10, Ne.11 (see Cnd.88 laggana “sticking to”, bandhana, upakkilesa).</p><p>abhi + lepana</p>

abhilābhi|abhilaabhi|abhilabhi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhilaabhi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhilābhin">abhilābhin</a></p><p>obtaining.</p>

abhilābhin|abhilaabhin|abhilabhin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhilaabhin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhilābhin">abhilābhin</a></p><p>obtaining.</p>

abhilāpa|abhilaapa|abhilapa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhilaapa</span></p><p>speaking; word, expression; name, designation.</p>

abhilāpa|abhilaapa|abhilapa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhilaapa</span></p><p>talk, phrasing, expression Snp.49 (vācâbhilāpa making phrases, talking, idle or objectionable speech = tiracchanakathā Cnd.561); Iti.89 (? reading abhilāpāyaṃ uncertain, vv.ll. abhipāyaṃ abhipāpāyaṃ abhisāpāyaṃ, abhisapāyaṃ, atisappāyaṃ. The corresp. passage SN.iii.93 reads abhisapayaṃ: curse, and C. on Iti.89 explains abhilāpo ti akkoso, see <em>Brethren</em> 376 n. 1); Dhs.1306 = Cnd.34 (as exegesis or paraphrase of adhivacana comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with vyañjana &amp; trsl. by Mrs. Rh. D. as “a distinctive mark of discourse”); DN-a.i.20, DN-a.i.23, DN-a.i.281; Dhs-a.51.</p><p>fr. abhi + <em>lap</em></p>

abhilāsa|abhilaasa|abhilasa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhilaasa</span></p><p>desire, wish, longing Pv-a.154.</p><p>Sk. abhilāṣa, abhi + <em>laṣ</em></p>

abhilāsi|abhilaasi|abhilasi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhilaasi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhilāsin">abhilāsin</a></p><p>wishing for, desiring.</p>

abhilāsin|abhilaasin|abhilasin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhilaasin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhilāsin">abhilāsin</a></p><p>wishing for, desiring.</p>

abhimaddati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>crushes; oppresses; destroys.</p>

abhimaddati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to crush SN.i.102; AN.i.198; Sdhp.288.</p><p>Sk. abhimardati &amp; ˚mṛdnāti; abhi + <em>mṛd</em></p>

abhimaddita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>crushed, oppressed; destroyed</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhimaddati">abhimaddati</a></p>

abhimana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>with one’s mind directed towards (acc.).</p>

abhimana
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective having one’s mind turned on, thinking of or on (c. acc.) Thag.1122; Ja.vi.451.</p><p>abhi + mano, BSk. abhimana, e.g. Mvu.iii.259</p>

abhimanthati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>churns, rotates (to make fire); rubs, grinds; afflicts, hurts</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhimatthati">abhimatthati</a></p>

abhimanthenta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>churning, making rotate</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhimatthenta">abhimatthenta</a>, <a href="bword://abhimanthati">abhimanthati</a></p>

abhimantheti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>see <em><a href="bword://abhimatthati">abhimatthati</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhimatthati">abhimatthati</a></p>

abhimanāpa|abhimanaapa|abhimanapa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhimanaapa</span></p><p>adjective very pleasing Vv-a.53 (where id. p. at Pv-a.71 has <em><a href="bword://atiman%C4%81pa">atimanāpa</a></em>).</p><p>abhi + manāpa</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://atimanāpa">atimanāpa</a></p>

abhimata
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective desired, wished for; agreeable, pleasant C on Thag.91.</p><p>BSk. abhimata, e.g. Jtm.211; pp. of abhimanyate</p>

abhimatthana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>rotating, rubbing together.</p>

abhimatthati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>churns, rotates (to make fire); rubs, grinds; afflicts, hurts</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhimanthati">abhimanthati</a></p>

abhimatthati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(˚eti) &amp; <em>-mantheti</em></p><ol><li>to cleave, cut; to crush, destroy MN.i.243 (sikharena muddhānaṃ ˚mantheti); SN.i.127; Dhp.161 (variant reading ˚nth˚); Ja.iv.457 (matthako sikharena ˚matthiyamāno) Dhp-a.iii.152 (= kantati viddhaṃseti).</li><li>to rub, to produce by friction (esp. fire, aggiṃ; cp. Vedic agniṃ nirmanthati) MN.i.240.</li></ol><p>abhi + <em>math</em> or <em>manth</em>, cp. nimmatheti</p>

abhimatthenta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>churning, making rotate</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhimanthenta">abhimanthenta</a>, <a href="bword://abhimatthati">abhimatthati</a></p>

abhimaṅgala|abhima"ngala|abhimangala
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhima"ngala</span></p><p>adjective (very) fortunate, lucky, anspicious, in ˚sammatā (of Visākhā) “benedicted” blessed Vin.iii.187 = Dhp-a.i.409. Opp. avamangala.</p><p>abhi + mangala</p>

abhimaṅgalasammata|abhima"ngalasammata|abhimangalasammata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhima"ngalasammata</span></p><p>considered auspicious.</p>

abhimaṇḍita|abhima.n.dita|abhimandita
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(pp.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhima.n.dita</span></p><p>-˚) adorned, embellished, beautified Mil.361; Sdhp.17.</p><p>abhi + maṇḍita</p>

abhimukha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective facing, turned towards, approaching Ja.ii.3 (˚ā ahesuṃ met each other). usually -˚ turned to, going to, inclined towards DN.i.50 (purattha˚) Ja.i.203 (devaloka˚), Ja.i.223 (varaṇa-rukkha˚); Ja.ii.3 (nagara˚), Ja.ii.416 (Jetavana˚); Dhp-a.i.170 (tad˚); Dhp-a.ii.89 (nagara˚); Pv-a.3 (kāma˚, opp. vimukha), Pv-a.74 (uyyāna˚)<br />■ nt. <em>-ṃ</em> adv. to towards Ja.i.263 (matta-vāraṇe); Pv-a.4 (āghātana˚, may here be taken as pred. adj.); Dhp-a.iii.310 (uttara˚).</p><p>abhi + mukha</p>

abhimāra|abhimaara|abhimara
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhimaara</span></p><p>bandit, bravo, robber Ja.ii.199; DN-a.i.152.</p><p>cp. Sk. abhimara slaughter</p>

abhinadati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>make a noise, sounds.</p>

abhinadati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to resound, to be full of noise Ja.vi.531. Cp. <em><a href="bword://abhin%C4%81dita">abhinādita</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + nadati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinādita">abhinādita</a></p>

abhinamati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to bend<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhinata">abhinata</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>abhi + namati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinata">abhinata</a></p>

abhinanda
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhinandat">abhinandat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinandati">abhinandati</a></p>

abhinandamāna|abhinandamaana|abhinandamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinandamaana</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinandati">abhinandati</a></p>

abhinandana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter \~ā, feminine</i></p><p>welcome; pleasure, delight.</p>

abhinandana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter &amp;</i></p><p><em>-ā</em> (f.), pleasure, delight, enjoyment DN.i.244; MN.i.498; Ja.iv.397.</p><p>fr. abhinandati, cp. <em><a href="bword://nandan%C4%81">nandanā</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nandanā">nandanā</a></p>

abhinandat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhinandat">abhinandat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinandati">abhinandati</a></p>

abhinandati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>rejoices at, welcomes; approves of; is pleased at.</p>

abhinandati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to rejoice at, find pleasure in (acc.), approve of, be pleased or delighted with (acc. DN.i.46 (bhāsitaṃ), DN.i.55 (id.), DN.i.158, DN.i.223; MN.i.109, MN.i.458; SN.i.32 (annaṃ), SN.i.57, SN.i.14, (cakkhuṃ, rūpe etc.); AN.iv.411 Thag.606; Dhp.75, Dhp.219; Snp.1054, Snp.1057, Snp.1111; Cnd.82; Mil.25; DN-a.i.160; Dhp-a.iii.194 (aor. abhinandi, opp paṭikkosi) Vv-a.65 (vacanaṃ)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhinandita">abhinandita</a></em> (q.v.). Often in comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with <em><a href="bword://abhivadati">abhivadati</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>abhi + nandati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinandita">abhinandita</a>, <a href="bword://abhivadati">abhivadati</a></p>

abhinandi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinandati">abhinandati</a></p>

abhinandin
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective rejoicing at, finding pleasure in (loc. or-˚), enjoying AN.ii.54 (piyarūpa); esp. freq. in phrase (taṇhā) tatratatr’âbhinandinī finding its pleasure in this or that [cp. B.Sk. tṛṣṇā tatra-tatr’âbhinandinī Mvu.iii.332] Vin.i.10; SN.v.421; Pts.ii.147; Ne.72, etc.</p><p>fr. abhinandati, cp. <em><a href="bword://nandin">nandin</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nandin">nandin</a></p>

abhinandita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn. &amp; neuter</i></p><ol><li>(mfn.) welcomed; liked.</li><li>(n.) liking; delight</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinandati">abhinandati</a></p>

abhinandita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>only in <em>an˚</em>; not enjoyed, not (being) an object of pleasure SN.iv.213 = Iti.38; SN.v.319.</p><p>pp. of abhinandati</p>

abhinandiṃsu|abhinandi.msu|abhinandimsu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 plural</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinandi.msu</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinandati">abhinandati</a></p>

abhinanduṃ|abhinandu.m|abhinandum
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 plural</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinandu.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinandati">abhinandati</a></p>

abhinata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>bent towards; inclined towards</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiṇata">abhiṇata</a></p>

abhinata
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>bent, (strained, fig. bent on pleasure MN.i.386 (+ apanata); SN.i.28 (id.; Mrs. Rh. D “strained forth”, cp. <em>Kindred S</em> i.39). See also <em><a href="bword://apanata">apanata</a></em>.</p><p>pp. of abhi + namati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://apanata">apanata</a></p>

abhinava
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective quite young, new or fresh Vin.iii.337; Ja.ii.143 (devaputta), Ja.ii.435 (so read for accuṇha in expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n<!-- raw HTML omitted --> of paccaggha; v.v. ll. abbhuṇha &amp; abhiṇha) Thag-a.201 (˚yobbana = abhiyobbana); Pv-a.40 (˚saṇṭhāna), Pv-a.87 (= paccaggha) Pv-a.155.</p><p>abhi + nava</p>

abhinaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i></p><p>dramatic representation Vv-a.209 (sākhā˚).</p><p>abhi + naya</p>

abhinetabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhineti">abhineti</a></p>

abhineti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>leads near; brings to; summons.</p>

abhinibbajjayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(?)</i></p><p>avoids; shuns</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbijjayati">abhinibbijjayati</a></p>

abhinibbatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>resulting; produced; reborn</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbattati">abhinibbattati</a></p>

abhinibbatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>reproduced, reborn AN.iv.40, AN.iv.401; Cnd.256 (nibbatta abhi pātubhūta); Dhs.1035, Dhs.1036 (so read for˚ nippatta) Vv-a.9 (puññ’ânubhāva˚ by the power of merit).</p><p>abhi + nibbatta, pp. of abhinibbattati</p>

abhinibbattaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>producing, causing to come into being.</p>

abhinibbattati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>results (from); is produced; becomes, is reborn.</p>

abhinibbattati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to become, to be reproduced, to result Pp.51<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhinibbatta">abhinibbatta</a></em><br />■ Cp B.Sk. wrongly abhinivartate].</p><p>abhi + nibbattati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbatta">abhinibbatta</a></p>

abhinibbattaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhinibbattayat">abhinibbattayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbattayati">abhinibbattayati</a></p>

abhinibbattayat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhinibbattayat">abhinibbattayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbattayati">abhinibbattayati</a></p>

abhinibbattayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>produces; causes to come into being</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbatteti">abhinibbatteti</a>, <a href="bword://abhinibbattati">abhinibbattati</a></p>

abhinibbattenta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbatteti">abhinibbatteti</a></p>

abhinibbattesuṃ|abhinibbattesu.m|abhinibbattesum
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 plural</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinibbattesu.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbatteti">abhinibbatteti</a></p>

abhinibbatteti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>produces; causes to come into being</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbattayati">abhinibbattayati</a>, <a href="bword://abhinibbattati">abhinibbattati</a></p>

abhinibbatteti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to produce, cause, cause to become SN.iii.152; AN.v.47; Nd ii.under jāneti.</p><p>abhi + nibbatteti, caus. of ˚nibbattati</p>

abhinibbatti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>production; becoming; birth, rebirth.</p>

abhinibbatti
<p>[Nyana]</p><p></p><p><strong>Abhinibbatti:</strong> a Sutta term for rebirth; see: <em>punabbhava</em></p>

abhinibbatti
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>becoming, birth, rebirth, DN.i.229; DN.ii.283 (variant reading for abhinipphatti) SN.ii.65 (punabbhava˚), SN.ii.101 (id.); SN.iv.14, SN.iv.215; AN.v.121; Pv-a.35.</p><p>abhi + nibbatti</p>

abhinibbhidā|abhinibbhidaa|abhinibbhida
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinibbhidaa</span></p><p>bursts through; breaks out</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbhijjati">abhinibbhijjati</a></p>

abhinibbhidā|abhinibbhidaa|abhinibbhida
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinibbhidaa</span></p><p><a href="bword://abhinibbid%C4%81">abhinibbidā</a>*, therefore spelling also <em>abhinibbidhā</em> (Vin.iii.4, C. on Ne.98) To abhinibbijjhati, cp. B.Sk. abhinirbheda Mvu.i.272 which is wrongly referred to <em>bhid</em> instead of <em>vyadh</em>.] the successful breaking through (like the chick through the shell of the egg), coming into (proper) life Vin.iii.4; MN.i.104; MN.i.357; Ne.98 (C. reading). See also <em><a href="bword://abhinibbid%C4%81">abhinibbidā</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbidā">abhinibbidā</a>, <a href="bword://abhinibbidā">abhinibbidā</a></p>

abhinibbhijja
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i></p><p>splitting asunder; breaking through.</p>

abhinibbhijjati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>bursts through; breaks out</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbhidā">abhinibbhidā</a></p>

abhinibbidā|abhinibbidaa|abhinibbida
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinibbidaa</span></p><p>disgust with the world, taedium Ne.61 (taken as abhinibbhidā, according to expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> as “padālanā-paññatti avijj˚aṇḍa-kosānaṃ”), Ne.98 (so MSS, but C. abhinibbidhā).</p><p>abhi + nibbidā; confused with abhinibbhidā</p>

abhinibbijja
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i></p><p>finding out; examining, analyzing; or piercing through.</p>

abhinibbijjati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to be disgusted with, to avoid, shun, turn away from Snp.281 (T. abhinibbijjayātha, variant reading BB˚ nibbijjiyātha &amp; ˚nibbajjiyātha, Snp-a explains by vivajjeyyātha mā bhajeyyātha; variant reading BB. abhinippajjiyā) = AN.iv.172 (T. abhinibbajjayātha vv.ll. ˚nibbajjeyyātha &amp; ˚nibbijjayātha); ger. <em>abhinibbijja</em> Thig.84.</p><p>either Med. fr. nibbindati of <em>vid</em> for *nirvidyate (see <em><a href="bword://nibbindati">nibbindati</a></em> B), or secondary formation fr ger. nibbijja. Reading however not beyond all doubt</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbindati">nibbindati</a></p>

abhinibbijjayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(?)</i></p><p>avoids; shuns</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbajjayati">abhinibbajjayati</a></p>

abhinibbijjhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to break quite through (of the chick coming through the shell of the egg) Vin.iii.3; MN.i.104 = SN.iii.153 (read˚ nibbijjheyyun for nibbijjeyyun.) Cp. <em>Buddh. Suttas</em> 233, 234.</p><p>abhi + nibbijjhati</p>

abhinibbuta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective perfectly cooled, calmed, serene, esp. in two phrases, viz. <em>diṭṭha dhamm’ ābhinibbuta</em> AN.i.142 = MN.iii.187; Snp.1087; Cnd.83, and <em>abhinibbutatta</em> of cooled mind Snp.343 (= apariḍayhamāna-citta Snp-a.347), Snp.456, Snp.469, Snp.783. Also at Sdhp.35.</p><p>abhi + nibbuta</p>

abhinibbutatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>with thoughts calmed; with self quenched.</p>

abhiniddisati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>points out, indicates, characterizes.</p>

abhiniggaṇha|abhinigga.nha|abhinigganha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinigga.nha</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhiniggaṇhat">abhiniggaṇhat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiniggaṇhāti">abhiniggaṇhāti</a></p>

abhiniggaṇhanā|abhinigga.nhanaa|abhinigganhana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinigga.nhanaa</span></p><p>taking a hold of.</p>

abhiniggaṇhanā|abhinigga.nhanaa|abhinigganhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinigga.nhanaa</span></p><p>holding back Vin.iii.121 (+ abhinippīḷanā).</p><p>abstr. fr. abhiniggaṇhāti</p>

abhiniggaṇhat|abhinigga.nhat|abhinigganhat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinigga.nhat</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhiniggaṇhat">abhiniggaṇhat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiniggaṇhāti">abhiniggaṇhāti</a></p>

abhiniggaṇhitabba|abhinigga.nhitabba|abhinigganhitabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinigga.nhitabba</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiniggaṇhāti">abhiniggaṇhāti</a></p>

abhiniggaṇhāti|abhinigga.nhaati|abhinigganhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinigga.nhaati</span></p><p>takes hold of; holds fast, restraints.</p>

abhiniggaṇhāti|abhinigga.nhaati|abhinigganhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinigga.nhaati</span></p><p>to hold back, restrain, prevent, prohibit; always in comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with <em><a href="bword://abhinipp%C4%AB%E1%B8%B7eti">abhinippīḷeti</a></em> MN.i.120; AN.v.230<br />■ Cp. <em><a href="bword://abhinigga%E1%B9%87han%C4%81">abhiniggaṇhanā</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + niggaṇhāti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinippīḷeti">abhinippīḷeti</a>, <a href="bword://abhiniggaṇhanā">abhiniggaṇhanā</a></p>

abhinihanati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>strikes, hits.</p>

abhinihata
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>past participle oppressed. crushed, slain Ja.iv.4.</p><p>abhi + nihata</p>

abhinikkhamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>coming out; going out, leaving a worldly life.</p>

abhinikkhamana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>departure, going away, esp. the going out into monastic life, retirement renunciation. Usually as <em>mahā˚</em>; the great renunciation Ja.i.61; Pv-a.19.</p><p>abhi + nikkhamana</p>

abhinikkhamati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>goes out, comes out; esp. goes out from a worldly life, retires from the world.</p>

abhinikkhamati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to go forth from (abl.), go out, issue Dhs-a.91; esp. fig. to leave the household life, to retire from the world Snp.64 (= gehā abhinikkhamitvā kāsāya-vattho hutvā Snp-a.117).</p><p>abhi + nikkhamati</p>

abhinikkhamitvā|abhinikkhamitvaa|abhinikkhamitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinikkhamitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinikkhamati">abhinikkhamati</a></p>

abhinikkhamma
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinikkhamati">abhinikkhamati</a></p>

abhinikkhipati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to lay down, put down D Avs.iii.12, Avs.iii.60.</p><p>abhi + nikkhipati</p>

abhinikūjita|abhinikuujita|abhinikujita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinikuujita</span></p><p>adjective resounding with, full of the noise of (birds) Ja.v.232 (of the barking of a dog), Ja.v.304 (of the cuckoo); so read for ˚kuñjita T.). Cp. <em><a href="bword://abhik%C5%ABjita">abhikūjita</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + nikūjita</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhikūjita">abhikūjita</a></p>

abhinimantana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>an invitation.</p>

abhinimantanatā|abhinimantanataa|abhinimantanata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinimantanataa</span></p><p>speaking to, adressing, invitation MN.i.331.</p><p>abstr. to abhinimanteti</p>

abhinimanteti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>invites (someone, acc.) to (instr.); offers.</p>

abhinimanteti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to invite to (c. instr.), to offer to DN.i.61 (āsanena).</p><p>abhi + nimanteti</p>

abhinimmadana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>subduing; controlling.</p>

abhinimmadana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>crushing, subduing, levelling out MN.iii.132; AN.iv.189 sq.</p><p>abhi + nimmadana</p>

abhinimmina
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>forming, creating (by magic).</p>

abhinimminanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinimmināti">abhinimmināti</a></p>

abhinimmini
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinimmināti">abhinimmināti</a></p>

abhinimminitvā|abhinimminitvaa|abhinimminitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinimminitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinimmināti">abhinimmināti</a></p>

abhinimmināti|abhinimminaati|abhinimminati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinimminaati</span></p><p>creates (by magic or supernatural power); produces, forms, shapes.</p>

abhinimmināti|abhinimminaati|abhinimminati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinimminaati</span></p><p>to create (by magic), produce, shape, make SN.iii.152 (rūpaṃ); AN.i.279 (oḷārikaṃ attabhāvaṃ); Nd ii.under pucchā<!-- raw HTML omitted -->6<!-- raw HTML omitted --> (rūpaṃ manomayaṃ); Vv-a.16 (mahantaṃ hatthi-rāja-vaṇṇaṃ)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhinimmita">abhinimmita</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>abhi + nimmināti, cp. BSk. abhinirmāti Jtm.32; abhinirminoti Divy.251; abhinirmimīte Divy.166</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinimmita">abhinimmita</a></p>

abhinimmita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>created (by magic) Vv.16#1 (pañca rathā satā; cp. Vv-a.79).</p><p>abhi + nimmita, pp. of abhinimmināti</p>

abhinimmitvā|abhinimmitvaa|abhinimmitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinimmitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinimmināti">abhinimmināti</a></p>

abhinindriya
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>doubtful meaning. The other is explained by Bdhgh at DN-a.i.120 as paripuṇṇ˚; and at DN-a.i.222 as avikal-indriya not defective, perfect sense-organ. He must have read ahīn˚ Abhi-n-indriya could only be explained as “with supersenseorgans”, i.e. with organs of supernormal thought or perception thus coming near in meaning to <em>*abhiññindriya</em> We should read ahīn˚ throughout DN.i.34, DN.i.77, DN.i.186, DN.i.195 DN.ii.13; MN.ii.18; MN.iii.121; Nd ii.under pucchā<!-- raw HTML omitted -->6<!-- raw HTML omitted --> (only ahīn˚).</p><p>vv.ll. at all passages for <em><a href="bword://ah%C4%ABnindriya">ahīnindriya</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ahīnindriya">ahīnindriya</a></p>

abhininnāmesi|abhininnaamesi|abhininnamesi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhininnaamesi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhininnāmeti">abhininnāmeti</a></p>

abhininnāmesiṃ|abhininnaamesi.m|abhininnamesim
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">1 plural</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhininnaamesi.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhininnāmeti">abhininnāmeti</a></p>

abhininnāmeti|abhininnaameti|abhininnameti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhininnaameti</span></p><p>bends; stretches out; directs (towards, dat./gen.)</p>

abhininnāmeti|abhininnaameti|abhininnameti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhininnaameti</span></p><p>to bend towards, to turn or direct to DN.i.76 (cittaṃ ñāṇa-dassanāya); MN.i.234; SN.i.123; SN.iv.178; Pp.60.</p><p>abhi + ninnāmeti cp. BSk. abhinirṇāmayati Lal.439</p>

abhinipajjati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>lies down on, lies down beside or with (+ acc. or loc).</p>

abhinipajjati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to lie down on Vin.iv.273 (+ abhinisīdati); AN.iv.188 (in = acc. + abhinisīdati) Pp.67 (id.).</p><p>abhi + nipajjati</p>

abhinipajjayamāna|abhinipajjayamaana|abhinipajjayamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pass. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinipajjayamaana</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinipajjati">abhinipajjati</a></p>

abhinipajjitabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinipajjati">abhinipajjati</a></p>

abhinipajjāpeti|abhinipajjaapeti|abhinipajjapeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinipajjaapeti</span></p><p>forces to lie down (on, acc.)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinipajjati">abhinipajjati</a></p>

abhinipatati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to rush on (to) Ja.ii.8.</p><p>abhi + nipatati</p>

abhinippajjati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to be produced, accrue, get, come (to) MN.i.86 (bhogā abhinipphajjanti: sic) Cnd.99 (has n’âbhinippajjanti)<br />■ Cp. <em><a href="bword://abhinipph%C4%81deti">abhinipphādeti</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + nippajjati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinipphādeti">abhinipphādeti</a></p>

abhinippanna
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(&amp; <em>-nipphanna</em>) produced, effected, accomplished DN.ii.223 (siloka); Ja.vi.36 (so read for abhinippata); Mil.8 (pph.).</p><p>abhi + nippanna, pp. of ˚nippajjati</p>

abhinippata
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>at Ja.vi.36 is to be read <em><a href="bword://abhinippanna">abhinippanna</a></em> (so variant reading BB.).</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinippanna">abhinippanna</a></p>

abhinippatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>at Dhs.1035, Dhs.1036 is to be read <em><a href="bword://abhinibbatta">abhinibbatta</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinibbatta">abhinibbatta</a></p>

abhinipphajjati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>arises, is produced.</p>

abhinipphanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>produced; accomplished</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinipphajjati">abhinipphajjati</a></p>

abhinipphatti
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>production, effecting DN.ii.283 (variant reading ˚nibbatti).</p><p>abhi + nipphatti</p>

