abhinippīḷeti|abhinippii.leti|abhinippileti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinippii.leti</span></p><p>to squeeze, crush, subdue Vism.399; often in comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with <em><a href="bword://abhinigga%E1%B9%87h%C4%81ti">abhiniggaṇhāti</a></em> MN.i.120; AN.v.230.</p><p>abhi + nippīḷeti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiniggaṇhāti">abhiniggaṇhāti</a></p>

abhinipuṇa|abhinipu.na|abhinipuna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinipu.na</span></p><p>very clever, very acute.</p>

abhinipuṇa|abhinipu.na|abhinipuna
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinipu.na</span></p><p>adjective very thorough, very clever DN.iii.167.</p><p>abhi + nipuṇa</p>

abhinipāta|abhinipaata|abhinipata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinipaata</span></p><p>(-matta) destroying, hurting (?) at Vb.321 is expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> by āpātha-matta.</p><p>cp. Divy.125 śastrâbhinipāta splitting open or cutting with a knife</p>

abhinipātana|abhinipaatana|abhinipatana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinipaatana</span></p><p>throwing down; striking.</p>

abhinipātana|abhinipaatana|abhinipatana
