<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><ol><li>devotion, adherence to, intentness on (loc); inclination (esp. to something bad); insistence, conviction (esp. of what is not true).</li><li>extension (in length or width).</li></ol>

abhinivesa
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>“settling in”, i.e. wishing for, tendency towards (-˚) inclination, adherence; as adj. liking, loving, being given or inclined to DN.iii.230; MN.i.136, MN.i.251; SN.ii.17; SN.iii.10 SN.iii.13, SN.iii.135, SN.iii.161, SN.iii.186 (saṃyojana˚) SN.iv.50; AN.iii.363 (paṭhavī˚ adj.); Cnd.227 (gāha parāmasa +); Pp.22; Vb.145; Dhs.381, Dhs.1003, Dhs.1099; Ne.28; Pv-a.252 (micchā˚), Pv-a.267 (taṇhā˚); Sdhp.71<br />■ Often comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with <em><a href="bword://adhi%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADh%C4%81na">adhiṭṭhāna</a></em> e.g. SN.ii.17; Cnd.176, and in phrase <em>idaṃ-sacc’ âbhinivesa</em> adherence to one’s dogmas, as one of the 4 Ties see kāyagantha and cp. <em>Cpd.</em> 171 n. 5.</p><p>abhi + nivesa, see *<a href="bword://nivesa">nivesa</a>*<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --> &amp; cp. nivesana</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhiṭṭhāna">adhiṭṭhāna</a>, <a href="bword://nivesa">nivesa</a></p>

abhiniveseti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>adheres to applies oneself to</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinivisati">abhinivisati</a></p>

abhinivisati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>enters, settles in; devotes oneself to, is intent on, adheres to (acc. or loc); is convinced, insists (on what is not true).</p>

abhinivisati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to cling to, adhere to, be attached to Mnd.308, Mnd.309 (parāmasati +)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhinivi%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADha">abhiniviṭṭha</a></em>; cp. also <em><a href="bword://abhinivesa">abhinivesa</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + nivisati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiniviṭṭha">abhiniviṭṭha</a>, <a href="bword://abhinivesa">abhinivesa</a></p>

abhinivissa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinivisati">abhinivisati</a></p>

abhiniviṭṭha|abhinivi.t.tha|abhinivittha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinivi.t.tha</span></p><p>adjective “settled in”, attached to, clinging on Cnd.152 (gahita parāmaṭṭha a.); Pv-a.267 (= ajjhāsita Pv.iv.8#4).</p><p>abhi + niviṭṭha, pp. of abhi-nivisati</p>

abhinivuttha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>having lived in</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinivuṭṭha">abhinivuṭṭha</a></p>

abhinivutthapubba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>having previously lived in</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinivuttha">abhinivuttha</a></p>

abhinivuṭṭha|abhinivu.t.tha|abhinivuttha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinivu.t.tha</span></p><p>having lived in</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinivuttha">abhinivuttha</a></p>

abhinādita|abhinaadita|abhinadita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhinaadita</span></p><p>resounding with (-˚), filled with the noise (or song) of (birds) Ja.vi.530 (= abhinadanto C.); Pv-a.157 (= abhiruda).</p><p>pp. of abhinādeti, Caus. of abhi + <em>nad</em>; see <em><a href="bword://nadati">nadati</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nadati">nadati</a></p>

abhinīhanati|abhiniihanati|abhinihanati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiniihanati</span></p><p>knocks out.</p>

abhinīhanati|abhiniihanati|abhinihanati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiniihanati</span></p><p>to drive away, put away, destroy, remove, avoid MN.i.119 (in phrase āṇiṃ a. abhinīharati abhinivajjeti).</p><p>abhi + nis + <em><a href="bword://han">han</a></em>, cp. Sk. nirhanti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://han">han</a></p>

abhinīharati|abhiniiharati|abhiniharati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiniiharati</span></p><p>draws out; stretches out (towards); moves (thought) out.</p>

abhinīharati|abhiniiharati|abhiniharati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiniiharati</span></p><ol><li>to take out, throw out MN.i.119 (see <em><a href="bword://abhin%C4%ABhanati">abhinīhanati</a></em>).</li><li>to direct to, to apply to (orig. to isolate? Is reading correct?) in phrase <em>ñāṇadassanāya cittaṃ abhinīharati abhininnāmeti</em> DN.i.76 (= tanninnaṃ tappoṇaṃ karoti DN-a.i.220, DN-a.i.224; variant reading abhini˚) Cp. the latter phrase also in BSk. as abhijñâbhinirhāra Avs.ii.3 (see ref. &amp; note Index p. 221); and the pp. abhinirhṛta (ṛddhiḥ) in Divy.48, Divy.49 (to obtain? Ind.), Divy.264 (take to burial), Divy.542.</li></ol><p>abhi + nīharati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinīhanati">abhinīhanati</a></p>

abhinīhāra|abhiniihaara|abhinihara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiniihaara</span></p><p>stretching out, moving (towards); intended action, firm intention; scheme.</p>

abhinīhāra|abhiniihaara|abhinihara
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiniihaara</span></p><p>being bent on (“downward force” <em>Dhs trsl.</em> 242), i.e. taking oneself out to, way of acting, (proper) behaviour, endeavour, resolve, aspiration SN.iii.267 sq. (˚kusala); AN.ii.189; AN.iii.311; AN.iv.34 (˚kusala) Ja.i.14 (Buddhabhāvāya a. resolve to become a Buddha), Ja.i.15 (Buddhattāya); Pts.i.61 sq.; Pts.ii.121; Ne.26; Mil.216; Dhp-a.i.392; Dhp-a.ii.82 (kata˚).</p><p>abhi + nīhāra, to abhinīharati; cp. BSk. sarīr’ âbhinirhāra taking (the body) out to burial, lit. meaning see note on abhinīharati</p>

abhinīla-m-āyata|abhiniila-m-aayata|abhinila-m-ayata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiniila-m-aayata</span></p><p>abhinīla-m-āyata</p><p>mfn. very black and long.</p>

abhinīla|abhiniila|abhinila
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiniila</span></p><p>adjective very black, deep black, only with ref. to the eyes, in phrase <em>-netta</em> with deep-black eyes DN.ii.18; DN.iii.144, DN.iii.167 sq. [cp. Sp. Avs.i.367 Avs.i.370 abhinīla-padma-netra]; Thig.257 (nettā ahesuṃ abbinīla-m-āyatā).</p><p>abhi + nīla</p>

abhinīlanetta|abhiniilanetta|abhinilanetta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiniilanetta</span></p><p>with very dark eyes.</p>

abhinīta|abhiniita|abhinita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiniita</span></p><ol><li>brought near, summoned; brought to (a parlous state), brought low.</li><li>highly finished, excellent</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhineti">abhineti</a></p>

abhinīta|abhiniita|abhinita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiniita</span></p><p>past participle led to, brought to, obliged by (-˚) MN.i.463 = Mil.32 (rājā &amp; cora˚); MN.i.282; SN.iii.93; Thag.350 = Thag.435 (vātaroga˚ “foredone with cramping pains” Mrs. Rk. D.); Pp.29; Mil.362.</p><p>pp. of abhi-neti</p>

abhipassa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhipassat">abhipassat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhipassati">abhipassati</a></p>

abhipassat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhipassat">abhipassat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhipassati">abhipassati</a></p>

abhipassati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>sees, looks for; regards, takes as; recognizes.</p>

abhipassati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to have regard for, look for, strive after AN.i.147 (nibbānaṃ); AN.iii.75; Snp.896 (khema˚), Snp.1070 (rattamahā˚) Mnd.308; Cnd.428; Ja.vi.370.</p><p>abhi + passati</p>

abhipatthaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhipatthayat">abhipatthayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhipatthayati">abhipatthayati</a></p>

abhipatthayana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhipatthayati">abhipatthayati</a></p>

abhipatthayat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhipatthayat">abhipatthayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhipatthayati">abhipatthayati</a></p>

abhipatthayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>longs for, wishes; desires</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhipattheti">abhipattheti</a></p>

abhipattheti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>longs for, wishes; desires</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhipatthayati">abhipatthayati</a></p>

abhipattheti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to hope for, long for, wish for Kp.viii.10; Snp-a.320; Dhp-a.i.30<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhipatthita">abhipatthita</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>abhi + pattheti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhipatthita">abhipatthita</a></p>

abhipatthita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>longed for, desires</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhipattheti">abhipattheti</a></p>

abhipatthita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>past participle hoped, wished, longed for Mil.383; Snp-a.85.</p><p>fr. abhipattheti</p>

abhipattika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective one who has attained, attaining (-˚), getting possession of SN.i.200 (devakañña˚).</p><p>fr. abhipatti</p>

abhippaharaṇa|abhippahara.na|abhippaharana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippahara.na</span></p><p>attacking, fighting, as adj. f. <em>-aṇī</em> fighting, epithet of Mārassa senā, the army of M. Snp.439 (kaṇhassa˚ the fighting army of k. = samaṇabrāhmaṇānaṃ nippothanī antarāyakārī Snp-a.390).</p><p>abhi + paharaṇa</p>

abhippahāri|abhippahaari|abhippahari
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippahaari</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhippahārin">abhippahārin</a></p><p>striking, attacking.</p>

abhippahārin|abhippahaarin|abhippaharin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippahaarin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhippahārin">abhippahārin</a></p><p>striking, attacking.</p>

abhippakirati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>scatters over, strews over, covers (completely).</p>

abhippakirati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to strew over, to cover (completely) DN.ii.137 (pupphāni Tathāgatassa sarīraṃ okiranti ajjhokiranti a.); Vv-a.38 (for abbhokirati Vv.5#9). pp. <em><a href="bword://abhippaki%E1%B9%87%E1%B9%87a">abhippakiṇṇa</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>abhi + pakirati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhippakiṇṇa">abhippakiṇṇa</a></p>

abhippakiṇṇa|abhippaki.n.na|abhippakinna
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippaki.n.na</span></p><p>completely strewn (with) Ja.i.62.</p><p>pp. of abhippakirati</p>

abhippalambati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>hangs down (over).</p>

abhippalambati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to hang down MN.iii.164 (olambati ajjholambati a.).</p><p>abhi + palambati</p>

abhippamodati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>rejoices (in).</p>

abhippamodati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to rejoice (intrs.); to please, satisfy (trs, c. acc.) MN.i.425; SN.v.312, SN.v.330; AN.v.112; Ja.iii.530; Pts.i.95, Pts.i.176, Pts.i.190.</p><p>abhi + pamodati</p>

abhippamodaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhippamodayat">abhippamodayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhippamodati">abhippamodati</a></p>

abhippamodayat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhippamodayat">abhippamodayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhippamodati">abhippamodati</a></p>

abhippasanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>well disposed (towards); having faith or confidence (in, loc, sometimes gen.)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhippasīdati">abhippasīdati</a></p>

abhippasanna
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective finding one’s peace in (c. loc.), trusting in having faith in, believing in, devoted to (loc.) Vin.iii.43; DN.i.211 (Bhagavati) SN.i.134; SN.iv.319; SN.v.225, SN.v.378; AN.iii.237, AN.iii.270, AN.iii.326 sq.; Snp.p.104 (brāhmaṇesu); Pv-a.54 (sāsand), Pv-a.142 (id.). Cp. <em><a href="bword://vippasanna">vippasanna</a></em> in same meaning.</p><p>pp. of abhippasīdati, cp. BSk. abhiprasanna</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://vippasanna">vippasanna</a></p>

abhippasāda|abhippasaada|abhippasada
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippasaada</span></p><p>faith, belief, reliance, trust Dhs.12 (“sense of assurance” <em>trsl.</em>, + saddhā), Dhs.25, Dhs.96, Dhs.288; Pv-a.223.</p><p>abhi + pasāda, cp. BSk. abhiprasāda Avs.12 (cittasyu˚) &amp; vippasāda</p>

abhippasādeti|abhippasaadeti|abhippasadeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippasaadeti</span></p><p>makes well-disposed (towards); makes have confidence (in)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhippasīdati">abhippasīdati</a></p>

abhippasādeti|abhippasaadeti|abhippasadeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippasaadeti</span></p><p>to establish one’s faith in (loc.), to be reconciled with, to propitiate Thag.1173 = Vv.21#2 (manaṃ arahantamhi = cittaṃ pasādeti Vv-a.105).</p><p>Caus. of abhippasīdati, cp. BSk. abhiprasādayati Divy.68, Divy.85, pp. abhiprasādita-manāḥ Jtm.213 220</p>

abhippasāreti|abhippasaareti|abhippasareti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippasaareti</span></p><p>stretches out towards.</p>

abhippasīdati|abhippasiidati|abhippasidati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippasiidati</span></p><p>has faith or confidence (in, loc); is well-disposed (towards, loc).</p>

abhippasīdati|abhippasiidati|abhippasidati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippasiidati</span></p><p>to have faith in DN.i.211 (fut. ˚issati)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhippasanna">abhippasanna</a></em>; Caus. <em><a href="bword://abhippas%C4%81deti">abhippasādeti</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + pasīdati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhippasanna">abhippasanna</a>, <a href="bword://abhippasādeti">abhippasādeti</a></p>

abhippasīdiṃsu|abhippasiidi.msu|abhippasidimsu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 plural</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippasiidi.msu</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhippasīdati">abhippasīdati</a></p>

abhippavassati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to shed rain upon, to pour down; intrs. to rain, to pour, fall. Usually in phrase mahāmegho abhippavassati a great cloud bursts Mil.8 Mil.13, Mil.36, Mil.304; Pv-a.132 (variant reading ati˚); intrs. Mil.18 (pupphāni ˚iṃsu poured down)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhippavu%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADha">abhippavuṭṭha</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + pavassati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhippavuṭṭha">abhippavuṭṭha</a></p>

abhippavaṭṭa|abhippava.t.ta|abhippavatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippava.t.ta</span></p><ol><li>(act.) having rained.</li><li>(pass.) rained upon</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhippavaṭṭha">abhippavaṭṭha</a></p>

abhippavaṭṭha|abhippava.t.tha|abhippavattha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippava.t.tha</span></p><ol><li>(act.) having rained.</li><li>(pass.) rained upon</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhippavaṭṭa">abhippavaṭṭa</a></p>

abhippavuṭṭha|abhippavu.t.tha|abhippavuttha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippavu.t.tha</span></p><ol><li>(act.) having rained.</li><li>(pass.) rained upon.</li></ol>

abhippavuṭṭha|abhippavu.t.tha|abhippavuttha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippavu.t.tha</span></p><p>past participle having rained, poured, fallen; trs. SN.v.51 (bandhanāni meghena ˚āni) AN.v.127; intrs. MN.ii.117 (mahāmegho ˚o there has been a cloudburst).</p><p>fr. abhippavassati</p>

abhipphuṭṭha|abhipphu.t.tha|abhipphuttha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhipphu.t.tha</span></p><p>irradiated.</p>

abhippāsāreti|abhippaasaareti|abhippasareti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhippaasaareti</span></p><p>to stretch out Vin.i.179 (pāde).</p><p>abhi + pasāreti, cp. BSk. abhiprasārayati Divy.389</p>

abhipucchati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Sk. abhipṛcchati] to ask Ja.iv.18.</p><p>abhi + pucchati</p>

abhipāleti|abhipaaleti|abhipaleti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhipaaleti</span></p><p>protects; watches over.</p>

abhipāleti|abhipaaleti|abhipaleti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhipaaleti</span></p><p>to protect Vv.84#21, cp. Vv-a.341.</p><p>abhi + pāleti</p>

abhipāruta|abhipaaruta|abhiparuta
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhipaaruta</span></p><p>adjective dressed Mil.222.</p><p>abhi + pāruta, pp. of abhipārupati</p>

abhipāteti|abhipaateti|abhipateti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhipaateti</span></p><p>to make fall, to bring to fall, to throw Ja.ii.91 (kaṇḍaṃ).</p><p>abhi + pāteti</p>

abhipīḷeti|abhipii.leti|abhipileti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhipii.leti</span></p><p>to crush, squeeze Mil.166. - pp. <em><a href="bword://abhip%C4%AB%E1%B8%B7ita">abhipīḷita</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>abhi + pīḷeti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhipīḷita">abhipīḷita</a></p>

abhipīḷita|abhipii.lita|abhipilita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhipii.lita</span></p><p>past participle crushed, squeezed Sdhp.278, Sdhp.279.</p><p>fr. abhipiḷeti</p>

abhipūreti|abhipuureti|abhipureti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhipuureti</span></p><p>to fill (up) Mil.238; Dāvs iii.60 (paṃsūhi).</p><p>abhi + pūreti</p>

abhiraddha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. &amp; neuter</i></p><ol><li>(mfn.) satisfied, pleased; conciliated; successful.</li><li>(n.) successful accomplishment, success.</li></ol>

abhiraddha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective propitiated, satisfied AN.iv.185 (+ attamana).</p><p>pp. of abhi + <em>rādh</em></p>

abhiraddhi
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>only in neg. <em>an˚</em>; displeasure, dislike, discontent AN.i.79; DN-a.i.52 (= kopass’ etaṃ adhivacanaṃ).</p><p>fr. abhiraddha</p>

abhirakkhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to guard, protect Ja.vi.589 (= pāleti C.). Cp. parirakkhati.</p><p>abhi + rakkhati</p>

abhirakkhā|abhirakkhaa|abhirakkha
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhirakkhaa</span></p><p>protection, guard Ja.i.204 (= ārakkhā Ja.i.203).</p><p>fr. abhirakkhati</p>

abhirama
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>delight; pleasure.</p>

abhiramana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>sporting, dallying, amusing oneself Pv-a.16.</p><p>fr. abhiramati</p>

abhiramanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiramati">abhiramati</a></p>

abhiramanā|abhiramanaa|abhiramana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiramanaa</span></p><p>delight, content</p><p>See also: abhiramāṇa</p>

abhiramati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>delights (in); finds pleasure (in); is content; has sexual intercourse (with, <em>saddhiṃ</em> + instr.)</p>

abhiramati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to sport, enjoy oneself, find pleasure in or with (c. loc.), to indulge in love Snp.718 Snp.1085; Ja.i.192; Ja.iii.189, Ja.iii.393; Dhp-a.i.119; Pv-a.3, Pv-a.61 Pv-a.145<br />ppr act. <em>abhiranto</em> only as nt. ˚ṃ in adv. phrase yathâbhirantaṃ after one’s liking, as much as he pleases after one’s heart’s content Vin.i.34; MN.i.170; Snp.53.<br />ppr med. <em>abhiramamāna</em> Ja.iii.188, Pv-a.162<br />pp abhirata (q.v.).<br />■ 2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->nd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> Caus. <em><a href="bword://abhiram%C4%81peti">abhiramāpeti</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>abhi + <em>ram</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiramāpeti">abhiramāpeti</a></p>

abhiramaṇā|abhirama.naa|abhiramana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhirama.naa</span></p><p>delight, content</p><p>See also: abhiramāna</p>

abhirami
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiramati">abhiramati</a></p>

abhiramittha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiramati">abhiramati</a></p>

abhiramiṃ|abhirami.m|abhiramim
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">1 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhirami.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiramati">abhiramati</a></p>

abhiramāpana|abhiramaapana|abhiramapana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiramaapana</span></p><p>gladdening, entertaining; causing to find pleasure (in); producing contentedness.</p>

abhiramāpana|abhiramaapana|abhiramapana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiramaapana</span></p><p>causing pleasure to (acc.), being a source of pleasure making happy MN.iii.132 (gāmante).</p><p>fr. abhiramāpeti, Caus<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --> of abhiramati</p>

abhiramāpeti|abhiramaapeti|abhiramapeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiramaapeti</span></p><ol><li>to induce to sport, to cause one to take pleasure Ja.iii.393.</li><li>to delight, amuse, divert Ja.i.61<br />■ Cp. <em><a href="bword://abhiram%C4%81pana">abhiramāpana</a></em>.</li></ol><p>Caus. ii. fr. abhiramati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiramāpana">abhiramāpana</a></p>

abhiranta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiramati">abhiramati</a></p>

abhirata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>finding delight (in); content (with, loc. or ifc)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiramati">abhiramati</a></p>

abhirata
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective (-˚) found of, indulging in, finding delight in AN.iv.224 (nekkhamma˚); AN.v.175 (id.) Snp.86 (nibbāna˚), Snp.275 (vihesa˚), Snp.276 (kalaha˚); Ja.v.382 (dāna˚); Pv-a.54 (puññakamma˚), Pv-a.61 (satibhavana˚), Pv-a.105 (dānâdipuñña˚).</p><p>pp. of abhiramati</p>

abhiratarūpa|abhirataruupa|abhiratarupa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhirataruupa</span></p><p>absolutely content</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhirata">abhirata</a></p>

abhiratatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>the fact of being fond of, delighting in (-˚) Ja.v.254 (kāma˚).</p><p>abstr. fr. abhirata</p>

abhirati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>pleasure, delighting (in, loc. or ifc.); contentment.</p>

abhirati
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>delight or pleasure in (loc. or-˚) SN.i.185; SN.iv.260; AN.v.122; Dhp.88. <em>-an˚</em>; displeasure discontent, distaste Vin.ii.110; DN.i.17 (+ paritassanā); SN.i.185; SN.v.132; AN.iii.259; AN.iv.50; AN.v.72 sq., AN.v.122; Ja.iii.395; DN-a.i.111; Pv-a.187.</p><p>fr. abhi + <em>ram</em></p>

abhiratta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>excited, impassioned.</p>

abhiratta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective very red Ja.v.156; fig. very much excited or affected with (-˚) Snp.891 (sandiṭṭhirāgena a.).</p><p>abhi + ratta</p>

abhiravati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to shout ont Bv.ii.90 = Ja.i.18 (verse 99)</p><p>abhi + ravati</p>

abhiroceti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>to like, to find delight in (acc.), to desire, long for Ja.iii.192; Ja.v.222 (roceti); Vv.64#23 (vataṃ abhirocayi = abhirocesi ruccitvā pūresi ti attho; abhirādhayi ti pi pāṭho; sādhesi nipphādesī ti attho Vv-a.282).</li><li>to please, satisfy, entertain gladden Vv.64#24 (but Vv-a.292: abhibhavitvā vijjotati thus to no. 3).</li><li>variant reading for <em>atiroceti</em> (to surpass in splendour) at Vv.81#12, cp. also no. 2.</li></ol><p>abhi + roceti, Caus. of <em>ruc</em></p>

abhiropana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>concentration of mind, attention (seems restricted to Pts ii. only) Pts.ii.82 (variant reading abhiniropana), Pts.ii.84, Pts.ii.93, Pts.ii.115 (buddhi˚), Pts.ii.142 (˚virāga), Pts.ii.145 (˚vimutti), Pts.ii.216 (˚abhisamaya). See also <em><a href="bword://abhiniropana">abhiniropana</a></em>.</p><p>fr. abhiropeti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiniropana">abhiniropana</a></p>

abhiropayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>causes to rise; plants; puts on, fixes on, fastens (esp. on a thūpa)/ presents as an offering</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiropeti">abhiropeti</a>, <a href="bword://abhirūhati">abhirūhati</a></p>

abhiropeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>causes to rise; plants; puts on, fixes on, fastens (esp. on a thūpa)/ presents as an offering</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiropayati">abhiropayati</a>, <a href="bword://abhirūhati">abhirūhati</a></p>

abhiropeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to fix one’s mind on, to pay attention, to show reverence, to honour Vv.37#7 (aor. ˚ropayi = ropesi Vv-a.169), Vv.37#10 (id.; = pūjaṃ kāresi Vv-a.172), Vv.60#4 (= pūjesi Vv-a.253); Dāvs v.19.</p><p>abhi + ropeti, cp. Sk. adhiropayati, Caus. of <em>ruh</em></p>

abhiruci
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>delight, longing, pleasure, satisfaction Pv-a.168 (= ajjhāsaya).</p><p>Sk. abhiruci, fr. abhi + <em>ruc</em></p>

abhirucita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>pleasing, agreeable, approved.</p>

abhirucita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective pleasing, agreeable, liked Ja.i.402; Dhp-a.i.45.</p><p>pp. fr. abhi + <em>ruc</em></p>

abhiruda
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective -˚ resounding with (the cries of animals, esp. the song of birds), full of the sound of (birds) Thag.1062 (kuñjara˚), Thag.1113 (mayūra-koñca˚) Ja.iv.466 (adāsakunta˚); Ja.v.304 (mayūra-koñca˚); Ja.vi.172 (id. = upagīta C.), Ja.vi.272 (sakunta˚; = abhigīta C.), Ja.vi.483 (mayūra-koñca˚), Ja.vi.539; Pv.ii.12#3 (haṃsa-koñca˚; = abhinādita Pv-a.157)<br />■ The form abhiruta occurs at Thag.49.</p><p>Sk. abhiruta</p>

abhiruhana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>climbing (on to); embarking</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhirūhana">abhirūhana</a></p>

abhiruhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>ascends, climbs; climbs on to or into; embarks (on); steps on</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhirūhati">abhirūhati</a></p>

abhiruhi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiruhati">abhiruhati</a></p>

abhiruhitvā|abhiruhitvaa|abhiruhitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruhitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiruhati">abhiruhati</a></p>

abhirādhana|abhiraadhana|abhiradhana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiraadhana</span></p><p>satisfaction.</p>

abhirādheti|abhiraadheti|abhiradheti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiraadheti</span></p><p>to please, satisfy, make happy Ja.i.421; DN-a.i.52<br />aor (pret.) <em>abhirādhayi</em> Vv.31#5 (= abhirādhesi Vv-a.130); Vv.64#23 (gloss for abhirocayi Vv-a.282); Ja.i.421; Ja.iii.386 (= paritosesi C.)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhir%C4%81dhita">abhirādhita</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + rādheti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhirādhita">abhirādhita</a></p>

abhirādhi|abhiraadhi|abhiradhi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiraadhi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhirādhin">abhirādhin</a></p><p>pleasing, giving satisfaction.</p>

abhirādhin|abhiraadhin|abhiradhin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiraadhin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhirādhin">abhirādhin</a></p><p>pleasing, giving satisfaction.</p>

abhirādhin|abhiraadhin|abhiradhin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiraadhin</span></p><p>adjective (-˚) pleasing, giving pleasure, satisfaction. Ja.iv.274 (mitta˚ = ārādhento tosento Commentary)</p><p>fr. abhirādheti</p>

abhirādhita|abhiraadhita|abhiradhita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiraadhita</span></p><p>successfully attained.</p>

abhirādhita|abhiraadhita|abhiradhita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiraadhita</span></p><p>having succeeded in, fallen to one’s share, attained Thag.259.</p><p>pp. of abhirādheti</p>

abhirāja|abhiraaja|abhiraja
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiraaja</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhirājan">abhirājan</a></p><p>supreme king.</p>

abhirājan|abhiraajan|abhirajan
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiraajan</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhirājan">abhirājan</a></p><p>supreme king.</p>

abhirūhana|abhiruuhana|abhiruhana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruuhana</span></p><p>climbing (on to); embarking</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiruhana">abhiruhana</a></p>

abhirūhana|abhiruuhana|abhiruhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruuhana</span></p><p>climbing, ascending, climb Mil.356.</p><p>BSk. ˚rūhana, e.g. Mvu.ii.289</p>

abhirūhanta|abhiruuhanta|abhiruhanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mf</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruuhanta</span></p><p>(~antī)n.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhirūhati">abhirūhati</a></p>

abhirūhati|abhiruuhati|abhiruhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruuhati</span></p><p>ascends, climbs; climbs on to or into; embarks (on); steps on</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiruhati">abhiruhati</a></p>

abhirūhati|abhiruuhati|abhiruhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruuhati</span></p><p>(abhiruhati) to ascend, mount, climb; to go on or in to (c. acc.) Dhp.321; Thag.271; Ja.i.259; Ja.ii.388; Ja.iii.220; Ja.iv.138 (navaṃ); Ja.vi.272 (peculiar aor. ˚rucchi with ābhi metri causa; = abhirūhi C.); DN-a.i.253<br />ger <strong>abhiruyha</strong> Ja.iii.189; Pv-a.75, Pv-a.152 (as variant reading T. has ˚ruyhitva), Pv-a.271 (nāvaṃ), &amp; <em>abhirūhitvā</em> Ja.i.50 (pabbataṃ), Ja.ii.128.</p><p>abhi + <em>ruh</em></p><p>See also: abhiruyha</p>

abhirūhi|abhiruuhi|abhiruhi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruuhi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhirūhati">abhirūhati</a></p>

abhirūhitabba|abhiruuhitabba|abhiruhitabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruuhitabba</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhirūhati">abhirūhati</a></p>

abhirūhitvā|abhiruuhitvaa|abhiruhitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruuhitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhirūhati">abhirūhati</a></p>

abhirūhiya|abhiruuhiya|abhiruhiya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruuhiya</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhirūhati">abhirūhati</a></p>

abhirūpa|abhiruupa|abhirupa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruupa</span></p><p>handsome; beautiful.</p>

abhirūpa|abhiruupa|abhirupa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruupa</span></p><p>adjective of perfect form, (very), handsome, beautiful, lovely Snp.410 (= dassaniya’ angapaccanga Snp-a.383); Ja.i.207; Pp.52; DN-a.i.281 (aññehi manussehi adhikarūpa); Vv-a.53; Pv-a.61 (abhikkanta). Occurs in the idiomatic phrase denoting the characteristics of true beauty <em>abhirūpa dassanīya pāsādika</em> (+ paramāya vaṇṇa-pokkharatāya samannāgata), e.g. Vin.i.268; DN.i.47, DN.i.114, DN.i.120; SN.ii.279; AN.ii.86, AN.ii.203 Cnd.659; Pp.66; Dhp-a.i.281 (compar.); Pv-a.46.</p><p>abhi + rūpa</p>

abhirūpanandā|abhiruupanandaa|abhirupananda
<p>[DPPN]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruupanandaa</span></p><p>AbhirūpanandāAbhirūpaNandā</p><p>The two verses preached to her by the Buddha are given in the Therīgāthā. Thig.19–20</p>

abhirūpatara|abhiruupatara|abhirupatara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. (compar.)</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruupatara</span></p><p>more beautiful</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhirūpa">abhirūpa</a></p>

abhirūḷha|abhiruu.lha|abhirulha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruu.lha</span></p><ol><li>(act.) having climbed on to; mounted (on).</li><li>(pass.) ascended, climbed by</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhirūhati">abhirūhati</a></p>

abhirūḷha|abhiruu.lha|abhirulha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiruu.lha</span></p><p>mounted, gone up to, ascended Ja.v.217; Dhp-a.i.103.</p><p>pp. of abhirūhati</p>

abhisaddaha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhisaddahat">abhisaddahat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaddahati">abhisaddahati</a></p>

abhisaddahanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaddahati">abhisaddahati</a></p>

abhisaddahat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhisaddahat">abhisaddahat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaddahati">abhisaddahati</a></p>

abhisaddahati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>has faith, believes (in, gen. personae, acc. rei).</p>

abhisaddahati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to have faith in, believe in (c. acc.) believe SN.v.226; Thag.785; Pv.iv.1#13, Pv.iv.1#25 (˚saddaheyya paṭiñeyya Pv-a.226); Ne.11; Mil.258; Pv-a.26 Dāvs iii.58.</p><p>abhi + saddahati, cp. Sk. abhiśraddadhāti, e.g. Divy.17, Divy.337</p>

abhisajati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>reviles; offends.</p>

abhisajjana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>adjective only as adv. f. ˚nī. Epithet of vācā scolding abusing, cursing AN.v.265 (para˚). Cp. next.</p><p>abstr. fr. abhisajjati in meaning of abhisanga 2</p>

abhisajjanā|abhisajjanaa|abhisajjana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisajjanaa</span></p><p>offense; (or attachment).</p>

abhisajjanā|abhisajjanaa|abhisajjana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisajjanaa</span></p><p>at Snp.49 evidently means “scolding, cursing, being in bad temper” (cp. abhisajjati), as its comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with vāc’ âbhilāpa indicates, but is expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> both by Nd ii.&amp; Bdhgh. as “sticking to, cleaving, craving, desire” (= taṇhā), after the meaning of abhisanga. See Cnd.89 &amp; Cnd.107; Snp-a.98 (sineha-vasena) cp. also the compromise-expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n<!-- raw HTML omitted --> by Bdhgh. of abhisajjati as kodha-vasena <em><a href="bword://laggati">laggati</a></em> (DN-a.i.257).</p><p>abstr. fr. abhisajjati, cp. abhisajjana</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://laggati">laggati</a></p>

abhisajjati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pass. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><ol><li>sticks, is attached; is occupied; lingers.</li><li>is offended, takes offense; is hostile</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisajati">abhisajati</a></p>

abhisajjati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to be in ill temper, to be angry, to curse, imprecate (in meaning of abhisanga 2) DN.i.91 (= kodha-vasena laggati DN-a.i.257), DN.iii.159; Ja.iii.120 (+ kuppati); Ja.iv.22 (abhisajji kuppi vyāpajji, cp. BSk. abhiṣajyate kupyati vyāpadyate. Avs.i.286); Ja.v.175 (= kopeti C.); Dhp.408 (abhisaje Pot. kujjhāpana-vasena laggapeyya Dhp-a.iv.182); Pp.30, Pp.36. See also abhisajjana &amp; abhisajjanā.</p><p>abhi + <em>sañj</em>; cp. abhisanga</p>

abhisajji
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisajati">abhisajati</a></p>

abhisallekhika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>concerned with austerity, with strict abstinence</p><p>See also: ābhisallekhika</p>

abhisallekhika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective austere, stern, only in f. <em>-ā</em> (scil. kathā) AN.iii.117 sq.; AN.iv.352, AN.iv.357; AN.v.67.</p><p>abhi + sallekha + ika</p>

abhisamaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>penetration into; right understanding (of).</p>

abhisamaya
<p>[Nyana]</p><p></p><p><strong>Abhisamaya:</strong> ‘breakthrough or penetration to the realization of the truth’, is the full and direct comprehension of the Four Noble Truths by the Stream-winner <em>sotāpanna</em> see: <em>ariya-puggala</em>. In the Com. the term is represented by ‘penetration’ <em>pativedha</em>. Frequently occurring as <em>dhammābhisamaya</em> ‘realization of the doctrine’ se e: XIII <em>ābhisamaya</em> - <em>samyutta</em> and Pts.M. <em>ābhisamaya</em> - <em>kathā.</em></p>

abhisamaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>“coming by completely”, insight into, comprehension, realization clear understanding, grasp, penetration. See on term <em>Kvu trsl.</em> 381 sq<br />■ Esp. in full phrases: <em>attha˚</em>; grasp of what is proficient SN.i.87 = AN.iii.49 = Iti.17, cp. AN.ii.46 <em>ariyasaccānaṃ</em> a. full understanding of the 4 noble truths SN.v.415, SN.v.440, SN.v.441 [cp. Divy.654: anabhisamitānāṃ caturnāṃ āryasatyānāṃ a.]; Snp.758 (sacca˚ = sacc’ âvabodha Snp-a.509); Mil.214 (catusacc˚); Sdhp.467 (catusacc˚), Sdhp.525 (saccānaṃ); <em>dhamm’ âbhisamaya</em> full grasp of the Dhamma, quasi conversion [cp. dharm’ âbhisamaya Divy.200] SN.ii.134; Mil.20, Mil.350; Vv-a.219; Pv-a.9 etc frequent; <em>sammā-</em> mān’ âbhisamaya full understanding of false pride in ster. phrase” acchecchi (for acchejji) taṇhaṃ vivattayi saññojanaṃ sammāmānâbhisamayā antam akāsi dukkhassa” at SN.iv.205, SN.iv.207, SN.iv.399; AN.iii.246, AN.iii.444; Iti.47 cp. māna˚ SN.i.188 = Thig.20 (tato mānâbhisamayā upasanto carissasi, trsl. by Mrs. Rh. D. in <em>K. S.</em> 239 “hath the mind mastered vain imaginings, then mayst thou go thy ways calm and serene”); Snp.342 (expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> by mānassa abhisamayo khayo vayo pahānaṃ Snp-a.344). Also in foll passages: SN.ii.5 (paññāya), SN.ii.104 (id.), SN.ii.133 sq. (Abhisamaya Saṃyutta); Snp.737 (phassa˚, expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> ad sensum but not at verbum by phassa-nirodha Snp-a.509); Pts.ii.215 Pp.41; Vv.16#10 (= saccapaṭivedha Vv-a.85); DN-a.i.32; Dhp-a.i.109; Vv-a.73 (bhāvana˚), Vv-a.84 (sacchikiriya˚); Dpvs.i.31. <em>-anabhisamaya</em> not grasping correctly, insufficient understanding, taken up wrongly SN.iii.260; Pp.21; Dhs.390, Dhs.1061, Dhs.1162 (Mrs. Rh. D. trsl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->s.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> “lack of coordination”).</p><p>abhi + samaya, from sam + <em><a href="bword://i">i</a></em>, cp. abhisameti &amp; sameti; BSk. abhisamaya, e.g. Divy.200, Divy.654</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://i">i</a></p>

abhisambhava
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>only in <em>dur˚</em>; hard to overcome or get over, hard to obtain or reach, troublesome SN.v.454; AN.v.202; Snp.429, Snp.701; Ja.v.269, Ja.vi.139, Ja.vi.439. Abhisambhavati (bhoti)</p><p>fr. abhisambhavati</p>

abhisambhavana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>(from abhisambhavati) mastering.</p>

abhisambhavati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>reaches, attains; is able, capable (of); is adequate; masters; endures, bears.</p>

abhisambhavati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Abhisambhavati (˚bhoti)</p><p>“to come up to”, i.e. to be able to (get or stand or overcome) to attain, reach, to bear AN.iv.241; Thag.436; Mnd.471 Mnd.485; Ja.iii.140; Ja.v.150, Ja.v.417; Ja.vi.292, Ja.vi.293, Ja.vi.507 (fut. med ˚sambhossaṃ = sahissāmi adhivāsessāmi C.); Pts.ii.193. ger. <em>-bhutvā</em> Thag.1057 &amp; <em>-bhavitvā</em> Snp.52 (cp. Cnd.85)<br />aor <em>-bhosi</em> DN.ii.232<br />grd <em>-bhavanīya</em> DN.ii.210; Pts.ii.193<br />■ See also <em><a href="bword://abhisambhu%E1%B9%87%C4%81ti">abhisambhuṇāti</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + sambhavati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisambhuṇāti">abhisambhuṇāti</a></p>

abhisambhavitvā|abhisambhavitvaa|abhisambhavitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisambhavitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisambhavati">abhisambhavati</a></p>

abhisambhonta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mf</i></p><p>(~ontī)n.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisambhoti">abhisambhoti</a></p>

abhisambhosi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisambhoti">abhisambhoti</a></p>

abhisambhoti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>reaches, attains; is able, capable (of); is adequate; masters; endures, bears.</p>

abhisambhoti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Abhisambhavati (˚bhoti)</p><p>“to come up to”, i.e. to be able to (get or stand or overcome) to attain, reach, to bear AN.iv.241; Thag.436; Mnd.471 Mnd.485; Ja.iii.140; Ja.v.150, Ja.v.417; Ja.vi.292, Ja.vi.293, Ja.vi.507 (fut. med ˚sambhossaṃ = sahissāmi adhivāsessāmi C.); Pts.ii.193. ger. <em>-bhutvā</em> Thag.1057 &amp; <em>-bhavitvā</em> Snp.52 (cp. Cnd.85)<br />aor <em>-bhosi</em> DN.ii.232<br />grd <em>-bhavanīya</em> DN.ii.210; Pts.ii.193<br />■ See also <em><a href="bword://abhisambhu%E1%B9%87%C4%81ti">abhisambhuṇāti</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + sambhavati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisambhuṇāti">abhisambhuṇāti</a></p>

abhisambhutvā|abhisambhutvaa|abhisambhutva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisambhutvaa</span></p><p>having mastered; having endured; having bore.</p>

abhisambhuṇāti|abhisambhu.naati|abhisambhunati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisambhu.naati</span></p><p>to be able (to get or reach); only in neg ppr. <em>anabhisambhuṇanto</em> unable DN.i.101 (= asampāpuṇanto avisahamāno vā DN-a.i.268); Mnd.77, Mnd.312.</p><p>considered to be a bastard form of abhisambhavati, but probably of diff. origin &amp; etym.; also in Bh. Sk. freq.</p>

abhisambhū|abhisambhuu|abhisambhu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisambhuu</span></p><p>(from abhisambhavati) mastering.</p>

abhisambhū|abhisambhuu|abhisambhu
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisambhuu</span></p><p>adjective getting, attaining (?) DN.ii.255 (lomahaṃsa˚).</p><p>fr. abhi + sam + <em><a href="bword://bh%C5%AB">bhū</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://bhū">bhū</a></p>

abhisambhūta|abhisambhuuta|abhisambhuta
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisambhuuta</span></p><p>attained, got Sdhp.556.</p><p>pp. of abhisambhavati</p>

abhisambodha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>perfect understanding; awakening.</p>

abhisambodhi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>perfect understanding (of a Buddha); complete awakening.</p>

abhisambodhi
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>the highest enlightenment Ja.i.14 (parama˚). Cp. abhisambujjhana and (sammā-) sambodhi.</p><p>abhi + sambodhi</p>

abhisambodhita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective awakened to the highest wisdom Pv-a.137 (Bhagavā).</p><p>pp. of abhisambodheti, Caus. of abhi + sambujjhati</p>

abhisambuddha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><ol><li><p>(mfn.)</p><ol><li>(act.) having understood; having attained complete understanding; become a Buddha.</li><li>(pass.) completely understood, realized</li></ol></li><li><p>(n.) complete understanding.</p></li></ol>

abhisambuddha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>(pass.) realised, perfectly understood DN.iii.273; SN.iv.331; Iti.121 <em>an˚</em>; not understood MN.i.71, MN.i.92, MN.i.114, MN.i.163, MN.i.240</li><li>(med.) one who has come to the realisation of the highest wisdom, fully-awakened, attained Buddhahood, realising enlightened (in or as to = acc.) Vin.i.1; DN.ii.4; MN.i.6 (sammāsambodhiṃ); SN.i.68, SN.i.138, SN.i.139 &amp; passim Pv-a.94, Pv-a.99.</li></ol><p>pp. of abhisambujjhati</p>

abhisambuddhatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>thorough realisation, perfect understanding SN.v.433.</p><p>abstr. fr. abhisambuddha</p>

abhisambudhāna|abhisambudhaana|abhisambudhana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisambudhaana</span></p><p>understanding; realizing.</p>

abhisambudhāna|abhisambudhaana|abhisambudhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisambudhaana</span></p><p>adjective awaking realising, knowing, understanding Dhp.46 (= bujjhanto jānanto ti attho Dhp-a.i.337).</p><p>formation of a ppr. med. fr. pp. abhsam + <em>budh</em> instead of abhisam + <em>bujjh˚</em>.</p>

abhisambujjhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>= abhisambodhi Ja.i.59.</p>

abhisambujjhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>attains perfect or complete understanding (of); becomes a Buddha.</p>

abhisambujjhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to become wideawake, to awake to the highest knowledge, to gain the highest wisdom (sammāsambodhiṃ) DN.iii.135; Iti.121 aor. <em>-sambujjhi</em> SN.v.433; Pv-a.19. In comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> <em>abhisambujjhati abhisameti</em>, e.g. SN.ii.25; SN.iii.139<br />ppr med <em>-sambudhāna</em>; pp. <em>-sambuddha</em> -Caus. <em>-sambodheti</em> to make awake, to awaken, to enlighten; pp. <em>-bodhita</em>.</p><p>abhi + sambujjhati</p>

abhisambujjhitvā|abhisambujjhitvaa|abhisambujjhitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisambujjhitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisambujjhati">abhisambujjhati</a></p>

abhisambujjhiṃsu|abhisambujjhi.msu|abhisambujjhimsu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 plural</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisambujjhi.msu</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisambujjhati">abhisambujjhati</a></p>

abhisamecca
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisameti">abhisameti</a></p>

abhisamekkhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Abhisamikkhati &amp; Abhisamekkhati</p><p>to behold, see, regard, notice Ja.iv.19 (2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->nd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg med. ˚samekkhase = olokesi C.)<br />ger <em>-samikkha ˚samekkha;</em> [B.Sk. ˚samīkṣya, e.g. Jtm.p.28, Jtm.p.30 etc.] Ja.v.340 (˚samikkha, variant reading sañcikkha = passitvā C.); Ja.v.393 Ja.v.394 (= disvā C.).</p><p>abhi + sam + ; <em>īks</em>, cp. samikkhati</p>

abhisamesuṃ|abhisamesu.m|abhisamesum
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 plural</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisamesu.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisameti">abhisameti</a></p>

abhisameta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>understood; grasped</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisameti">abhisameti</a></p>

abhisameta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>completely grasped or realised, understood mastered SN.v.128 (dhamma a.), SN.v.440 (anabhisametāni cattāri ariyasaccāni, cp. Divy.654 anabhisamitāni c.a.) AN.iv.384 (appattaṃ asacchikataṃ +).</p><p>pp. of abhisameti, fr. abhi + sam + <em><a href="bword://i">i</a></em>, taken as caus. formation, against the regular form Sk.P. samita &amp; B.Sk. abhisamita</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://i">i</a></p>

abhisameti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>attains; grasps; understands.</p>

abhisameti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to come by, to attain, to realise grasp, understand (cp. adhigacchati) Mil.214 (catusaccâbhisamayaṃ abhisameti). frequently in comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> <em>abhisambujjhati abhisameti; abhisambujjhitvā abhisametvā</em>, e.g. SN.ii.25 SN.iii.139; Kv.321<br />fut <em>-samessati</em> SN.v.441<br />aor <em>-samiṃsu</em> Mil.350; <em>-samesuṃ</em> SN.v.415<br />ger <em>-samecca</em> (for ˚icca under influence of ˚sametvā as caus. form. Trenckner’s expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --><em>Notes</em> 56<!-- raw HTML omitted -->4<!-- raw HTML omitted --> is unnecessary &amp; hardly justifiable) SN.v.438 (an˚ by not thoroughly understanding) AN.v.50 (samm’attha˚ through complete realisation of what is proficient); Snp.143 (= abhisamāgantvā Kp-a.236) and <em>-sametvā</em> SN.ii.25; SN.iii.139<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhisameta">abhisameta</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>abhi + sameti, sam + <em><a href="bword://i">i</a></em>; in inflexion base is taken partly as ordinary &amp; partly as causative, e.g. aor ˚samiṃsu &amp; ˚samesuṃ, pp. sameta: Sk. samita. Cp. B.Sk abhisamayati, either caus. or denom. formation, Divy.617 caturāryasatyāni a.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisameta">abhisameta</a>, <a href="bword://i">i</a></p>

abhisametvā|abhisametvaa|abhisametva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisametvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisameti">abhisameti</a></p>

abhisametāvi|abhisametaavi|abhisametavi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisametaavi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhisametāvin">abhisametāvin</a></p><p>who has understood; understanding clearly.</p>

abhisametāvin|abhisametaavin|abhisametavin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisametaavin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhisametāvin">abhisametāvin</a></p><p>who has understood; understanding clearly.</p>

abhisametāvin|abhisametaavin|abhisametavin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisametaavin</span></p><p>adjective commanding full understanding or penetration, possessing complete insight (of the truth) Vin.iii.189; SN.ii.133; SN.v.458 sq.</p><p>possess. adj<br />■ formation, equalling a n. ag. form., pp. abhisameta</p>

abhisamikkhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Abhisamikkhati &amp; Abhisamekkhati</p><p>to behold, see, regard, notice Ja.iv.19 (2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->nd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg med. ˚samekkhase = olokesi C.)<br />ger <em>-samikkha ˚samekkha;</em> [B.Sk. ˚samīkṣya, e.g. Jtm.p.28, Jtm.p.30 etc.] Ja.v.340 (˚samikkha, variant reading sañcikkha = passitvā C.); Ja.v.393 Ja.v.394 (= disvā C.).</p><p>abhi + sam + ; <em>īks</em>, cp. samikkhati</p>

abhisamita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>understood; grasped</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisameti">abhisameti</a></p>

abhisammati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to cease, stop; trs. (Caus.) to allay, pacify, still Ja.vi.420 (pp. abhisammanto for ˚śammento? Reading uncertain).</p><p>abhi + <em>śam</em>, Sk. abhiśamyati</p>

abhisampanna
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>at Pv-a.144 is wrong reading for variant reading abhisapana (curse).</p>

abhisamparāya|abhisamparaaya|abhisamparaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisamparaaya</span></p><p>future fate, condition in one’s next rebirth.</p>

abhisamparāya|abhisamparaaya|abhisamparaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisamparaaya</span></p><p>future lot, fate, state after death, future condition of rebirth; usually in foll phrases: <em>kā gati ko abhisamparāyo</em> (as hendiadys) ʻwhat fate in the world-to-come’, DN.ii.91; Vin.i.293; SN.iv.59 SN.iv.63; SN.v.346, SN.v.356, SN.v.369; Dhp-a.i.221<br />■ <em>evaṃ-gatika evanabhisamparāya</em> (adj.) “leading to such &amp; such a revirn such &amp; such a future state” DN.i.16, DN.i.24, DN.i.32, DN.i.33 etc (= evaṃ-vidhā paralokā ti DN-a.i.108)<br />■ abhisamparāyaṃ (acc. as adv.) in future, after death AN.i.48; AN.ii.197; AN.iii.347 AN.iv.104; Pv.iii.5#10 (= punabbhave Pv-a.200)<br />■ <em>diṭṭhe c’eva dhamme abhisamparāyañ ca</em> “in this world and in the world to come” AN.ii.61; Pp.38; Mil.162; Pv-a.195 etc. (see also <em><a href="bword://di%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADha">diṭṭha</a></em>)<br />■ Used absolutely at Pv-a.122 (= fate).</p><p>abhi + samparāya</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://diṭṭha">diṭṭha</a></p>

abhisamparāyaṃ|abhisamparaaya.m|abhisamparayam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisamparaaya.m</span></p><p>in a future state; in the next existence.</p>

abhisamācita|abhisamaacita|abhisamacita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisamaacita</span></p><p>heaped together; accumulated.</p>

abhisamācāra|abhisamaacaara|abhisamacara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisamaacaara</span></p><p>good conduct.</p>

abhisamācārika|abhisamaacaarika|abhisamacarika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisamaacaarika</span></p><p>belonging to good conduct (the minimum of decent behavior), proper; relating to the basic discipline; belonging to the basic or minor discipline</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ābhisamācārika">ābhisamācārika</a></p>

abhisamācārika|abhisamaacaarika|abhisamacarika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisamaacaarika</span></p><p>adjective belonging to the practice of the lesser ethics; to be practiced; belonging to or what is the least to be expected of good conduct, proper. Of <em><a href="bword://sikkh%C4%81">sikkhā</a></em> Vin.v.181; AN.ii.243 sq.; of <em><a href="bword://dhamma">dhamma</a></em> MN.i.469; AN.iii.14 sq.; AN.iii.422.</p><p>abhi + samācārika, to samācāra</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://sikkhā">sikkhā</a>, <a href="bword://dhamma">dhamma</a></p>

abhisamācārika-sīla|abhisamaacaarika-siila|abhisamacarika-sila
<p>[Nyana]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisamaacaarika-siila</span></p><p><strong>Abhisamācārika-sīla: ’</strong> morality consisting in good behaviour’, relates to the external duties of a Bhikkhu such as towards his senior, etc. <strong>abhisamācārika-sīla</strong> is a name for those moral rules other than the 8 ending with right livelihood i.e. 4-fold right speech, 3-fold right action and right livelihood, as in the 8-fold path Vis.M I; see: <em>sacca</em> IV, 3-5. Impossible is it, o Bhikkhus, that without having fulfilled the law of good behaviour, a Bhikkhu could fulfill the law of genuine pure conduct A. V, 21. Cf. <em>ādibrahmacariyaka-sīla</em></p>

abhisamāgacchati|abhisamaagacchati|abhisamagacchati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisamaagacchati</span></p><p>to come to (understand) completely, to grasp fully, to master Kp-a.236 (for abhisamecca Snp.143).</p><p>abhi + sam + āgacchati, cp. in meaning adhigacchati</p>

abhisanda
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>outflow, overflow, yield, issue, result only in foll. phrases: <em>cattāro puññ’ âbhisandā kusal’ âbhisandā</em> (yields in merit) SN.v.391 sq.; AN.ii.54 sq. AN.iii.51, AN.iii.337; AN.vi.245, &amp; <em>kamm’ âbhisanda</em> result of kamma Mil.276<br />■ Cp. <em><a href="bword://abhisandana">abhisandana</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + sanda of <em>syad</em>, cp. BSk. abhisyanda, e.g. Mvu.ii.276</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisandana">abhisandana</a></p>

abhisandahati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>puts or places together; arranges.</p>

abhisandahati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to put together, to make ready Thag.151; ger. <em>abhisandhāya</em> in sense of a prep. = on account of, because of Ja.ii.386 (= paṭicca C.).</p><p>abhi + sandahati of saṃ + <em>dhā</em></p>

abhisandahitvā|abhisandahitvaa|abhisandahitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisandahitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisandahati">abhisandahati</a></p>

abhisandana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>result, outcome, consequence Pts.i.17 (sukhassa).</p><p>= abhisanda</p>

abhisandayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>makes overflow; floods, drenches</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisandeti">abhisandeti</a></p>

abhisandeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>makes overflow; floods, drenches</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisandayati">abhisandayati</a></p>

abhisandeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to make overflow, to make full, fill, pervade DN.i.73, DN.i.74.</p><p>abhi + sandeti, Caus. of <em>syad</em></p>

abhisankhāra|abhisankhaara|abhisankhara
<p>[Nyana]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisankhaara</span></p><p><strong>Abhisankhāra:</strong> Construction identical with the 2nd link of the <em>paticca</em> - <em>samuppāda</em>, <em>sankhāra</em>, under I, 1 or kammic-constructions.</p>

abhisanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>flooded, drenched; filled (with), overflowing</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhissanna">abhissanna</a></p>

abhisanna
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective overflowing, filled with (-˚), full Vin.i.279 (˚kāya a body full of humours, cp. Vin.ii.119 &amp; Mil.134) Ja.i.17 (Ja.v.88 pītiyā); Mil.112 (duggandha˚).</p><p>pp. of abhisandati = abhi + <em>syand</em>, cp. Sk. abhisanna</p>

abhisantāpaya|abhisantaapaya|abhisantapaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisantaapaya</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhisantāpayat">abhisantāpayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisantāyati">abhisantāyati</a></p>

abhisantāpayat|abhisantaapayat|abhisantapayat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisantaapayat</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhisantāpayat">abhisantāpayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisantāyati">abhisantāyati</a></p>

abhisantāpetabba|abhisantaapetabba|abhisantapetabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisantaapetabba</span></p><p>torments; afflicts</p><p>See also: abhisañtāpeti</p>

abhisantāpeti|abhisantaapeti|abhisantapeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisantaapeti</span></p><p>torments; afflicts</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisantāyati">abhisantāyati</a></p>

abhisantāpeti|abhisantaapeti|abhisantapeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisantaapeti</span></p><p>to burn out, scorch, destroy MN.i.121.</p><p>ahhi + santāpeti, Caus. of santapati</p>

abhisantāyati|abhisantaayati|abhisantayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisantaayati</span></p><p>torments; afflicts</p><p>See also: abhisañtāpeti</p>

abhisapana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>cursing, curse Pv-a.144 (so read for abhisampanna).</p><p>fr. abhisapati</p>

abhisapanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mf</i></p><p>(~antī)n.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisapati">abhisapati</a></p>

abhisapati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>curses, puts a curse on; swears.</p>

abhisapati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to execrate, curse, accurse Vin.iv.276; Ja.iv.389; Ja.v.87; Dhp-a.i.42<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhisatta">abhisatta</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + sapati, of <em>śap</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisatta">abhisatta</a></p>

abhisapi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisapati">abhisapati</a></p>

abhisapita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>cursed; reviled</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisapati">abhisapati</a></p>

abhisapitvā|abhisapitvaa|abhisapitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisapitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisapati">abhisapati</a></p>

abhisara
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>retinue Ja.v.373.</p><p>fr. abhi + sarati, of <em>sṛ</em>; to go</p>

abhisasi
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor.</i></p><p>of <em><a href="bword://abhisa%E1%B9%83sati">abhisaṃsati</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṃsati">abhisaṃsati</a></p>

abhisatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>ordered, controlled.</p>

abhisatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>cursed, accursed, railed at, reviled Ja.iii.460; Ja.v.71; Snp-a.364 (= akkuṭṭha); Vv-a.335.</p><p>pp. of abhisapati, cp. Sk. abhiśapta, fr. abhi + <em>śap</em></p>

abhisattha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>cursed, accursed Thag.118 “old age falls on her as if it had been cursed upon her (that is, laid upon her by a curse). Morris J.P.T.S. 1886 145 gives the commentator’s equivalents, “commanded worked by a charm”. This is a curious idiom. Any European would say that the woman herself, not the old age was accursed. But the whole verse is a riddle and Kern’s translation (</p><blockquote><p>Toevoegselen</p></blockquote><p>s. v.) ʻhurried up’ seems to us impossible.</p><p>pp. of abhisaṃsati</p>

abhisavati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(better <em>-ssavati</em>?) to flow towards or into Ja.vi.359 (najjo Gangaṃ a.).</p><p>abhi + savati, of <em>sru</em></p>

abhisañcayati|abhisa~ncayati|abhisancayati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa~ncayati</span></p><p>Abhisañcināti &amp; ˚cayati</p><p>to accumulate, collect (merit) Vv.47#6 (Pot. ˚sañceyyaṃ = ˚sañcineyyaṃ Vv-a.202).</p><p>abhi + sañcināti</p>

abhisañcetayati|abhisa~ncetayati|abhisancetayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa~ncetayati</span></p><p>thinks out, plans.</p>

abhisañcetayita|abhisa~ncetayita|abhisancetayita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa~ncetayita</span></p><p>thought out, planned</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisañcetayati">abhisañcetayati</a></p>

abhisañcetayita|abhisa~ncetayita|abhisancetayita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa~ncetayita</span></p><p>raised into consciousness, thought out, intended, planned MN.i.350; SN.ii.65; SN.iv.132; AN.v.343.</p><p>pp. of abhisañceteti</p>

abhisañceteti|abhisa~nceteti|abhisanceteti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa~nceteti</span></p><p>to bring to consciousness, think out, devise, plan SN.ii.82<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhisa%C3%B1cetayita">abhisañcetayita</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>abhi + sañceteti or ˚cinteti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisañcetayita">abhisañcetayita</a></p>

abhisañchanna|abhisa~nchanna|abhisanchanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa~nchanna</span></p><p>completely covered.</p>

abhisañcināti|abhisa~ncinaati|abhisancinati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa~ncinaati</span></p><p>Abhisañcināti &amp; ˚cayati</p><p>to accumulate, collect (merit) Vv.47#6 (Pot. ˚sañceyyaṃ = ˚sañcineyyaṃ Vv-a.202).</p><p>abhi + sañcināti</p>

abhisaññanirodha|abhisa~n~nanirodha|abhisannanirodha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa~n~nanirodha</span></p><p>cessation of perception, of awareness.</p>

abhisaññā|abhisa~n~naa|abhisanna
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa~n~naa</span></p><p>Only in the compound <em>abhi-saññā-nirodha</em> DN.i.179, DN.i.184. The prefix abhi qualifies, not saññā, but the whole compound, which means ʻtrance’. It is an expression used, not by Buddhists, but by certain wanderers See <em>saññā-vedayita-nirodha</em>.</p>

abhisaññūhati|abhisa~n~nuuhati|abhisannuhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa~n~nuuhati</span></p><p>to heap up, concentrate Vb.1, Vb.2, Vb.82 sq.; Vb.216 sq., Vb.400; Mil.46 Cp. <em><a href="bword://abhisa%E1%B9%85khipati">abhisaṅkhipati</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + saññūhati, i.e. saṃ-ni-ūhati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkhipati">abhisaṅkhipati</a></p>

abhisaṃhati|abhisa.mhati|abhisamhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa.mhati</span></p><p>is excited; rejoices in the prospect of</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhihasati">abhihasati</a></p>

abhisaṃsanā|abhisa.msanaa|abhisamsana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa.msanaa</span></p><p>is doubtful reading at Vv.64#10; meaning “neighing” (of horses) Vv-a.272, Vv-a.279.</p><p>? abhisaṃsati</p>

abhisaṃsati|abhisa.msati|abhisamsati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa.msati</span></p><p>to execrate, revile, lay a curse on Ja.v.174 (˚saṃsittha 3<!-- raw HTML omitted -->rd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg. pret med. = paribhāsi C.)<br />aor <em><a href="bword://abhisasi">abhisasi</a></em> Ja.vi.187, Ja.vi.505, Ja.vi.522 (= akkosi C.), Ja.vi.563 (id.)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhisattha">abhisattha</a></em>. Cp. also <em><a href="bword://abhisi%E1%B9%83sati">abhisiṃsati</a></em>.</p><p>Vedic abhiśaṃsati, abhi + <em>śaṃs</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisasi">abhisasi</a>, <a href="bword://abhisattha">abhisattha</a>, <a href="bword://abhisiṃsati">abhisiṃsati</a></p>

abhisaṃvisati|abhisa.mvisati|abhisamvisati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa.mvisati</span></p><p>attaches oneself to; clings to.</p>

abhisaṃvisati|abhisa.mvisati|abhisamvisati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa.mvisati</span></p><p>Only in <em>abhisaṃvisseyyagattaṃ</em> (or -bhastaṃ or -santuṃ) Thig.466 a compound of doubtful derivation and meaning. Mrs. Rh. D., following Dhammapāla (p. 283) ʻa bag of skin with carrion filled’.</p><p>abhi + saṃvisati</p>

abhisaṅga|abhisa"nga|abhisanga
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nga</span></p><p>I. sticking to, cleaving to, adherence to Ja.v.6; Ne.110 Ne.112; Dhs-a.129 (˚hetukaṃ dukkhaṃ), Dhs-a.249 (˚rasa).</p><p>fr. abhi + sañj, cp. abhisajjati &amp; Sk. abhisanga</p>

abhisaṅgi|abhisa"ngi|abhisangi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"ngi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhisaṅgin">abhisaṅgin</a></p><ol><li>sticking to, attached to.</li><li>taking offense, being hostile.</li></ol>

abhisaṅgin|abhisa"ngin|abhisangin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"ngin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhisaṅgin">abhisaṅgin</a></p><ol><li>sticking to, attached to.</li><li>taking offense, being hostile.</li></ol>

abhisaṅgin|abhisa"ngin|abhisangin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"ngin</span></p><p>adjective cleaving to (-˚) Sdhp.566.</p><p>fr. abhisanga</p>

abhisaṅkhacca|abhisa"nkhacca|abhisankhacca
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhacca</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkharoti">abhisaṅkharoti</a></p>

abhisaṅkharesi|abhisa"nkharesi|abhisankharesi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkharesi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkhareti">abhisaṅkhareti</a></p>

abhisaṅkhareti|abhisa"nkhareti|abhisankhareti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhareti</span></p><p>causes to be prepared, created; forms</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkharoti">abhisaṅkharoti</a></p>

abhisaṅkharitvā|abhisa"nkharitvaa|abhisankharitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkharitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkharoti">abhisaṅkharoti</a></p>

abhisaṅkharo|abhisa"nkharo|abhisankharo
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkharo</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkharot">abhisaṅkharot</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkharoti">abhisaṅkharoti</a></p>

abhisaṅkharot|abhisa"nkharot|abhisankharot
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkharot</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkharot">abhisaṅkharot</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkharoti">abhisaṅkharoti</a></p>

abhisaṅkharoti|abhisa"nkharoti|abhisankharoti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkharoti</span></p><p>plans, prepares; creates, constructs, concocts; accumulates; produces a motive force (as a result of action).</p>

abhisaṅkharoti|abhisa"nkharoti|abhisankharoti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkharoti</span></p><p>(&amp; <em>-khāreti</em> in Pot.) to prepare, do, perform, work, get up Vin.i.16 (iddh’ âbhisankhāraṃ ˚khāreyya); DN.i.184 (id.); SN.ii.40; SN.iii.87 SN.iii.92; SN.iv.132, SN.iv.290; SN.v.449; AN.i.201; Snp.984 (ger. ˚itvā having got up this curse, cp. Snp-a.582); Pv-a.56 (iddh’ âbhisaṃkhāraṃ), Pv-a.172 (id.), Pv-a.212 (id.)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhisa%E1%B9%85khata">abhisaṅkhata</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>abhi + sankharoti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkhata">abhisaṅkhata</a></p>

abhisaṅkhata|abhisa"nkhata|abhisankhata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhata</span></p><p>planned, prepared, arranged; concocted, constructed, produced artificially; accumulated</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkhaṭa">abhisaṅkhaṭa</a>, <a href="bword://abhisaṅkhita">abhisaṅkhita</a>, <a href="bword://abhisaṅkharoti">abhisaṅkharoti</a></p>

abhisaṅkhata|abhisa"nkhata|abhisankhata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhata</span></p><p>adjective prepared, fixed, made up, arranged, done MN.i.350; AN.ii.43; AN.v.343; Ja.i.50; Mnd.186 (kappita +); Pv-a.7, Pv-a.8.</p><p>abhi + sankhata, pp. of abhisankharoti</p>

abhisaṅkhaṭa|abhisa"nkha.ta|abhisankhata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkha.ta</span></p><p>planned, prepared, arranged; concocted, constructed, produced artificially; accumulated</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkhata">abhisaṅkhata</a>, <a href="bword://abhisaṅkhita">abhisaṅkhita</a>, <a href="bword://abhisaṅkharoti">abhisaṅkharoti</a></p>

abhisaṅkhipati|abhisa"nkhipati|abhisankhipati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhipati</span></p><p>to throw together, heap together, concentrate Vb.1 sq., Vb.82 sq., Vb.216 sq. Vb.400; Mil.46.</p><p>abhi + sankhipati</p>

abhisaṅkhita|abhisa"nkhita|abhisankhita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhita</span></p><p>planned, prepared, arranged; concocted, constructed, produced artificially; accumulated</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkhaṭa">abhisaṅkhaṭa</a>, <a href="bword://abhisaṅkhata">abhisaṅkhata</a>, <a href="bword://abhisaṅkharoti">abhisaṅkharoti</a></p>

abhisaṅkhitta|abhisa"nkhitta|abhisankhitta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhitta</span></p><p>heaped together, collected; concentrated, condensed.</p>

abhisaṅkhāra|abhisa"nkhaara|abhisankhara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhaara</span></p><p>preparation; development; performance; accumulation of motive force (as a result of action), impetus.</p>

abhisaṅkhāra|abhisa"nkhaara|abhisankhara
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhaara</span></p><ol><li><p>putting forth, performance, doing, working, practice: only in two comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->ns.<!-- raw HTML omitted -->, viz</p><ol><li><em>gamiya˚</em>; (or gamika˚) a heathenish practice Vin.i.233; AN.iv.180, &amp;</li><li><em>iddha˚</em>; (= iddḥi˚) working of supernormal powers Vin.i.16; DN.i.106; SN.iii.92; SN.iv.289; SN.v.270 Snp.p.107; Pv-a.56, Pv-a.172, Pv-a.212.</li></ol></li><li><p>preparation, store accumulation (of kamma, merit or demerit), substratum state (see for detail sankhāra) SN.iii.58 (an˚); Mnd.334 Mnd.442; Cnd. s.v.; Vb.135 (puñña˚ etc.), Vb.340; Dhs-a.357 (˚viññāna “storing intellect” <em>Dhs trsl.</em> 262).</p></li></ol><p>abhi + sankhāra</p>

abhisaṅkhāri|abhisa"nkhaari|abhisankhari
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhaari</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkharoti">abhisaṅkharoti</a></p>

abhisaṅkhārika|abhisa"nkhaarika|abhisankharika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhaarika</span></p><p>specially prepared; produced artificially.</p>

abhisaṅkhārika|abhisa"nkhaarika|abhisankharika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhaarika</span></p><p>adjective what belongs to or is done by the sankhāras; accumulated by or accumulating merit, having special (meritorious) effect (or specially prepared?) Vin.ii.77 = Vin.iii.160; Sdhp.309 (sa ˚paccaya).</p><p>fr. abhisankhāra</p>

abhisaṅkhārituṃ|abhisa"nkhaaritu.m|abhisankharitum
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">inf.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhaaritu.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkharoti">abhisaṅkharoti</a></p>

abhisaṅkhāsi|abhisa"nkhaasi|abhisankhasi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa"nkhaasi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisaṅkharoti">abhisaṅkharoti</a></p>

abhisaṭa|abhisa.ta|abhisata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn. (pass.)</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa.ta</span></p><p>visited; approached.</p>

abhisaṭa|abhisa.ta|abhisata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisa.ta</span></p><ol><li>(med.) streamed forth, come together Ja.vi.56 (= sannipatita C.).</li><li>(pass.) approached, visited Vin.i.268.</li></ol><p>pp. of abhisarati, abhi + <em>sṛ</em>; to flow</p>

abhisecana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>= abhiseka, viz.</p><ol><li>ablution, washing off Thig.239 &amp; Thig.245 (udaka˚)</li><li>consecration Ja.ii.353.</li></ol>

abhiseceti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to cause to be sprinkled or inaugurated Ja.v.26. (imper. abhisecayassu).</p><p>caus. of abhisiñcati</p>

abhiseka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>worthy of inauguration as king</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ābhiseka">ābhiseka</a></p>

abhiseka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>anointing, consecration, inauguration (as king) AN.i.107 (cp. abhisitta), AN.ii.87 read abhisek’-anabhisitto; Ja.ii.104, Ja.ii.352; Dhp-a.i.350; Pv-a.74. Cp. ābhisekika.</p><p>fr. abhi + <em>sic</em>, cp. Sk. abhiṣeka</p>

abhisekika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>belonging to or used for the inauguration (of a king)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisekiya">abhisekiya</a>, <a href="bword://ābhisekika">ābhisekika</a></p>

abhisekiya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>belonging to or used for the inauguration (of a king)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisekiya">abhisekiya</a>, <a href="bword://ābhisekika">ābhisekika</a></p>

abhisevana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>pursuit of; indulgence in.</p>

abhisevanā|abhisevanaa|abhisevana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisevanaa</span></p><p>pursuit, indulgence in (-˚) Sdhp.210 (pāpakamma˚).</p><p>abhi + sevana fr. <em>sev</em></p>

abhisitta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>sprinkled; inaugurated (as king or queen)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisiñcati">abhisiñcati</a></p>

abhisitta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>sprinkled over, anointed Snp.889 (manasā, cp. Mnd.298); Mil.336 (amatena loka a.).</li><li>consecrated (King), inaugurated (more freq. in this conn. is avasitta), Vin.iii.44; AN.i.107 (khattiyo khattiyehi khattiy’ âbhisekena a.); AN.ii.87 (variant reading for avasitta also an˚).</li></ol><p>pp. of abhisiñcati, Sk. ˚sikta</p>

abhisiñcapeti|abhisi~ncapeti|abhisincapeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisi~ncapeti</span></p><p>causes to be inaugurated; has made king or queen.</p>

abhisiñcati|abhisi~ncati|abhisincati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisi~ncati</span></p><p>sprinkles; sprinkles (with water) to inaugurate as king or queen; consecrates.</p>

abhisiñcati|abhisi~ncati|abhisincati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisi~ncati</span></p><p>to sprinkle over, fig. to anoint (King), to consecrate AN.i.107 (Khattiy’ âbhisekena Ja.i.399 (fig. ˚itvā ger. Ja.ii.409 (id.); Ja.vi.161 (id.); Mnd.298; Mil.336 (amatena lokaṃ abhisiñci Bhagavā); Pv-a.144 (read abhisiñci cimillikañ ca…)-Pass. abhisiñcati Mil.359<br />pp <em><a href="bword://abhisitta">abhisitta</a></em><br />caus <em><a href="bword://abhiseceti">abhiseceti</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + siñncati fr. <em>sic</em> to sprinkle; see also <em><a href="bword://%C4%81si%C3%B1cati">āsiñcati</a></em> &amp; ava˚, Vedic only ā˚</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisitta">abhisitta</a>, <a href="bword://abhiseceti">abhiseceti</a>, <a href="bword://āsiñcati">āsiñcati</a></p>

abhisiñcayati|abhisi~ncayati|abhisincayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisi~ncayati</span></p><p>sprinkles; inaugurates (as king).</p>

abhisiñciṃsu|abhisi~nci.msu|abhisincimsu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisi~nci.msu</span></p><p>3 p.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisiñcati">abhisiñcati</a></p>

abhisiṃsati|abhisi.msati|abhisimsati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisi.msati</span></p><p>to utter a solemn wish, Vv.81#18 (aor. ˚sīsi. variant reading ˚sisi. Vv-a.316 explains by icchi sampaṭicchi).</p><p>= abhisaṃsati, abhi + <em>śaṃs</em>. As to Sk. <em>śaṃs</em> → P. <em>siṃs</em> cp. āsiṃsati, as to meaning cp. nature of prayer as a solemn rite to the “infernals”, cp. im-precare</p>

abhisobhita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>adorned; looking bright.</p>

abhissanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>flooded, drenched; filled (with), overflowing</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisanna">abhisanna</a></p>

abhissara
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective only neg. <em>an˚</em>; in formula atāṇo loko anabhissaro “without a Lord or protector MN.ii.68 (variant reading ˚abhisaro); Pts.i.126 (variant reading id.).</p><p>abhi + issara</p>

abhisādheti|abhisaadheti|abhisadheti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisaadheti</span></p><p>to carry out, arrange; to get; procure, attain Ja.vi.180; Mil.264.</p><p>abhi + sādheti</p>

abhisāpa|abhisaapa|abhisapa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisaapa</span></p><p>curse; term of abuse.</p>

abhisāpa|abhisaapa|abhisapa
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisaapa</span></p><p>curse, anathema SN.iii.93 = Iti.89 (which latter reads abhilāpa and It A explains by akkosa see vv.ll. under abhilāpa &amp; cp.; <em>Brethren</em> 376 n. 1.) Thag.1118.</p><p>abhisapati</p>

abhisāpayati|abhisaapayati|abhisapayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisaapayati</span></p><p>cursed</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisāpeti">abhisāpeti</a>, <a href="bword://abhisapati">abhisapati</a></p>

abhisāpeti|abhisaapeti|abhisapeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisaapeti</span></p><p>cursed</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhisāpayati">abhisāpayati</a>, <a href="bword://abhisapati">abhisapati</a></p>

abhisāreti|abhisaareti|abhisareti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisaareti</span></p><p>to approach, to persecute Ja.vi.377.</p><p>abhi + sāreti, Caus. of abhisarati</p>

abhisāriyā|abhisaariyaa|abhisariya
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhisaariyaa</span></p><p>woman who goes to meet her lover Ja.iii.139.</p><p>Sk. abhisārikā, fr. abhi + <em>sṛ</em>.</p>

abhitakketi
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to search for Dāvs v.4.</p><p>abhi + takketi</p>

abhitatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>scorched; distressed, exhausted (by heat).</p>

abhitatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>scorched (by heat), dried up, exhausted, in phrases uṇha˚ Vin.ii.220; Mil.97, and ghamma˚ SN.ii.110, SN.ii.118; Snp.1014; Ja.ii.223; Vv-a.40; Pv-a.114.</p><p>pp. of abhi + tapati</p>

abhitiṭṭhati|abhiti.t.thati|abhititthati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiti.t.thati</span></p><p>stands supreme over; overpowers; surpasses.</p>

abhitiṭṭhati|abhiti.t.thati|abhititthati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiti.t.thati</span></p><p>to stand out supreme, to excel, surpass DN.ii.261; Ja.vi.474 (abhiṭṭhāya = abhibhavitvā C.).</p><p>abhi + tiṭṭhati</p>

abhito
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i></p><p>near, in the presence of (+ acc. or gen.); round about, on both sides (of, acc.).</p>

abhito
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>indeclinable adv. case fr. prep. abhi etym.</p><ol><li>round about, on both sides Ja.vi.535 (= ubhayapassesu C.) Ja.vi.539</li><li>near, in the presence of Vv.64#1 (= samīpe Vv-a.275).</li></ol>

abhitosaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhitosayat">abhitosayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhitosayati">abhitosayati</a></p>

abhitosayat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhitosayat">abhitosayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhitosayati">abhitosayati</a></p>

abhitosayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>gratifies; delights.</p>

abhitoseti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to please thoroughly, to satisfy, gratify Snp.709 (= atīva toseti Snp-a.496).</p><p>abhi + toseti</p>

abhitthaneti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to roar, to thunder Ja.i.330, Ja.i.332 = Cp.iii.10#7.</p><p>abhi + thaneti</p>

abhittharati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>makes haste.</p>

abhittharati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to make haste Dhp.116 (= turitaturitaṃ sīghasīghaṃ karoti Dhp-a.iii.4).</p><p>abhi + tarati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->, evidently wrong for abhittarati</p>

abhitthavana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>praise Thag-a.74.</p><p>fr. prec.</p>

abhitthavati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>praises; praises (someone in their presence).</p>

abhitthavati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to praise Ja.i.89; Ja.iii.531; Dāvs iii.23; Dhp-a.i.77; Pv-a.22; cp. <em><a href="bword://abhitthunati">abhitthunati</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + thavati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhitthunati">abhitthunati</a></p>

abhitthavi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhitthavati">abhitthavati</a></p>

abhitthunati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to praise Ja.i.17 (aor abhitthuniṃsu); cp. thunati 2<br />pp <em>-tthuta</em> Dhp-a.i.88.</p><p>abhi + thunati; cp. abhitthavati</p>

abhitunna
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(tuṇṇa). Overwhelmed, overcome overpowered SN.ii.20; Pts.i.129 (dukkha˚), Pts.i.164; Ja.i.407 Ja.i.509 (˚tuṇṇa); Ja.ii.399, Ja.ii.401; Ja.iii.23 (soka˚); Ja.iv.330; Ja.v.268, Sdhp.281.</p><p>not as Morris, J.P.T.S. 1886, 135, suggested fr. abhi + <em>tud</em>, but acc. to Kern,</p><blockquote><p>Toevoegselen</p></blockquote><p>p. 4 fr. abhi + <em>tūrv</em>. (Cp. turati &amp; tarati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --> and Ved. turvati) Thus the correct spelling is <em>-tuṇṇa</em> = Sk. abhitūrṇa. The latter occurs as variant reading under the disguise of (sok-)âhituṇḍa for ˚abhituṇṇa at M. Vastu iii.2</p>

abhitāpa|abhitaapa|abhitapa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhitaapa</span></p><p>extreme heat or pain.</p>

abhitāpa|abhitaapa|abhitapa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhitaapa</span></p><p>extreme heat, glow; adj. very hot Vin.iii.83 (sīsa˚ sunstroke); MN.i.507 (mahā˚ very hot) Mil.67 (mahābhitāpatara much hotter); Pv.iv.1#8 (mahā˚ of niraya).</p><p>abhi + tāpa</p>

abhitāḷita|abhitaa.lita|abhitalita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhitaa.lita</span></p><p>struck.</p>

abhitāḷita|abhitaa.lita|abhitalita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhitaa.lita</span></p><p>hammered to pieces, beaten, struck Vism.231 (muggara˚).</p><p>abhi + tāḷita fr. tāḷeti</p>

abhivada
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhivadat">abhivadat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivadati">abhivadati</a></p>

abhivadat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhivadat">abhivadat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivadati">abhivadati</a></p>

abhivadati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><ol><li>addresses (respectfully), salutes; welcomes; approves of.</li><li>declares, asserts; speaks, names.</li></ol>

abhivadati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>to speak out, declare, promise Ja.i.83 = Vin.i.36; Ja.vi.220.</li><li>to speak (kindly to, to welcome, salute, greet. In this sense always comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with <em><a href="bword://abhinandati">abhinandati</a></em>, e.g. at MN.i.109, MN.i.266, MN.i.458; SN.iii.14 SN.iv.36 sq.; Mil.69</li></ol><p>caus <em><a href="bword://abhiv%C4%81deti">abhivādeti</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + vadati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinandati">abhinandati</a>, <a href="bword://abhivādeti">abhivādeti</a></p>

abhivadita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>saluted</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivadati">abhivadati</a></p>

abhivaditabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivadati">abhivadati</a></p>

abhivadiṃ|abhivadi.m|abhivadim
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">1 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivadi.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivadati">abhivadati</a></p>

abhivagga
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine a</i></p><p>sort of portcullis or large spiked defensive weapon.</p>

abhivagga
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>great mass (?), superior force (?), only in phrase <em>-ena omaddati</em> to crush with sup. force or overpower MN.i.87 = Cnd.199#6.</p><p>abhi + vagga</p>

abhivandati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>salutes respectfully.</p>

abhivandati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to salute respectfully, to honour, greet; grd. <em>-vandanīya</em> Mil.227.</p><p>abhi + vandati</p>

abhivandita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>saluted; greeted with honor</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivandati">abhivandati</a></p>

abhivasana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>clothing, clothes.</p>

abhivasanavaratara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>the very best of clothing, choice clothes</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivasana">abhivasana</a></p>

abhivassa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>rain; a shower.</p>

abhivassaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>raining, pouring out.</p>

abhivassaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective raining, fig. shedding, pouring ont, yielding Vv-a.38 (puppha˚).</p><p>fr. abhivassati</p>

abhivassat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">par. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhivassat">abhivassat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivassati">abhivassati</a></p>

abhivassati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>rains, rains down (upon, acc.); showers.</p>

abhivassati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to rain, shed rain, pour; fig. rain down, pour out, shed DN.iii.160 (ābhivassaṃ metri causa); AN.iii.34; Thag.985; Ja.i.18 (Ja.v.100 pupphā a. stream down); Cp.iii.10#6; Mil.132, Mil.411. pp. <em>abhivaṭṭa &amp; abhivuṭṭha;</em> (q.v.)<br />caus <em>II. abhivassāpeti</em> to cause (the sky to) rain Mil.132.</p><p>abhi + vassati from <em>vṛṣ</em></p>

abhivassin
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective = <em><a href="bword://abhivassaka">abhivassaka</a></em> Iti.64, Iti.65 (sabbattha˚).</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivassaka">abhivassaka</a></p>

abhivañcana|abhiva~ncana|abhivancana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiva~ncana</span></p><p>deceit, fraud Dāvs iii.64.</p><p>abhi + <em>vañc</em></p>

abhivaḍḍhana|abhiva.d.dhana|abhivaddhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiva.d.dhana</span></p><p>adjective noun increasing (trs.), augmenting; f. ˚ī Sdhp.68.</p><p>fr. abhivaḍḍhati</p>

abhivaḍḍhati|abhiva.d.dhati|abhivaddhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiva.d.dhati</span></p><p>increases, grows more and more; grows higher than, outgrows (+ acc.).</p>

abhivaḍḍhati|abhiva.d.dhati|abhivaddhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiva.d.dhati</span></p><ol><li>to increase (intrs.) DN.i.113, DN.i.195 (opp. hāyati); MN.ii.225; AN.iii.46 (bhogā a.); Dhp.24; Mil.374; Pv-a.8, Pv-a.133; Sdhp.288, Sdhp.523.</li><li>to grow over or beyond, to outgrow Ja.iii.399 (vanaspatiṃ)</li></ol><p>pp <em>abhivuḍḍha &amp; ˚vuddha;</em> (q.v.).</p><p>Vedic abhivardhati, abhi + <em>vṛdh</em></p>

abhivaḍḍhi|abhiva.d.dhi|abhivaddhi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiva.d.dhi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivaḍḍhati">abhivaḍḍhati</a></p>

abhivaḍḍhi|abhiva.d.dhi|abhivaddhi
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiva.d.dhi</span></p><p>increase, growth Mil.94<br />■ See also <em><a href="bword://abhivuddhi">abhivuddhi</a></em>.</p><p>cp. Sk. abhivṛddhi, fr. abhi + <em>vṛdh</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivuddhi">abhivuddhi</a></p>

abhivaṇṇayati|abhiva.n.nayati|abhivannayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiva.n.nayati</span></p><p>praises; describes</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivaṇṇeti">abhivaṇṇeti</a></p>

abhivaṇṇeti|abhiva.n.neti|abhivanneti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiva.n.neti</span></p><p>praises; describes</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivaṇṇayati">abhivaṇṇayati</a></p>

abhivaṇṇeti|abhiva.n.neti|abhivanneti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiva.n.neti</span></p><p>to praise Sdhp.588 (˚ayi). - pp. <em><a href="bword://abhiva%E1%B9%87%E1%B9%87ita">abhivaṇṇita</a></em>.</p><p>abhi + vanneti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivaṇṇita">abhivaṇṇita</a></p>

abhivaṇṇita|abhiva.n.nita|abhivannita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiva.n.nita</span></p><p>praised Dpvs.i.4.</p><p>pp. of abhivanneti</p>

abhivaṭṭa|abhiva.t.ta|abhivatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiva.t.ta</span></p><p>rained upon Dhp.335 (gloss ˚vuṭṭha; cp. Dhp-a.iv.45); Mil.176 Mil.197, Mil.286<br />■ <em>Note.</em> Andersen <em>P. R.</em> prefers reading abhivaḍḍha at Dhp.335 “the abounding Bīraṇa grass”).</p><p>pp. of abhivassati, see also <em><a href="bword://abhivu%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADha">abhivuṭṭha</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivuṭṭha">abhivuṭṭha</a></p>

abhivaṭṭha|abhiva.t.tha|abhivattha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiva.t.tha</span></p><p>(pass.) rained upon</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivuṭṭha">abhivuṭṭha</a>, <a href="bword://abhivassati">abhivassati</a></p>

abhivedeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>to make known, to communicate Dāvs v.2, Dāvs v.11.</li><li>to know Ja.vi.175 (jānāti C.).</li></ol><p>abhi + Caus. of <em>vid</em></p>

abhiveṭheti|abhive.theti|abhivetheti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhive.theti</span></p><p>Kern’s (</p><blockquote><p>Toevoegselen</p></blockquote><p>s. v.) proposed reading at Ja.v.452 for <em>ati˚</em>; which however does not agree with C expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> on p. 454.</p>

abhivihacca
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i></p><p>dispersing, removing; having destroyed.</p>

abhivihacca
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>having destroyed, removed or expelled; only in one simile of the sun driving darkness away at MN.i.317 = SN.iii.156; SN.v.44 = Iti.20.</p><p>ger. of abhi + vihanati</p>

abhivijayati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(&amp; <strong>vijināti</strong>) to overpower, to conquer. Of <em>-jayati</em> the ger. <em>-jiya</em> at DN.i.89, DN.i.134 DN.ii.16. Of <em>-jināti</em> the pres. 3<!-- raw HTML omitted -->rd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> pl. <em>-jinanti</em> at Mil.39 the ger. <em>-jinitvā</em> at MN.i.253; Pp.66.</p><p>abhi + vijayati</p><p>See also: vijināti</p>

abhivijinituṃ|abhivijinitu.m|abhivijinitum
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">inf.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivijinitu.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivijināti">abhivijināti</a></p>

abhivijinitvā|abhivijinitvaa|abhivijinitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivijinitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivijināti">abhivijināti</a></p>

abhivijināti|abhivijinaati|abhivijinati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivijinaati</span></p><p>overpowers; wins; is victorious.</p>

abhivijiya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivijināti">abhivijināti</a></p>

abhivinaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>higher discipline; the discipline in detail or analyzed.</p>

abhivinaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>higher discipline, the refinements of discipline or Vinaya; comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with abhidhamma, e.g. DN.iii.267; MN.i.472; also with vinaya Vin.v.1 sg.</p><p>abhi + vinaya</p>

abhivinaye
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i></p><p>as to the Vinaya; as regards the discipline.</p>

abhivindati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>finds; obtains.</p>

abhivindati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to find, get, obtain Snp.460 (= labhati adhigacchati Snp-a.405).</p><p>abhi + vindati</p>

abhivinde
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">opt. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivindati">abhivindati</a></p>

abhivirājetvā|abhiviraajetvaa|abhivirajetva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhiviraajetvaa</span></p><p>being completely free from desire.</p>

abhivisajati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>pours forth; gives away, dispenses.</p>

abhivisaji
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivisajati">abhivisajati</a></p>

abhivisiṭṭha|abhivisi.t.tha|abhivisittha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivisi.t.tha</span></p><p>adjective most excellent, very distinguished DN-a.i.99, DN-a.i.313.</p><p>abhi + visiṭṭha</p>

abhivissajjati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to send out, send forth, deal out, give DN.iii.160.</p><p>abhi + vissajjati</p>

abhivissattha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>trusting; confident in.</p>

abhivissattha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>confided in, taken into confidence MN.ii.52 (variant reading ˚visaṭṭha).</p><p>abhi + vissattha, pp. of abhivissasati, Sk. abhiviśvasta</p>

abhivitarati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>goes through, finds out for certain; is sure.</p>

abhivitarati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>“to go down to”, i.e. give in, to pay heed, observe Vin.i.134 and in ster. expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> of sañcicca at Vin.ii.91; Vin.iii.73, Vin.iii.112; Vin.iv.290.</p><p>abhi + vitarati</p>

abhivitaritvā|abhivitaritvaa|abhivitaritva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivitaritvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivitarati">abhivitarati</a></p>

abhiviññāpesi|abhivi~n~naapesi|abhivinnapesi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivi~n~naapesi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhiviññāpeti">abhiviññāpeti</a></p>

abhiviññāpeti|abhivi~n~naapeti|abhivinnapeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivi~n~naapeti</span></p><p>begs, entreats; solicits (from); induces (to do something).</p>

abhiviññāpeti|abhivi~n~naapeti|abhivinnapeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivi~n~naapeti</span></p><p>to turn somebody’s mind on (c. acc.), to induce somebody (dat.) to (acc.) Vin.iii.18 (purāṇadutiyikāya methunaṃ dhammaṃ abhiviññāpesi).</p><p>abhi + viññāpeti</p>

abhivuddha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>grown up Mil.361.</p><p>pp. of abhivaḍḍhati, see also ˚*<a href="bword://vu%E1%B8%8D%E1%B8%8Dha">vuḍḍha</a>*</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://vuḍḍha">vuḍḍha</a></p>

abhivuddhi
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>increase, growth, prosperity Mil.34.</p><p>Sk. abhivṛddhi, see also <em><a href="bword://abhiva%E1%B8%8D%E1%B8%8Dhi">abhivaḍḍhi</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivaḍḍhi">abhivaḍḍhi</a></p>

abhivuḍḍha|abhivu.d.dha|abhivuddha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivu.d.dha</span></p><p>increased, enriched Pv-a.150.</p><p>pp. of abhivaḍḍhati, see also ˚*<a href="bword://vuddha">vuddha</a>*</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://vuddha">vuddha</a></p>

abhivuṭṭha|abhivu.t.tha|abhivuttha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivu.t.tha</span></p><p>(pass.) rained upon</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivaṭṭha">abhivaṭṭha</a>, <a href="bword://abhivassati">abhivassati</a></p>

abhivuṭṭha|abhivu.t.tha|abhivuttha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivu.t.tha</span></p><p>poured out or over, shed out (of water or rain) Thag.1065; Dhp.335 (gloss); Pv-a.29.</p><p>pp. of abhivassati, see also <em><a href="bword://abhiva%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADa">abhivaṭṭa</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivaṭṭa">abhivaṭṭa</a></p>

abhivyāpeti|abhivyaapeti|abhivyapeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivyaapeti</span></p><p>see <em><a href="bword://abhiby%C4%81peti">abhibyāpeti</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhibyāpeti">abhibyāpeti</a></p>

abhivādana|abhivaadana|abhivadana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter \~ā, feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivaadana</span></p><p>respectful greeting; salutation.</p>

abhivādana|abhivaadana|abhivadana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivaadana</span></p><p>respectful greeting, salutation, giving welcome, showing respect or devotion. AN.ii.180 AN.iv.130 AN.iv.276 Ja.i.81 Ja.i.82 Ja.i.218 Dhp.109 (˚sīlin of devout character, cp. Dhp-a.ii.239) Vv-a.24 Sdhp.549 (˚sīla)</p><p>fr. abhivādeti</p>

abhivādanasīlī|abhivaadanasiilii|abhivadanasili
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivaadanasiilii</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhivādanasīlīn">abhivādanasīlīn</a></p><p>habitually respectful</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivādana">abhivādana</a></p>

abhivādanasīlīn|abhivaadanasiiliin|abhivadanasilin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivaadanasiiliin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://abhivādanasīlīn">abhivādanasīlīn</a></p><p>habitually respectful</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivādana">abhivādana</a></p>

abhivādayati|abhivaadayati|abhivadayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivaadayati</span></p><p>addresses reverently; greets; salutes respectfully</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivādeti">abhivādeti</a>, <a href="bword://abhivadati">abhivadati</a></p>

abhivādayitvā|abhivaadayitvaa|abhivadayitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">1 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivaadayitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivādayati">abhivādayati</a></p>

abhivādenta|abhivaadenta|abhivadenta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivaadenta</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivādeti">abhivādeti</a></p>

abhivādesi|abhivaadesi|abhivadesi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivaadesi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivādeti">abhivādeti</a></p>

abhivādesiṃ|abhivaadesi.m|abhivadesim
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">1 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivaadesi.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivādeti">abhivādeti</a></p>

abhivādesuṃ|abhivaadesu.m|abhivadesum
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 plural</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivaadesu.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivādeti">abhivādeti</a></p>

abhivādetabba|abhivaadetabba|abhivadetabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn. &amp; n. impers.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivaadetabba</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivādeti">abhivādeti</a></p>

abhivādeti|abhivaadeti|abhivadeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivaadeti</span></p><p>addresses reverently; greets; salutes respectfully</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhivādayati">abhivādayati</a>, <a href="bword://abhivadati">abhivadati</a></p>

abhivādeti|abhivaadeti|abhivadeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">abhivaadeti</span></p><p>to salute, greet, welcome, honour Vin.ii.208 sq.; DN.i.61; AN.iii.223; AN.iv.173; Vv.1#5 (abhivādayiṃ aor. = abhivādanaṃ kāresiṃ vandiṃ Vv-a.24) Mil.162. Often in combination with <em>padakkhiṇaṃ karoti</em> in sense of to bid goodbye, to say adieu, farewell, e.g. DN.i.89, DN.i.125, DN.i.225; Snp.1010<br />caus 2 <em>abhivādāpeti</em> to cause some one to salute, to make welcome Vin.ii.208 (˚etabba).</p><p>Caus. of abhivadati</p>

abhivādetvā|abhivaadetvaa|abhivadetva
