accussanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>too thick; in lumps.</p>

accussanna
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective too full, too thick Vin.ii.151.</p><p>ati + ussanna</p>

accuta
<p>[DPPN]</p><p></p><p>A Pacceka Buddha, mentioned in a list of Pacceka Buddhas. MN.iii.70</p>

accuta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective immoveable; everlasting, eternal; nt. ˚ṃ. Epithet of Nibbāna (see also <em><a href="bword://cuta">cuta</a></em>) AN.iv.295, AN.iv.327; Snp.204, Snp.1086 (= nicca etc. Cnd.12); Dhp.225 (= sassata Dhp-a.iii.321); Sdhp.47.</p><p>a + cuta</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://cuta">cuta</a></p>

accutadevā|accutadevaa|accutadeva
<p>[DPPN]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">accutadevaa</span></p><p>A class of devas mentioned among those assembled on the occasion of the preaching of the Mahāsamaya Sutta. DN.ii.260</p>

accutagāmabyāmaka|accutagaamabyaamaka|accutagamabyamaka
