accādhāya|accaadhaaya|accadhaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">accaadhaaya</span></p><p>putting on top of; on top of.</p>

accāhita|accaahita|accahita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">accaahita</span></p><p>adjective very cruel, very unfriendly, terrible Ja.iv.46 = Ja.v.146 (= ati ahita C.) = Ja.vi.306 (id.).</p><p>ati + ahita</p>

accāraddha|accaaraddha|accaraddha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">accaaraddha</span></p><p>undertaken or practiced excessively.</p>

accāraddha|accaaraddha|accaraddha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">accaaraddha</span></p><p>adjective &amp; adverb exerting oneself very or too much, with great exertion Vin.i.182; Thag.638; Snp-a.21.</p><p>ati + āraddha</p>

accāraddhaviriya|accaaraddhaviriya|accaraddhaviriya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter &amp; mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">accaaraddhaviriya</span></p><ol><li>(n.) to great exertion.</li><li>(mfn.) exerting oneself too much</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://accāraddha">accāraddha</a></p>

