adhicca
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. &amp; ind.</i></p><ol><li>(mfn.) fortuitous, occurring by mere chance; rare.</li><li>(ind.) fortuitously, without cause or reason; rarely; only.</li></ol>

adhicca
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Adhicca<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>learning, studying, learning by heart Ja.iii.218, Ja.iii.327 = Ja.iv.301; Ja.iv.184 (vede = adhīyitvā C.), Ja.iv.477 (sajjhāyitvā C.); Ja.vi.213; Mil.164.</p><p>ger. of adhi + eti, see <em><a href="bword://adh%C4%AByati">adhīyati</a></em></p><p>Adhicca<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>(˚-) unsupported, uncaused fortuitous, without cause or reason; in foll. phrases <em>-āpattika</em> guilty without intention MN.i.443; <em>-uppatti</em> spontaneous origin Dhs-a.238; <em>-laddha</em> obtained without being asked for, unexpectedly Vv.84#22 = Ja.v.171 Ja.vi.315 (expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> at Ja.v.171 by ahetunā, at Ja.vi.316 by akāraṇena <em>-samuppanna</em> arisen without a cause, spontaneous unconditioned DN.i.28 = Ud.69; DN.iii.33, DN.iii.138; SN.ii.22–⁠ SN.ii.23 (sukhadukkhaṃ); AN.iii.440 (id.); Pts.i.155; DN-a.i.118 (= akāraṇa˚).</p><p>Sk. *adhṛtya, a + *dhicca, ger. of <em>dhṛ</em>; cp. dhāra, dhāraṇa 3, dhāreti 4</p><p>Adhicca<!-- raw HTML omitted -->3<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>adjective without a cause (for assumption) unreasonable, unlikely SN.v.457.</p><p>= adhicca 2 in adj. function, influenced by, homonym abhabba</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhīyati">adhīyati</a></p>

adhiccasamuppanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>arisen fortuitously, without cause or reason; connected with fortuitous or causeless origination</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhicca">adhicca</a></p>

adhiccasamuppannika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>one who believes in fortuitous or causeless origination</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhicca">adhicca</a></p>

adhiccāpattika|adhiccaapattika|adhiccapattika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhiccaapattika</span></p><p>rarely, or occasionally offending</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhicca">adhicca</a></p>

adhiceta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://adhicetas">adhicetas</a></p><p>attentive.</p>

adhicetas
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://adhicetas">adhicetas</a></p><p>attentive.</p>

adhiceto
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective lofty-minded, entranced Thag.68 = Ud.43 = Vin.iv.54 = Dhp-a.iii.384.</p><p>adhi + ceto</p>

adhicitta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>“higher thought”, meditation, contemplation, nsually in comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with <em><a href="bword://adhis%C4%ABla">adhisīla</a></em> and <em><a href="bword://adhipa%C3%B1%C3%B1%C4%81">adhipaññā</a></em> Vin.i.70; DN.iii.219; MN.i.451; AN.i.254, AN.i.256 Mnd.39 = Cnd.689 (˚sikkhā); Dhp.185 (= aṭṭha-samāpattisankhāta adhika-citta Dhp-a.iii.238).</p><p>adhi + citta</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhisīla">adhisīla</a>, <a href="bword://adhipaññā">adhipaññā</a></p>

adhicitta-sikkhā|adhicitta-sikkhaa|adhicitta-sikkha
<p>[Nyana]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhicitta-sikkhaa</span></p><p><strong>Adhicitta-sikkhā</strong> ‘training in higher mentality’; see: <em>sikkhā</em></p>

adhicittasikkhā|adhicittasikkhaa|adhicittasikkha
