<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>exceeding, surpassing; superior, predominant; more; too much, in excess.</p>

adhika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective exceeding, extraordinary, superior, Pp.35; Vv-a.80 (= anadhivara, visiṭṭha); DN-a.i.141, DN-a.i.222; Dpvs.v.32 (an˚); Dhp-a.iii.238 Kp-a.193 (= anuttara); Sdhp.337, Sdhp.447<br />■ compar <strong>adhikatara</strong> Dhp-a.ii.7; Dhp-a.iii.176; nt. <em>-ṃ</em> as adv. extraordinarily Pv-a.86 (= adhimattaṃ). In comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with <em>numerals</em> adhika has the meaning of “in addition, with an additional, plus” (cp. ādi + ādika, with which it is evidently confounded, adhika being constructed in the same way as ādika, i.e. preceding the noun-determination), e.g. catunahutâdhikāni dve yojana-sahassāni 2000 + 94 (= 294 000; Ja.i.25; sattamāsâdhikāni sattavassāni 7 years and 7 months Ja.v.319; paññāsâdhikāni pañca vassa-satani 500 + 50 (550) Pv-a.152. See also sâdhika.</p><p>fr. adhi; cp. Sk. adhika</p><p>See also: adhikatara</p>

adhikakkā|adhikakkaa|adhikakka
<p>[DPPN]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhikakkaa</span></p><p>A ford, evidently a well-known bathing-ghat, where pilgrims used to bathe in order to obtain purification from their sins. It is mentioned in a list of rivers and ghats. MN.i.39</p><p>4ford</p>

adhikaraṇa|adhikara.na|adhikarana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhikara.na</span></p><ol><li>subject of discussion or attention; case, legal question; dispute (in the <em>saṅgha</em>, to be formally dealt with).</li><li>cause.</li></ol>

adhikaraṇa|adhikara.na|adhikarana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhikara.na</span></p><ol><li>attendance, supervision, management of affairs, administration Pv-a.209.</li><li>relation, reference, reason, cause, consequence DN.ii.59 (-˚: in consequence of); SN.ii.41; SN.v.19. Esp. acc. <em>-ṃ</em> as adv. (-˚) in consequence of, for the sake of, because of from MN.i.410 (rūpâdhikaraṇaṃ); SN.iv.339 (rāga˚); Mil.281 (mudda˚ for the sake of the royal seal, orig. in attendance on the r. s.). Kimâdhikaraṇaṃ why, on account of what Ja.iv.4 (= kiṃkāraṇaṃ) yatvâdhikaraṇaṃ (yato adhi˚) by reason of what, since, because (used as conj. DN.i.70 = AN.i.113 = AN.ii.16 = DN.iii.225.</li><li>case, question, cause, subject of discussion, dispute. There are 4 sorts of a. enumerated at var. passages, viz. <em>vivāda˚ anuvāda˚ āpatta kicca˚</em>; “questions of dispute, of censure, of misconduct of duties” Vin.ii.88; Vin.iii.164; Vin.iv.126, Vin.iv.238; MN.ii.247. Often ref.: Vin.ii.74; SN.iv.63 = SN.v.346 (dhamma˚ a question of the Dh.); AN.i.53 (case), AN.i.79; AN.ii.239 (vūpasanta) AN.v.71, AN.v.72; Pp.20, Pp.55; Dhp-a.iv.2 (˚ssa uppamassa vūpasama), adhikaraṇaṃ karoti to raise a dispute MN.i.122 ˚ṃ vūpasameti to settle a question or difficulty Vin.ii.261.</li></ol><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://k%C4%81raka">kāraka</a></em> one who causes dispute discussions or dissent Vin.iv.230 (f. ˚ikā); AN.iii.252.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://samatha">samatha</a></em> the settlings of questions that have arisen. There are seven rules for settling cases enumerated at DN.iii.254; MN.ii.247; AN.i.99; AN.iv.144.</li></ul><p>adhi + karaṇa</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://kāraka">kāraka</a>, <a href="bword://samatha">samatha</a></p>

adhikaraṇakārika|adhikara.nakaarika|adhikaranakarika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhikara.nakaarika</span></p><p>one who causes disputes or lawsuits</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhikaraṇa">adhikaraṇa</a></p>

adhikaraṇasamatha|adhikara.nasamatha|adhikaranasamatha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhikara.nasamatha</span></p><p>(a method) of settling a case or dispute</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhikaraṇa">adhikaraṇa</a></p>

adhikaraṇika|adhikara.nika|adhikaranika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhikara.nika</span></p><p>disputatious.</p>

adhikaraṇika|adhikara.nika|adhikaranika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhikara.nika</span></p><p>one who has to do with the settling of disputes or questions, a judge AN.v.164, AN.v.167.</p><p>fr. adhikaraṇa</p>

adhikaraṇī|adhikara.nii|adhikarani
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhikara.nii</span></p><p>smith’s anvil Ja.iii.285; Dāvs iii.16 sq.; Dhs-a.263.</p><p>to adhikaraṇa 1, orig. meaning “serving, that which serves, i.e. instrument”</p>

adhikasatasahassa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>more than 100, 000</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhika">adhika</a></p>

adhikata
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective</p><ol><li>commissioned with, an overseer, Pv.ii.9#27 (dāne adhikata ṭhapita Pv-a.124).</li><li>caused by Mil.67 (kamma˚).</li><li>affected by something, i.e. confused, puzzled, in doubt Mil.144 (+ vimātijāta).</li></ol><p>adhi + kata; cp. Sk. adhikṛta</p>

adhikodhita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective very angry Ja.v.117.</p><p>adhi + kodhita</p>

adhikusala
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>of high merit.</p>

adhikusala
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective in ˚ā dhammā “items of higher righteousness” DN.iii.145.</p><p>adhi + kusala</p>

adhikuṭṭana|adhiku.t.tana|adhikuttana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhiku.t.tana</span></p><p>chopping block.</p>

adhikuṭṭanā|adhiku.t.tanaa|adhikuttana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhiku.t.tanaa</span></p><p>an executioner’s block Thig.58; cp. Thag-a.65 (variant reading kuḍḍanā, should prob. be read koṭṭana); Thag-a.287.</p><p>adhi + koṭṭanā or koṭṭana</p>

adhikāra|adhikaara|adhikara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhikaara</span></p><p>service, help; act of merit.</p>

adhikāra|adhikaara|adhikara
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhikaara</span></p><p>attendance, service, administration, supervision, management, help Vin.i.55; Ja.i.56 Ja.vi.251; Mil.60, Mil.115, Mil.165; Pv-a.124 (dāna˚; cp. Pv.ii.9#27); Dhp-a.ii.41.</p><p>cp. Sk. adhikāra</p>

adhikārika|adhikaarika|adhikarika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhikaarika</span></p><p>adjective (-˚) serving as, referring to Vin.iii.274 (Bdhgh).</p><p>to adhikāra</p>

adhimana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>‘having the mind directed towards’, intent on, desiring; pleased; not anxious.</p>

adhimana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">n</i></p><p>-adj. n. attention, direction of mind, concentration Snp.692 (adhimanasā bhavātha). (adj.) directing one’s mind upon, intent (on) Ja.iv.433 (= pasannacitta); Ja.v.29 (an˚; variant reading ˚māna).</p><p>adhi + mano</p>

adhimanassa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>‘having the mind directed towards’, intent on, desiring; pleased; not anxious.</p>

adhimatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>above measure, excessive; very great; greater.</p>

adhimatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective extreme, exceeding, extraordinary; nt. adv. ˚ṃ extremely MN.i.152, MN.i.243; SN.iv.160; AN.ii.150; AN.iv.241; Ja.i.92; Pp.15; Mil.146, Mil.189 Mil.274, Mil.290; Pv.ii.3#6 (= adhikataraṃ Pv-a.86); Dhp-a.ii.85 cp. Pv-a.281.</p><p>adhi + matta of <em><a href="bword://m%C4%81">mā</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://mā">mā</a></p>

adhimattakasimāna|adhimattakasimaana|adhimattakasimana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhimattakasimaana</span></p><p>excessive leanness; serious emaciation</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhimatta">adhimatta</a></p>

adhimattata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>preponderance AN.ii.150; Dhs-a.334 (cp. <em>Dhs. trsl.</em> 200).</p><p>abstr. fr. prec.</p>

adhimoceti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>makes incline to; sets on; makes enter (another’s body)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhimuccati">adhimuccati</a></p>

adhimocita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhimoceti">adhimoceti</a></p>

adhimokkha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>faith, conviction; firm resolve, decision.</p>

adhimokkha
<p>[Nyana]</p><p></p><p><strong>Adhimokkha:</strong> ‘determination’, decision, resolve: is one of the mental properties <em>cetasika</em> and belongs to the group of mental constructions <em>sankhāra</em> - <em>khandha.</em> In M. 111, it is mentioned together with other mental properties. See Tab. II, III.</p>

adhimokkha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>firm resolve, determination, decision MN.iii.25 sq.; Vb.165 sq., Vb.425; Dhs-a.145, Dhs-a.264 See <em>Dhs. trsl.</em> 5; <em>Cpd.</em> 17, 40, 95.</p><p>fr. adhi + <em>muc</em></p>

adhimuccamāna|adhimuccamaana|adhimuccamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhimuccamaana</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhimuccati">adhimuccati</a></p>

adhimuccana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>making up one’s mind, confidence Dhs-a.133, Dhs-a.190.</p><p>fr. adhi + <em>muc</em></p>

adhimuccati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><ol><li>inclines to; believes, is sure of; is convinced.</li><li>concentrates on; pervades (in thought or meditation); wills (magically), changes (by magic).</li><li>enters the body.</li></ol>

adhimuccati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>to be drawn to, feel attached to or inclined towards, to indulge in (c. loc. SN.iii.225; SN.iv.185; AN.iv.24, AN.iv.145 sq., AN.iv.460; AN.v.17; Pp.63.</li><li>to become settled, to make up one’s mind as to (with loc.), to become clear about Vin.i.209 (aor. ˚mucci); DN.i.106; SN.i.116 (pot. ˚mucceyya); Iti.43; DN-a.i.275.</li><li>to take courage, to have faith Snp.559; Mil.234; DN-a.i.214, DN-a.i.316; Ja.iv.272; Ja.v.103; Dhp-a.i.196; Dhp-a.iii.258; Dhp-a.iv.170.</li><li>of a spirit, to possess, to enter into a body, with loc of the body. A late idiom for the older anvāvisati. Ja.iv.172; Ja.v.103, Ja.v.429; Dhp-a.i.196; Dhp-a.iii.258; Dhp-a.iv.170. pp. <em>adhimuccita</em> and <em><a href="bword://adhimutta">adhimutta</a></em></li></ol><p>caus <em>adhimoceti</em> to incline to (trs.); to direct upon (with loc.) SN.v.409 (cittaṃ devesu a.).</p><p>Pass. of adhi + <em>muc</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhimutta">adhimutta</a></p>

adhimucchita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>infatuated; clinging to (loc.).</p>

adhimucchita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Adhimuccita &amp; Adhimucchita</p><p>past participle drawn towards, attached to, infatuated, indulging in (with loc.) MN.ii.223 (an˚); SN.i.113; Thag.732 (variant reading ˚muccita), Thag.923 (cch), Thag.1175; Ja.ii.437 (cch); Ja.iii.242; Ja.v.255 (kāmesu ˚mucchita, variant reading ˚muccita). Cp. ajjhomucchita.</p><p>either adhi + <em>muc</em> or <em>mūrch</em>; it would seem more probable to connect it with the former (cp. adhimuccati) and consider all vv. ll ˚mucchita as spurious; but in view of the credit of several passages we have to assume a regular analogy-form ˚mucchita, cp. mucchati and see also J.P.T.S. 1886, 109</p>

adhimucci
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhimuccati">adhimuccati</a></p>

adhimuccita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://adhimuccitar">adhimuccitar</a></p><p>one who believes; who is convinced.</p>

adhimuccita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Adhimuccita &amp; Adhimucchita</p><p>past participle drawn towards, attached to, infatuated, indulging in (with loc.) MN.ii.223 (an˚); SN.i.113; Thag.732 (variant reading ˚muccita), Thag.923 (cch), Thag.1175; Ja.ii.437 (cch); Ja.iii.242; Ja.v.255 (kāmesu ˚mucchita, variant reading ˚muccita). Cp. ajjhomucchita.</p><p>either adhi + <em>muc</em> or <em>mūrch</em>; it would seem more probable to connect it with the former (cp. adhimuccati) and consider all vv. ll ˚mucchita as spurious; but in view of the credit of several passages we have to assume a regular analogy-form ˚mucchita, cp. mucchati and see also J.P.T.S. 1886, 109</p>

adhimuccitar
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://adhimuccitar">adhimuccitar</a></p><p>one who believes; who is convinced.</p>

adhimuccitar
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>one who determines for something, easily trusting, giving credence. AN.iii.165 (variant reading ˚mucchitā)</p><p>n. ag. of adhimuccati</p>

adhimuccitvā|adhimuccitvaa|adhimuccitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhimuccitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhimuccati">adhimuccati</a></p>

adhimutta
<p>[DPPN]</p><p></p><p>A Brahmin of Sāvatthī. A verse addressed by him to some corpulent monks is found in the Theragāthā. Thag.114</p>

adhimutta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>who is inclined to; applying oneself (to, acc. or loc); believing in; set on</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhimuccati">adhimuccati</a></p>

adhimutta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective intent upon (-˚ or with loc. or acc.), applying oneself to, keen on, inclined to, given to Vin.i.183; AN.v.34, AN.v.38; Dhp.226; Snp.1071 Snp.1149 (˚citta); Cnd.33; Ja.i.370 (dān˚) Pp.26; Pv-a.134 (dān˚).</p><p>pp. of adhimuccati, cp. BSk. adhimukta. Avs.i.8, Avs.i.112; Divy.49, Divy.302 etc.</p>

adhimuttacitta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>whose mind is so inclined, or has such a conviction</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhimutta">adhimutta</a></p>

adhimutti
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>resolve, intention, disposition DN.i.174; AN.v.36; Pts.i.124; Mil.161, Mil.169; Vb.340 Vb.341; DN-a.i.44, DN-a.i.103; Sdhp.378.</p><p>adhi + mutti</p>

adhimuttika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective inclined to, attached to, bent on SN.ii.154, SN.ii.158; Iti.70; Vb.339 sq. + <em>tā</em> (f. inclination DN.i.2.</p><p>= adhimutta</p>

adhimāna|adhimaana|adhimana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhimaana</span></p><p>an undue estimate of oneself, undue confidence in oneself. illusion; conceit.</p>

adhimāna|adhimaana|adhimana
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhimaana</span></p><p>undue estimate of oneself MN.ii.252; AN.v.162 sq.</p><p>adhi + māna</p>

adhimānika|adhimaanika|adhimanika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhimaanika</span></p><p>having undue confidence in oneself an undue estimate of oneself; conceited.</p>

adhimānika|adhimaanika|adhimanika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhimaanika</span></p><p>adjective having undue confidence in oneself, conceited AN.v.162, AN.v.169, AN.v.317; Dhp-a.iii.111.</p><p>fr. adhimāna</p>

adhipa
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>ruler, lord, master Ja.ii.369; Ja.iii.324; Ja.v.393; Pv.ii.8#6 (jan˚ king); Dāvs iii.52; Vv-a.314.</p><p>Sk. adhipa, abbrev. of adhipati</p>

adhipajjati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>falls into; attains.</p>

adhipajjati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to come to, reach, attain AN.iv.96 (anatthaṃ); pp. <em><a href="bword://adhipanna">adhipanna</a></em>.</p><p>adhi + pajjati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhipanna">adhipanna</a></p>

adhipaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective (-˚) mastering, ruling or governed, influenced by (cp. adhipati) AN.i.150 (atta loka˚ dhamma˚).</p><p>fr. prec.</p>

adhipanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><ol><li>fallen into; having done wrong.</li><li>fallen into the power of; assailed by</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhipajjati">adhipajjati</a></p>

adhipanna
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>gone into, affected with, seized by (-˚), a victim of (c. loc.) SN.i.72 Thig.345 (kāmesu); Snp.1123 (taṇhā˚ = taṇhânugata Cnd.32); Dhp.288; Ja.iii.38, Ja.iii.369; Ja.iv.396; Ja.v.91, Ja.v.379 (= dosena ajjhotthaṭa); Ja.vi.27.</p><p>cp. Sk. abhipanna, adhi + <em>pad</em></p>

adhipatana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>attack, pressing Thag-a.271.</p><p>fr. adhipatati</p>

adhipatati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>falls on; rushes; against; attacks.</p>

adhipatati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to fly past, vanish Ja.iv.111 (= ativiya patati sīghaṃ atikkamati C.)<br />caus <em><a href="bword://adhip%C4%81teti">adhipāteti</a></em> (q.v.) in diff. meaning. Cp. also adhipāta.</p><p>adhi + patati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhipāteti">adhipāteti</a></p>

adhipateyya
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>AN.i.147; AN.iii.33 = SN.iv.275 is probably misreading for ādhipateyya.</p>

adhipati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>lord; master; ruler; owner; controller; dominant influence.</p>

adhipati-paccaya
<p>[Nyana]</p><p></p><p><strong>Adhipati-paccaya:</strong> ’ Predominance-condition ’ is one of the 24 conditions <em>paccaya</em>, if developed, it is considered as the fourfold road to force <em>iddhi-pāda</em>.</p>

adhipati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>noun adjective</p><ol><li>ruler, master Ja.iv.223; Vv.81#1; Mil.388; Dhp-a.i.36 (= seṭṭha).</li><li>ruling over, governing, predominant; ruled or governed by Vb.216 sq. (chandaṃ adhipatiṃ katvā making energy predominant); Dhs-a.125, Dhs-a.126 (atta˚ autonomous, loka heteronomous, influenced by society). See alṣo <em>Dhs. trsl.</em> 20 &amp; <em>Cpd.</em> 60.</li></ol><p>adhi + pati, cp. adhipa</p>

adhipatikā|adhipatikaa|adhipatika
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipatikaa</span></p><p>moth, a mosquito Mnd.484 (see *<a href="bword://adhip%C4%81ta">adhipāta</a>*<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->).</p><p>fr. adhipāta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhipāta">adhipāta</a></p>

adhipatitvā|adhipatitvaa|adhipatitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipatitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhipatati">adhipatati</a></p>

adhipatthita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>desire, wished; longed for.</p>

adhipatthita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>desired, wished, begged for DN.i.120.</p><p>pp. adhi + pattheti, cp. Sk. abhi + arthayati</p>

adhipaññā-dhamma-vipassanā|adhipa~n~naa-dhamma-vipassanaa|adhipanna-dhamma-vipassana
<p>[Nyana]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipa~n~naa-dhamma-vipassanaa</span></p><p><strong>Adhipaññā-dhamma-vipassanā:</strong> ‘insight into things based on higher understanding’, is one of the 18 chief kinds of insight see: <em>vipassanā</em>.</p>

adhipaññā|adhipa~n~naa|adhipanna
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipa~n~naa</span></p><p>higher wisdom or knowledge, insight (cp. jhāna &amp; paññā); usually in comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with adhicitta &amp; adhisīla Vin.i.70; DN.i.174; DN.iii.219 (˚sikkhā); AN.i.240; AN.ii.92 sq., AN.ii.239; AN.iii.106 sq., AN.iii.327, AN.iv.360; Mnd.39 (id.); Pts.i.20, Pts.i.25 sq., Pts.i.45 sq., Pts.i.169; Pts.ii.11, Pts.ii.244; Pp.61.</p><p>adhi + paññā</p>

adhipaññāsikkhā|adhipa~n~naasikkhaa|adhipannasikkha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipa~n~naasikkhaa</span></p><p>training in (higher) wisdom.</p>

adhipaññātti|adhipa~n~naatti|adhipannatti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipa~n~naatti</span></p><p>with regard to exposition.</p>

adhipaññāya|adhipa~n~naaya|adhipannaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipa~n~naaya</span></p><p>in regard to wisdom.</p>

adhipaññāṃ|adhipa~n~naa.m|adhipannam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipa~n~naa.m</span></p><p>as regards wisdom.</p>

adhippagharati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to flow, to trickle Thag-a.284.</p><p>adhi + ppa + gharati</p>

adhippayāsa|adhippayaasa|adhippayasa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhippayaasa</span></p><p>particular effort.</p>

adhippeta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>meant; intended; desired, aimed at; referred to.</p>

adhippeta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>desired, approved of, agreeable DN.i.120; DN.ii.236; Vv-a.312, Vv-a.315.</li><li>meant, understood intended as Ja.iii.263; Pv-a.9, Pv-a.80, Pv-a.120, Pv-a.164.</li></ol><p>Sk. abhipreta, adhi + ppa + <em><a href="bword://i">i</a></em>, lit. gone into, gone for; cp. adhippāya</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://i">i</a></p>

adhippetatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>the fact of being meant or understood as, in abl. ˚ā with reference to, as is to be understood of Vv-a.13; Pv-a.52.</p><p>abstr. fr. adhippeta</p>

adhippāgā|adhippaagaa|adhippaga
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 sg. aor.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhippaagaa</span></p><p>of adhippagacchati to go to Ja.v.59.</p>

adhippāya|adhippaaya|adhippaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhippaaya</span></p><ol><li>meaning, intention; wish, desire.</li><li>particular meaning, distinction, difference.</li></ol>

adhippāya|adhippaaya|adhippaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhippaaya</span></p><ol><li>intention, wish desire SN.i.124; SN.v.108; AN.ii.81; AN.iii.363 (bhoga˚), AN.v.65; Ja.i.79, Ja.i.83; Sdhp.62. As adj. (-˚) desiring Pv-a.226 (hass˚ in play = khiḍḍatthika).</li><li>sense, meaning conclusion, inference (cp. adhigama) Mil.148; Pv-a.8 Pv-a.16, Pv-a.48, Pv-a.131 (the moral of a story). <em>-adhippāyena</em> (instr. in the way of, like Pv-a.215 (kīḷ for fun).</li></ol><p>adhi + ppa + <em><a href="bword://i">i</a></em>; Sk. abhiprāya</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://i">i</a></p>

adhippāyosa|adhippaayosa|adhippayosa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhippaayosa</span></p><p>distinction, difference, peculiarity, special meaning MN.i.46; SN.iii.66; SN.iv.208; AN.i.267; AN.iv.158; AN.v.48 sq.</p><p>adhi + pāyosa</p>

adhipāta|adhipaata|adhipata
<p>[Dhammika]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipaata</span></p><p>See <em>Kīṭa</em>.</p><p>See also: Kīṭa</p>

adhipāta|adhipaata|adhipata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipaata</span></p><p>adhipāta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>masculine making fall; injuring; (or splitting).</p><p>adhipāta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>masculine flying insect; moth.</p>

adhipāta|adhipaata|adhipata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipaata</span></p><p>Adhipāta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>splitting, breaking, only in phrase <em>muddhā˚</em>; head-splitting Snp.988 sq., Snp.1004, Snp.1025 (variant reading Nd ii.˚vipāta).</p><p>adhipāteti</p><p>Adhipāta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>a moth Snp.964. Expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> at Mnd.484 as “adhipātikā ti tā uppatitvā khādanti taṃkāraṇā a. vuccanti”; Ud.72 (expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> by C. as salabhā).</p><p>from adhipatati = Sk. atipatati, to fly past, flit</p>

adhipātaka|adhipaataka|adhipataka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipaataka</span></p><p>flying insect; moth.</p>

adhipāteti|adhipaateti|adhipateti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipaateti</span></p><p>to break, split Ja.iv.337 (= chindati). At Ud.8 prob. to be read <em><a href="bword://adhib%C4%81dheti">adhibādheti</a></em> (variant reading avibādeti. T. adhipāteti).</p><p>Caus. fr. adhipatati, cp. Sk. abhipātayati &amp; P. atipāteti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhibādheti">adhibādheti</a></p>

adhipātetvā|adhipaatetvaa|adhipatetva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipaatetvaa</span></p><p>having made fall; having laid low.</p>

adhipāti|adhipaati|adhipati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipaati</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://adhipātin">adhipātin</a></p><p>making fall; injuring; (or splitting)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhipāta">adhipāta</a></p>

adhipātikā|adhipaatikaa|adhipatika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipaatikaa</span></p><p>flying insect; moth.</p>

adhipātimokkha|adhipaatimokkha|adhipatimokkha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipaatimokkha</span></p><p>the extension to the rule of discipline; the further code of discipline.</p>

adhipātimokkhe|adhipaatimokkhe|adhipatimokkhe
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipaatimokkhe</span></p><p>concerning the code of discipline.</p>

adhipātin|adhipaatin|adhipatin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipaatin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://adhipātin">adhipātin</a></p><p>making fall; injuring; (or splitting)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhipāta">adhipāta</a></p>

adhipāṭimokkha|adhipaa.timokkha|adhipatimokkha
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhipaa.timokkha</span></p><p>the higher, moral, code Vin.v.1 (pāṭim˚ +); MN.ii.245 (+ ajjhājīva).</p><p>adhi + pāṭimokkha</p>

adhiroha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>ascent, ascending; in <em>dur˚</em>; hard to ascend Mil.322.</p><p>fr. adhi + <em>ruh</em></p>

adhisallikhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>is over scrupulous.</p>

adhisayana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>adjective lying on or in, inhabiting Pv-a.80 (mañcaṃ).</p><p>fr. adhiseti</p>

adhisayita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>sat on, addled (of eggs) Vin.iii.3; SN.iii.153.</p><p>pp. of adhiseti</p>

adhiseti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>adhiseti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted -->adhisayati</p><p>pr. 3 sg. lies down on.</p><p>adhiseti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->adhisseti</p><p>pr. 3 sg. has recourse to, resorts to.</p>

adhiseti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to lie on, sit on, live in, to follow, pursue Dhp.41; Snp.671 (= gacchati C.)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://adhisayita">adhisayita</a></em>.</p><p>adhi + <em><a href="bword://seti">seti</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhisayita">adhisayita</a>, <a href="bword://seti">seti</a></p>

adhisīla|adhisiila|adhisila
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhisiila</span></p><p>higher morality, usually in threefold set of <em>adhicitta-sikkha, adhipaññā˚ adhisīla˚</em> Vin.i.70; DN.i.174; DN.iii.219; AN.iii.133; AN.iv.25; Dhp-a.i.334; Pv-a.207. See also adhicitta, sikkhā &amp; sīla.</p><p>adhi + sīla</p>

adhisīla-sikkhā|adhisiila-sikkhaa|adhisila-sikkha
<p>[Nyana]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhisiila-sikkhaa</span></p><p><strong>Adhisīla-sikkhā:</strong> ‘training in higher morality’: see: <em>sikkhā</em></p>

adhisīlasikkhā|adhisiilasikkhaa|adhisilasikkha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhisiilasikkhaa</span></p><p>training in (higher) moral behavior.</p>

adhisīlaṃ|adhisiila.m|adhisilam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhisiila.m</span></p><p>as regards to moral behavior.</p>

adhisīle|adhisiile|adhisile
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhisiile</span></p><p>in regard to morality.</p>

adhitiṭṭhati|adhiti.t.thati|adhititthati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhiti.t.thati</span></p><p>stands upon, depends upon; mounts; stands over, supervises; controls; designates, takes (formal) possession of (robe, bowl etc); resolves on, fixes the mind on, undertakes; resolves, determines, produces (by supernatural power)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhitiṭṭhati">adhitiṭṭhati</a>, <a href="bword://adhiṭṭhāti">adhiṭṭhāti</a></p>

adhitthāna|adhitthaana|adhitthana
<p>[Nyana]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhitthaana</span></p><p><strong>Adhitthāna,</strong> as a doctrinal term, occurs chiefly in two meanings:</p><blockquote><ol><li>‘Foundation’: four ‘foundations or basics’ of an Arahat’s mentality, mentioned and explained in M. 140: the foundation of understanding <em>paññā,</em> of truthfulness <em>sacca</em> of generosity <em>cāga</em> and of peace <em>upasama.</em> See also D. 33 and Com.</li></ol><p>dic2-abbrev.htm#Com.</p><ol start="2"><li>‘Determination’, resolution, resolve in: <em>adhitthāna</em> - <em>iddhi</em> magical power of determination’ see: <em>iddhi</em>, <em>adhitthāna</em> - <em>pāramī</em> perfection of resolution’ see: <em>pāramī.</em></li></ol></blockquote>

adhivacana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>name, designation; metaphorical expression; near-synonym.</p>

adhivacana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>designation, term, attrîbute, metaphor, metaphorical expression DN.ii.62; MN.i.113 MN.i.144, MN.i.460; AN.ii.70, AN.ii.124; AN.iii.310; AN.iv.89, AN.iv.285, AN.iv.340; Iti.15 Iti.114; Snp.p.218; Ja.i.117; Cnd.34 = Dhs.1306 (= nāma sankhā paññatti etc.); Vb.6; Pv-a.63. See on term <em>Dhs. trsl.</em> 340.</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://patha">patha</a></em> “process of synonymous nomenclature” (Mrs Rh. D.) DN.ii.68; SN.iii.71; Dhs.1306; Dhs-a.51.</li></ul><p>adhi + vacana</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://patha">patha</a></p>

adhivacanapatha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>mode of expression</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhivacana">adhivacana</a></p>

adhivara
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective superb, excellent, surpassing Vv.16#3 (<em>an˚</em>; unsurpassed, unrivalled; Vv-a.80 = adhika visiṭṭha).</p><p>adhi + vara</p>

adhivattati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>comes on; moves over; overwhelms.</p>

adhivattati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to come on, proceed, issue, result SN.i.101; AN.ii.32.</p><p>adhi + vattati</p>

adhivattha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>adhivattha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>pp mfn. (act.) living in, inhabiting (loc).</p><p>adhivattha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>pp mfn. accepted; consented to</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhivāseti">adhivāseti</a></p>

adhivattha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective inhabiting, living in (c. loc.) Vin.i.28; SN.i.197; Ja.i.223; Ja.ii.385; Ja.iii.327; Pv-a.17. The form <em><a href="bword://adhivuttha">adhivuttha</a></em> occurs at Ja.vi.370.</p><p>pp. of adhivasati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhivuttha">adhivuttha</a></p>

adhivimokkhatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>= adhimokkha; being inclined to Dhs-a.261.</p>

adhivimuttatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>= adhivimokkhatta &amp; adhimutti, i.e. propensity, the fact of being inclined or given to Ja.v.254 (T. kāmādhivimuttitā, variant reading ˚muttata).</p>

adhivimutti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine &amp; ind.</i></p><p>higher, superior release; as to release.</p>

adhivivuttipada
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>expression, saying; opinion, theory.</p>

adhivuttha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp. mfn.</i></p><ol><li>(act.) having accepted (an invitation).</li><li>(pass.) accepted, consented to</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhivāseti">adhivāseti</a></p>

adhivuttha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>see <em><a href="bword://adhivattha">adhivattha</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhivattha">adhivattha</a></p>

adhivutti
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>expression, saying, opinion; only in tt. <em>adhivuttipada</em> (variant reading <em>adhimutti-p</em>. at all passages) DN.i.13 (expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> by adhivacana-pada DN-a.i.103); MN.ii.228; AN.v.36.</p><p>adhi + vutti, fr. adhi + <em>vac</em>, cp. Sk. abhivadati</p>

adhivāha|adhivaaha|adhivaha
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaaha</span></p><p>carrier, bearer, adj. bringing SN.iv.70 (dukkha˚); AN.i.6; Thag.494.</p><p>fr. adhi + <em>vah</em>; cp. Sk. abhivahati</p>

adhivāhana|adhivaahana|adhivahana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter &amp;</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaahana</span></p><p>adjective carrying, bringing, bearing Snp.79; f. <em>-ī</em> Thag.519.</p><p>fr. adhi + <em>vah</em></p>

adhivāhi|adhivaahi|adhivahi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaahi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://adhivāhin">adhivāhin</a></p><p>bringing.</p>

adhivāhin|adhivaahin|adhivahin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaahin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://adhivāhin">adhivāhin</a></p><p>bringing.</p>

adhivāsa|adhivaasa|adhivasa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaasa</span></p><p>endurance, forbearance, holding out; only as adj. in <em>dur˚</em>; difficult to hold out Thag.111.</p><p>fr. adhi + <em>vas</em></p>

adhivāsaka|adhivaasaka|adhivasaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaasaka</span></p><p>Adhivāsaka &amp; Adhivāsika</p><p>adjective willing, agreeable, enduring, patient Vin.iv.130; MN.i.10, MN.i.526; AN.ii.118 AN.iii.163; AN.v.132; Ja.iii.369 (an˚); Ja.iv.11, Ja.iv.77.</p><p>fr. adhivāsa</p>

adhivāsakajātika|adhivaasakajaatika|adhivasakajatika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaasakajaatika</span></p><p>enduring or patient by nature.</p>

adhivāsana|adhivaasana|adhivasana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter \~ā, feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaasana</span></p><ol><li>endurance; forbearance.</li><li>assent; acceptance (esp. of an invitation).</li></ol>

adhivāsana|adhivaasana|adhivasana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaasana</span></p><ol><li>assent AN.iii.31; Dhp-a.i.33.</li><li>forbearance, endurance MN.i.10; Ja.ii.237 Ja.iii.263; Ja.iv.307; Ja.v.174.</li></ol><p>fr. adhi + <em>vas</em></p>

adhivāsanatā|adhivaasanataa|adhivasanata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaasanataa</span></p><p>patience, endurance, Dhs.1342; Vb.360 (an˚).</p><p>abstr. fr. adhivāsana</p>

adhivāsaya|adhivaasaya|adhivasaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaasaya</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://adhivāsayat">adhivāsayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhivāseti">adhivāseti</a></p>

adhivāsayat|adhivaasayat|adhivasayat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaasayat</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://adhivāsayat">adhivāsayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhivāseti">adhivāseti</a></p>

adhivāsayati|adhivaasayati|adhivasayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaasayati</span></p><p>is patient, waits; bears patiently, endures; assents, gives in to; accepts (an invitation).</p>

adhivāsaye|adhivaasaye|adhivasaye
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">opt. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhivaasaye</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhivāseti">adhivāseti</a></p>

adhivāsayeyya|adhivaasayeyya|adhivasayeyya
