adhiṭṭhahanta|adhi.t.thahanta|adhitthahanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thahanta</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhiṭṭhahati">adhiṭṭhahati</a></p>

adhiṭṭhahat|adhi.t.thahat|adhitthahat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thahat</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://adhiṭṭhahat">adhiṭṭhahat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhiṭṭhahati">adhiṭṭhahati</a></p>

adhiṭṭhahati|adhi.t.thahati|adhitthahati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thahati</span></p><p>stands upon, depends upon; mounts; stands over, supervises; controls; designates, takes (formal) possession of (robe, bowl etc); resolves on, fixes the mind on, undertakes; resolves, determines, produces (by supernatural power)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhitiṭṭhati">adhitiṭṭhati</a>, <a href="bword://adhiṭṭhāti">adhiṭṭhāti</a></p>

adhiṭṭhahi|adhi.t.thahi|adhitthahi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thahi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhiṭṭheti">adhiṭṭheti</a></p>

adhiṭṭhahitva|adhi.t.thahitva|adhitthahitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thahitva</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhiṭṭheti">adhiṭṭheti</a></p>

adhiṭṭhaka|adhi.t.thaka|adhitthaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thaka</span></p><p>adjective (-˚) bent on, given to, addicted to Ja.v.427 (surā˚).</p><p>fr. adhiṭṭhāti</p>

adhiṭṭheti|adhi.t.theti|adhittheti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.theti</span></p><p>stands upon, depends upon; mounts; stands over, supervises; controls; designates, takes (formal) possession of (robe, bowl etc); resolves on, fixes the mind on, undertakes; resolves, determines, produces (by supernatural power)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhitiṭṭhati">adhitiṭṭhati</a></p>

adhiṭṭhita|adhi.t.thita|adhitthita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thita</span></p><ol><li><p>(mfn.)</p><ol><li>(pass.) supervised; resolved on, undertaken; brought under control; possessed, designated, formally taken possession of; used.</li><li>(act.) standing upon, mounted upon; resolving on; fixing one’s mind on.</li></ol></li><li><p>(n.) supervising</p></li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhitiṭṭhati">adhitiṭṭhati</a></p>

adhiṭṭhita|adhi.t.thita|adhitthita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thita</span></p><p>adjective<br />standing on (c. loc.), esp. with the idea of standing above, towering over Vv.63#30 (hemarathe a. = sakalaṃ ṭhānaṃ abhibhavitvā ṭhita Vv-a.269)</p><ol><li>looked after, managed, undertaken governed Vin.i.57; SN.v.278 (sv’âdhiṭṭhita); Pv-a.141 (kammanta)</li><li>undertaking, bent on (c. acc.) Snp.820 (ekacariyaṃ).</li></ol><p>pp. of adhiṭṭhāti</p>

adhiṭṭhāna|adhi.t.thaana|adhitthana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thaana</span></p><p>support, basis; standpoint; abode; determination, resolution; fixing the mind on; determining, controlling, producing (by supernatural power); taking (formal) possession of, designating.</p>

adhiṭṭhāna|adhi.t.thaana|adhitthana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thaana</span></p><ol><li>decision, resolution, self-determination, will (cp. on this meaning <em>Cpd.</em> 62; DN.iii.229 (where 4 are enumerated, viz. paññā˚, sacca˚ cāga upasama˚); Ja.i.23; Ja.v.174; Pts.i.108; Pts.ii.171 sq., Pts.ii.207; Dhs-a.166 (cp. <em>Dhs. trsl.</em> 44).</li><li>mentioned in bad sense with <em><a href="bword://abhinivesa">abhinivesa</a></em> and <em><a href="bword://anusaya">anusaya</a></em>, obstinacy, prejudice and bias MN.i.136; MN.iii.31, MN.iii.240; SN.ii.17; SN.iii.10, SN.iii.135 SN.iii.194<br />■ As adj. (-˚) applying oneself to, bent on AN.iii.363.</li><li>looking after, management, direction, power Mil.309 (devānaṃ); Pv-a.141 (so read for adhitaṭṭhāna) <a href="bword://%C4%81v%C4%81sa">āvāsa</a>* should perhaps be read <em><a href="bword://adhi%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADh%C4%81na">adhiṭṭhāna</a></em> in the sense of fixed permanent, abode].</li></ol><p>fr. adhi + <em>sthā</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://abhinivesa">abhinivesa</a>, <a href="bword://anusaya">anusaya</a>, <a href="bword://āvāsa">āvāsa</a>, <a href="bword://adhiṭṭhāna">adhiṭṭhāna</a></p>

adhiṭṭhātabba|adhi.t.thaatabba|adhitthatabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thaatabba</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhiṭṭhāti">adhiṭṭhāti</a></p>

adhiṭṭhāti|adhi.t.thaati|adhitthati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thaati</span></p><p>stands upon, depends upon; mounts; stands over, supervises; controls; designates, takes (formal) possession of (robe, bowl etc); resolves on, fixes the mind on, undertakes; resolves, determines, produces (by supernatural power)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhitiṭṭhati">adhitiṭṭhati</a>, <a href="bword://adhiṭṭhāti">adhiṭṭhāti</a></p>

adhiṭṭhāti|adhi.t.thaati|adhitthati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thaati</span></p><p><em>(adhiṭṭhahati)</em></p><ol><li>to stand on Ja.iii.278 (ger. ˚āya); Dhp-a.iv.183 (ger ˚hitvā); fig. to insist on Thag.1131 (aor. ˚āhi).</li><li>to concentrate or fix one’s attention on (c. acc.), to direct one’s thoughts to, to make up one’s mind, to wish Vin.i.115 (inf. ˚ṭhātuṃ), Vin.i.297 (id.), Vin.i.125 (grd. ˚ṭhātabba) Ja.i.80 (aor. ˚ahi); Ja.iii.278; Ja.iv.134 (variant reading ati˚ C. explains abhibhavitvā tiṭṭhati); Dhp-a.i.34; Dhp-a.iv.201 (ger. ˚hitvā) Pv-a.23 (aor. ˚ṭhāsi), Pv-a.171 (id.), Pv-a.75 (ger. ˚hitvā). On adhiṭṭheyya see <em>Cpd.</em> 209, n. 2; 219, n. 1.</li><li>to undertake practice, perform, look after, to celebrate SN.ii.17; AN.i.115 sq.; Ja.i.50; Pv-a.209 (ger. ˚ṭhāya)</li></ol><p>pp <em><a href="bword://adhi%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADhita">adhiṭṭhita</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>Sk. adhitiṣṭhati, adhi + <em>sthā</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhiṭṭhita">adhiṭṭhita</a></p>

adhiṭṭhātuṃ|adhi.t.thaatu.m|adhitthatum
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">inf.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thaatu.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhiṭṭhāti">adhiṭṭhāti</a></p>

adhiṭṭhāya|adhi.t.thaaya|adhitthaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thaaya</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhiṭṭheti">adhiṭṭheti</a></p>

adhiṭṭhāyaka|adhi.t.thaayaka|adhitthayaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhi.t.thaayaka</span></p><p>adjective (-˚) superintending, watching, looking after, in <em>kamma˚</em>; Mhvs.5, Mhvs.175; Mhvs.30, Mhvs.98; <em>kammanta˚</em> Dhp-a.i.393.</p>

adho
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i></p><p>below; down; downwards (one of the ten disā); downstream.</p>

adho
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adverb below, usually comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> or contrasted with <em><a href="bword://uddha%E1%B9%83">uddhaṃ</a></em> “above” and <em><a href="bword://tiriya%E1%B9%83">tiriyaṃ</a></em> “across”, describing the 3 dimensions<br />■ <em><a href="bword://uddha%E1%B9%83">uddhaṃ</a></em> and <em><a href="bword://adho">adho</a></em> above and below marking zenith &amp; nadir. Thus with uddhaṃ and the 4 bearings; <em>(disā)</em> and intermediate points <em>(anudisā)</em> at SN.i.122; SN.iii.124; AN.iv.167; with uddhaṃ &amp; tiriyaṃ at Snp.150, Snp.537, Snp.1055, Snp.1068. Expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> at Kp-a.248 by heṭṭhā and in detail (dogmatically &amp; speculatively) at Cnd.155. For further ref. see <em><a href="bword://uddha%E1%B9%83">uddhaṃ</a></em>. The comp<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> form of adho before vowels is adh˚.</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://akkhaka">akkhaka</a></em> beneath the collar-bone Vin.iv.213.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://agga">agga</a></em> with the points downward (of the upper row of teeth Ja.v.156 (+ uddh˚ expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> by uparima-danta C.).</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://kata">kata</a></em> turned down, or upside down Ja.i.20; Ja.vi.298.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://gata">gata</a></em> gone by, past. Adv. ˚ṃ since (cp. uddhaṃ adv. later or after Ja.vi.187 (ito māsaṃ adhogataṃ since one month ago)</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://gala">gala</a></em> (so read for T. udho˚) down the throat Pv-a.104</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://mukha">mukha</a></em> head forward, face downward, bent over, upturned Vin.ii.78; MN.i.132, MN.i.234: Vv.16#1 (= heṭṭhā mukha Vv-a.78).</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://bh%C4%81ga">bhāga</a></em> the lower part (of the body) MN.i.473; Dhp-a.i.148.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://virecana">virecana</a></em> action of a purgative (opp. uddha˚ of an emetic) DN.i.12; DN-a.i.98 (= adho dosānaṃ nīharaṇaṃ) Dhs-a.404.</li><li><em>-sākhaṃ</em> (+ uddhamūlaṃ) branches down (roots up, i.e. uprooted) Dhp-a.i.75.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://sira">sira</a></em> (adj.) head downward Ja.iv.194.</li><li><em>-siraṃ</em> (adv.) with bowed head (cp. avaṃsiraṃ) Ja.vi.298 (= siraṃ adhokatvā heṭṭhāmukho C.).</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://s%C4%ABsa">sīsa</a></em> (adj.) head first, headlong Ja.i.233; Ja.v.472 (˚ka).</li></ul><p>Vedic adhaḥ; compar. adharaḥ = Lat. inferus, Goth. undar, E. under, Ind. *n̊dher-; superl. adhamaḥ Lat. infimus</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uddhaṃ">uddhaṃ</a>, <a href="bword://tiriyaṃ">tiriyaṃ</a>, <a href="bword://uddhaṃ">uddhaṃ</a>, <a href="bword://adho">adho</a>, <a href="bword://uddhaṃ">uddhaṃ</a>, <a href="bword://akkhaka">akkhaka</a>, <a href="bword://agga">agga</a>, <a href="bword://kata">kata</a>, <a href="bword://gata">gata</a>, <a href="bword://gala">gala</a>, <a href="bword://mukha">mukha</a>, <a href="bword://bhāga">bhāga</a>, <a href="bword://virecana">virecana</a>, <a href="bword://sira">sira</a>, <a href="bword://sīsa">sīsa</a></p>

adhobhāga|adhobhaaga|adhobhaga
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhobhaaga</span></p><p>the lower part; the lower part of the body, the anus</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adho">adho</a></p>

adhobhāvaṅgamanīya|adhobhaava"ngamaniiya|adhobhavangamaniya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhobhaava"ngamaniiya</span></p><p>tending to go downwards (to lower existences)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adho">adho</a></p>

adhojānumaṇḍalami|adhojaanuma.n.dalami|adhojanumandalami
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhojaanuma.n.dalami</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://adhojānumaṇḍalamin">adhojānumaṇḍalamin</a></p><p>what is below the knee-cap</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adho">adho</a></p>

adhojānumaṇḍalamin|adhojaanuma.n.dalamin|adhojanumandalamin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhojaanuma.n.dalamin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://adhojānumaṇḍalamin">adhojānumaṇḍalamin</a></p><p>what is below the knee-cap</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adho">adho</a></p>

adhomukha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mf</i></p><p>(~ī)n. with the face downward; with head bent; facing downward</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adho">adho</a></p>

adhomukhaṃ|adhomukha.m|adhomukham
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">adv.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhomukha.m</span></p><p>downwards</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adhomukha">adhomukha</a></p>

adhonābhiṃ|adhonaabhi.m|adhonabhim
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind. &amp; neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">adhonaabhi.m</span></p><p>below the navel; what is below the navel; see adho)</p>

adhosira
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>with the head downward; headfirst</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adho">adho</a></p>

adhovirecana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>purging; purgative</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://adho">adho</a></p>

