ajjhiṭṭha|ajjhi.t.tha|ajjhittha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ajjhi.t.tha</span></p><p>requested; asked (esp. to preach the dhamma)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ajjhesati">ajjhesati</a></p>

ajjhiṭṭha|ajjhi.t.tha|ajjhittha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ajjhi.t.tha</span></p><p>requested, asked, invited Vin.i.113 (an˚ unbidden); DN.ii.289 (Buddhaghosa and text read ajjhitta); Snp.p.218 (= ajjhesita Cnd.16); Ja.vi.292 (= āṇatta C.); Dhp-a.iv.100 (variant reading abhijjhiṭṭha). See also an˚.</p><p>pp. of ajjhesati</p>

ajjhiṭṭhapañha|ajjhi.t.thapa~nha|ajjhitthapanha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ajjhi.t.thapa~nha</span></p><p>the question asked; the chosen question</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ajjhiṭṭha">ajjhiṭṭha</a></p>

ajjhobhavati
