<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ajjhogaahitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ajjhogāhati">ajjhogāhati</a></p>

ajjhogāḷha|ajjhogaa.lha|ajjhogalha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ajjhogaa.lha</span></p><p>who has plunged into; entered; immersed</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ajjhogāhati">ajjhogāhati</a></p>

ajjhogāḷha|ajjhogaa.lha|ajjhogalha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ajjhogaa.lha</span></p><p>plunged into, immersed; having entered MN.i.457; SN.i.201; Mil.348.</p><p>pp. of ajjhogāhati</p>

ajjhogāḷhappatta|ajjhogaa.lhappatta|ajjhogalhappatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ajjhogaa.lhappatta</span></p><p>immersed in, intimate</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ajjhogāḷha">ajjhogāḷha</a></p>

ajjhoharati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><ol><li>brings down or near; puts in.</li><li>swallows, eats.</li></ol>

ajjhoharati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to swallow, eat, take as food MN.i.245; Ja.i.460; Ja.ii.293 Ja.vi.205, Ja.vi.213; Mil.366; Pv-a.283 (aor.)<br />pp <strong>ajjhohaṭa</strong> (q.v.).</p><p>Sk. abhyavaharati; adhi (= abhi) + ava + <em>hṛ</em>.</p><p>See also: ajjhohaṭa</p>

ajjhoharaṇa|ajjhohara.na|ajjhoharana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ajjhohara.na</span></p><p>(from ajjhoharati) bringing down or near.</p>

ajjhoharaṇa|ajjhohara.na|ajjhoharana
