aneka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not one, i.e. many, various; of various kinds; countless, numberless</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

aneka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective (usually ˚-) not one, i.e. many, various; countlcss, numberless Iti.99 (saṃvaṭṭakappā countless aeons); Snp.688 (˚sākhā); Dhp.153 (˚jātisāra); Ja.iv.2 Ja.vi.366.</p><ul><li><em>-pariyāyena</em> (instr.) in many ways Vin.i.16; Snp.p.15</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://r%C5%ABpa">rūpa</a></em> various, manifold Snp.1049, Snp.1079, Snp.1082; Cnd.54 (= anekavidha).</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://vidha">vidha</a></em> manifold Cnd.54; DN-a.i.103</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://vihita">vihita</a></em> various, manifold DN.i.12, DN.i.13, DN.i.178; Iti.98; Pp.55; DN-a.i.103 (= anekavidha).</li></ul><p>an + eka</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://rūpa">rūpa</a>, <a href="bword://vidha">vidha</a>, <a href="bword://vihita">vihita</a></p>

anekabhāga|anekabhaaga|anekabhaga
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anekabhaaga</span></p><p>multiplied; manifold</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://aneka">aneka</a></p>

