antalikkha
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>the atmosphere or air DN.ii.15; AN.iii.239; AN.iv.199; Snp.222, Snp.688; Dhp.127; Mil.150 = Pv-a.104; Pv.i.3#1 (= vehāyasa-saññita a Pv-a.14); Kp-a.166.</p><ul><li><em>-ga</em> going through the air AN.i.215.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://cara">cara</a></em> walking through the air Vin.i.21; DN.i.17; SN.i.111; Ja.v.267; DN-a.i.110.</li></ul><p>Vedic antarikṣa = antari-kṣa (<em>kṣi</em>), lit. situated in between sky and earth</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://cara">cara</a></p>

antamaso
