antarahita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective</p><ol><li>disappeared, gone, left DN.i.222. MN.i.487. Mil.18. Pv-a.245.</li><li>in phrase <em>anantarahitāya bhūmiyā</em> (loc) on the bare soil (lit. on the ground with nothing put in between it &amp; the person lying down, i.e. on an uncovered or unobstructed ground) Vin.i.47; Vin.ii.209; MN.ii.57.</li></ol><p>pp. of antaradhāyati</p>

antarakappa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>( &amp; n.) a subdivision or intermediate cycle of a mahākappa</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antara">antara</a></p>

antarato
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i></p><p>from within, inwardly</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antara">antara</a></p>

antaravassa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>the rainy season</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antara">antara</a></p>

antaravāsaka|antaravaasaka|antaravasaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaravaasaka</span></p><p>an inner garment, esp. the innermost of the three robes of a <em>bhikkhu</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antara">antara</a></p>

antarayati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to go or step in between, ger. <em>antaritvā</em> (= antarayitvā) Ja.i.218.</p><p>cp. denom. fr. antara</p>

antaraṃ karoti|antara.m karoti|antaram karoti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(?)</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antara.m karoti</span></p><p>concentrates on; keeps in mind</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antara">antara</a></p>

antaraṃsa|antara.msa|antaramsa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antara.msa</span></p><p>“in between the shoulders”, i.e. the chest Ja.v.173 = Ja.vi.171 (phrase <em>lohitakkho vihat’ antaraṃso</em>).</p><p>B.Sk. antarâṃsa; antara + aṃsa</p>

antaraṭṭhaka|antara.t.thaka|antaratthaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antara.t.thaka</span></p><p>occuring between the <em>aṭṭhakā</em> days</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antara">antara</a></p>

antaraṭṭhaka|antara.t.thaka|antaratthaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antara.t.thaka</span></p><p>adjective only in phrases <em>rattisu antaraṭṭhakāsu</em> and <em>antaraṭṭhake hima-pātasamaye</em> (in which antara functions as prep. c. loc., according to antara II. b.) i.e. in the nights (&amp; in the time of the falling of snow) between the eighths (i.e. the eighth day before &amp; after the full moon: see *<a href="bword://a%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADhaka">aṭṭhaka</a>*<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->) First phrase at Vin.i.31, Vin.i.288; Vin.iii.31; second at MN.i.79 (cp. MN.i.536 where <em>Trenckner</em> divides anta-raṭṭhaka) AN.i.136 (in nom.); Ja.i.390; Mil.396.</p><p>antara + aṭṭhaka</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://aṭṭhaka">aṭṭhaka</a></p>

antarena
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">instr.</i></p><p>through, between (acc. or gen.)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antara">antara</a></p>

antarika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective “being in between”, i.e.</p><ol><li>intermediate, next, following: see <em>an</em>˚.</li><li>distant lying in between Pv-a.173 (aneka-yojan˚ ṭhāna). See also f. antarikā.</li><li>inside: see <em><a href="bword://antarik%C4%81">antarikā</a></em>. <em>-anantarika</em> with no interval, succeeding, immediately following, next Vin.ii.165, Vin.ii.212 (ān˚); Vin.iv.234.</li></ol><p>fr. antara</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antarikā">antarikā</a></p>

antarikā|antarikaa|antarika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antarikaa</span></p><p>space between, interstice, interval; cleft, chink.</p>

antarikā|antarikaa|antarika
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antarikaa</span></p><p>“what lies in between or near”, i.e.</p><ol><li>the inside of Vin.iv.272 (bhājan˚).</li><li>the neighbourhood, region of (-˚), sphere, compass Vin.iii.39 (ur˚, angul˚); Ja.i.265 (yakkhassa sīm˚ inside the yṡ sphere of influence).</li><li>interval, interstice Vin.ii.116 (sutt˚ in lace); AN.i.124 (vijj˚ the interval of lightning).</li></ol><p>abstr. fr. antarika</p>

antarubbhāra|antarubbhaara|antarubbhara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antarubbhaara</span></p><p>the removal (of the <em>kaṭhina</em>), ending (of the <em>kaṭhina</em> period and its special allowances) before the usual time</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antarā">antarā</a></p>

antarā-hosi|antaraa-hosi|antara-hosi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraa-hosi</span></p><p>antarā-hosi</p><p>aor. 3 sg. was interrupted; was drowned.</p>

antarā|antaraa|antara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">adv. &amp;</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraa</span></p><p>prep.</p><ol><li>(adv.) inside; on the way, in the meantime; beforehand, before (reaching something).</li><li>(prep.) between (gen. or acc).</li></ol>

antarā-parinibbāyī|antaraa-parinibbaayii|antara-parinibbayi
<p>[Nyana]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraa-parinibbaayii</span></p><p><strong>Antarā-parinibbāyī:</strong> is one of the 5 kinds of Non-Returners or <em>Anāgāmī</em>.</p>

antarā|antaraa|antara
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraa</span></p><p>adverb <em>prep.</em> (c. gen. acc. or loc.), <em>pref.</em> (˚-) and <em>adv.</em> “in between” (of space &amp; time), midway, inside; during meanwhile, between. On interpretation of term see DN-a.i.34 sq</p><ol><li>(prep.) c. acc. (of the two points compared as termini; cp. B.Sk. antarā ca Divy.94 etc.) DN.i.1 (antarā ca Rājagahaṃ antarā ca Nāḷandaṃ between R. and N.)<br />■ c. gen. &amp; loc. Vin.ii.161 (satthīnaṃ between the thighs, where id. p. at Ja.i.218 has antara-satthīsu); AN.ii.245 (satthīnaṃ. but variant reading satthimhi)</li><li>(adv.) meanwhile Snp.291, Snp.694; Iti.85; Dhp.237<br />■ occasionally Mil.251</li><li>(pref.) see compounds</li></ol><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://kath%C4%81">kathā</a></em> “in between talk, talk for pastime, chance conversation DN.ii.1, DN.ii.8, DN.ii.9; SN.i.79; SN.iv.281; AN.iii.167; Snp.p.115; DN-a.i.49 and freq. passim.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://gacchati">gacchati</a></em> to come in between, to prevent Ja.vi.295.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://parinibb%C4%81yin">parinibbāyin</a></em> an Anāgāmin who passes away in the middle of his term of life in some particular heaven DN.iii.237; AN.i.233; Pp.16</li><li><em>-magge</em> (loc.) on the road, on the way Ja.i.253; Mil.16; Dhp-a.ii.21; Dhp-a.iii.337; Pv-a.151, Pv-a.258, Pv-a.269, Pv-a.273 (cp. antara˚)</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://mara%E1%B9%87a">maraṇa</a></em> premature death Dhp-a.i.409; Pv-a.136.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://muttaka">muttaka</a></em> one who is released in the meantime Vin.ii.167.</li></ul><p>abl. or adv. formation fr. antara; Vedic antarā.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://kathā">kathā</a>, <a href="bword://gacchati">gacchati</a>, <a href="bword://parinibbāyin">parinibbāyin</a>, <a href="bword://maraṇa">maraṇa</a>, <a href="bword://muttaka">muttaka</a></p>

antarākathā|antaraakathaa|antarakatha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraakathaa</span></p><p>mutual talk, conversation (between)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antarā">antarā</a></p>

antarākāja|antaraakaaja|antarakaja
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraakaaja</span></p><p>load on a carrying pole suspended between two persons</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antarā">antarā</a></p>

antarāmaggato|antaraamaggato|antaramaggato
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraamaggato</span></p><p>from on the road</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antarā">antarā</a></p>

antarāmagge|antaraamagge|antaramagge
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraamagge</span></p><p>on the way</p><p>See also: antaraā</p>

antarāmuttaka|antaraamuttaka|antaramuttaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraamuttaka</span></p><p>released or vacant in the meantime</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antarā">antarā</a></p>

antarāntara|antaraantara|antarantara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraantara</span></p><p>in the middle; as an interruption</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antarā">antarā</a></p>

antarāparinibbāyi|antaraaparinibbaayi|antaraparinibbayi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraaparinibbaayi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://antarāparinibbāyin">antarāparinibbāyin</a></p><p>one who realized nibbāna beforehand (before passing the midpoint of his term life in heaven)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antarā">antarā</a></p>

antarāparinibbāyin|antaraaparinibbaayin|antaraparinibbayin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraaparinibbaayin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://antarāparinibbāyin">antarāparinibbāyin</a></p><p>one who realized nibbāna beforehand (before passing the midpoint of his term life in heaven)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antarā">antarā</a></p>

antarāpaṇa|antaraapa.na|antarapana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraapa.na</span></p><p>market, bazaar.</p>

antarāpaṇa|antaraapa.na|antarapana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraapa.na</span></p><p>place where the trading goes on, bazaar Ja.i.55; Ja.vi.52; Mil.1, Mil.330; Dhp-a.i.181.</p><p>antarā + paṇa “in between the shopping or trading”</p>

antarāppati|antaraappati|antarappati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraappati</span></p><p>an offence committed in the meantime (i.e. before the expiration of a parivāsa or mānatta period)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antarā">antarā</a></p>

antarāvosāna|antaraavosaana|antaravosana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraavosaana</span></p><p>giving up half-way</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antarā">antarā</a></p>

antarāya|antaraaya|antaraya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraaya</span></p><p>an obstacle, hindrance; danger, accident; (euphemism for) ruin, death.</p>

antarāya|antaraaya|antaraya
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraaya</span></p><p>Antarāya<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>obstacle, hindrance, impediment to (-˚); prevention, bar danger, accident to (-). There are 10 dangers (to or from) enumerated at Vin.i.112, Vin.i.169 etc., viz. <em>rāja˚, cora˚ aggi˚, udaka˚, manussa˚, amanussa˚, vāḷa˚, siriṃsapa˚ jīvita˚, brahmacariya˚</em>. In B.Sk. 7 at Divy.544, viz rājā-caura-manuṣy-amanuṣya-vyāḍ-agny-udakaṃ<br />■ DN.i.3 DN.i.25, DN.i.26; AN.iii.243, AN.iii.306; AN.iv.320; Snp.691, Snp.692; Dhp.286 (= jīvit˚ Dhp-a.iii.431); Ja.i.62, Ja.i.128; Kp-a.181; Dhp-a.ii.52; Vv-a.1 = Pv-a.1 (hat˚ removing the obstacles <em>-antarāyaṃ karoti</em> to keep away from, hinder, hold back prevent, destroy Vin.i.15; Ja.vi.171; Vism.120; Pv-a.20.</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://kara">kara</a></em> one who causes impediments or bars the way an obstructor DN.i.227; SN.i.34; AN.i.161; Pv.iv.3#22.</li></ul><p>antara + aya from <em><a href="bword://i">i</a></em>, lit. “coming in between”</p><p>Antarāya<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>adverb <a href="bword://i">i</a>*?) in the meantime Snp.1120 (cp Cnd.58) antarā Snp-a.603.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://kara">kara</a>, <a href="bword://i">i</a>, <a href="bword://i">i</a></p>

antarāyakara|antaraayakara|antarayakara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mf</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraayakara</span></p><p>(~ī)n. causing obstacles; preventing</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antarāya">antarāya</a></p>

antarāyaṃ karoti|antaraaya.m karoti|antarayam karoti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(?)</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraaya.m karoti</span></p><p>hinders, prevents (+gen. rei and personae or +acc. personae, loc. rei)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antarāya">antarāya</a></p>

antarāyika|antaraayika|antarayika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraayika</span></p><p>causing obstacles, forming an impediment.</p>

antarāyika|antaraayika|antarayika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraayika</span></p><p>adjective causing an obstacle, forming an impediment Vin.i.94 = Vin.ii.272; MN.i.130; SN.ii.226 Thag-a.288.</p><p>fr. antarāya</p>

antarāyikin|antaraayikin|antarayikin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraayikin</span></p><p>adjective noun one who meets with an obstacle, finding difficulties Vin.iv.280 (an˚ = asati antarāye).</p><p>cp. antarāyika</p>

antarāḷa|antaraa.la|antarala
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antaraa.la</span></p><p>interior, interval Dāvs i.52; Dāvs iii.53 (nabh˚).</p><p>Sk antarāla</p>

antava
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(m)f(n.)</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://antavat">antavat</a></p><p>having an end, limited, finite</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anta">anta</a></p>

antavant
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective having an end, finite DN.i.22, DN.i.31, DN.i.187; Pts.i.151 sq.; Pts.i.157; Dhs.1099, Dhs.1117, Dhs.1175; Mil.145. <em>-anantavant</em> endless, infinite AN.v.193 (loka) See also loka.</p><p>anta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --> + ˚vant</p>

antavat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(m)f(n.)</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://antavat">antavat</a></p><p>having an end, limited, finite</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anta">anta</a></p>

antaḷikkha|anta.likkha|antalikkha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anta.likkha</span></p><p>( &amp; m.?) intermediate space, the atmosphere, the air; the sky.</p>

antaḷikkhacara|anta.likkhacara|antalikkhacara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anta.likkhacara</span></p><p>traveling through the air</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antaḷikkha">antaḷikkha</a></p>

antaḷikkhaga|anta.likkhaga|antalikkhaga
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anta.likkhaga</span></p><p>going through the air</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antaḷikkha">antaḷikkha</a></p>

antaḷikkhecara|anta.likkhecara|antalikkhecara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anta.likkhecara</span></p><p>traveling through the air.</p>

anta’anta|anta'anta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>the most remote</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anta">anta</a></p>

ante
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Ante˚</p><p>prefix near, inside, within; only in foll. compounds: <em>-pura</em> (nt.) “inner town”, the king’s palace, esp. its inner apartments i.e. harem [Sk. antaḥpura, cp. also P. antopura] Vin.i.75, Vin.i.269; AN.v.81; Ja.ii.125; Ja.iv.472; Mil.1; Pv-a.23 Pv-a.81, Pv-a.280; <em>-purikā</em> harem woman Dhs-a.403; <em>-vāsika</em> one who lives in, i.e. lodges or lives with his master or teacher, a pupil Vin.i.60; Vin.iii.25; SN.i.180; SN.iv.136; Ja.i.166; Ja.ii.278; Ja.iii.83, Ja.iii.463; Pv-a.12; Vv-a.138; <em>-vāsin</em> ˚vāsika Vin.iii.66; DN.i.1, DN.i.45, DN.i.74, DN.i.78, DN.i.88, DN.i.108, DN.i.157; MN.iii.116; DN-a.i.36.</p><p>Sk. antaḥ, with change of-aḥ to-e, instead of the usual-o, prob. through interpreting it as loc. of anta</p>

antena
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">instr. adv.</i></p><p>at last, in the end</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anta">anta</a></p>

antepura
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>the royal palace, esp. the inner apartments, the harem.</p>

antevāsi|antevaasi|antevasi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antevaasi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://antevāsin">antevāsin</a></p><p>‘dwelling near or in the house (of his master)’, (who is) a (resident) pupil; an apprentice</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antevāsinī">antevāsinī</a></p>

antevāsika|antevaasika|antevasika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">m</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antevaasika</span></p><p>(being) a (resident) pupil.</p>

antevāsin|antevaasin|antevasin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antevaasin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://antevāsin">antevāsin</a></p><p>‘dwelling near or in the house (of his master)’, (who is) a (resident) pupil; an apprentice</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antevāsinī">antevāsinī</a></p>

antevāsinikamyatā|antevaasinikamyataa|antevasinikamyata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antevaasinikamyataa</span></p><p>desire to get pupils</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antevāsin">antevāsin</a></p>

antevāsinī|antevaasinii|antevasini
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antevaasinii</span></p><p>‘dwelling near or in the house (of her master)’, (who is) a (resident) pupil; an apprentice</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antevāsin">antevāsin</a></p>

anti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>indeclinable adv. &amp; prep. c. gen.: opposite near Ja.v.399 (tav’ antiṃ āgatā, read as tav’ anti-m-āgatā C. santikaṃ), Ja.v.400, Ja.v.404; Ja.vi.565 (sāmikass’ anti = antike C.)-Cp. <em><a href="bword://antika">antika</a></em>.</p><p>Vedic anti = Lat ante, Gr. ἀντί, Goth. and; Ags. and-, Ger. ant-, ent-</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antika">antika</a></p>

antika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>teaching to; reaching to the end of.</p>

antika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective noun</p><ol><li>near Kp-a.217; nt. neighbourhood Kp.viii.1. (odak˚); Ja.vi.565 (antike loc. anti near).</li><li>[der fr. anta = Sk. antya] being at the end, final, finished, over SN.i.130 (purisā etad-antikā, variant reading SS antiyā: men are (to me) at the end for that, i.e. men do not exist any more for me, for the purpose of begetting sons.</li></ol><p>der fr. anti</p>

antima
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>last, final; lowest, meanest.</p>

antima
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective last, final (used almost exclusively with ref. to the last &amp; final reincarnation thus in comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with <em>deha &amp; sarīra;</em>, the last body) DN.ii.15; Dhp.351; Iti.50 (antimaṃ dehaṃ dhāreti), Iti.53 (id.); Vv.5#12 Snp.478 (sarīraṃ antimaṃ dhāreti) Snp.502; Mil.122, Mil.148; Vv-a.106 (sarīr’ antima-dhārin); Sdhp.278.</p><ul><li><em>-dehadhara</em> one who wears his last body Iti.101 (dhāra T, ˚dhara variant reading); Vv-a.163.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://dh%C4%81rin">dhārin</a></em> = prec. SN.i.14, SN.i.53 (+ khīṇāsava); SN.ii.278; Iti.32, Iti.40; Snp.471.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://vatthu">vatthu</a></em> “the last thing”, i.e. the extreme, final or worst (sin) Vin.i.121, Vin.i.135, Vin.i.167, Vin.i.320.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://sar%C4%ABra">sarīra</a></em> the last body; (adj.) having ones last rebirth SN.i.210 (Buddho a˚-sarīro); AN.ii.37; Snp.624; Dhp.352, Dhp.400; Dhp-a.iv.166 (= koṭiyaṃ ṭhito attabhāvo).</li></ul><p>Cp. superl. of anta</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://dhārin">dhārin</a>, <a href="bword://vatthu">vatthu</a>, <a href="bword://sarīra">sarīra</a></p>

antimadehadhara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>who has his last body</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antima">antima</a></p>

antimadehadhāri|antimadehadhaari|antimadehadhari
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. id.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antimadehadhaari</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://antimadehadhārin">antimadehadhārin</a></p><p>who has his last body</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antima">antima</a></p>

antimadehadhārin|antimadehadhaarin|antimadehadharin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. id.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antimadehadhaarin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://antimadehadhārin">antimadehadhārin</a></p><p>who has his last body</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antima">antima</a></p>

antimapurisa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>the last man, the meanest man; last of the line</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antima">antima</a></p>

antimasārīra|antimasaariira|antimasarira
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">antimasaariira</span></p><p>having his last body</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antima">antima</a></p>

antimavattu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>an extreme offense</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://antima">antima</a></p>

antinomies
<p>[Nyana]</p><p></p><p><strong>Antinomies:</strong> see: <em>ditthi</em></p>

anto-aruna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>anto-aruna</p><p>neuter the time before sunrise</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anto">anto</a></p>

anto
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">adv. &amp;</i></p><p>prep.</p><ol><li>(adv.) within, inside.</li><li>(prep.)<ol><li>+ loc. (sometimes written as cpd): within, inside, in the middle (of)</li><li>+ acc. (sometimes written as cpd): within, inside.</li></ol></li></ol>

anto
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>indeclinable prep. inside, either c. acc. denoting direction = into, or c. loc. denoting place where = in. As prefix (˚-) in, within, inside, inner (see compounds)</p><ol><li>prep <em>c. acc.</em> anto nivesanaṃ gata gone into the house Ja.i.158 anto jālaṃ pavisati go into the net Dhp-a.iii.175; anto gāmaṃ pavisati to go into the village Dhp-a.ii.273; anto nagaraṃ pavisati Dhp-a.ii.89; Pv-a.47</li><li><em>c. loc.</em> anto gabbhe Ja.ii.182; gāme Dhp-a.ii.52; gehe Dhp-a.ii.84 nadiyaṃ Ja.vi.278; nivesane Ja.ii.323; vasse in the rainy season Ja.iv.242; vimānasmiṃ Pv.i.10#1; sattāhe inside of a week Pv-a.55.</li></ol><ul><li><p><em>-koṭisanthāra</em> “house of the Golden Pavement” Ja.iv.113</p></li><li><p><em>-gadha</em> (˚gata? Kern</p><blockquote><p>Toevoegselen</p></blockquote><p>) in phrase <em>˚hetu</em>, by inner reason or by reason of its intensity Pv-a.10; Vv-a.12</p></li><li><p><em>-<a href="bword://jana">jana</a></em> “the inside people”, i.e. people belonging to the house, the family (= Lat. familia) DN.iii.61 (opp. to servants); AN.i.152; Ja.vi.301; DN-a.i.300.</p></li><li><p><em>-<a href="bword://j%C4%81la">jāla</a></em> the inside of the net, the net Dhp-a.iv.41.</p></li><li><p><em>-jālikata</em> “in-netted”, gone into the net DN.i.45; DN-a.i.127.</p></li><li><p><em>-<a href="bword://nijjh%C4%81na">nijjhāna</a></em> inner conflagration Pv-a.18.</p></li><li><p><em>-<a href="bword://nimugga">nimugga</a></em> altogether immersed DN.i.75; AN.iii.26.</p></li><li><p><em>-<a href="bword://parisoka">parisoka</a></em> inner grief Pts.i.38.</p></li><li><p><em>-<a href="bword://pura">pura</a></em> = antepura Ja.i.262.</p></li><li><p><em>-<a href="bword://mano">mano</a></em> “turning ones mind inside”, thoughtful melancholy Vin.iii.19.</p></li><li><p><em>-bhavika</em> being inside Mil.95</p></li><li><p><em>-rukkhatā</em> being among trees Ja.i.7.</p></li><li><p><em>-<a href="bword://vasati">vasati</a></em> to inhabit live within SN.iv.136.</p></li><li><p><em>-vaḷañjanaka</em> (parijana) indoorpeople Ja.v.118.</p></li><li><p><em>-<a href="bword://vassa">vassa</a></em> the rainy season (lit. the interval of the r. s.) Vv-a.66.</p></li><li><p><em>-<a href="bword://vih%C4%81ra">vihāra</a></em> the inside of the V. Dhp-a.i.50 (˚âbhimukhī turning towards etc.),</p></li><li><p><em>-<a href="bword://samorodha">samorodha</a></em> barricading within Dhs.1157 (so read for anta˚, cp. <em>Dhs trsl.</em> 311).</p></li><li><p><em>-<a href="bword://soka">soka</a></em> inner grief Pts.i.38.</p></li></ul><p>Sk. antaḥ; Av antarə Lat. inter, Oir. etar between, Ohg. untar; Idg. *entar, compar. of *en (in) inner, inside</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://jana">jana</a>, <a href="bword://jāla">jāla</a>, <a href="bword://nijjhāna">nijjhāna</a>, <a href="bword://nimugga">nimugga</a>, <a href="bword://parisoka">parisoka</a>, <a href="bword://pura">pura</a>, <a href="bword://mano">mano</a>, <a href="bword://vasati">vasati</a>, <a href="bword://vassa">vassa</a>, <a href="bword://vihāra">vihāra</a>, <a href="bword://samorodha">samorodha</a>, <a href="bword://soka">soka</a></p>

anto-ārāma|anto-aaraama|anto-arama
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anto-aaraama</span></p><p>anto-ārāma</p><p>masculine the inner part of an ārāma</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anto">anto</a></p>

anto-āvasatha|anto-aavasatha|anto-avasatha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anto-aavasatha</span></p><p>anto-āvasatha</p><p>masculine the inner part of a dwelling</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anto">anto</a></p>

antogadha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>included; contained in</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anto">anto</a></p>

antogata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>being within, turned inward; being contained within</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anto">anto</a></p>

