anubhavana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>experiencing, suffering; sensation or physical sensibility (cf. <em>Cpd.</em> 229, 232<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted -->) Ne.28 (iṭṭhâniṭṭh-ânubhavana-lakkhanā vedanā “feeling is characterised by the experiencing of what is pleasant and unpleasant”); Mil.60 (vedayita-lakkhaṇā vedanā anubhavana-lakkhaṇā ca); Pv-a.152 (kamma-vipāka˚). Esp. in comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with <em>dukkha˚</em>; suffering painful sensations, e.g. at Ja.iv.3; Mil.181; Dhp-a.iv.75; Pv-a.52.</p><p>fr. anubhavati</p>

anubhavati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>experiences, enjoys, suffers; partakes of, has a share in; attains, is equal to; is able; suffices</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubhoti">anubhoti</a></p>

anubhavati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Anubhavati &amp; Anubhoti</p><p>to come to or by, to undergo, suffer (feel), get, undertake, partake in, experience DN.i.129; DN.ii.12 (˚bhonti); MN.ii.204; AN.i.61 (atthaṃ ˚bhoti to have a good result); Ja.vi.97 (˚bhoma) Pv.i.10#11 (˚bhomi vipākaṃ); Pv-a.52 (˚issati = vedissati) Sdhp.290. Esp. freq. with <em><a href="bword://dukkha%E1%B9%83">dukkhaṃ</a></em> to suffer pain, e.g Pv-a.i.11#2 (˚bhonti); Pv-a.43, Pv-a.68, Pv-a.79 etc. (cp. anubhavana)<br />ppr med. <em>-bhavamāna</em> Ja.i.50; aor. <em>-bhavi</em> Pv-a.75 (sampattiṃ); ger. <em>-bhavitvā</em> Ja.iv.1; Pv-a.4 (sampattiṃ), Pv-a.67 (dukkhaṃ), Pv-a.73 (sampattiṃ); grd. <em>-bhaviyāna</em> (in order to receive) Pv.ii.8#5 (= anubhavitvā Pv-a.109). Pass. <em>anubhūyati &amp; ˚bhavīyati;</em> to be undergone or being experienced; ppr. <em>-bhūyamāna</em> Pv-a.8, Pv-a.159 (mayā a. anubhūta), Pv-a.214 (attanā by him) &amp; <em>-bhavīyamāna</em> Pv-a.33 (dukkhaṃ)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://anubh%C5%ABta">anubhūta</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + bhavati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://dukkhaṃ">dukkhaṃ</a>, <a href="bword://anubhūta">anubhūta</a></p>

anubhavi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubhavati">anubhavati</a></p>

anubhavissati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fut. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubhavati">anubhavati</a></p>

anubhavissāma|anubhavissaama|anubhavissama
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 plural</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubhavissaama</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubhavati">anubhavati</a></p>

anubhaṇanā|anubha.nanaa|anubhanana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubha.nanaa</span></p><p>assenting, approval, supporting.</p>

anubhaṇanā|anubha.nanaa|anubhanana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubha.nanaa</span></p><p>talking to, admonition, scolding Vin.ii.88 (anuvadanā +).</p><p>anu + bhaṇana</p>

anubhohisi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">2 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubhoti">anubhoti</a></p>

anubhoti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>experiences, enjoys, suffers; partakes of, has a share in. attains, is equal to; is able; suffices</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubhavati">anubhavati</a></p>

anubhoti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Anubhavati &amp; Anubhoti</p><p>to come to or by, to undergo, suffer (feel), get, undertake, partake in, experience DN.i.129; DN.ii.12 (˚bhonti); MN.ii.204; AN.i.61 (atthaṃ ˚bhoti to have a good result); Ja.vi.97 (˚bhoma) Pv.i.10#11 (˚bhomi vipākaṃ); Pv-a.52 (˚issati = vedissati) Sdhp.290. Esp. freq. with <em><a href="bword://dukkha%E1%B9%83">dukkhaṃ</a></em> to suffer pain, e.g Pv-a.i.11#2 (˚bhonti); Pv-a.43, Pv-a.68, Pv-a.79 etc. (cp. anubhavana)<br />ppr med. <em>-bhavamāna</em> Ja.i.50; aor. <em>-bhavi</em> Pv-a.75 (sampattiṃ); ger. <em>-bhavitvā</em> Ja.iv.1; Pv-a.4 (sampattiṃ), Pv-a.67 (dukkhaṃ), Pv-a.73 (sampattiṃ); grd. <em>-bhaviyāna</em> (in order to receive) Pv.ii.8#5 (= anubhavitvā Pv-a.109). Pass. <em>anubhūyati &amp; ˚bhavīyati;</em> to be undergone or being experienced; ppr. <em>-bhūyamāna</em> Pv-a.8, Pv-a.159 (mayā a. anubhūta), Pv-a.214 (attanā by him) &amp; <em>-bhavīyamāna</em> Pv-a.33 (dukkhaṃ)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://anubh%C5%ABta">anubhūta</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + bhavati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://dukkhaṃ">dukkhaṃ</a>, <a href="bword://anubhūta">anubhūta</a></p>

anubhāga|anubhaaga|anubhaga
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubhaaga</span></p><p>an additional share.</p>

anubhāga|anubhaaga|anubhaga
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubhaaga</span></p><p>secondary or inferior part, (after-)share, what is left over Vin.ii.167.</p><p>anu + bhāga</p>

anubhāsati|anubhaasati|anubhasati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubhaasati</span></p><p>speaks after, repeats; continually speaks.</p>

anubhāsati|anubhaasati|anubhasati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubhaasati</span></p><p>to speak after, to repeat DN.i.104; Mil.345; DN-a.i.273.</p><p>anu + bhāsati</p>

anubhāva|anubhaava|anubhava
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubhaava</span></p><p>orig. meaning “experience, concomitance” and found only in compounds as-˚, in meaning “experiencing the sensation of or belonging to, experience of, accordance with”, e.g. maha˚ sensation of greatness rājâ˚ s. belonging to a king, what is in accordance with kingship, i.e. majesty. Through preponderance of expressions of distinction there arises the meaning of anubhāva as “power, majesty, greatness, splendour etc.” &amp; as such it was separated from the 1<!-- raw HTML omitted -->st<!-- raw HTML omitted --> component and taken as <em><a href="bword://%C4%81nubh%C4%81va">ānubhāva</a></em> with ā instead of a, since the compositional character had obliterated the character of the a. As such (ānubhāva abs.) found only in later language</p><ol><li><em><a href="bword://anubh%C4%81va">anubhāva</a></em> (-˚): <em>mahānubhāva</em> (of) great majesty, eminence power SN.i.146 sq.; SN.ii.274; SN.iv.323; Snp.p.93; Pv.ii.1#12 Pv-a.76. <em>deva˚</em>; of divine power or majesty DN.ii.12; <em>devatā˚</em>; id. Ja.i.168; <em>dibba˚</em>; id. Pv-a.71, Pv-a.110. <em>rājā˚</em>; kingly splendour, pomp DN.i.49; Ja.iv.247; Pv-a.279 etc. <em>-anubhāvena</em> (instr -˚) in accordance with, by means of Ja.ii.200 (angavijjā˚); Pv-a.53 (iddh˚), Pv-a.77 (kamma˚), Pv-a.148 (id.), Pv-a.162 (rāja˚), Pv-a.184 (dāna˚), Pv-a.186 (puñña˚). <strong>yathānubhāvaṃ</strong> (adv.) in accordance with (me), as much as (1 can); after ability, according to power SN.i.31; Vv.1#5 (yathābalaṃ Vv-a.25)</li><li><em><a href="bword://%C4%81nubh%C4%81va">ānubhāva</a></em> majesty power magnificence, glory, splendour Ja.v.10, Ja.v.456; Pv.ii.8#11 Vv-a.14; Pv-a.43, Pv-a.122, Pv-a.272. See also ānu˚.</li></ol><p>fr. anubhavati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ānubhāva">ānubhāva</a>, <a href="bword://anubhāva">anubhāva</a>, yathānubhāvaṃ, <a href="bword://ānubhāva">ānubhāva</a></p>

anubhāvatā|anubhaavataa|anubhavata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubhaavataa</span></p><p>majesty, power SN.i.156 (mahā˚).</p><p>= anubhāva + tā</p>

anubhāyati|anubhaayati|anubhayati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubhaayati</span></p><p>to be afraid of Ja.vi.302 (kissa nv’ ânubhāyissaṃ, so read for kissânu˚).</p><p>anu + bhāyati</p>

anubhūta|anubhuuta|anubhuta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubhuuta</span></p><p>experienced, suffered, enjoyed</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubhavati">anubhavati</a></p>

anubhūta|anubhuuta|anubhuta
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubhuuta</span></p><p>(having or being) experienced, suffered, enjoyed Pv-a.ii.12#2. nt. suffering, experience Ja.i.254; Mil.78, Mil.80.</p><p>pp. of anubhavati</p>

anubhūyamānatta|anubhuuyamaanatta|anubhuyamanatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubhuuyamaanatta</span></p><p>the fact of having to undergo, experiencing Pv-a.103.</p><p>abstr. fr. ppr. Pass. of anubhavati</p>

anubodha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>awakening; perception, recognition, understanding SN.i.126 (?) = AN.v.46 (anubodhiṃ as aor. of anubodhati?); Pp.21; Mil.233. Freq. in comp<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> <em>ananubodha</em> (adj.) not understanding, not knowing the truth SN.ii.92; SN.iii.261; SN.v.431; AN.ii.1; AN.iv.105; Dhs.390 Dhs.1061; Vv-a.321 (= anavabodha) and <em><a href="bword://duranubodha">duranubodha</a></em> (adj. hard to understand, difficult to know DN.i.12, DN.i.22; SN.i.136.</p><p>anu + <em>budh</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://duranubodha">duranubodha</a></p>

anubodhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>awakening, understanding, recognition Pts.i.18 (bodhana +).</p><p>fr. anubodhati</p>

anubodhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to wake up, to realise, perceive, understand; aor. anubodhiṃ AN.v.46 (?) = SN.i.126 (anubodhaṃ)<br />caus <em>-bodheti</em> to awaken, fig. to make see to instruct Ja.vi.139 (˚ayamāna)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://anubuddha">anubuddha</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + <em>budh</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubuddha">anubuddha</a></p>

anubodhiṃ|anubodhi.m|anubodhim
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">1 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubodhi.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubujjhati">anubujjhati</a></p>

anubrūhati|anubruuhati|anubruhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubruuhati</span></p><p>makes increase, fosters; devotes oneself to; practices</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubrūheti">anubrūheti</a></p>

anubrūhaya|anubruuhaya|anubruhaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubruuhaya</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anubrūhayat">anubrūhayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubrūheti">anubrūheti</a></p>

anubrūhayamāna|anubruuhayamaana|anubruhayamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubruuhayamaana</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubrūheti">anubrūheti</a></p>

anubrūhayat|anubruuhayat|anubruhayat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubruuhayat</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anubrūhayat">anubrūhayat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubrūheti">anubrūheti</a></p>

anubrūhayati|anubruuhayati|anubruhayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubruuhayati</span></p><p>makes increase, fosters; devotes oneself to; practices</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubrūheti">anubrūheti</a></p>

anubrūheti|anubruuheti|anubruheti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubruuheti</span></p><p>makes increase, fosters; devotes oneself to; practices</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubrūhati">anubrūhati</a>, <a href="bword://anubrūhayati">anubrūhayati</a></p>

anubrūheti|anubruuheti|anubruheti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubruuheti</span></p><p>to do very much or often, to practice, frequent, to be fond of (c. acc.), foster SN.i.178 (anubrūhaye); MN.iii.187 (id., so read for manu˚), Thig.163 (˚ehi); Cp.iii.1#2 (saṃvegaṃ anubrūhayiṃ aor.); Ja.iii.191 (suññāgāraṃ). Often in phrase <em>vivekaṃ anubrūheti</em> to devote oneself to detachment or solitude, e.g. Ja.i.9 (inf ˚brūhetuṃ); Ja.iii.31 (˚brūhessāmi), Dhp.75 (˚brūhaye ˚brūheyya vaḍḍheyya Dhp-a.ii.103)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://anubr%C5%ABhita">anubrūhita</a></em> (q.v.) Cp. also <em><a href="bword://br%C5%ABhana">brūhana</a></em>.</p><p>brūheti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubrūhita">anubrūhita</a>, <a href="bword://brūhana">brūhana</a></p>

anubrūhita|anubruuhita|anubruhita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubruuhita</span></p><p>increased; strengthened</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubrūheti">anubrūheti</a></p>

anubrūhita|anubruuhita|anubruhita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubruuhita</span></p><p>strengthened with (-˚), full of Pts.i.167.</p><p><em>pp</em>. of anubrūheti</p>

anubuddha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn. (mfn.)</i></p><ol><li>(pass.) realised, understood.</li><li>(act.) understanding; enlightened.</li></ol>

anubuddha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>awakened (act. &amp; pass.), recognised, conceived, seen, known DN.ii.123 (˚ā ime dhammā); SN.i.137 (dhammo vimalen’ ânubuddho ii.203; iv.188; AN.ii.1; AN.iii.14; AN.iv.105; Snp-a.431. In phrase <em>buddhānubuddha</em> (as to nature of cpd. see <em><a href="bword://anu">anu</a></em> B iv. either “fully awakened (enlightened)” or “wakened by the wake” (Mrs. Rh. D.) Thag.679 = Thag.1246.</li><li>a lesser Buddha, inferior than the Buddha DN-a.i.40. Cp <em>buddhānubuddha</em>.</li></ol><p>pp. of anu + bodhati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anu">anu</a></p>

anubujjhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>awakening, recognition Pts.i.18 (bujjhana +).</p><p>fr. anubujjhati</p>

anubujjhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>understands; is conscious of; recollects.</p>

anubujjhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to remember, recollect Ja.iii.387 (with <em><a href="bword://avabujjhati">avabujjhati</a></em> in prec. verse).</p><p>anu + bujjhati, Med. of <em>budh</em>, cp. Sk. avabudhyate</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://avabujjhati">avabujjhati</a></p>

anubyañjana FIXME double|anubya~njana FIXME double|anubyanjana FIXME double
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubya~njana FIXME double</span></p><p>Anuvyañjana &amp; anubyañjana</p><p>(e.g. Vin.iv.15; Ja.i.12) neuter accompanying (i.e. secondary attribute, minor or inferior characteristic, supplementary or additional sign or mark (cf. mahāpurisa-lakkhaṇa) Vin.i.65 (abl. anuvyañjanaso “in detail”); MN.iii.126; SN.iv.168; AN.iv.279 (abl.); AN.v.73 sq.; Pp.24, Pp.58; Mil.339; Vv-a.315; Dhs-a.400.</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://g%C4%81hin">gāhin</a></em> taking up or occupying oneself with details, taken up with lesser or inferior marks DN.i.70 (cf. Mvu.iii.52); DN.iii.225; SN.iv.104; AN.i.113; AN.ii.16, AN.ii.152 sq.; Dhs.1345 (cf. <em>Dhs trsl.</em> 351).</li></ul><p>anu + vyañjana</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://gāhin">gāhin</a></p>

anubyañjana|anubya~njana|anubyanjana
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anubya~njana</span></p><p>see <em><a href="bword://anuvya%C3%B1jana">anuvyañjana</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuvyañjana">anuvyañjana</a></p>

anucarati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>walks after or along; walks with; follows; pursues; prosecutes.</p>

anucarati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to move along, to follow; to practice; pp. <em>anuciṇṇa &amp; anucarita;</em> (q.v.)</p><p>anu + cariti</p>

anucarita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(-˚) connected with, accompanied by, pervaded with DN.i.16, DN.i.21 (vīmaṃsa˚ anuvicarita DN-a.i.106); MN.i.68 (id.); Mil.226.</p><p>pp. of anucarati</p>

anucariyamāna|anucariyamaana|anucariyamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pass. part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anucariyamaana</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anucarati">anucarati</a></p>

anucariyā|anucariyaa|anucariya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anucariyaa</span></p><p>following; attendance.</p>

anucaṅkamamāna|anuca"nkamamaana|anucankamamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuca"nkamamaana</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anucaṅkamati">anucaṅkamati</a></p>

anucaṅkamana|anuca"nkamana|anucankamana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuca"nkamana</span></p><p>sidewalk Ja.i.7.</p><p>fr. anucankamati</p>

anucaṅkamanta|anuca"nkamanta|anucankamanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuca"nkamanta</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anucaṅkamati">anucaṅkamati</a></p>

anucaṅkamati|anuca"nkamati|anucankamati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuca"nkamati</span></p><p>walks up and down along; walks up and down with or after.</p>

anucaṅkamati|anuca"nkamati|anucankamati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuca"nkamati</span></p><p>to follow (along) after, to go after DN.i.235; MN.i.227; Thag.481, Thag.1044; Caus ˚āpeti MN.i.253, cp. Lal.147, Lal.3; Mvu.i.350.</p><p>anu + cankamati</p>

anucaṅkamiṃ|anuca"nkami.m|anucankamim
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuca"nkami.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anucaṅkamati">anucaṅkamati</a></p>

anucaṅkamiṃsu|anuca"nkami.msu|anucankamimsu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 plural</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuca"nkami.msu</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anucaṅkamati">anucaṅkamati</a></p>

anucaṅkamāpeti|anuca"nkamaapeti|anucankamapeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuca"nkamaapeti</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anucaṅkamati">anucaṅkamati</a></p>

anuccaṅgin|anucca"ngin|anuccangin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anucca"ngin</span></p><p>see <em>anujjangin</em>.</p>

anucchava
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>suitable, proper; fit for; corresponding to</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anucchavi">anucchavi</a></p>

anucchavi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>suitable, proper; fit for; corresponding to</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anucchava">anucchava</a></p>

anucchavika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>suitable (for); fit; proper</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anucchaviya">anucchaviya</a></p>

anucchavika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Anucchavika &amp; ˚ya</p><p>(adj.) “according to one’s skin”, befitting, suitable, proper, pleasing, fit for, Ja.i.58, Ja.i.62, Ja.i.126, Ja.i.218; Ja.ii.5; Ja.iv.137, Ja.iv.138; Mil.358; Dhp-a.i.203, Dhp-a.i.390; Dhp-a.ii.55, Dhp-a.ii.56; Vv-a.68, Vv-a.78; Pv-a.13, Pv-a.26 (= kappiya), Pv-a.66, Pv-a.81, Pv-a.286. <em>anucchaviya</em> at Vin.ii.7 (an˚), Vin.iii.120 (id. + ananulomika); Mil.13.</p><p>anu + chavi + ka</p>

anucchaviya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>suitable (for); fit; proper</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anucchavika">anucchavika</a></p>

anucchaviya
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Anucchavika &amp; ˚ya</p><p>(adj.) “according to one’s skin”, befitting, suitable, proper, pleasing, fit for, Ja.i.58, Ja.i.62, Ja.i.126, Ja.i.218; Ja.ii.5; Ja.iv.137, Ja.iv.138; Mil.358; Dhp-a.i.203, Dhp-a.i.390; Dhp-a.ii.55, Dhp-a.ii.56; Vv-a.68, Vv-a.78; Pv-a.13, Pv-a.26 (= kappiya), Pv-a.66, Pv-a.81, Pv-a.286. <em>anucchaviya</em> at Vin.ii.7 (an˚), Vin.iii.120 (id. + ananulomika); Mil.13.</p><p>anu + chavi + ka</p>

anucchiṭṭha|anucchi.t.tha|anucchittha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anucchi.t.tha</span></p><p>adjective (food) that is not thrown away or left over; untouched, clean (food) Ja.iii.257; Dhp-a.ii.3 (vv.ll. anucciṭṭha).</p><p>see <em><a href="bword://ucchi%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADha">ucchiṭṭha</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ucchiṭṭha">ucchiṭṭha</a></p>

anuccāritakamma|anuccaaritakamma|anuccaritakamma
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuccaaritakamma</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uccāritakata">uccāritakata</a></p>

anucintana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>thinking of; considering.</p>

anucintana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>thinking, upon, intention, care for Pv-a.164.</p><p>fr. anucinteti</p>

anucinteti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to think upon, to meditate, consider SN.i.203 (variant reading for anuvicinteti).</p><p>anu + cinteti</p>

anuciṇṇa|anuci.n.na|anucinna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuci.n.na</span></p><ol><li>(pass.) followed, practiced; pervaded; filled with.</li><li>(act.) pursuing,</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://anucarati">anucarati</a></p>

anuciṇṇa|anuci.n.na|anucinna
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuci.n.na</span></p><p>past participle</p><ol><li>pursuing, following out, practising, doing; having attained or practised Vin.ii.203 = Iti.86 (pamādaṃ); Ja.i.20 (verse 126); Thag.236 Thag.2, Thag.206; Dpvs.iv.9.</li><li>adorned with, accompanied by connected with Ja.iv.286.</li></ol><p>pp. of anucarati</p>

anudadāti|anudadaati|anudadati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudadaati</span></p><p>to concede, grant, admit, fut. <em>anudassati</em> Mil.276, Mil.375.</p><p>anu + dadāti</p>

anudahati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>burns; consumes</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuḍahati">anuḍahati</a></p>

anudahati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>see <em><a href="bword://anu%E1%B8%8Dahati">anuḍahati</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuḍahati">anuḍahati</a></p>

anudaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>without water</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anūdaka">anūdaka</a>, <a href="bword://anodaka">anodaka</a>, <a href="bword://udaka">udaka</a></p>

anudasseti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>shows; instructs.</p>

anudassita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>manifested Mil.119.</p><p>pp. of anudasseti</p>

anudayati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(to sympathise with) see under <em><a href="bword://anudd%C4%81">anuddā</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuddā">anuddā</a></p>

anudayatā|anudayataa|anudayata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine abstr.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudayataa</span></p><p>compassion, kindness, favor</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuddayatā">anuddayatā</a></p>

anudayā|anudayaa|anudaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudayaa</span></p><p>compassion, care</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuddayā">anuddayā</a></p>

anuddayatā|anuddayataa|anuddayata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine abstr.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuddayataa</span></p><p>compassion, kindness, favor</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anudayatā">anudayatā</a></p>

anuddayatā|anuddayataa|anuddayata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuddayataa</span></p><p>sympathy with (-˚) compassion, kindness, favour, usually as <em>par˚</em>; kindness to or sympathy with other people SN.ii.218; SN.v.169 (T. anudayatā); AN.iii.184; Iti.72; Vb.356.</p><p>abstr. to anuddayā</p>

anuddayā|anuddayaa|anuddaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuddayaa</span></p><p>compassion, care</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anudayā">anudayā</a></p>

anuddayā|anuddayaa|anuddaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuddayaa</span></p><p>(&amp; anudayā) feminine compassion, pity, mercy, care Vin.ii.196; SN.i.204; SN.ii.199; SN.iv.323; AN.ii.176 AN.iii.189; Pp.35 (anukampā); Ja.i.147, Ja.i.186, Ja.i.214; Pv-a.70 Pv-a.88, Pv-a.181 (= anukampā). In compound <em>anudaya˚</em>; e.g. <em>-sampanna</em> full of mercy Ja.i.151, Ja.i.262; Pv-a.66.</p><p>anu + dayā</p>

anuddhacca
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>absence of over-excitement</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uddhacca">uddhacca</a></p>

anuddharin
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective not proud Snp.952 (= anussukin Snp-a.569) see <em><a href="bword://ni%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADhurin">niṭṭhurin</a></em>.</p><p>an + uddharin</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://niṭṭhurin">niṭṭhurin</a></p>

anuddharitvā|anuddharitvaa|anuddharitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuddharitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uddharitvā">uddharitvā</a></p>

anuddhasta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective spoilt, corrupt, degraded MN.i.462 (citta); AN.ii.126 (id.).</p><p>anu + dhasta, pp. of <em><a href="bword://anuddha%E1%B9%83seti">anuddhaṃseti</a></em>, cp. Sk. apadhvasta</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuddhaṃseti">anuddhaṃseti</a></p>

anuddhata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not puffed-up; not over-excited, not flurried; calm</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuddhaṭa">anuddhaṭa</a>, <a href="bword://uddhata">uddhata</a></p>

anuddhata
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective not puffed up, not proud, unconceited calm, subdued Snp.850 (= uddhacca-virahita Snp-a.549, cp. anuṇṇata); Iti.30; Dhp.363 (= nibbutacitta Dhp-a.iv.93); Vv.64#8; Pp.59.</p><p>an + uddhata</p>

anuddhaṃsenta|anuddha.msenta|anuddhamsenta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuddha.msenta</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuddhaṃseti">anuddhaṃseti</a></p>

anuddhaṃsesi|anuddha.msesi|anuddhamsesi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuddha.msesi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuddhaṃseti">anuddhaṃseti</a></p>

anuddhaṃseti|anuddha.mseti|anuddhamseti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuddha.mseti</span></p><ol><li>disturbs, contaminates, taints.</li><li>accuses (falsely); defames.</li></ol>

anuddhaṃseti|anuddha.mseti|anuddhamseti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuddha.mseti</span></p><p>to spoil, corrupt, degrade Vin.iv.148 (expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> here in slightly diff. meaning = codeti vā codāpeti vā to reprove, scold, bring down); Iti.42 Usually in ster. phrase <em>rāgo cittaṃ a</em>. lust degrades the heart Vin.iii.111; MN.i.26; SN.i.186; AN.i.266; AN.ii.126; AN.iii.393 sq<br />pp <em><a href="bword://anuddhasta">anuddhasta</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + dhaṃseti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuddhasta">anuddhasta</a></p>

anuddhaṃsita|anuddha.msita|anuddhamsita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuddha.msita</span></p><ol><li>disturbed, contaminated.</li><li>(falsely) accused; defamed</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuddhaṃseti">anuddhaṃseti</a></p>

anuddhaṭa|anuddha.ta|anuddhata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuddha.ta</span></p><p>not puffed-up; not over-excited, not flurried; calm</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuddhata">anuddhata</a>, <a href="bword://uddhaṭa">uddhaṭa</a></p>

anuddiṭṭha|anuddi.t.tha|anuddittha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuddi.t.tha</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uddiṭṭha">uddiṭṭha</a></p>

anuddā|anuddaa|anudda
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuddaa</span></p><p>= <em><a href="bword://anudday%C4%81">anuddayā</a></em> Dhs.1056, where also the other abstr. formations <em>anuddāyanā &amp; anuddāyitattaṃ</em> “care, forbearance &amp; consideration”; Dhs-a.362 (anudayatī ti anuḍdā).</p><p>contracted form of anuddayā</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuddayā">anuddayā</a></p>

anudeva
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>see <em><a href="bword://anvadeva">anvadeva</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvadeva">anvadeva</a></p>

anudhamma
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>natural state or essential property; right method; method according to the dhamma, to the doctrine.</p>

anudhamma
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>in comp<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with dhamma as <strong>dhammānudhamma</strong> to be judged as a redupl. cpd after the manner of compounds mentioned under anu iv. meaning “the Law in all its parts, the dhamma and what belongs to it, the Law in its fullness”. For instances see <em><a href="bword://dhamma">dhamma</a></em> C. iv. Freq. in phrase dh˚-ânudh˚ <em>-<a href="bword://pa%E1%B9%ADipanna">paṭipanna</a></em> “one who masters the completeness of the Dh.”, e.g. SN.ii.18; SN.iii.163; Iti.81; Pts.ii.189.</li><li>conformity or accordance with the Law, lawfulness, relation, essence, consistency truth; in phrase <em>dhammassa</em> (c˚) <em>anudhammaṃ vyākaroti</em> to explain the truth of the Dh. Vin.i.234; DN.i.161; MN.i.368, MN.i.482; SN.ii.33; SN.iii.6; SN.iv.51; SN.v.7. See further MN.iii.30; Snp.963 (cp. Mnd.481 for exegesis) Also in cpd. <em>-cārin</em> living according to the Dhamma living in truth SN.ii.81, SN.ii.108; AN.ii.8; Dhp.20 (cp. Dhp-a.i.158); Vv.31#7; Snp.69 (see Cnd.51).</li></ol><p>anu + dhamma</p><p>See also: dhammānudhamma, <a href="bword://dhamma">dhamma</a>, <a href="bword://paṭipanna">paṭipanna</a></p>

anudhammacāri|anudhammacaari|anudhammacari
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudhammacaari</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anudhammacārin">anudhammacārin</a></p><p>following the (right) doctrine; living in accordance with the doctrine</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anudhammaṃ">anudhammaṃ</a></p>

anudhammacārin|anudhammacaarin|anudhammacarin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudhammacaarin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anudhammacārin">anudhammacārin</a></p><p>following the (right) doctrine; living in accordance with the doctrine</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anudhammaṃ">anudhammaṃ</a></p>

anudhammatā|anudhammataa|anudhammata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine abstr.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudhammataa</span></p><p>conformity to the doctrine; right method</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anudhammaṃ">anudhammaṃ</a></p>

anudhammatā|anudhammataa|anudhammata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudhammataa</span></p><p>[abstr. to anudhamma) lawfulness, conformity to the Dhamma AN.ii.46; Pts.i.35, Pts.i.36.</p>

anudhammaṃ|anudhamma.m|anudhammam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudhamma.m</span></p><ol><li>in accordance with the dhamma, with the doctrine.</li><li>in accordance with.</li></ol>

anudhaṃsana|anudha.msana|anudhamsana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter \~ā, feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudha.msana</span></p><p>(falsely) accusing; (false) accusation; defamation.</p>

anudhāreti|anudhaareti|anudhareti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudhaareti</span></p><p>to hold up DN-a.i.61 (chattaṃ), cp. Ja.1.53, dhariyamāna.</p><p>anu + dhāreti</p>

anudhāvanaka|anudhaavanaka|anudhavanaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudhaavanaka</span></p><p>pursuing; following.</p>

anudhāvati|anudhaavati|anudhavati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudhaavati</span></p><p>runs after, follows; chases; runs along.</p>

anudhāvati|anudhaavati|anudhavati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudhaavati</span></p><p>to run after, to chase, follow, persecute, pursue MN.i.474; SN.i.9; Dhp.85; Thag.1174; Mil.253, Mil.372.</p><p>anu + dhāvati</p>

anudhāvi|anudhaavi|anudhavi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">2 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudhaavi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anudhāvati">anudhāvati</a></p>

anudhāvin|anudhaavin|anudhavin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudhaavin</span></p><p>adjective noun one who runs after SN.i.9, SN.i.117.</p><p>fr. anudhāvati</p>

anudhāvita|anudhaavita|anudhavita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudhaavita</span></p><p>pursuing</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anudhāvati">anudhāvati</a></p>

anudisati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to point out, direct, bid, address Pv-a.99 (aor. anudesi + anvesi)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://anudi%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADha">anudiṭṭha</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + disati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anudiṭṭha">anudiṭṭha</a></p>

anudisaṃ|anudisa.m|anudisam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudisa.m</span></p><p>in all directions.</p>

anudissati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>points out; declares; assigns, dedicates (a gift)</p>

anudisā|anudisaa|anudisa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudisaa</span></p><p>an intermediate point of the compass.</p>

anudisā|anudisaa|anudisa
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudisaa</span></p><p>an intermediate point of the compass, often collectively for the usual 4 intermediate points DN.i.222; SN.i.122; SN.iii.124.</p><p>anu + disā</p>

anudiṭṭha|anudi.t.tha|anudittha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudi.t.tha</span></p><p>pointed out, appointed, dedicated, <em>nt.</em> consecration, dedication Ja.v.393 (anudiṭṭha asukassa nāma dassatī ti C.); Pv.i.10#7 (= uddiṭṭha Pv-a.50).</p><p>pp. of anudisati</p>

anudiṭṭhi|anudi.t.thi|anuditthi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudi.t.thi</span></p><p>(dogmatic) view.</p>

anudiṭṭhi|anudi.t.thi|anuditthi
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudi.t.thi</span></p><p>an “after-view”, sceptical view, speculation, heresy DN.i.12; MN.ii.228; SN.iii.45 sq. Thag.754; Mil.325; DN-a.i.103. <em>attānudiṭṭhi</em> (q.v.) a soul-speculation.</p><p>anu + diṭṭhi</p>

anudīpeti|anudiipeti|anudipeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anudiipeti</span></p><p>to explain Mil.227 (dhammâdhammaṃ).</p><p>anu + dīpeti</p>

anudūta|anuduuta|anuduta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuduuta</span></p><p>messenger sent with another; a companion.</p>

anudūta|anuduuta|anuduta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuduuta</span></p><p>person sent with another, a travelling companion Vin.ii.19, Vin.ii.295; Dhp-a.ii.76, Dhp-a.ii.78.</p><p>anu + dūta</p>

anuga
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>going after, following, accompanying (+ gen.).</p>

anuga
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(-˚) adjective suffix following or followed by, going after, undergoing, being in or under standing under the influence of Snp.332 (<em>vasa˚</em>; in the power of), Snp.791 (<em>ejā˚</em>; = abhibhūta Snp.527), 1095 (Māra <em>vasa˚</em>; = abhibhuyya viharanti Cnd.507); Iti.91 (<em>ejā˚</em>;) Ja.iii.224 (<em>vasa˚</em>; = vasavattin C.); Mhvs.7, Mhvs.3.</p><p>fr. anu + <em>gam</em></p>

anugacchanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mf</i></p><p>(~antī) neuter</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anugacchati">anugacchati</a></p>

anugacchati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>goes along; goes after, follows; goes or falls into (acc).</p>

anugacchati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to go after, to follow, to go or fall into (w. acc.) Kp-a.223; Pv-a.141 (˚gacchanto) aor. <em>-gamāsi</em> Vin.i.16, &amp; <em><a href="bword://anvag%C4%81">anvagā</a></em> Mhvs.7, Mhvs.10; 3<!-- raw HTML omitted -->rd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> pl <em><a href="bword://anvag%C5%AB">anvagū</a></em> Snp.586 (vasaṃ = vasaṃ gata Snp-a.461). Pass <em>anugammati</em>, ppr. anugammamāna accompanied or followed by, surrounded, adorned with Ja.i.53; Ja.v.370. pp. <em><a href="bword://anugata">anugata</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + gacchati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvagā">anvagā</a>, <a href="bword://anvagū">anvagū</a>, <a href="bword://anugata">anugata</a></p>

anugama
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>following after, only as adj. in dur˚ difficult to be followed Ja.iv.65.</p><p>fr. anu + <em>gam</em></p>

anugamāsi|anugamaasi|anugamasi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugamaasi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anugacchati">anugacchati</a></p>

anugata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>following; accompanied by; fallen or gone into; affected by; relating to</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anugacchati">anugacchati</a></p>

anugata
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective gone after, accompanied by, come to; following; fig. fallen or gone into, affected with (-˚), being a victim of, suffering MN.i.16; DN.iii.85 DN.iii.173 (parisā); AN.ii.185 (sota˚, variant reading anudhata); Ja.ii.292 (samudda˚); Ja.v.369; Cnd.32 (taṇhā˚); Pv-a.102 (nāmaṃ mayhaṃ a. has been given to me), Pv-a.133 (kammaphala˚).</p><p>pp. of anugacchati</p>

anugati
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>(-˚) following, being in the train of, falling under, adherence to, dependence on SN.i.104 (vas˚ being in the power). Usually in cpd. <em><a href="bword://di%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADh%C4%81nugati">diṭṭhānugati</a></em> a sign (lit. belonging to) of speculation Vin.ii.108; SN.ii.203; Pp.33; Dhp-a.iv.39.</p><p>fr. anu + <em>gam</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://diṭṭhānugati">diṭṭhānugati</a></p>

anugaṇhāti|anuga.nhaati|anuganhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuga.nhaati</span></p><p>favors, treats with kindness; protects, helps; acknowledges, admits</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuggaṇhāti">anuggaṇhāti</a></p>

anugaṇhāti|anuga.nhaati|anuganhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuga.nhaati</span></p><p>Also written as: Anuggaṇhāti</p><p>to have pity on, to feel sorry for, to help, give protection DN.i.53 (vācaṃ; cp. DN-a.i.160: sārato agaṇhaṇto); Ja.ii.74; Cnd.50 (ppr. med <em>-gayhamāna</em> = anukampamāna); Pp.36; Pv-a.181 (imper. <em><a href="bword://anugga%E1%B9%87ha">anuggaṇha</a></em> = anukampassu). pp. <em><a href="bword://anuggah%C4%ABta">anuggahīta</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + gaṇhāti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuggaṇha">anuggaṇha</a>, <a href="bword://anuggahīta">anuggahīta</a></p>

anuggaha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>anuggaha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>masculine favor, kindness; help, assistance.</p><p>anuggaha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>mfn. not taking up</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uggaha">uggaha</a></p>

anuggaha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Anuggaha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>“taking up”, compassion, love for, kindness, assistance, help, favour, benefit SN.ii.11 SN.iii.109; SN.iv.104; SN.v.162; AN.i.92, AN.i.114; AN.ii.145; AN.iv.167; AN.v.70; Iti.12, Iti.98; Ja.i.151; Ja.v.150; Pp.25; Pv-a.145; Thag-a.104.</p><p>anu + <em>grah</em></p><p>Anuggaha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>adjective not taking up Snp.912 (= na gaṇhāti Mnd.330).</p><p>an + uggaha</p>

anuggahesi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuggaṇhāti">anuggaṇhāti</a></p>

anuggahetabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuggahita">anuggahita</a></p>

anuggahetvā|anuggahetvaa|anuggahetva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuggahetvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uggahetvā">uggahetvā</a></p>

anuggahi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuggaṇhāti">anuggaṇhāti</a></p>

anuggahita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>anuggahita<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted -->anuggahīta</p><p>pp mfn. made happy; satisfied; helped, furthered</p><p>anuggahita<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>neg. mfn.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuggaṇhāti">anuggaṇhāti</a>, <a href="bword://uggahita">uggahita</a></p>

anuggahitacitta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not grasping in one’s thoughts</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuggahita">anuggahita</a></p>

anuggahāpenta|anuggahaapenta|anuggahapenta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mf</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuggahaapenta</span></p><p>(~entī)n.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuggaṇhāpeti">anuggaṇhāpeti</a></p>

anuggahāpesi|anuggahaapesi|anuggahapesi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuggahaapesi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuggaṇhāpeti">anuggaṇhāpeti</a></p>

anuggahāpeti|anuggahaapeti|anuggahapeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuggahaapeti</span></p><p>causes (someone) to help, to favor</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuggaṇhāti">anuggaṇhāti</a></p>

anuggahāya|anuggahaaya|anuggahaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuggahaaya</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uggaṇhāti">uggaṇhāti</a></p>

anuggahīta|anuggahiita|anuggahita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuggahiita</span></p><p>(&amp; ˚ita) commiserated, made happy, satisfied MN.i.457; SN.ii.274; SN.iii.91; SN.iv.263; AN.iii.172; Ja.iii.428.</p><p>pp. of anuggaṇhāti</p>

anuggata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>anuggata<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>mfn. arisen along with.</p><p>anuggata<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>neg mfn. not risen; not high</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uggata">uggata</a></p>

anuggaṇha|anugga.nha|anugganha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugga.nha</span></p><p>adjective compassionate, ready to help Pv-a.42 ˚sīla.</p><p>cp. anuggaha</p>

anuggaṇhana|anugga.nhana|anugganhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugga.nhana</span></p><p>anuggaha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --> Dhs-a.403. Anu(g)ganhati</p>

anuggaṇhanta|anugga.nhanta|anugganhanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugga.nhanta</span></p><p>anuggaṇhanta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>part. pr. mf(~antī)n.</p><p>anuggaṇhanta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>neg. mfn.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuggaṇhāti">anuggaṇhāti</a>, <a href="bword://uggaṇhanta">uggaṇhanta</a></p>

anuggaṇhataka|anugga.nhataka|anugganhataka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugga.nhataka</span></p><p>adjective compassionate, commiserating, helping Pv-a.69 (= anukampaka).</p><p>= anugganha</p>

anuggaṇhāpeti|anugga.nhaapeti|anugganhapeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugga.nhaapeti</span></p><p>causes (someone) to help, to favor</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuggaṇhāti">anuggaṇhāti</a></p>

anuggaṇhāti|anugga.nhaati|anugganhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugga.nhaati</span></p><p>favors, treats with kindness; protects, helps; acknowledges, admits.</p>

anuggaṇhāti|anugga.nhaati|anugganhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugga.nhaati</span></p><p>Also written as: Anuggaṇhāti</p><p>to have pity on, to feel sorry for, to help, give protection DN.i.53 (vācaṃ; cp. DN-a.i.160: sārato agaṇhaṇto); Ja.ii.74; Cnd.50 (ppr. med <em>-gayhamāna</em> = anukampamāna); Pp.36; Pv-a.181 (imper. <em><a href="bword://anugga%E1%B9%87ha">anuggaṇha</a></em> = anukampassu). pp. <em><a href="bword://anuggah%C4%ABta">anuggahīta</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + gaṇhāti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuggaṇha">anuggaṇha</a>, <a href="bword://anuggahīta">anuggahīta</a></p>

anugghāta|anugghaata|anugghata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugghaata</span></p><p>not shaking, a steady walk Ja.vi.253.</p><p>an + ugghāta</p>

anugghātin|anugghaatin|anugghatin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugghaatin</span></p><p>adjective not shaking, not jerking, Ja.vi.252; Vv.5#3 (read ˚ī for i); Vv-a.36.</p><p>fr. last</p>

anugghāṭeti|anugghaa.teti|anugghateti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugghaa.teti</span></p><p>not to unfasten or open (a door) Mil.371 (kavāṭaṃ).</p><p>an + ugghāṭeti</p>

anuggāhaka|anuggaahaka|anuggahaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mf</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuggaahaka</span></p><p>(-ikā)n. helping; furthering.</p>

anuggāhaka|anuggaahaka|anuggahaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuggaahaka</span></p><p>adjective helping, assisting SN.iii.5; SN.v.162; Mil.354 (nt. = help).</p><p>fr. anuggaha</p>

anugharakaṃ|anugharaka.m|anugharakam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugharaka.m</span></p><p>to each house; from house to house.</p>

anughāyati|anughaayati|anughayati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anughaayati</span></p><p>to smell, snuff, sniff up Mil.343 (gandhaṃ).</p><p>anu + ghāyati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p>

anugiddha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>greedy after, coveting</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anugijjhati">anugijjhati</a></p>

anugiddha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>greedy after, hankering after, desiring, coveting Snp.86 (anânu˚), Snp.144, Snp.952; Thag.580.</p><p>pp. of anugijjhati</p>

anugijjhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>covets, is greedy after.</p>

anugijjhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to be greedy after, to covet Snp.769 (cp. Mnd.12); Ja.iii.207; Ja.iv.4 (= giddhā gathitā hutvā allīyanti C.). pp. <em>-giddhā</em> (q.v.). Cp. abhigijjhati.</p><p>anu + gijjhati</p>

anugāhati|anugaahati|anugahati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugaahati</span></p><p>to plunge into, to enter (acc.) Sdhp.611.</p><p>anu + gāhati</p>

anugāmika|anugaamika|anugamika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugaamika</span></p><p>adjective going along with, following, accompanying; resulting from, consequential on Kp.viii.8 (<em><a href="bword://nidhi">nidhi</a></em> a treasure acc. a man to the next world); Ja.iv.280 (<em>-nidhi</em>); Mil.159 (parisā); Pv-a.132, Pv-a.253 (dānaṃ nāma ˚aṃ nidānan ti).</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nidhi">nidhi</a></p>

anugāmin|anugaamin|anugamin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugaamin</span></p><p>adjective following, attending on; an attendant, follower Snp-a.453 (= anuyutta).</p><p>fr. anugacchati</p>

anugāra|anugaara|anugara
<p>[DPPN]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugaara</span></p><p>An eminent wandering ascetic. He is mentioned as living in the Paribbājakārāma in the Moranivāpa in Veḷuvana near Rājagaha. He was probably one of the company who was with Sakuludāyi when the Buddha came to visit the latter. MN.ii.1</p>

anugāyati|anugaayati|anugayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugaayati</span></p><p>sings after; repeats in verse; recites (a text or hymn); praises.</p>

anugāyati|anugaayati|anugayati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugaayati</span></p><p>to sing after or to, recite (a magic formula or hymn) praise, celebrate DN.i.104, DN.i.238; Snp.1131 (anugāyissaṃ); Mil.120.</p><p>anu + gāyati</p>

anugīyati|anugiiyati|anugiyati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pass. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anugiiyati</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anugāyati">anugāyati</a></p>

anuhasati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to laugh at, to ridicule DN-a.i.256.</p><p>anu + hasati</p>

anuhīramāna|anuhiiramaana|anuhiramana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuhiiramaana</span></p><p>being held over.</p>

anuhīrati|anuhiirati|anuhirati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuhiirati</span></p><p>to be held up over, ppr. <em><a href="bword://anuh%C4%ABram%C4%81na">anuhīramāna</a></em> DN.ii.15 (vv.ll. variant reading anubhiram˚ glosses B. K. anudhāriyam˚, cp. Trenckner, <em>Notes</em> 79).</p><p>for ˚hariyati, anu + <em>hṛ</em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuhīramāna">anuhīramāna</a></p>

anujagghanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anujagghati">anujagghati</a></p>

anujagghati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>laughs at; mocks</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anojagghati">anojagghati</a></p>

anujagghati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to laugh at, deride, mock DN.i.91; DN-a.i.258 (cp. sañjagghati ibid 256).</p><p>anu + jagghati</p>

anujavati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to run after, to hasten after, to follow Ja.vi.452 (= anubandhati).</p><p>anu + javati</p>

anujjhāna|anujjhaana|anujjhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujjhaana</span></p><p>meditation, reflection, introspection Mil.352 (˚bahula).</p><p>anu + jhāna</p>

anujju
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective not straight, crooked, bent, in compounds <em>-aṅgin</em> (anujjangin) with (evenly) bent limbs, i.e. with perfect limbs, graceful f. <em>-ī</em>. Epithet of a beautiful woman Ja.v.40 (= kañcana-sannibha-sarīrā C.); Ja.vi.500 (T. anuccangī C. aninditā agarahitangī); <em>-gāmin</em> going crooked i.e. snake Ja.iv.330; <em>-bhūta</em> not upright (fig. of citta Ja.v.293.</p><p>an + ujju</p>

anujjuka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not straight, crooked, curved; crafty</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ujjuka">ujjuka</a></p>

anujjuka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>= anujju Ja.iii.318.</p>

anujuka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not straight, crooked, curved; crafty</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ujuka">ujuka</a></p>

anujāneti|anujaaneti|anujaneti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujaaneti</span></p><p>asks for or obtains permission or approval; asks leave</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anujānāti">anujānāti</a></p>

anujāneyya|anujaaneyya|anujaneyya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">opt. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujaaneyya</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anujānāti">anujānāti</a></p>

anujānitabba|anujaanitabba|anujanitabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn. id.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujaanitabba</span></p><p>worthy of approval; allowable</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anujānāti">anujānāti</a></p>

anujānāti|anujaanaati|anujanati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujaanaati</span></p><p>gives permission; grants, allows; grants leave; excuses; advises; prescribes.</p>

anujānāti|anujaanaati|anujanati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujaanaati</span></p><ol><li>to give permission, grant, allow Vin.iv.225; AN.ii.197; Pv.iv.1#67; Pv-a.55, Pv-a.79 Pv-a.142.</li><li>to advise, prescribe Vin.i.83; Vin.ii.301: Snp.982. grd. <em>anuññeyya</em> that which is allowed AN.ii.197; pp <em><a href="bword://anu%C3%B1%C3%B1%C4%81ta">anuññāta</a></em> (q.v.) Caus. <em>anujānāpeti</em> Ja.i.156.</li></ol><p>anu + jānāti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuññāta">anuññāta</a></p>

anujāta|anujaata|anujata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujaata</span></p><p>like, resembling; taking after, following the example of (one’s parents or teacher).</p>

anujāta|anujaata|anujata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujaata</span></p><p>adjective “born after” i.e. after the image of, resembling, taking after; esp. said of a son (putta), resembling his father, a worthy son Iti.64 (atijāta + opp. avajāta); Thag.827 (fig. following the example of) 1279; Ja.vi.380; Dhp-a.i.129; Dāvs ii.66.</p><p>anu + jāta</p>

anujāñña|anujaa~n~na|anujanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">opt. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujaa~n~na</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anujānāti">anujānāti</a></p>

anujīvati|anujiivati|anujivati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujiivati</span></p><p>to live after, i.e. like (acc.), to live for or on, subsist by Ja.iv.271 (= upajīvati, tassânubhāvena jīvitaṃ laddhaṃ (Comm.)<br />pp <em>anujīvata</em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + jīvati</p>

anujīvi|anujiivi|anujivi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. &amp; m. (mfn.)</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujiivi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anujīvin">anujīvin</a></p><p>living upon; dependent; (m.) a follower, a dependent.</p>

anujīvin|anujiivin|anujivin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. &amp; m. (mfn.)</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujiivin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anujīvin">anujīvin</a></p><p>living upon; dependent; (m.) a follower, a dependent.</p>

anujīvin|anujiivin|anujivin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujiivin</span></p><p>adjective noun living upon, another, dependent; a follower, a dependant AN.i.152; AN.iii.44; Ja.iii.485; Dāvs v.43.</p><p>fr. anujīvati</p>

anujīvita|anujiivita|anujivita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujiivita</span></p><p>living after, living according to.</p>

anujīvita|anujiivita|anujivita
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anujiivita</span></p><p>living (after), living, livelihood, subsistence, life Snp.836 (= jīvitaṃ Snp-a.545).</p><p>pp. of anujīvati</p>

anukampa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anukampat">anukampat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukampati">anukampati</a></p>

anukampaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mf</i></p><p>(~ā &amp; -ikā)n. kind, caring, compassionate.</p>

anukampaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">&amp;</i></p><p>˚ika (adj.) kind of heart, merciful, compassionate, full of pity (-˚ or c. loc.) DN.iii.187; SN.i.105 (loka˚), SN.i.197; SN.v.157; AN.iv.265 sq.; Iti.66 (sabba-bhūta˚); Pv.i.3#3 (= kārunika Pv-a.16), Pv.i.5#3 (atthakāma, hitesin Pv-a.25), Pv.i.8#8; Pv.ii.1#4 (= anuggaṇhataka Pv-a.69), Pv.ii.2#7; Thag-a.174; Pv-a.196 (satthā sattesu a.).</p><p>fr. anukampati</p>

anukampamāna|anukampamaana|anukampamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukampamaana</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukampati">anukampati</a></p>

anukampana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>compassion, pity Pv-a.16, Pv-a.88.</p><p>fr. last</p>

anukampanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mf</i></p><p>(~antī)n.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukampati">anukampati</a></p>

anukampat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anukampat">anukampat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukampati">anukampati</a></p>

anukampata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine abstr.</i></p><p>compassion, kindness</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukampā">anukampā</a></p>

anukampati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>takes pity on; cares for; commiserates, sympathizes with (acc. or gen.).</p>

anukampati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to have pity on, to commiserate, to pity, to sympathise with (c. acc.) SN.i.82, SN.i.206 SN.v.189. Imper. <em>anukampa</em> Pv.ii.1#6 (= anuddayaṃ karohi Pv-a.70) &amp; <em>anukampassu</em> Pv.iii.2#8 (= anuggaṇha Pv-a.181). Med. ppr. <em>anukampamāna</em> Snp.37 (= anupekkhamāna anugayhamāna Cnd.50); Pv-a.35 (taṃ), Pv-a.62 (pitaraṃ), Pv-a.104<br />pp <em><a href="bword://anukampita">anukampita</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + kampati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukampita">anukampita</a></p>

anukampi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukampati">anukampati</a></p>

anukampin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anukampin">anukampin</a></p><p>compassionate; sympathizing with.</p>

anukampin
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective compassionate, anxious for, commiserating. Only in foll. phrases: <em>hita˚</em>; full of solicitude for the welfare of SN.v.86; Snp.693; Pv.iii.7#6 <em>sabbapāṇa-bhūta-hita˚</em>; id. SN.iv.314; AN.ii.210; AN.iii.92 AN.iv.249; Pp.57, Pp.68. <em>sabba-bhūta˚</em>; SN.i.25, SN.i.110; AN.ii.9; Iti.102.</p><p>cp. anukampaka</p>

anukampita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>favored; pitied; treated with compassion</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukampati">anukampati</a></p>

anukampita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective compassioned, gratified, remembered, having done a good deed (of mercy Pv.iii.2#30.</p><p>pp. of anukampati</p>

anukampā|anukampaa|anukampa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukampaa</span></p><p>compassion, pity, mercy; kindness.</p>

anukampā|anukampaa|anukampa
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukampaa</span></p><p>compassion, pity, mercy DN.i.204; MN.i.161; MN.ii.113; SN.i.206; SN.ii.274 (loka˚), SN.iv.323; SN.v.259 sq.; AN.i.64, AN.i.92; AN.ii.159; AN.iii.49; AN.iv.139 Pp.35<br />■ Often in abl. <em>anukampāya</em> out of pity, for the sake of DN.iii.211 (loka˚ out of compassion for all mankind, + atthaya hitāya); Ja.iii.280; Pv-a.47, Pv-a.147.</p><p>abstr. fr. anukampati</p>

anukantati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>cuts.</p>

anukantati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to cut Dhp.311 (hatthaṃ = phāleti Dhp-a.iii.484).</p><p>anu + kantati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p>

anukaronti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 plural</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukaroti">anukaroti</a></p>

anukaroti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>does after; imitates, emulates; equals (gen. of person); follows.</p>

anukaroti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to imitate, “to do after” AN.i.212; Ja.i.491; Ja.ii.162; Dhp-a.iv.197<br />ppr <em>anukabbaṃ</em> Vin.ii.201 (mamâ˚)<br />■ Med. <em><a href="bword://anukubbati">anukubbati</a></em> SN.i.19 = Ja.iv.65. See also anukubba. On <em><a href="bword://anvak%C4%81si">anvakāsi</a></em> see <em><a href="bword://anukassati">anukassati</a></em> 2.</p><p>anu + <em>kṛ</em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukubbati">anukubbati</a>, <a href="bword://anvakāsi">anvakāsi</a>, <a href="bword://anukassati">anukassati</a></p>

anukassati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>[Sk. anukaṛṣati] to draw after, to repeat, recite, quote DN.ii.255 (silokaṃ).</li><li>[Sk. <em>ava-</em> kaṛṣati] to draw or take of, to remove, throw down, Thag.869 (aor. <em><a href="bword://anvak%C4%81si">anvakāsi</a></em> = khipi, chaḍḍesi C.).</li></ol><p>anu + kassati, <em>kṛṣ</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvakāsi">anvakāsi</a></p>

anukassāmi|anukassaami|anukassami
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fut. 1 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukassaami</span></p><p>I will recite, I will quote.</p>

anukaṅkhin|anuka"nkhin|anukankhin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuka"nkhin</span></p><p>adjective striving after, longing for Ja.v.499 (piya˚).</p><p>fr. anu + <em>kāṅkṣ</em></p>

anukhaṇati|anukha.nati|anukhanati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukha.nati</span></p><p>to dig after or further Ja.v.233.</p><p>anu + khaṇati</p>

anukhuddaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective in cpd. <em>khudda˚</em>; whatever there is of minor things, all less important items Vin.ii.287 = DN.ii.154 = Mil.142; Mil.144.</p><p>anu + khuddaka</p>

anukiṇṇa|anuki.n.na|anukinna
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuki.n.na</span></p><p>strewn with, beset with, dotted all over Pv.iv.12#1 (bhamara-gaṇa˚).</p><p>pp. of anu + kirati</p>

anukkama
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>an element in the training of horses.</p>

anukkama
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>order, turn, succession, going along; only in instr. <strong>anukkamena</strong> gradually, in due course or succession Ja.i.157, Ja.i.262, Ja.i.290; Vv-a.157; Pv-a.5, Pv-a.14, Pv-a.35 etc.</li><li>that which keeps an animal in (regular step, i.e. a bridle MN.i.446; Snp.622 (sandānaṃ saha˚).</li></ol><p>to anukkamati</p><p>See also: anukkamena</p>

anukkamamāna|anukkamamaana|anukkamamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukkamamaana</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukkamati">anukkamati</a></p>

anukkamat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anukkamat">anukkamat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukkamati">anukkamati</a></p>

anukkamati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>goes after, follow; treads upon.</p>

anukkamati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>to follow, go along (a path = acc.) AN.v.195; Iti.80 (maggaṃ).</li><li>to advance (not with Morris J.P.T.S. 1886, 111 as “abandon”) SN.i.24 Thag.194.</li></ol><p>anu + <em>kram</em></p>

anukkaṇṭhana|anukka.n.thana|anukkanthana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukka.n.thana</span></p><p>having no lack anything, being contented or happy Ja.vi.4.</p><p>an + ukkaṇṭhana</p>

anukkaṇṭhati|anukka.n.thati|anukkanthati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukka.n.thati</span></p><p>not to be sorry or not to lack anything, in ppr. <em>-anto</em> Ja.v.10; and pp. <em>-ita</em> without regret or in plenty Pv-a.13.</p><p>an + ukkaṇṭhati</p>

anukkaṭṭhita|anukka.t.thita|anukkatthita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukka.t.thita</span></p><p>not boiling</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ukkaṭṭhita">ukkaṭṭhita</a></p>

anukkhepa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>throwing back; compensation.</p>

anukkhepa
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>compensation Vin.i.285.</p><p>anu + khepa, see <em><a href="bword://anukkhipati">anukkhipati</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukkhipati">anukkhipati</a></p>

anukkhipanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>throwing away; rejecting; dismissing</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ukkhipati">ukkhipati</a></p>

anukkhipati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to throw out Cp.xi.6 (vaṭṭaṃ).</p><p>anu + khipati</p>

anukkhittaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>who has not been suspended</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ukkhittaka">ukkhittaka</a></p>

anukubba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anukubbat">anukubbat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukaroti">anukaroti</a></p>

anukubba
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective (-˚) “doing correspondingly” giving back, retaliating Ja.ii.205 (kicca˚)</p><p>= Sk. anukurvat, ppr. of anukaroti</p>

anukubbanti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 plural</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukaroti">anukaroti</a></p>

anukubbat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anukubbat">anukubbat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukaroti">anukaroti</a></p>

anukubbati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>see <em><a href="bword://anukaroti">anukaroti</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukaroti">anukaroti</a></p>

anukula
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>freq. spelling for <em><a href="bword://anuk%C5%ABla">anukūla</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukūla">anukūla</a></p>

anukulaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective = anukula Sdhp.242 (iccha˚ according to wish).</p>

anukulayañña|anukulaya~n~na|anukulayanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukulaya~n~na</span></p><p>or neuter (being) an offering according to family custom</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anukulaṃ">anukulaṃ</a></p>

anukulaṃ|anukula.m|anukulam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukula.m</span></p><p>in each family; according to custom.</p>

anukulesu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i></p><p>in each family; according to custom.</p>

anukāma|anukaama|anukama
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukaama</span></p><p>adjective responding to love, loving in return Ja.ii.157.</p><p>anu + kāma</p>

anukāra|anukaara|anukara
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukaara</span></p><p>imitation Dpvs.v.39.</p><p>cp. anukaroti</p>

anukārin|anukaarin|anukarin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukaarin</span></p><p>adjective imitating Dāvs v.32.</p>

anukūla|anukuula|anukula
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anukuula</span></p><p>adjective favourable, agreeable, suitable, pleasant Vv-a.280; spelt anukula at Sdhp.297, Sdhp.312.</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://bhava">bhava</a></em> complaisance, willingness Vva.71.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://ya%C3%B1%C3%B1a">yañña</a></em> a propitiative sacrifice DN.i.144 (expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> at DN-a.i.302 as anukula˚ = sacrifice for the propagation of the clan).</li></ul><p>anu + kūla, opp. paṭikūla</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://bhava">bhava</a>, <a href="bword://yañña">yañña</a></p>

anulapanā|anulapanaa|anulapana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anulapanaa</span></p><p>scolding, blame, accusation Vin.ii.88 (spelt anullapanā; comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with anuvadana &amp; anubhaṇanā).</p><p>anu + lapanā, <em>lap</em></p>

anulepa
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>anointing Mil.152.</p><p>fr. anu + <em>lip</em></p>

anulimpana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>anointing Mil.353, Mil.394.</p><p>fr. anulimpati</p>

anulimpati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to anoint, besmear, Mil.394 (˚limpitabba). Caus. <em>-limpeti</em> in same meaning Mil.169 and <em>-lepeti</em> Mil.169 (grd. <em>-lepanīya</em> to be treated with ointment)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://anulitta">anulitta</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + limpati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anulitta">anulitta</a></p>

anulitta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective anointed, besmeared Ja.i.266; Pv-a.211.</p><p>cp. Sk. anulipta, pp. of anulimpati</p>

anullapanā|anullapanaa|anullapana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anullapanaa</span></p><p>approbation, complimentary speech.</p>

anulokin
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective looking (up) at, seeing (-˚) MN.i.147 (sīsa˚).</p><p>fr. anu + loketi, cp. Sk. &amp; P. avalokin &amp; anuviloketi</p>

anuloma-citta
<p>[Nyana]</p><p></p><p><strong>Anuloma-citta:</strong> ‘adaptation-moment of consciousness’, denotes the third of the 4 moments of impulsion <em>javana</em> flashing up immediately before either reaching the absorptions <em>jhāna</em> or the supra-mundane paths see: <em>ariya-puggala</em>. These 4 moments of impulsion are: the preparation <em>parikamma</em>, access <em>upacāra</em>, adaptation <em>anuloma</em> and change-of-lineage <em>gotrabhū</em> moments. For further details see: <em>javana</em> <em>gotrabhū</em></p>

anuloma
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mf</i></p><p>(~ī?)n. n. &amp; masculine ‘with the hair’, in a natural direction or order; suitable,</p><ol><li>(mfn.) fit; in accordance with.</li><li>(n.m.) direct order, natural order; conformity, affirmation.</li></ol>

anuloma
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective “with the hair or grain”, i.e. in natural order, suitable, fit, adapted to, adaptable straight forward DN.ii.273 (anānuloma, q.v.) SN.iv.401; Pts.ii.67, Pts.ii.70; Dhp-a.ii.208<br />■ nt. direct order, state of fitting in, adaptation Mil.148.</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://%C3%B1%C4%81%E1%B9%87a">ñāṇa</a></em> insight of adaptation (cp. <em>Cpd.</em> 66, 68) Dhp-a.ii.208.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://pa%E1%B9%ADiloma">paṭiloma</a></em> in regular order &amp; reversed, forward backward (Ep. of paṭiccasamuppāda, also in BSk.) Vin.i.1; AN.iv.448.</li></ul><p>Sk. anu + loma</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ñāṇa">ñāṇa</a>, <a href="bword://paṭiloma">paṭiloma</a></p>

anuloma-ñāna|anuloma-~naana|anuloma-nana
<p>[Nyana]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuloma-~naana</span></p><p><strong>Anuloma-ñāna:</strong> ‘adaptation-knowledge’ or conformity-knowledge, is identical with the ‘adaptation-to-truth knowledge’, the last of 9 insight-knowledges <em>vipassanā</em> - <em>ñāna</em> which constitute the purification of knowledge and vision of the path -progress’ see: <em>visuddhi</em> VI, 9. Cf. Vis.M XXI.</p>

anulomapaṭilena|anulomapa.tilena|anulomapatilena
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">instr. adv.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anulomapa.tilena</span></p><p>in direct and reversed order, forwards and backwards:</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuloma">anuloma</a></p>

anulomapaṭilomaṃ|anulomapa.tiloma.m|anulomapatilomam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">acc. adv.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anulomapa.tiloma.m</span></p><p>in direct and reversed order, forwards and backwards:</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuloma">anuloma</a></p>

anulomayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>bends with; conforms to, is in accordance (with, acc. or gen.); sets right, puts in proper order</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anulometi">anulometi</a></p>

anulomaṃ|anuloma.m|anulomam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">adv.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuloma.m</span></p><p>in a natural order; forwards</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuloma">anuloma</a></p>

anulometi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>bends with; conforms to, is in accordance (with, acc. or gen.); sets right, puts in proper order</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anulomayati">anulomayati</a></p>

anulometi
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to conform to, to be in accordance with Mil.372.</p><p>v. denom. fr. anuloma</p>

anulomika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. &amp; neuter</i></p><ol><li>(mfn.) suitableagreeable; in accordance.</li><li>(n.) conformity; that which accords.</li></ol>

anulomika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(&amp; <em>-ya</em>) adjective suitable, fit, agreeable; in proper order, adapted to (-˚) Vin.ii.7 (an˚), Vin.iii.120 (an˚ = ananucchaviya); Vin.iv.239; AN.i.106; AN.iii.116 sq.; Iti.103 (sāmaññassa˚); Snp.385 (pabbajita˚); Kp-a.243 (ananulomiya); Dhs-a.25; Sdhp.65.</p><p>fr. anuloma</p>

anuma
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(-dassika) see *<a href="bword://anoma">anoma</a>*˚.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anoma">anoma</a></p>

anumagge
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>at Ja.v.201 should be read <em>anu magge</em> along the road, by the way; anu here used as prep. c. loc (see <em><a href="bword://anu">anu</a></em> A b).</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anu">anu</a></p>

anumajjana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>threshing out, pounding up (<em>Dhs. trsl.</em> 11), always used with ref. to the term <em><a href="bword://vic%C4%81ra">vicāra</a></em> (q.v.) Mil.62; Dhs-a.114; DN-a.i.63, DN-a.i.122.</p><p>abstr. fr. anumajjati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://vicāra">vicāra</a></p>

anumajjanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mf</i></p><p>(~antī)n.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumajjati">anumajjati</a></p>

anumajjati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>rubs, wipes; beats; applies (continuous) pressureconsiders thoroughly.</p>

anumajjati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>to strike along, to stroke, to touch DN-a.i.276 (= anumasati).</li><li>to beat, thresh fig. to thresh ont Ja.vi.548; Mil.90</li></ol><p>pass <em>anumajjīyati</em> Mil.275 (cp. p. 428).</p><p>anu + majjati</p>

anumajjha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective mediocre, without going to extremes Ja.iv.192; Ja.v.387.</p><p>anu + majjha</p>

anumajjitvā|anumajjitvaa|anumajjitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anumajjitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumajjati">anumajjati</a></p>

anumasati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>touches; takes hold of (to examine); considers, examines.</p>

anumasati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to touch DN.i.106 (= anumajjati DN-a.i.276).</p><p>anu + masati</p>

anumasi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumasati">anumasati</a></p>

anumassa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i></p><p>examining each point; point by point</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumasati">anumasati</a></p>

anumata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>approved, consented to; permitted</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumaññati">anumaññati</a></p>

anumata
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>approved of, given consent to, finding approval, given leave DN.i.99 (= anuññāta DN-a.i.267); Ja.v.399 (= muta); Mil.185, Mil.212, Mil.231, Mil.275; Pv-a.64 (= annuññāta).</p><p>pp. of anumaññati</p>

anumati
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>consent, permission, agreement, assent, approval Vin.ii.294, Vin.ii.301, Vin.ii.306; DN.i.137 DN.i.143; Dpvs.iv.47, Cf. Dpvs.v.18; DN-a.i.297; Vv-a.17, Pv-a.114.</p><p>from anumaññati</p>

anumatikappa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>the practice of carrying out a formal act without a quorum, intending to ratify it later.</p>

anumatipakkha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine a</i></p><p>consenting party.</p>

anumatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>see *<a href="bword://a%E1%B9%87u">aṇu</a>*˚.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://aṇu">aṇu</a></p>

anumaññati|anuma~n~nati|anumannati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuma~n~nati</span></p><p>assents to; approves; gives leave.</p>

anumaññati|anuma~n~nati|anumannati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuma~n~nati</span></p><p>to assent, approve, give leave Thag.72<br />pp <em><a href="bword://anumata">anumata</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + maññati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumata">anumata</a></p>

anuminitabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>will have drawn an inference, concluded.</p>

anumināti|anuminaati|anuminati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuminaati</span></p><p>to observe, draw an inference MN.i.97; Pv-a.227 (˚anto + <em>nayaṃ nento</em>). See also anumīyati.</p><p>cf. Sk. anumāti, anu + mināti from <em>mi</em>, Sk. minoti, with confusion of roots <em>mā &amp; mi;</em></p>

anumitta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i></p><p>secondary friend, a follower. acquaintance Ja.v.77.</p><p>anu + mitta</p>

anummatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective not out of mind, sane, of sound mind Mil.122; Sdhp.205.</p><p>an + ummatta</p>

anummattaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mf</i></p><p>(-ikā)n. not distracted; not insane</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ummattaka">ummattaka</a></p>

anumodaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>who gives thanks; who gives approvals.</p>

anumodaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective one who enjoys, one who is glad of or thankful for (c. acc.) Vin.v.172; Pv-a.122; Sdhf.512.</p><p>fr. anumodati</p>

anumodamāna|anumodamaana|anumodamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anumodamaana</span></p><p>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumodati">anumodati</a></p>

anumodana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter \~ā, feminine</i></p><p>approval, assent; thanks, expression of appreciation (esp. in the form of a discourse by <em>bhikkhus</em> after receiving a meal or gifts)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumodaniya">anumodaniya</a></p>

anumodana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>“according to taste”, i.e. satisfaction, thanks, esp. after a meal or after receiving gifts = to say grace or benediction, blessing, thanksgiving. In latter sense with <em>dadāti</em> (give thanks for = locative) karoti (= Latin gratias agere) or <em>vacati</em> (say or tell thanks) ˚ṁ <em>datvā</em> Pv-a.89 ˚ṁ <em>katvā</em> Ja.i.91 Dhp-a.iii.170 Dhp-a.iii.172.Vv-a 118 Pv-a.17 Pv-a.47; ˚ṁ <em>vatvā</em> Vv-a.40 (pānīyadāne for the gift of water), Vv-a.295, Vv-a.306 etc. ˚ṁ <em>karoti</em> also “to do a favour” Pv-a.275 cp. further Dhp-a.i.198 (˚gāthā verses expressing thanks, benediction); Dhp-a.ii.97 (Satthāraṁ ˚ṁ yāciṁsu asked his blessing) Pv-a.23 (˚atthaṁ in order to thank), Pv-a.26 (identical), Pv-a.121, Pv-a.141 (katabhatta˚), Pv-a.142; Sdhp.213 Sdhp.218 Sdhp.516</p><p>fr. anumodati</p>

anumodaniya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>thanks; expression of appreciation</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumodanīya">anumodanīya</a></p>

anumodanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumodati">anumodati</a></p>

anumodanīya|anumodaniiya|anumodaniya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anumodaniiya</span></p><p>thanks; expression of appreciation</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumodaniya">anumodaniya</a></p>

anumodati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>rejoices in, approves; thanks; gives thanks (esp. with a benediction or discourse, see anumodana).</p>

anumodati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to find satisfaction in (acc.), to rejoice in, be thankful for (c. acc.), appreciate, benefit from, to be pleased, to enjoy Vin.ii.212 (bhattagge a. to say grace after a meal); SN.ii.54; AN.iii.50 (<em>-modanīya</em>), AN.iv.411; Dhp.177 (ppr. <em>-modamāna</em>); Iti.78; Pv.ii.9#19 (dānaṃ <em>-modamāna</em> = enjoying, gladly receiving); Pv.i.5#4 (anumodare = are pleased; pitisomanassajātā honti Pv-a.27); Ja.ii.112; Pv-a.19, Pv-a.46, Pv-a.81, Pv-a.201) imper. <em>modāhi</em>) Sdhp.501 sq<br />pp <em><a href="bword://anumodita">anumodita</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + modati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumodita">anumodita</a></p>

anumodita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anumoditar">anumoditar</a></p><p>(from anumodati), one who rejoices in, one who approves.</p>

anumodita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>enjoyed, rejoiced in Pv-a.77.</p><p>pp. of anumodati</p>

anumoditabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn. &amp; n. impers.</i></p><p>in, one who approves.</p>

anumoditar
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anumoditar">anumoditar</a></p><p>(from anumodati), one who rejoices in, one who approves.</p>

anumoditvā|anumoditvaa|anumoditva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anumoditvaa</span></p><p>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumodati">anumodati</a></p>

anumodiṃsu|anumodi.msu|anumodimsu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 plural</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anumodi.msu</span></p><p>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumodati">anumodati</a></p>

anumāna|anumaana|anumana
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anumaana</span></p><p>inference Mil.330 (<em><a href="bword://naya">naya</a></em> +), Mil.372, Mil.413; Sdhp.74.</p><p>fr. anu + <em>man</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://naya">naya</a></p>

anumāssa|anumaassa|anumassa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anumaassa</span></p><p>examining each point; point by point</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anumasati">anumasati</a></p>

anumīyati|anumiiyati|anumiyati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pass. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anumiiyati</span></p><p>infers; concludes.</p>

anumīyati|anumiiyati|anumiyati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anumiiyati</span></p><p>to observe, conclude or infer from SN.iii.36 Cp. anumināti.</p><p>Sk. anumīyate, Pass. of anu + <em><a href="bword://m%C4%81">mā</a></em>, measure, in sense of Med.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://mā">mā</a></p>

anunadī|anunadii|anunadi
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anunadii</span></p><p>(-tire) along the bank of the river SN.iv.177 should be read anu nadītīre (= anu prep. c. loc.; see under <em><a href="bword://anu">anu</a></em> A).</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anu">anu</a></p>

anunadītīre|anunadiitiire|anunaditire
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anunadiitiire</span></p><p>along the bank of the river.</p>

anunamati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to incline, bend (intrs.), give way Mil.372 (of a bow).</p><p>anu + namati</p>

anunaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>affection, inclination towards; winning over, conciliation.</p>

anunaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>“leading along”, friendliness, courtesy, falling in with, fawning DN.iii.254 (˚saṃyojana); AN.iv.7 sq (id.) MN.i.191; Dhs.1059; Vb.145; Ne.79; comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> w opp. <em><a href="bword://pa%E1%B9%ADigha">paṭigha</a></em> (repugnance) at Mil.44, Mil.122, Mil.322.</p><p>fr. anuneti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://paṭigha">paṭigha</a></p>

anunayamāna|anunayamaana|anunayamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anunayamaana</span></p><p>leading; conciliating; supplicating, persuading.</p>

anunayana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>fawning Dhs-a.362.</p><p>fr. anuneti</p>

anunenta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mf</i></p><p>(~entī)n. leading; conciliating; supplicating, persuading.</p>

anuneta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anunetar">anunetar</a></p><p>one who leads or persuades or conciliates.</p>

anunetar
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anunetar">anunetar</a></p><p>one who leads or persuades or conciliates.</p>

anunetar
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>one who reconciles or conciliates Pts.ii.194 (netā vinetā anunetā).</p><p>n. ag. fr. anuneti</p>

anuneti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to conciliate, appease, win over, flatter SN.i.232 (ppr. anunayamāna); pp. <em><a href="bword://anun%C4%ABta">anunīta</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + neti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anunīta">anunīta</a></p>

anunnala
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not boisterous; controlled</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://unnala">unnala</a></p>

anunnata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://unnata">unnata</a></p>

anunnaḷa|anunna.la|anunnala
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anunna.la</span></p><p>not boisterous; controlled</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://unnaḷa">unnaḷa</a></p>

anunnāmaninnāmi|anunnaamaninnaami|anunnamaninnami
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anunnaamaninnaami</span></p><p>level; even</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://unnāmaninnāmin">unnāmaninnāmin</a></p>

anunnāmininnāmi|anunnaamininnaami|anunnamininnami
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anunnaamininnaami</span></p><p>level; even</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://unnāmininnāmin">unnāmininnāmin</a></p>

anunāsika|anunaasika|anunasika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anunaasika</span></p><p>adjective nasal; as tt. g. the sound ṃ; in <em>-lopa</em> apocope of the nasal ṃ Vv-a.114 Vv-a.253, Vv-a.275, Vv-a.333.</p><p>anu + nāsā + ika</p>

anunīta|anuniita|anunita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuniita</span></p><p>adjective led, induced SN.iv.71; Snp.781.</p><p>pp. of anuneti</p>

anupa
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>see <em><a href="bword://an%C5%ABpa">anūpa</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anūpa">anūpa</a></p>

anupabandhanatā|anupabandhanataa|anupabandhanata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupabandhanataa</span></p><p>(anuppa˚) feminine nonstopping, not ceasing Mil.132.</p><p>abstr. to prec.</p>

anupabandhanā|anupabandhanaa|anupabandhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupabandhanaa</span></p><p>(anuppa˚) feminine continuance, incessance, Pp.18 = Vb.357 (in exegesis of upanāha).</p><p>abstr. fr. anupabandhati</p>

anupabandhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(anuppa˚) to follow immediately, to be incessant, to keep on (without stopping), to continue Mil.132<br />caus <em>-āpeti</em> ibid.</p><p>anu + pa + bandhati</p>

anupabbajati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>adopts the wanderer’s life after or in imitation (of another).</p>

anupabbajiṃsu|anupabbaji.msu|anupabbajimsu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 plural</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupabbaji.msu</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupabbajati">anupabbajati</a></p>

anupabbajjā|anupabbajjaa|anupabbajja
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupabbajjaa</span></p><p>giving up worldly life in imitation of another SN.v.67 = Iti.107</p><p>anu + pabbajjā, cp. BSk. anupravrajati Divy.61</p>

anupabbajā|anupabbajaa|anupabbaja
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupabbajaa</span></p><p>adopts the wanderer’s life after or in imitation (of another).</p>

anupacchinna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upacchinna">upacchinna</a></p>

anupacināti|anupacinaati|anupacinati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupacinaati</span></p><p>not to observe or notice Ja.v.339 (= anoloketi C.; variant reading anapaviṇāti).</p><p>an + upacināti</p>

anupacita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upacita">upacita</a></p>

anupacita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective heaped up, accumulated Thag-a.56.</p><p>anu + pa + cita, pp. of anupacināti</p>

anupada
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter a</i></p><p>following word; the following quarter-stanza.</p>

anupada
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>the “afterfoot”, i.e. second foot of a verse, also a mode of reciting where the second foot is recited without the first one Vin.iv.15 (cp. 355); Mil.340 (anupadena anupadaṃ katheti).</li><li>(adj.) (following) on foot, at every, step continuous, repeated, in ˚dhamma-vipassanā uninterrupted contemplation MN.iii.25; ˚vaṇṇanā word-by-word explanation Dhs-a.168. As nt. adv. <em>-ṃ</em> close behind, immediately after (c. gen.) Ja.ii.230 (tassânupadaṃ agamāsi), Ja.vi.422. Esp. freq. in comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> <em>padānupadaṃ</em> (adv.) foot after foot, i.e. in the footsteps, immediately behind Ja.iii.504; Ja.vi.555; Dhp-a.i.69; Dhp-a.ii.38.</li></ol><p>cp. Sk. anupadaṃ adv., anu + pada</p>

anupadajjeyya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">opt. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuppadeti">anuppadeti</a></p>

anupadajjeyyāsi|anupadajjeyyaasi|anupadajjeyyasi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">opt. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupadajjeyyaasi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuppadeti">anuppadeti</a></p>

anupaddava
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>free from misfortune or accident; safe; undamaged</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upaddava">upaddava</a></p>

anupaddava
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective free from danger, uninjured, safe Vin.ii.79 = Vin.ii.124 (+ anītika); Vin.iii.162; Dhp.338; Dhp-a.iv.48; Pv-a.250 (expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> for siva).</p><p>an + upaddava</p>

anupadduta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not assailed; free from distress or calamity</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upadduta">upadduta</a></p>

anupadeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>gives (in addition), hands over, provides; encourages, supports</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuppadeti">anuppadeti</a></p>

anupadeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(anuppadeti) to give out, give as a present, hand over; to design, set forth, undertake SN.iii.131 (Pot. anuppadajjuṃ); MN.i.416 (Pot. anupadajjeyya see <em><a href="bword://dad%C4%81ti">dadāti</a></em> i.3); Mil.210 (˚deti). fut. <em>-dassati</em> (see <em><a href="bword://dad%C4%81ti">dadāti</a></em> i.1); DN.iii.92; SN.iv.303 (variant reading SS for T. anusarissati); AN.iii.43; Snp.983. ger. <em>-datvā</em> Snp-a.35. inf <em>-dātuṃ</em> AN.i.117. pp. <em>-dinna</em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + pa + dadāti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://dadāti">dadāti</a>, <a href="bword://dadāti">dadāti</a></p>

anupadhika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>free from attachment; free from acquisitions (which lead to rebirth)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anūpadhīka">anūpadhīka</a></p>

anupadhika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective free from attachment (see <em><a href="bword://upadhi">upadhi</a></em>) Vin.i.36 (anupadhīka); DN.iii.112 (anupadhika opp. to sa-upadhika); Snp.1057 (anūpadhīka T. but Nd ii.anūpadhika. with ū for u metri causa).</p><p>an + upadhi + ka</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upadhi">upadhi</a></p>

anupadhāreti|anupadhaareti|anupadhareti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupadhaareti</span></p><p>to disregard, to heed not, to neglect Dhp-a.iv.197; Vv-a.260.</p><p>an + upadhār˚</p>

anupadinna
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(anuppadinna) given, handed over, furnished, dedicated Pv.i.5#12.</p><p>pp. of anupadeti</p>

anupadāna|anupadaana|anupadana
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupadaana</span></p><p>(anuppadāna) neuter</p><p>giving, administering, furnishing, the giving of (—˚) DN.i.12 (cp. DN-a.i.98 both read anuppādāna) Ja.iii.205 Mil.315</p><p>anu + pa + dāna, cp. anupadeti</p>

anupadātar|anupadaatar|anupadatar
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupadaatar</span></p><p>(anuppadātar) one who gives, or one who sets forth, effects, designs DN.i.4 (cp DN-a.i.74); AN.ii.209.</p><p>n. ag. of anupadeti</p>

anupagacchati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>goes over to, passes (into).</p>

anupagacchati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to go or return into (c. acc.) DN.i.55 (anupeti +).</p><p>anu + pa + gacchati</p>

anupagamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>the not reaching, not entering upon</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upagamana">upagamana</a></p>

anupagamma
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. absol.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upagamma">upagamma</a></p>

anupagantvā|anupagantvaa|anupagantva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupagantvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upagantvā">upagantvā</a></p>

anupagata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upagata">upagata</a></p>

anupaghāta|anupaghaata|anupaghata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine &amp; mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupaghaata</span></p><ol><li>(m.) non-injury; the not hurting.</li><li>(mfn.) free from harm; not involving injury</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://upaghāta">upaghāta</a></p>

anupaghāta|anupaghaata|anupaghata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupaghaata</span></p><p>not hurting Dhp.185 (<em>anūpa˚</em>; metri causa; expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> by anupahananañ c’eva anupaghātanañ ca Dhp-a.iii.238).</p><p>an + upaghāta</p>

anupahacca
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. absol.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upahacca">upahacca</a></p>

anupahata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anūpahata">anūpahata</a>, <a href="bword://upahata">upahata</a></p>

anupahata
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Anupahata<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>thrown up, blown up Mil.274.</p><p>anu + pa + hata, pp. of anu + pa + <em><a href="bword://han">han</a></em></p><p>Anupahata<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>adjective not destroyed, not spoilt Dhp-a.ii.33 (˚jivhapasāda).</p><p>an + upahata</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://han">han</a></p>

anupahāra|anupahaara|anupahara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupahaara</span></p><p>not bringing; non-supply</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upahāra">upahāra</a></p>

anupajagghati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>laughs at, derides.</p>

anupajagghati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to laugh at, to deride, mock over AN.i.198 (variant reading anusaṃ˚).</p><p>anu + pa + jagghati</p>

anupajjati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to follow, accompany Ja.iv.304. - pp. <em><a href="bword://anupanna">anupanna</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + <em>pad</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupanna">anupanna</a></p>

anupajjhāyaka|anupajjhaayaka|anupajjhayaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupajjhaayaka</span></p><p>without a teacher, without a preceptor.</p>

anupakampati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>shakes; quivers.</p>

anupakampati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to shake, move, to be unsteady Thag.191 = Ud.41.</p><p>anu + pakampati</p>

anupakhajja
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuppakkhandati">anuppakkhandati</a></p>

anupakhajjana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>(formed from anupakhajja) encroaching upon.</p>

anupakhajjanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not encroaching upon.</p>

anupakhajjati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to encroach, intrude Vin.v.163.</p><p>den. fr. anupakhajja, ger. of anupakkhandati</p>

anupakkama
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>not the action (of another); not an act of violence</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upakkama">upakkama</a></p>

anupakkama
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>not attacking, instr. <em>-ena</em> not by attack (from external enemies) Vin.ii.195.</p><p>an + upakkama</p>

anupakkhandati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to push oneself forward, to encroach on DN.i.122 (= anupavisati DN-a.i.290) ger. <em><a href="bword://anupakhajja">anupakhajja</a></em> pushing oneself in, intruding Vin.ii.88 (= antopavisati), Vin.ii.213; Vin.iv.43 (= anupavisati); MN.i.151, MN.i.469; SN.iii.113; Vism.18.</p><p>anu + pa + khandati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupakhajja">anupakhajja</a></p>

anupakkhipitvā|anupakkhipitvaa|anupakkhipitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupakkhipitvaa</span></p><p>placing in.</p>

anupakkilesa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>not a stain; non-defilement</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upakkilesa">upakkilesa</a></p>

anupakkuṭṭha|anupakku.t.tha|anupakkuttha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupakku.t.tha</span></p><p>blameless; irreproachable</p><p>See also: anupakuttha</p>

anupakkuṭṭha|anupakku.t.tha|anupakkuttha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupakku.t.tha</span></p><p>adjective blameless, irreproachahle DN.i.113; Vin.iv.160; Snp.p.115; DN-a.i.281.</p><p>an + upak˚</p>

anupakuṭṭha|anupaku.t.tha|anupakuttha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupaku.t.tha</span></p><p>blameless; irreproachable</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupakkuṭṭha">anupakkuṭṭha</a></p>

anupalabbhamāna|anupalabbhamaana|anupalabbhamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupalabbhamaana</span></p><p>non-existent; is not perceived; is not ascertained.</p>

anupalabbhiyamāna|anupalabbhiyamaana|anupalabbhiyamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupalabbhiyamaana</span></p><p>non-existent; is not perceived; is not ascertained.</p>

anupalakkhaṇa|anupalakkha.na|anupalakkhana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupalakkha.na</span></p><p>lack of observation, lack of attention.</p>

anupalitta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>not attached to; not sticking to</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anūpalitta">anūpalitta</a>, <a href="bword://upalitta">upalitta</a></p>

anupalitta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective unsmeared, unstained, free from taint MN.i.319, MN.i.386 (in verse); as <em>-ūpalitta</em> in verse of Sn &amp; Dh: Snp.211 (= lepānaṃ abhāvā Snp-a.261), 392 468, 790, 845; Dhp.353.</p><p>an + upalitta</p>

anupama
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>incomparable, peerless; excellent, best</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anūpama">anūpama</a>, <a href="bword://anopama">anopama</a>, <a href="bword://upamā">upamā</a></p>

anupanenta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upanenta">upanenta</a></p>

anupaneyya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. absol.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upaneyya">upaneyya</a></p>

anupanisa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><ol><li>lacking attention, inattentive.</li><li>without a cause, without prerequisite</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://upanisa">upanisa</a></p>

anupanna
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>gone into, reached, attained Snp.764 (māradheyya˚).</p><p>pp. of anupajjati</p>

anupanāha|anupanaaha|anupanaha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupanaaha</span></p><p>freedom from resentment; goodwill</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upanāha">upanāha</a></p>

anupanāhi|anupanaahi|anupanahi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupanaahi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anupanāhin">anupanāhin</a></p><p>(also <em>anūpanāhi(n)</em>) not resentful; without rancor.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upanāhin">upanāhin</a></p>

anupanāhin|anupanaahin|anupanahin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupanaahin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anupanāhin">anupanāhin</a></p><p>(also <em>anūpanāhi(n)</em>) not resentful; without rancor.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upanāhin">upanāhin</a></p>

anupanīta|anupaniita|anupanita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupaniita</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anūpanīta">anūpanīta</a>, <a href="bword://upanīta">upanīta</a></p>

anupapanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upapanna">upapanna</a></p>

anupaparikkha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anupaparikkhat">anupaparikkhat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upaparikkhat">upaparikkhat</a></p>

anupaparikkhat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anupaparikkhat">anupaparikkhat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upaparikkhat">upaparikkhat</a></p>

anupapīḷa|anupapii.la|anupapila
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupapii.la</span></p><p>free from oppression; free from distress.</p>

anuparidhāva|anuparidhaava|anuparidhava
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuparidhaava</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anuparidhāvat">anuparidhāvat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuparidhāvati">anuparidhāvati</a></p>

anuparidhāvat|anuparidhaavat|anuparidhavat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuparidhaavat</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anuparidhāvat">anuparidhāvat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuparidhāvati">anuparidhāvati</a></p>

anuparidhāvati|anuparidhaavati|anuparidhavati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuparidhaavati</span></p><p>runs round and round; surrounds.</p>

anuparidhāvati|anuparidhaavati|anuparidhavati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuparidhaavati</span></p><p>to run up &amp; down or to move round &amp; round (cp. anuparivattati) SN.iii.150 (khīlan).</p><p>anu + pari + dhāvati</p>

anuparigacchati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to walk round and round, to go round about (c. acc.) Vin.iii.119; SN.i.75 (ger. <em>-gamma</em>); Snp.447 (aor. <em>-pariyagā</em> = parito parito agamāsi Snp-a.393); Ja.iv.267.</p><p>anu + pari + gacchati</p>

anuparigamma
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i></p><p>having went round about.</p>

anuparigantuṃ|anuparigantu.m|anuparigantum
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">inf.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuparigantu.m</span></p><p>to go round about.</p>

anuparigantvā|anuparigantvaa|anuparigantva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuparigantvaa</span></p><p>having went round about.</p>

anupariharati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>surrounds, encircles; embraces.</p>

anupariharati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to surround, enfold, embrace MN.i.306.</p><p>anu + pari + harati</p>

anuparisakkana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>following, escorting.</p>

anuparisakkana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>dealing with, interest in SN.iv.312 (variant reading ˚vattana).</p><p>fr. anuparisakkati</p>

anuparisakkati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>moves round after; escorts.</p>

anuparisakkati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to move round, to be occupied with, take an interest in (c. acc.) SN.iv.312 (variant reading ˚vattati).</p><p>anu + pari + sakkati</p>

anuparivatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anuparivattat">anuparivattat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuparivattati">anuparivattati</a></p>

anuparivattat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anuparivattat">anuparivattat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuparivattati">anuparivattati</a></p>

anuparivattati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>turns or moves round after or along with; keeps on moving.</p>

anuparivattati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to go or move round, viz.</p><ol><li>to deal with, be engaged in, perform, worship Vin.iii.307 (ādiccaṃ); DN.i.240; Pv-a.97.</li><li>to meet Mil.204 (Devadatto ca Bodhisatto ca ekato anuparivattanti).</li><li>to move round &amp; round, move on and on keep on rolling (c. acc.), evolve SN.iii.150 (anuparidhāvati +) Mil.253 (anudhāvati + kāyan).</li></ol><p>anu + pari + vṛt</p>

anuparivatti
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>(-˚) dealing with, occupation, connection with SN.iii.16.</p><p>anu + parivatti</p>

anuparivattīyati|anuparivattiiyati|anuparivattiyati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pass. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuparivattiiyati</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuparivattati">anuparivattati</a></p>

anupariveṇiyam|anuparive.niyam|anupariveniyam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuparive.niyam</span></p><p>to every cell; cell by cell.</p>

anupariveṇiyaṃ|anuparive.niya.m|anupariveniyam
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuparive.niya.m</span></p><p>should be written anu pariveṇiyaṃ (“in every cell, cell by cell”), anu here functioning as prep. c. loc. (see <em><a href="bword://anu">anu</a></em> A Vin.i.80, Vin.i.106.</p><p>anu + pariveṇiyaṃ = loc. of pariveṇi</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anu">anu</a></p>

anuparivāreti|anuparivaareti|anuparivareti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuparivaareti</span></p><p>surrounds; stands by, takes the side of.</p>

anuparivāreti|anuparivaareti|anuparivareti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anuparivaareti</span></p><p>to surround, stand by, attend on (c. acc.) Vin.i.338; MN.i.153; Dhp-a.1.55.</p><p>anu + pari + vāreti</p>

anupariyagā|anupariyagaa|anupariyaga
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg &amp; 3 pl</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupariyagaa</span></p><p>went round about; went around.</p>

anupariyeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>goes round and round; goes round in order.</p>

anupariyāsi|anupariyaasi|anupariyasi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 1 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupariyaasi</span></p><p>see anupariyāti)</p>

anupariyāti|anupariyaati|anupariyati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupariyaati</span></p><p>goes round about; goes round after; travels about</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupariyāyati">anupariyāyati</a></p>

anupariyāti|anupariyaati|anupariyati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupariyaati</span></p><p>to go round about, to go about, to wander or travel all over (c. acc.) Vin.ii.111; SN.i.102, SN.i.124; Thag.1235 (˚pariyeti), Thag.1250 (id. to search) Pv.iii.3#4 (= anuvicarati); Mil.38; Pv-a.92 (<em>-yāyitvā</em> ger.) Pv-a.217</p><p>auu + pari + yāti</p>

anupariyāya|anupariyaaya|anupariyaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupariyaaya</span></p><p>going around.</p>

anupariyāya|anupariyaaya|anupariyaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupariyaaya</span></p><p>adjective going round, encircling, in <em>-patha</em> the path leading or going round the city DN.ii.83 = SN.iv.194 = AN.v.195; AN.iv.107.</p><p>adjectivised ger. of anupariyāti</p>

anupariyāyapatha|anupariyaayapatha|anupariyayapatha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupariyaayapatha</span></p><p>path leading round, an encircling path; a path on a rampart</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupariyāya">anupariyāya</a></p>

anupariyāyati|anupariyaayati|anupariyayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupariyaayati</span></p><p>goes round about; goes round after; travels about</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupariyāti">anupariyāti</a></p>

anupasagga
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not causing trouble or misfortune</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupassagga">anupassagga</a>, <a href="bword://upasagga">upasagga</a></p>

anupasampanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upasampanna">upasampanna</a></p>

anupasanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upasanta">upasanta</a></p>

anupasaṅkamati|anupasa"nkamati|anupasankamati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupasa"nkamati</span></p><p>Anupasaṅkamati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>to go along up to (c. acc.) Pv-a.179.</p><p>anu + pa + saṃkamati</p><p>Anupasaṅkamati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>not to go to. not to approach Dhp-a.ii.30 (+ apayirupāsati).</p><p>an + upasank˚</p>

anupasaṅkanta|anupasa"nkanta|anupasankanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupasa"nkanta</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upasaṅkanta">upasaṅkanta</a></p>

anupasaṇṭhapanā|anupasa.n.thapanaa|anupasanthapana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupasa.n.thapanaa</span></p><p>not stopping, incessance, continuance Pp.18 (but id. p. at Vb.357 has anusansandanā instead); cp. <em><a href="bword://anupabandhan%C4%81">anupabandhanā</a></em>.</p><p>an + upasaṇṭhapanā</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupabandhanā">anupabandhanā</a></p>

anupasaṭṭha|anupasa.t.tha|anupasattha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupasa.t.tha</span></p><p>free from trouble; free from affliction</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupassaṭṭha">anupassaṭṭha</a>, <a href="bword://upassaṭṭha">upassaṭṭha</a></p>

anupassagga
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not causing trouble or misfortune</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupasagga">anupasagga</a>, <a href="bword://upassagga">upassagga</a></p>

anupassaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>looking at, regarding as; showing.</p>

anupassaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective observing, viewing, contemplating Thag.420.</p><p>fr. anupassati</p>

anupassanā|anupassanaa|anupassana
<p>[Nyana]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupassanaa</span></p><p><strong>Anupassanā:</strong> Contemplation, deep reflection, profound consideration:<br />The 4 fold: see: <em>satipatthāna.</em><br />The 18 fold: see: <em>vipassanā.</em><br />The 7 fold: The seven contemplations:<br />1: Contemplating constructions as impermanent, one leaves behind the perception of permanence.<br />2: Contemplating them as painful, one leaves behind the perception of happiness.<br />3: Contemplating them as not self, one leaves behind the perception of ownership.<br />4: Becoming disillusioned, one leaves behind delighting.<br />5: Causing fading away of lust, one leaves behind greed.<br />6: Causing ceasing, one leaves behind creating.<br />7: Relinquishing, one leaves behind clinging.<br />Pts.M. I, p. 58. - See also Vis.M XXI, 43; XXII, 114.</p>

anupassanā|anupassanaa|anupassana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupassanaa</span></p><p>looking at, viewing, contemplating, consideration, realisation SN.v.178 sq., Snp.p.140; Pts.i.10, Pts.i.20, Pts.i.96; Pts.ii.37, Pts.ii.41 sq. Pts.ii.67 sq.; Vb.194. See <em>anicca˚, anatta˚, dukkha˚</em>.</p><p>abstr. of anupassati, cf. Sk. anudarśana</p>

anupassati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>looks at; contemplates.</p>

anupassati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to look at, contemplate, observe Snp.477; Pts.i.57, Pts.i.187; Snp-a.505.</p><p>anu + passati</p>

anupassaṭṭha|anupassa.t.tha|anupassattha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupassa.t.tha</span></p><p>free from trouble; free from affliction</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupasaṭṭha">anupasaṭṭha</a>, <a href="bword://upassaṭṭha">upassaṭṭha</a></p>

anupassi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anupassin">anupassin</a></p><p>looking for; observing, considering.</p>

anupassin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anupassin">anupassin</a></p><p>looking for; observing, considering.</p>

anupassin
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(-˚) adjective viewing, observing, realising SN.ii.84 sq., SN.v.294 sq., SN.v.311 sq., SN.v.345, Dhp.7, Dhp.253; Snp.255, Snp.728; Pts.i.191 sq.; Vb.193 sq., Vb.236; Sdhp.411.</p><p>fr. anupassati</p>

anupatati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>follows, pursues; falls in; falls upon, attacks.</p>

anupatati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>to follow, go after, Ja.vi.555 anupatiyāsi Subj.).</li><li>to fall upon, to befall, attack Vin.iii.106 = MN.i.364; SN.i.23 (read ˚patanti for ˚patatanti = Dhp.221 (dukkhā); Thag.41 = Thag.1167 (of lightning). pp. <em><a href="bword://anupatita">anupatita</a></em> (q.v.). Cp. also <em>anupāta &amp; anupātin</em>.</li></ol><p>anu + patati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupatita">anupatita</a></p>

anupathe
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>at Ja.v.302 should be read as anu pathe by the way at the wayside; anu to be taken as prep. c. loc. (see <em><a href="bword://anu">anu</a></em> A). C. explains as janghamagga-mahāmaggānaṃ antare.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anu">anu</a></p>

anupatita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>following, accompanying, involved; followed by, affected with</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupatati">anupatati</a></p>

anupatita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>“befallen”, affected with, oppressed by (-˚) SN.ii.173 (dukkha˚); SN.iii.69 (id.); Snp.334 (pamāda˚).</p><p>pp. of anupatati</p>

anupatitatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>the fact of being attacked by, being a victim of (-˚) Snp-a.339.</p><p>abstr. of anupatita</p>

anupatitvā|anupatitvaa|anupatitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupatitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupatati">anupatati</a></p>

anupatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><ol><li>(pass.) attained, reached.</li><li>(act.) having attained, reached; arrived (at)</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuppatta">anuppatta</a></p>

anupatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(anuppatta) (having) attained, received, got to (c. acc), reached DN.i.87–DN.i.111; DN.ii.2; Iti.38; Snp.027, Snp.635; Dhp.386, Dhp.403; Pv.iv.1#66; Pv-a.59 (dukkhaṃ), Pv-a.242. In phrase <em>addhagata vayo-anuppatta</em> having reached old age, e.g. Vin.ii.188; DN.i.48; Snp.p.50, 92; Pv-a.149.</p><p>pp. of anupāpuṇāti; cp. Sk. anuprāpta</p>

anupatti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>attainment; accomplishment</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuppatti">anuppatti</a></p>

anupatti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(anuppatti) feminine attainment, accomplishment, wish, desire (fulfilled), ideal SN.i.46, SN.i.52.</p><p>anu + patti</p>

anupavadita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upavadita">upavadita</a></p>

anupavajja
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anūpavajja">anūpavajja</a>, <a href="bword://upavajja">upavajja</a></p>

anupavajja
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective blameless, without fault, Mil.391.</p><p>grd. of an + upavadati</p>

anupavattaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(anuppa˚) adjective to anupavatteti] one who succeeds (another) King or Ruler in the ruling of an empire (cakkaṃ) Mil.342, Mil.362; Snp-a.454. See also <em><a href="bword://anuvattaka">anuvattaka</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuvattaka">anuvattaka</a></p>

anupavattayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>keeps moving on after (another) or in succession; continues, maintains</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupavatteti">anupavatteti</a></p>

anupavattesi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupavatteti">anupavatteti</a></p>

anupavatteti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>keeps moving on after (another) or in succession; continues, maintains</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupavattayati">anupavattayati</a></p>

anupavatteti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(anuppa˚) to keep moving on after, to continue rolling, with <em>cakkaṃ</em> to wield supreme power after, i.e. in succession or imitation of a predecessor SN.i.191; Mil.362. See also <em><a href="bword://anuvatteti">anuvatteti</a></em>.</p><p>anu + pa + vatteti, fr. <em>vṛt</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuvatteti">anuvatteti</a></p>

anupavecchanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupavecchati">anupavecchati</a></p>

anupavecchati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>gives, presents; supplies, confers upon</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuppavecchati">anuppavecchati</a></p>

anupavecchati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(anuppa˚) to give, give over to, offer up, present, supply Vin.i.221 (˚pavacchati); DN.i.74 (= pavesati DN-a.i.218); DN-a.ii.78; MN.i.446 MN.iii.133; AN.ii.64; AN.iii.26 (variant reading ˚vacch˚); Ja.v.394; Snp.208 (variant reading ˚vacch˚); Snp-a.256 (= anupavesati); Pv-a.28.</p><p>see under <em><a href="bword://pavecchati">pavecchati</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://pavecchati">pavecchati</a></p>

anupavecchi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupavecchati">anupavecchati</a></p>

anupaveseti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to make enter, to give over, to supply Snp-a.256 (= ˚pavecchati).</p><p>anu + pa + <em>vis</em>, cp. BSk. anupraveśayati Divy.238</p>

anupavisati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>enters (after); goes into; resorts to; is present (in)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuppavisati">anuppavisati</a></p>

anupavisati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to go into, to enter Dhp.i.290; Vv-a.42 (= ogāhati)<br />pp <em>-paviṭṭha</em> (q.v.) Caus. <em>-paveseti</em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + pa + visati</p>

anupavisitvā|anupavisitvaa|anupavisitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupavisitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupavisati">anupavisati</a></p>

anupaviṭṭha|anupavi.t.tha|anupavittha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupavi.t.tha</span></p><p>having entered, gone into; resorted to; present (in)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anupavisati">anupavisati</a></p>

anupaviṭṭha|anupavi.t.tha|anupavittha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupavi.t.tha</span></p><p>(anuppa˚) entered, gone or got into, fallen into (c. acc.) Mil.270, Mil.318 sq., Mil.409 (coming for shelter); Pv-a.97, Pv-a.152 (Gangānadiṃ a. nadī flowing into the G.).</p><p>pp. of anupavisati</p>

anupaviṭṭhatā|anupavi.t.thataa|anupavitthata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupavi.t.thataa</span></p><p>the fact of having entered Mil.257.</p><p>abstr. to anupaviṭṭha</p>

anupavāda|anupavaada|anupavada
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupavaada</span></p><p>lack of abuse; not blaming or criticizing</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anūpavāda">anūpavāda</a>, <a href="bword://upavāda">upavāda</a></p>

anupavāda|anupavaada|anupavada
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupavaada</span></p><p>not blaming or finding fault, abstaining from grumbling or abuse Dhp.185 (anūpa˚ in metre; explained at Dhp-a.iii.238 as anupavādanañ c’eva anupavādāpanañ ca “not scolding as well as not inciting others to grumbling”); adj. <em>-vādaka</em> Pp.60, &amp; <em>-vādin</em> MN.i.360.</p><p>an + upavāda</p>

anupavādaka|anupavaadaka|anupavadaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupavaadaka</span></p><p>one who does not criticize or abuse</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upavādaka">upavādaka</a></p>

anupavādi|anupavaadi|anupavadi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupavaadi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anupavādin">anupavādin</a></p><p>not criticizing.</p>

anupavādin|anupavaadin|anupavadin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupavaadin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anupavādin">anupavādin</a></p><p>not criticizing.</p>

anupaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not going near (to); free from involvement</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anūpaya">anūpaya</a>, <a href="bword://upaya">upaya</a></p>

anupaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective unattached, “aloof” SN.i.181 (akankha apiha +).</p><p>an + upaya</p>

anupañcāhaṃ|anupa~ncaaha.m|anupancaham
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupa~ncaaha.m</span></p><p>adverb every five days Pv-a.139 (+ anudasāhaṃ).</p><p>anu + pañcā + ahaṃ</p>

anupaññatta|anupa~n~natta|anupannatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupa~n~natta</span></p><p>additionally ordered or ruled</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuppaññatta">anuppaññatta</a></p>

anupaññatti|anupa~n~natti|anupannatti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupa~n~natti</span></p><p>an additional or supplemental rule</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuppaññatti">anuppaññatti</a></p>

anupaññatti|anupa~n~natti|anupannatti
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anupa~n~natti</span></p><p>supplementary regulation or order Vin.ii.286; Vin.v.2 sq.</p><p>anu + paññatti</p>

anupaṭipāti|anupa.tipaati|anupatipati
