anuññāta|anu~n~naata|anunnata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu~n~naata</span></p><p>adjective permitted, allowed; sanctioned, given leave, ordained DN.i.88; Ja.i.92; Ja.ii.353 Ja.ii.416; Pv.i.12#3 (na a. = ananuññāta at id. p. Thig.129 expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> at Pv-a.64 by ananumata); Pp.28; DN-a.i.247 DN-a.i.248, DN-a.i.267; Pv-a.12, Pv-a.81.</p><p>pp. of anujānāti</p>

anuññātapatīññāta|anu~n~naatapatii~n~naata|anunnatapatinnata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu~n~naatapatii~n~naata</span></p><p>acknowledged and self-professed</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuññāta">anuññāta</a></p>

