anuṭṭhahat|anu.t.thahat|anutthahat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu.t.thahat</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anuṭṭhahat">anuṭṭhahat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uṭṭhahat">uṭṭhahat</a></p>

anuṭṭhahati|anu.t.thahati|anutthahati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu.t.thahati</span></p><p>to carry out, look after, practise do Ja.v.121<br />pp <em><a href="bword://anu%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADhita">anuṭṭhita</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + ṭhahati = ˚thāti, see ˚*<a href="bword://ti%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADhati">tiṭṭhati</a>*</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anuṭṭhita">anuṭṭhita</a>, <a href="bword://tiṭṭhati">tiṭṭhati</a></p>

anuṭṭhahāna|anu.t.thahaana|anutthahana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu.t.thahaana</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uṭṭhahati">uṭṭhahati</a></p>

anuṭṭhahāna|anu.t.thahaana|anutthahana
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu.t.thahaana</span></p><p>adjective one who does not rouse himself, not getting up, inactive Dhp.280 (anuṭṭhahanto avāyāmanto Dhp-a.iii.409).</p><p>ppr. of an + uṭṭhahati</p>

anuṭṭhaka|anu.t.thaka|anutthaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu.t.thaka</span></p><p>adjective not rising, not rousing oneself, inactive, lazy Thag.1033.</p><p>fr. an + uṭṭhahati</p>

anuṭṭhita|anu.t.thita|anutthita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu.t.thita</span></p><p>practising, effecting or effected, come to, experienced, done DN.ii.103; SN.iv.200; AN.iii.290 sq.; AN.iv.300; Ja.ii.61; Mil.198; Pv-a.132 (cp. anugata).</p><p>pp. of anuṭṭhati = anutiṭṭhati</p>

anuṭṭhubhati|anu.t.thubhati|anutthubhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu.t.thubhati</span></p><p>to lick up with one’s saliva DN-a.i.138.</p><p>formally Sk. anuṣṭobhati, but in meaning = *anuṣṭīvati; anu + ṭṭhubhati, the etym. of which see under <em><a href="bword://ni%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADhubhati">niṭṭhubhati</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://niṭṭhubhati">niṭṭhubhati</a></p>

anuṭṭhurin|anu.t.thurin|anutthurin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu.t.thurin</span></p><p>variant reading at Snp-a.569, see <em><a href="bword://ni%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADhurin">niṭṭhurin</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://niṭṭhurin">niṭṭhurin</a></p>

anuṭṭhāna|anu.t.thaana|anutthana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu.t.thaana</span></p><p>not getting up; lack of energy; laziness</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uṭṭhāna">uṭṭhāna</a></p>

anuṭṭhāna|anu.t.thaana|anutthana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu.t.thaana</span></p><p>“the not getting up”, inactivity, want of energy Dhp.241 (sarīra-paṭijagganaṃ akaronto Dhp-a.iii.347).</p><p>an + uṭṭhāna</p>

anuṭṭhāta|anu.t.thaata|anutthata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu.t.thaata</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anuṭṭhātar">anuṭṭhātar</a></p><p>one who does not exert himself</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uṭṭhātar">uṭṭhātar</a></p>

anuṭṭhātar|anu.t.thaatar|anutthatar
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anu.t.thaatar</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anuṭṭhātar">anuṭṭhātar</a></p><p>one who does not exert himself</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uṭṭhātar">uṭṭhātar</a></p>

anuṭṭhātar|anu.t.thaatar|anutthatar
