anvakāsi|anvakaasi|anvakasi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvakaasi</span></p><p>he threw, scattered.</p>

anvakāsi|anvakaasi|anvakasi
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvakaasi</span></p><p>3<!-- raw HTML omitted -->rd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg. aor. of anukassati 2: drew out, removed, threw down Thag.869 (= khipi, chaḍḍesi C.).</p>

anvattha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective according to the sense, answering to the matter, having scnse Thag-a.6 (˚saññābhāva).</p><p>anu + attha</p>

anvaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><ol><li>lineage, succession; what follows, (logical) connection, inference, consequence.</li><li>successor, immediate follower</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://anu-aya">anu-aya</a></p>

anvaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>noun adjective</p><ol><li>(n.) conformity, accordance DN.ii.83 = DN.iii.100; MN.i.69 (dhamm˚ logical conclusion of) SN.ii.58; DN.iii.226 (anvaye ñāṇaṃ); Pv.ii.11#3 (tassa kammassa anvāya, variant reading BB anvaya &amp; anvāya; accordingly according to = paccayā Pv-a.147); Pv-a.228 (anvayato adv. in accordance).</li><li>(adj.) following, having the same course, behaving according to, consequential, in conformity with (-˚) DN.i.46 (tad˚); MN.i.238 (kāyo citt acting in conformity to the mind, obeying the mind) Snp.254 (an˚ inconsistent); Iti.79 (tass˚)<br />■ dur˚ spelt <em>durannaya</em> conforming with difficulty, hard to manage or to find out Dhp.92 (gati = na sakkā paññāpetuṃ Dhp-a.ii.173); Snp.243, Snp.251 (= duviññāpaya Snp-a.287 dunneyya ibid. Snp.293).</li></ol><p>Vedic anvaya in diff. meaning; fr. anu + <em><a href="bword://i">i</a></em>, see <em><a href="bword://anveti">anveti</a></em> &amp; anvāya</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://i">i</a>, <a href="bword://anveti">anveti</a></p>

anvayatā|anvayataa|anvayata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvayataa</span></p><p>conformity, accordance MN.i.500 (kāy˚ giving in to the body)</p><p>abstr. to anvaya</p>

anvaḍḍhamāsaṃ|anva.d.dhamaasa.m|anvaddhamasam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anva.d.dhamaasa.m</span></p><p>every fortnight</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvaddhamāsaṃ">anvaddhamāsaṃ</a></p>

anvaḍḍhamāsaṃ|anva.d.dhamaasa.m|anvaddhamasam
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anva.d.dhamaasa.m</span></p><p>adverb every fortnight, twice a month MN.ii.8; Vin.iv.315 (= anuposathikaṃ) Dhp-a.i.162; Dhp-a.ii.25.</p><p>anu + aḍḍha + māsa</p>

anventa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anveti">anveti</a></p>

anvesa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anvesat">anvesat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvesati">anvesati</a></p>

anvesa
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>seeking, searching, investigation, MN.i.140 (˚ṃ n’ âdhigacchanti do not find).</p><p>from next</p>

anvesanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvesati">anvesati</a></p>

anvesat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://anvesat">anvesat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvesati">anvesati</a></p>

anvesati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>searches; looks for</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anu-esati">anu-esati</a></p>

anvesati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to look, for search, seek SN.i.112 (ppr. anvesaṃ = pariyesamāna C.); Cp.iii.11#7 (ppr. anvesanto)<br />aor <em>anvesi</em> [Sk. anveṣi fr. icchati] Pv.ii.6#20 (? perhaps better with variant reading Pv-a.99 as anventi of anveti).</p><p>anu + esati</p>

anvesaṃ|anvesa.m|anvesam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvesa.m</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvesati">anvesati</a></p>

anvesin
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective striving after, seeking, wishing for Snp.965 (kusala˚).</p><p>anu-esin</p>

anveti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><ol><li>follows; goes along with.</li><li>goes into, enters; goes through</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://anu-iti">anu-iti</a>, <a href="bword://anu-eti">anu-eti</a></p>

anveti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to follow, approach, go with Snp.1103 (= anugacchati anvāyiko hoti Cnd.59); Dhp.1 (= kāyikaṃ… dukkhaṃ anugacchati Dhp-a.i.24), Dhp.2, Dhp.71 Dhp.124; perhaps at Pv.ii.6#20 (with variant reading BB at Pv-a.99) for <em>anvesi</em> (see <em><a href="bword://anvesati">anvesati</a></em>; expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> by anudesi = was anxious for, helped, instructed).</p><p>cp. anu + eti, from <em><a href="bword://i">i</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvesati">anvesati</a>, <a href="bword://i">i</a></p>

anvādhika|anvaadhika|anvadhika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(mf)n.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaadhika</span></p><p>extra; an extra supply.</p>

anvādhika|anvaadhika|anvadhika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaadhika</span></p><p>adjective a tailoring term. Only at Vin.i.297. Rendered (<em>Vinaya Texts</em> ii.232) by ʻhalf and half’; that is a patchwork, half of new material half of old. Bdhgh’s note (see the text, p. 392) adds that the new material must be cut up.</p><p>derivation uncertain</p>

anvādisati|anvaadisati|anvadisati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaadisati</span></p><p>to advise, dedicate, assign; imper. ˚disāhi Pv.ii.2#6 (= uddissa dehi Pv-a.80); Pv.iii.2#8 (= ādisa Pv-a.181).</p><p>anu + ā + disati</p>

anvāgacchati|anvaagacchati|anvagacchati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaagacchati</span></p><ol><li>to go along after, to follow, run after, pursue; aor. <em>anvāgacchi</em> Pv.iv.5#6 (= anubandhi Pv-a.260).</li><li>to come back again Ja.i.454 (ger. ˚gantvāna)</li></ol><p>pp <em><a href="bword://anv%C4%81gata">anvāgata</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>anu + ā + gacchati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvāgata">anvāgata</a></p>

anvāgameti|anvaagameti|anvagameti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaagameti</span></p><p>makes follow; makes return.</p>

anvāgata|anvaagata|anvagata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. (pass.)</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaagata</span></p><p>followed by; affected by</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anu-āgata">anu-āgata</a></p>

anvāgata|anvaagata|anvagata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaagata</span></p><p>having pursued, attained; endowed with Thag.63; Ja.iv.385; Ja.v.4.</p><p>pp. of anvāgacchati</p>

anvāhata|anvaahata|anvahata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaahata</span></p><p>struck; injured.</p>

anvāhata|anvaahata|anvahata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaahata</span></p><p>struck, beaten; perplexed Dhp.39 (˚cetasa).</p><p>pp. of anu + ā + <em><a href="bword://han">han</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://han">han</a></p>

anvāhiṇḍati|anvaahi.n.dati|anvahindati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaahi.n.dati</span></p><p>wanders about; wanders through.</p>

anvāhiṇḍati|anvaahi.n.dati|anvahindati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaahi.n.dati</span></p><p>to wander to (acc.) AN.iv.374, AN.iv.376 [BSk. same, e.g. Divy.68 etc.].</p><p>anu + ā + hiṇḍati</p>

anvāmaddati|anvaamaddati|anvamaddati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaamaddati</span></p><p>to squeeze, wring Ja.iii.481 (galakaṃ anvāmaddi wrung his neck; vv.ll. anvānumaṭṭi &amp; anvāvamaddi; C. gīvaṃ maddi).</p><p>anu + ā + maddati</p>

anvānayati|anvaanayati|anvanayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaanayati</span></p><p>leads or brings after oneself; incurs</p><p>See also: anu-āyanati</p>

anvārohati|anvaarohati|anvarohati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaarohati</span></p><p>to go up to, visit, ascend Ja.iv.465 (aor. anvāruhi).</p><p>anu + ā + rohati</p>

anvāsanna|anvaasanna|anvasanna
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaasanna</span></p><p>endowed with, possessed of, attacked by, Ud.35 (doubtfull; variant reading ajjhāpanna) = AN.iv.356 which has <em><a href="bword://anv%C4%81satta">anvāsatta</a></em>.</p><p>pp. of anu + ā + <em>sad</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvāsatta">anvāsatta</a></p>

anvāsatta|anvaasatta|anvasatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaasatta</span></p><p>ensnared, entwined (by).</p>

anvāsatta|anvaasatta|anvasatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaasatta</span></p><p>clung on to, befallen by (instr.), attached to AN.iv.356 (variant reading anvāhata), cp. Ud.35 (anvāsanna q.v.) See also foll.</p><p>pp. of anu + ā + <em>sañj</em>, cp. anusatta = Sk. anusakta</p>

anvāsattatā|anvaasattataa|anvasattata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaasattataa</span></p><p>being attacked by, falling a prey to (instr.), attachment to Dhp-a.i.287 (in same context as anvāsatta AN.iv.356 &amp; anvāsanna Ud.35).</p><p>abstr. fr. anvāsatta</p>

anvāsavati|anvaasavati|anvasavati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaasavati</span></p><p>flows after, flows upon, flows continually over</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvāssavati">anvāssavati</a></p>

anvāssavati|anvaassavati|anvassavati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaassavati</span></p><p>flows after, flows upon, flows continually over</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvāsavati">anvāsavati</a></p>

anvāssavati|anvaassavati|anvassavati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaassavati</span></p><p>to stream into, to attack, befall DN.i.70; AN.iii.99; Pp.20, Pp.58.</p><p>anu + ā + savati, <em>sru</em></p>

anvāvassa|anvaavassa|anvavassa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaavassa</span></p><p>at Ja.v.317 should be read with variant reading BB as <em><a href="bword://anovassa">anovassa</a></em> absence of rain.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anovassa">anovassa</a></p>

anvāvaṭṭa|anvaava.t.ta|anvavatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaava.t.ta</span></p><p>fmn. following</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvāvaṭṭati">anvāvaṭṭati</a></p>

anvāvaṭṭati|anvaava.t.tati|anvavattati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaava.t.tati</span></p><p>moves after, follows.</p>

anvāvisati|anvaavisati|anvavisati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaavisati</span></p><p>enters, occupies, possesses (said esp. of Māra)</p>

anvāvisati|anvaavisati|anvavisati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaavisati</span></p><p>to go into, to take possession of, to visit MN.i.326; SN.i.67; Mil.156<br />pp <em><a href="bword://anv%C4%81vi%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADha">anvāviṭṭha</a></em> (q.v.). Cp. adhimuccati.</p><p>anu + ā + visati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvāviṭṭha">anvāviṭṭha</a></p>

anvāvisitvā|anvaavisitvaa|anvavisitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaavisitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anvāvisati">anvāvisati</a></p>

anvāviṭṭha|anvaavi.t.tha|anvavittha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaavi.t.tha</span></p><p>entered (by), possessed (by)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anu-āviṭṭha">anu-āviṭṭha</a>, <a href="bword://anvāvisati">anvāvisati</a></p>

anvāviṭṭha|anvaavi.t.tha|anvavittha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaavi.t.tha</span></p><p>possessed (by evil spirits) SN.i.114.</p><p>pp. of anvāvisati</p>

anvāya|anvaaya|anvaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaaya</span></p><p>following; after; in consequence of</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anveti">anveti</a></p>

anvāya|anvaaya|anvaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaaya</span></p><p>undergoing, experiencing, attaining; as prep. (c. acc.) in consequence of, through after DN.i.13 (ātappaṃ by means of self-sacrifice), DN.i.97 (saṃvāsaṃ as a result of their cohabitation); Ja.i.56 (buddhiṃ), Ja.i.127 (piyasaṃvāsaṃ), Ja.i.148 (gabbhaparipākaṃ). Often in phrase <em>vuddhiṃ anvāya</em> growing up, e.g. Ja.i.278; Ja.iii.126; Dhp-a.ii.87.</p><p>ger. of anveti; cp. anvaya</p>

anvāyika|anvaayika|anvayika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. &amp; masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaayika</span></p><p>following; a follower.</p>

anvāyika|anvaayika|anvayika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anvaayika</span></p><p>adjective noun following; one who follows, a companion DN.iii.169; Cnd.59; Ja.iii.348.</p><p>fr. anvāya</p>

anābhoga|anaabhoga|anabhoga
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaabhoga</span></p><p>absence of enjoyment</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ābhoga">ābhoga</a></p>

anābādha|anaabaadha|anabadha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaabaadha</span></p><p>adjective safe and sound Vv-a.351.</p><p>an + ābādha</p>

anācariyaka|anaacariyaka|anacariyaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaacariyaka</span></p><ol><li>not having a teacher; not dependent on an instructor.</li><li>free from bad influences.</li></ol>

anāciṇṇa|anaaci.n.na|anacinna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn. &amp; neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaaci.n.na</span></p><p>not done, not practiced; not the custom</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://āciṇṇa">āciṇṇa</a></p>

anācāra|anaacaara|anacara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine &amp; mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaacaara</span></p><ol><li>(m.) misconduct, esp. sexual misconduct.</li><li>(mfn.) immoral, unchaste</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://ācāra">ācāra</a></p>

anācāra|anaacaara|anacara
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaacaara</span></p><p>misconduct, immorality Ja.ii.133; Ja.iii.276; adj. <em>anācārin</em> Pp.57.</p><p>an + ācāra</p>

anādara|anaadara|anadara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaadara</span></p><p>disrespectful; regardless, unconcerned; indifferent.</p>

anādara|anaadara|anadara
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaadara</span></p><ol><li>(m) disrespect Pv-a.257</li><li>(adj.) disrespectful Snp.247 (= ādaravirahita Snp-a.290).</li></ol><p>an + ādara</p>

anādaratā|anaadarataa|anadarata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaadarataa</span></p><p>want of consideration, in expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> of dovacassatā at Dhs.1325 = Vb.359 = Pp.30 (where reading is <em>anādariyatā</em>).</p><p>abstr. fr. anādara</p>

anādari|anaadari|anadari
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaadari</span></p><p>disrespect, disregard.</p>

anādariya|anaadariya|anadariya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaadariya</span></p><p>disrespect, disregard; carelessness.</p>

anādariya|anaadariya|anadariya
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaadariya</span></p><p>disregard, disrespect Vin.i.176; Vin.iv.113 (where expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> in extenso); Dhs.1325 d<!-- raw HTML omitted -->ug<!-- raw HTML omitted --> 20 = Vb.359.</p><p>fr. anādara</p>

anādhānagāhin|anaadhaanagaahin|anadhanagahin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaadhaanagaahin</span></p><p>Also written as: anādhānagāhinanādhānaggāhin</p><p>See also: ādhānaggāhin</p>

anādhāra|anaadhaara|anadhara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaadhaara</span></p><p>without support; without a stand or holder</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ādhāra">ādhāra</a></p>

anādinna|anaadinna|anadinna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaadinna</span></p><p>not used; with no mark used or added</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ādinna">ādinna</a></p>

anāditvā|anaaditvaa|anaditva
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaaditvaa</span></p><p>not taking up, not heeding Ja.iv.352 (variant reading for T. anādiyitvā).</p><p>ger. of an + ādiyati</p>

anādiyana|anaadiyana|anadiyana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neg. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaadiyana</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ādiyati">ādiyati</a></p>

anādiyanta|anaadiyanta|anadiyanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaadiyanta</span></p><p>anādiyanta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>neg. mfn.</p><p>anādiyanta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>neg. mfn.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ādiyanta">ādiyanta</a>, <a href="bword://ādiyati">ādiyati</a></p>

