<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaamaya</span></p><p>adjective free from illness, not decaying, healthy Vv.15#10 (= aroga Vv-a.74), Vv.17#7.</p><p>an + āmaya</p>

anānu|anaanu|ananu
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">anaanu</span></p><p>Anānu-</p><p>represents the metrically lengthened from of ananu(an + anu), as found e.g. in the foll. compounds: <em>-tappaṃ</em> (ppr.) not regretting Ja.v.492; <em>-puṭṭha</em> questioned Snp.782 (= apucchita Snp-a.521); <em>-yāyin</em> not following or not defiled by evil Snp.1071 (expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> at Cnd.42 by both avedhamāna (?) avigacchamāna &amp; by arajjamāna adussamāna); <em>-loma</em> not fit or suitable DN.ii.273 (variant reading anu˚).</p>

