atthantara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>taking the goal or meaning to heart; intent on the goal or meaning</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthanusiṭṭhi|atthanusi.t.thi|atthanusitthi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthanusi.t.thi</span></p><p>administration of practical affairs or policy</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthapada
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>profitable saying; word of good sense</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthapaṭisambhidā|atthapa.tisambhidaa|atthapatisambhida
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">f.; \~a neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthapa.tisambhidaa</span></p><p>analysis of the meaning</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthapucchana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>questioning about the aim</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthapurekkhāra|atthapurekkhaara|atthapurekkhara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthapurekkhaara</span></p><p>aiming at the meaning, or at the benefit</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthara
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i></p><p>rug (for horses, elephants etc.) DN.i.7.</p><p>fr. attharati</p>

attharaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i></p><p>covering Ja.i.9; DN-a.i.87<br />■ f. <em>-ikā</em> a layer Ja.i.9; Ja.v.280.</p><p>= atthara</p>

attharati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>spreads out, spreads; spreads over, covers; lays out; esp. <em>kaṭhinam attharati</em>, covers the <em>kaṭhina</em>, participates in the <em>kaṭhina</em> robe-making and ritual.</p>

attharati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to spread, to cover, to spread out; stretch, lay out Vin.i.254; Vin.v.172; Ja.i.199; Ja.v.113; Ja.vi.428; Dhp.i.272<br />pp <em><a href="bword://atthata">atthata</a></em> (q.v.)<br />caus <strong>attharāpeti</strong> to caused to be spread Ja.v.110; Mhvs.3, Mhvs.20; Mhvs.29, Mhvs.7; Mhvs.34, Mhvs.69.</p><p>ā + <em>stṛ</em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://atthata">atthata</a>, attharāpeti</p>

attharaṇa|atthara.na|attharana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthara.na</span></p><p>covering, carpet; laying out.</p>

attharaṇa|atthara.na|attharana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthara.na</span></p><p>covering, carpet, cover, rug Vin.ii.291; AN.ii.56; AN.iii.53; Mhvs.3, Mhvs.20; Mhvs.15, Mhvs.40 Mhvs.25, Mhvs.102; Thag-a.22.</p><p>fr. attharati</p>

attharitabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attharati">attharati</a></p>

attharitvā|attharitvaa|attharitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">attharitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attharati">attharati</a></p>

atthasaṃhita|atthasa.mhita|atthasamhita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthasa.mhita</span></p><p>connected with the goal; useful, profitable; having meaning</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>covered; (of the <em>kaṭhina</em>) properly covered; (of the <em>kaṭhina</em> robe-making and ritual) properly carried out, properly performed</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attharati">attharati</a></p>

atthata
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>spread, covered, spread over with (-˚) Vin.i.265; Vin.iv.287; Vin.v.172 (see <em>˚an</em>); AN.iii.50; Pv-a.141.</p><p>pp. of attharati</p><p>See also: ˚an</p>

atthatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>reason, cause; only in abl. atthattā according to the sense, by reason of, on account of Pv-a.189 (-˚).</p><p>abstr. fr. attha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p>

atthava
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://atthavat">atthavat</a></p><ol><li>profitable; significant.</li><li>possessing the goal; or possessing worldly knowledge</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthavant
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective full of benefit SN.i.30; Thag.740; Mil.172.</p><p>cp. Sk. arthavant</p>

atthavasa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>reason; motive</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthavasi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://atthavasin">atthavasin</a></p><p>pursuing an aim</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthavasika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>pursuing an aim; pursuing the goal</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthavasin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://atthavasin">atthavasin</a></p><p>pursuing an aim</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthavat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://atthavat">atthavat</a></p><ol><li>profitable; significant.</li><li>possessing the goal; or possessing worldly knowledge</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthaveda
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>knowledge or joy in the goal, or the practice</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthavādi|atthavaadi|atthavadi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthavaadi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://atthavādin">atthavādin</a></p><p>speaking about the goal or what is beneficial</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthavādin|atthavaadin|atthavadin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthavaadin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://atthavādin">atthavādin</a></p><p>speaking about the goal or what is beneficial</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthaññū|attha~n~nuu|atthannu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">attha~n~nuu</span></p><p>ū knowing the means; knowing the goal; knowing the meaning</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthaṃ anubhavati|attha.m anubhavati|attham anubhavati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(?)</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">attha.m anubhavati</span></p><p>serves the interest, the purpose (of, gen.); benefits</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubhavati">anubhavati</a></p>

atthaṃ anubhoti|attha.m anubhoti|attham anubhoti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(?)</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">attha.m anubhoti</span></p><p>serves the interest, the purpose (of, gen.); benefits</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anubhoti">anubhoti</a></p>

atthaṃ|attha.m|attham
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">acc.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">attha.m</span></p><p>for the sake of; for the purpose of</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthaṭakaṭhina|attha.taka.thina|atthatakathina
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">attha.taka.thina</span></p><p>who has participated in the <em>kaṭhina</em> robe-making (and is therefore eligible for the five concessions)</p><p>See also: atthaṭa</p>

atthi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>Also written as: atthin<sup>1</sup></p><ol><li>is exists; is found.</li><li>is of, belongs to (gen.).</li><li>as auxiliary verb with pp.</li><li>atthi is frequently used (usually at the beginning of a clause), with sg. or pi. subject (even with 1 sg. or 2sg.), to mean: there is, there are; there exists; or with a following verb (so also santiy to mean: there is (exists)… who…; it is the case that….</li></ol><p>atthi(n)<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>mfn. (mfn., sg. nom. m. ~i) desirous; wanting something; having an aim.</p>

atthi-paccaya
<p>[Nyana]</p><p></p><p><strong>Atthi-paccaya:</strong> Presence, is one of the 24 conditional relations <em>paccaya</em>.</p>

atthi
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to be, to exist.<br />pres Ind. 1<!-- raw HTML omitted -->st<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg. <em><a href="bword://asmi">asmi</a></em> Snp.1120, Snp.1143; Ja.i.151; Ja.iii.55 and <strong>amhi</strong> MN.i.429; Snp.694; Ja.ii.153; Pv.i.10#2; Pv.ii.8#2.<br />■ 2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->nd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg. <em><a href="bword://asi">asi</a></em> Snp.420; Ja.ii.160 (’si); Ja.iii.278; Vv.32#4 Pv-a.4.<br />■ 3<!-- raw HTML omitted -->rd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg. <em><a href="bword://atthi">atthi</a></em> Snp.377, Snp.672, Snp.884; Ja.i.278 Often used for 3<!-- raw HTML omitted -->rd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> pl. (= santi), e.g. Ja.i.280; Ja.ii.2 Ja.iii.55.<br />■ 1<!-- raw HTML omitted -->st<!-- raw HTML omitted --> pl. <em>asma</em> [Sk. smaḥ] Snp.594, Snp.595; asmase Snp.595, and <em><a href="bword://amha">amha</a></em> Snp.570; Ja.ii.128.<br />■ 2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->nd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> pl. <em><a href="bword://attha">attha</a></em> Ja.ii.128; Pv-a.39, Pv-a.74 (āgat’ attha you <em>have</em> come).<br />■ 3<!-- raw HTML omitted -->rd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> pl. <em><a href="bword://santi">santi</a></em> Snp.1077; Cnd.637 (= saṃvijjanti atthi upalabbhanti); Ja.ii.353; Pv-a.7, Pv-a.22<br />imper <em><a href="bword://atthu">atthu</a></em> Snp.340; Ja.i.59; Ja.iii.26<br />pot 1<!-- raw HTML omitted -->st<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg. <em>siyā</em> [Sk. syām] Pv.ii.8#8, and <em>assaṃ</em> [Cond. used as Pot.] Snp.1120; Pv.i.12#5 (= bhaveyyaṃ Pv-a.64).<br />■ 2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->nd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg. <em>siyā</em> [Sk. syāḥ] Pv.ii.8#7.<br />■ 3<!-- raw HTML omitted -->rd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg. <em>siyā</em> [Sk. syāt] DN.ii.154; Snp.325, Snp.1092 Cnd.105 (= jāneyya, nibbatteyya); Ja.i.262; Pv-a.13, and <em><a href="bword://assa">assa</a></em> DN.i.135, DN.i.196; DN.ii.154; AN.v.194; Snp.49, Snp.143; Dhp.124, Dhp.260; Pv.ii.3#24; Pv.ii.9#24.<br />■ 1<!-- raw HTML omitted -->st<!-- raw HTML omitted --> pl. <em><a href="bword://assu">assu</a></em> Pv-a.27.<br />■ 3<!-- raw HTML omitted -->rd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> pl. <em><a href="bword://assu">assu</a></em> [cp. Sk. syuḥ] Snp.532; Dhp.74; Pv.iv.1#36 (= bhaveyyuṃ Pv-a.231)<br />aor 1<!-- raw HTML omitted -->st<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg. <em><a href="bword://%C4%81si%E1%B9%83">āsiṃ</a></em> [Sk. āsaṃ] Snp.284; Pv.i.2#1 (= ahosiṃ Pv-a.10); Pv.ii.3#4 (= ahosiṃ Pv-a.83)<br />■ 3<!-- raw HTML omitted -->rd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg. <em><a href="bword://%C4%81si">āsi</a></em> [Sk. āsīt] Snp.994.<br />■ 3<!-- raw HTML omitted -->rd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> <em><a href="bword://%C4%81su%E1%B9%83">āsuṃ</a></em> [cp. Sk. Perf. āsuḥ] Pv.ii.3#21, Pv.ii.13#3 (ti pi pāṭho for su).<br />ppr <em>*sat</em> only in loc. <em><a href="bword://sati">sati</a></em> (as loc. abs.) Dhp.146; Ja.i.150 Ja.i.263, <em><a href="bword://santa">santa</a></em> Snp.105; Cnd.635; Ja.i.150 (loc. evaṃ sante in this case); Ja.iii.26, and <em><a href="bword://sam%C4%81na">samāna</a></em> (q.v.) Ja.i.266; Ja.iv.138.</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://bh%C4%81va">bhāva</a></em> state of being, existence, being Ja.i.222, Ja.i.290 Ja.ii.415; Dhp-a.ii.5; Dhp-a.iv.217 (atthibhāva vā natthibhāva vā whether there is or not).</li></ul><p>Sk. asti, 1<!-- raw HTML omitted -->st<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg. asmi; Gr. εἰμί ἐστί; Lat. sum-est; Goth. im-ist; Ags. eom-is E. am-is</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://asmi">asmi</a>, amhi, <a href="bword://asi">asi</a>, <a href="bword://atthi">atthi</a>, <a href="bword://amha">amha</a>, <a href="bword://attha">attha</a>, <a href="bword://santi">santi</a>, <a href="bword://atthu">atthu</a>, <a href="bword://assa">assa</a>, <a href="bword://assu">assu</a>, <a href="bword://assu">assu</a>, <a href="bword://āsiṃ">āsiṃ</a>, <a href="bword://āsi">āsi</a>, <a href="bword://āsuṃ">āsuṃ</a>, <a href="bword://sati">sati</a>, <a href="bword://santa">santa</a>, <a href="bword://samāna">samāna</a>, <a href="bword://bhāva">bhāva</a></p>

atthika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>atthika<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>mfn. desiring, wanting (instr.); aiming at, having as purpose (instr.); in need (of, instr.).</p><p>atthika<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>mfn. who believes in the existence (of merit, another world, etc).</p>

atthika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective</p><ol><li>(to attha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted -->) profitable, good, proper. In this meaning the MSS show a variance of spelling either <em><a href="bword://atthika">atthika</a></em> or <em><a href="bword://a%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADhika">aṭṭhika</a></em> or <em><a href="bword://a%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADhita">aṭṭhita</a></em>; in all cases atthika should be preferred DN.i.55 (˚vāda); MN.ii.212 (aṭṭhita); AN.iii.219 sq. (idaṃ atthikaṃ this is suitable, of good avail; T aṭṭhitaṃ, vv.ll. as above); Snp.1058 (aṭṭhita Cnd.20 also aṭṭhita, which at this pass. shows a confusion between aṭṭha and a-ṭhita); Ja.v.151 (in def. of aṭṭhikatvā q.v.); Pp.69, Pp.70 (T aṭṭhika, aṭṭhita SS; expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> by Pp AN.v.4 by kalyāṇāya).</li><li>(to attha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --> 2) desirous of (-˚) wanting, seeking for, in need of (c. instr.) AN.ii.199 (uday desirous of increase); Snp.333, Snp.460, Snp.487 (puññ˚), Snp.987 (dhan˚ greedy for wealth); Ja.i.263 (rajj˚ coveting a kingdom); Ja.v.19; Pv.ii.2#28 (bhojan˚ in need of food); Pv.iv.1#1 (kāraṇ˚), Pv.iv.1#21 (khiḍḍ˚ for play), Pv.iv.1#63 (puññ˚); Pv-a.95 (sasena a. wanting a rabbit), Pv-a.120; DN-a.i.70 (atthikā those who like to). <em>-anatthika</em> one who does not care for, or is not satisfied with (c. instr.) Ja.v.460; Pv-a.20; of no good Thag.956 (“of little zeal” Mrs. Rh. D.).</li></ol><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://bh%C4%81va">bhāva</a></em></li></ul><ol><li>usefulness, profitableness Pp AN.v.4.</li><li>state of need, distress Pv-a.120.</li></ol><p>cp. Sk. arthika</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://atthika">atthika</a>, <a href="bword://aṭṭhika">aṭṭhika</a>, <a href="bword://aṭṭhita">aṭṭhita</a>, <a href="bword://bhāva">bhāva</a></p>

atthikava
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://atthikavat">atthikavat</a></p><p>wanting something; having a purpose</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://atthika">atthika</a></p>

atthikavant
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective one who wants something, one who is on a certain errand DN.i.90 (atthikaṃ assa atthī ti DN-a.i.255).</p><p>atthika + vant</p>

atthikavat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://atthikavat">atthikavat</a></p><p>wanting something; having a purpose</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://atthika">atthika</a></p>

atthikavāda|atthikavaada|atthikavada
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine &amp; mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthikavaada</span></p><ol><li>(m.) the doctrine that (merit, another world, etc) exists.</li><li>(mfn.) following, professing that doctrine</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://atthika">atthika</a></p>

atthin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>Also written as: atthin<sup>1</sup></p><ol><li>is exists; is found.</li><li>is of, belongs to (gen.).</li><li>as auxiliary verb with pp.</li><li>atthi is frequently used (usually at the beginning of a clause), with sg. or pi. subject (even with 1 sg. or 2sg.), to mean: there is, there are; there exists; or with a following verb (so also santiy to mean: there is (exists)… who…; it is the case that….</li></ol><p>atthi(n)<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>mfn. (mfn., sg. nom. m. ~i) desirous; wanting something; having an aim.</p>

atthin
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective (-˚) desirous, wanting anything; see mant˚, vād˚.</p><p>Vedic arthin</p>

atthisukha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>delighting in possessing something, in the existence of something.</p>

atthitā|atthitaa|atthita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthitaa</span></p><p>existence; being; reality.</p>

atthitā|atthitaa|atthita
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthitaa</span></p><p>state of being, existence, being, reality MN.i.486; SN.ii.17 (˚añ c˚ eva natthitañ ca to be and not to be); SN.iii.135; Ja.v.110 (kassaci atthitaṃ vā natthitaṃ vā jānāhi see if there is anybody or not); Dhs-a.394<br />■ Often in abl. <em>atthitāya</em> by reason of, on account of, this being so Dhp-a.iii.344 (idamatthitāya under this condition) Pv-a.94, Pv-a.97, Pv-a.143.</p><p>f. abstr. fr. atthi cp. atthibhāva</p>

atthiya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>having a purpose or goal; useful, proper, fit.</p>

atthiya
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective (-˚) having a purpose or end SN.iii.189 (kim˚ for what purpose?); AN.v.1 sq. (id.), Snp.311 sq.; Thag.1097 (att˚ having one’s purpose in oneself) Thag.1274; Snp.354 (yad atthiyaṃ on account of what).</p><p>= atthika</p>

atthopasaṃhita|atthopasa.mhita|atthopasamhita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthopasa.mhita</span></p><p>connected with the goal, or with what is beneficial</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://atthi">atthi</a></p>

atthāra|atthaara|atthara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthaara</span></p><p>spreading, covering (the <em>kaṭhina</em>); performing the <em>kaṭhina</em> robe-making and ritual; displaying the <em>kaṭhina</em> robe.</p>

atthāra|atthaara|atthara
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthaara</span></p><p>spreading out Vin.v.172 (see <em><a href="bword://ka%E1%B9%ADhina">kaṭhina</a></em>). <em><a href="bword://atth%C4%81raka">atthāraka</a></em> same ibid.; Vin.ii.87 (covering).</p><p>cp. Sk. āstāra, fr. attharati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://kaṭhina">kaṭhina</a>, <a href="bword://atthāraka">atthāraka</a></p>

atthāraka|atthaaraka|attharaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">m(fn).</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthaaraka</span></p><p>(one) who covers (the <em>kaṭhina</em>); who supervises the communal robe-making and ritual.</p>

atthāya|atthaaya|atthaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">dat.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthaaya</span></p><p>for the benefit of; for the sake of (gen.)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthūpaparikkhi|atthuupaparikkhi|atthupaparikkhi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthuupaparikkhi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://atthūpaparikkhin">atthūpaparikkhin</a></p><p>investigating the meaning; inquiring into the significance</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

atthūpaparikkhin|atthuupaparikkhin|atthupaparikkhin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atthuupaparikkhin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://atthūpaparikkhin">atthūpaparikkhin</a></p><p>investigating the meaning; inquiring into the significance</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a></p>

