attukkaṃsana|attukka.msana|attukkamsana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter \~ā, feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">attukka.msana</span></p><p>self-praise</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://atta">atta</a></p>

attā|attaa|atta
<p>[Nyana]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">attaa</span></p><p><strong>Attā:</strong> Self, ego, personality, soul, is in Buddhism a mere conventional expression <em>vohāradesanā,</em> and not a designation for anything really existing; see: <em>paramattha-desanā, anattā, puggala, satta, jīva.</em></p>

attādhipateyya|attaadhipateyya|attadhipateyya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">attaadhipateyya</span></p><p>controlled by oneself</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://atta">atta</a></p>

attādāna|attaadaana|attadana
