atītaṃ|atiita.m|atitam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">acc.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atiita.m</span></p><p>in the past</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://atīta">atīta</a></p>

atītaṃsa|atiita.msa|atitamsa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atiita.msa</span></p><p>the past</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://atīta">atīta</a></p>

atītaṭṭha|atiita.t.tha|atitattha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. &amp; masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atiita.t.tha</span></p><p>who has missed his profit</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://atīta">atīta</a></p>

atīte|atiite|atite
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">loc.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atiite</span></p><p>in the past</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://atīta">atīta</a></p>

atīva|atiiva|ativa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(?)</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atiiva</span></p><p>very much, exceedingly</p><p>See also: ati-</p>

atīva|atiiva|ativa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">atiiva</span></p><p>indeclinable very much, exceedingly Ja.ii.413; Mhvs.33, Mhvs.2 etc.</p><p>ati + iva, see also <em><a href="bword://ativiya">ativiya</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ativiya">ativiya</a></p>

auditory organ
