<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">a~n~naataavin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://aññātāvin">aññātāvin</a></p><p>who has complete insight; (completely understood?).</p>

aññātāvin|a~n~naataavin|annatavin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">a~n~naataavin</span></p><p>adjective noun one who has complete insight Dhs-a.291.</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://indriya">indriya</a></em> (˚tāv’ indr.) the faculty of one whose knowledge is made perfect Dhs.555 (cp. <em>Dhs trsl.</em> 150) and same loci as under aññindriya (see <em><a href="bword://a%C3%B1%C3%B1%C4%81">aññā</a></em>).</li></ul><p>from ājānāti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://indriya">indriya</a>, <a href="bword://aññā">aññā</a></p>

aññātāvindriya|a~n~naataavindriya|annatavindriya
