aṭṭhika|a.t.thika|atthika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">a.t.thika</span></p><ol><li>a bone.</li><li>a stone or seed (of a fruit).</li></ol>

aṭṭhika|a.t.thika|atthika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">a.t.thika</span></p><p>Aṭṭhika<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>neuter</p><ol><li>= aṭṭhi 1, a bone MN.iii.92; Ja.i.265, Ja.i.428; Ja.vi.404; Pv-a.41.</li><li>= aṭṭhi 2, kernel, stone Dhp-a.ii.53 (tāl˚); Mhvs.15, Mhvs.42.</li></ol><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://sa%E1%B9%85khalik%C4%81">saṅkhalikā</a></em> a chain of bones, a skeleton AN.iii.324 see also under kaṭaṭṭhika.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://sa%C3%B1%C3%B1%C4%81">saññā</a></em> the idea of a skeleton SN.v.129 sq.; AN.ii.17; Dhs.264.</li></ul><p>fr. aṭṭhi</p><p>Aṭṭhika<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>at Pv-a.180 (sūcik˚) to be read aṭṭita (q.v.) for aṭṭika.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://saṅkhalikā">saṅkhalikā</a>, <a href="bword://saññā">saññā</a></p>

aṭṭhikadali|a.t.thikadali|atthikadali
<p>[Dhammika]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">a.t.thikadali</span></p><p>A type of banana tree Ja.v.406.</p>

