catu-vokāra-bhava|catu-vokaara-bhava|catu-vokara-bhava
<p>[Nyana]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">catu-vokaara-bhava</span></p><p><strong>Catu-vokāra-bhava:</strong> ‘four-group existence’, is the existence in the immaterial world <em>arūpa</em> - <em>loka</em> see: <em>loka</em> since only the four mental groups feeling, perception, mental constructions, consciousness, see: <em>khandha</em> are found there, the materiality group being absent. Cf. <em>pañca-vokāra-bhava, eka-vokāra-bhava</em> App.: <em>vokāra</em>.</p>

