chava
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">m.f. &amp; mfn.</i></p><ol><li>(m. f.) a corpse; a dead body.</li><li>(mfn.) vile; base; wretched; inferior; paltry.</li></ol>

chava
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>a corpse Vin.ii.115 (˚sīsassa patta a bowl made out of a skull) See compounds</li><li>(adj.) vile, low, miserable, wretched Vin.ii.112, Vin.ii.188; SN.i.66; MN.i.374; AN.ii.57; Ja.iv.263.</li></ol><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://a%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADhika">aṭṭhika</a></em> bones of a corpses, a skeleton C iii.15, 1 (?)</li><li><em>-ālāta</em> a torch from a pyre SN.iii.93 = AN.ii.95 = Iti.90; Ja.i.482; Vism.54, Vism.299 (˚ûpama).</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://ku%E1%B9%ADik%C4%81">kuṭikā</a></em> a charnelhouse morgue, Vin.i.152;</li><li><em>-dāhaka</em> one who (officially burns the dead, an “undertaker” Vin.i.152; Dhp-a.i.68 (f. ˚ikā); Vism.230; Mil.331.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://dussa">dussa</a></em> a miserable garment DN.i.166≈AN.i.240; AN.ii.206.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://sar%C4%ABra">sarīra</a></em> a corpse Vism.178 sq.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://sitta">sitta</a></em> a water pot (see above 1) Thag.127.</li></ul><p>Derivation doubtful. Vedic śava</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://aṭṭhika">aṭṭhika</a>, <a href="bword://kuṭikā">kuṭikā</a>, <a href="bword://dussa">dussa</a>, <a href="bword://sarīra">sarīra</a>, <a href="bword://sitta">sitta</a></p>

chavadussa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>clothes from corpses or very poor clothes.</p>

