chaḍḍaka|cha.d.daka|chaddaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cha.d.daka</span></p><p>adjective throwing away, removing, in <em>puppha˚ a</em> flower-rubbish remover (see <em><a href="bword://pukkusa">pukkusa</a></em>) Thag.620; Vism.194<br />■ f. <em>chaḍḍikā</em> see *<a href="bword://kacavara">kacavara</a>*˚.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://pukkusa">pukkusa</a>, <a href="bword://kacavara">kacavara</a></p>

chaḍḍana|cha.d.dana|chaddana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cha.d.dana</span></p><p>throwing away, rejecting Ja.i.290; Dhtp.571<br />■ ī (f.) a shovel, dust-pan Dhp-a.iii.7. See kacavara˚</p>

chaḍḍanīyadhamma|cha.d.daniiyadhamma|chaddaniyadhamma
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cha.d.daniiyadhamma</span></p><p>to be thrown away.</p>

chaḍḍayati|cha.d.dayati|chaddayati
