cheda
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>cutting, destruction, loss Snp.367 (˚bandhana); Ja.i.419; Ja.i.485; <em>sīsa˚</em>; decapitation Dhp-a.ii.204; Pv-a.5; <em>aṇḍa˚</em>; castration Ja.iv.364; - <em><a href="bword://bhatta">bhatta</a></em> ˚ṃ karoti to put on short rations Ja.i.156. <em>pada˚</em>; separation of words Snp-a.150. <em>-gāmin</em> (adj.) liable to break fragile AN.ii.81; Ja.v.453<br />■ Cp. vi˚.</p><p>see <em><a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://bhatta">bhatta</a>, <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a></p>

chedagāmi|chedagaami|chedagami
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chedagaami</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://chedagāmin">chedagāmin</a></p><p>going to naught, ending in loss; certain to break.</p>

chedagāmin|chedagaamin|chedagamin
