cheka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><ol><li>competent, expert, knowledgeable (about); skilful, skilled (in, usually loc.); clever, good at.</li><li>good, bright, pure; proper, true, genuine.</li></ol>

cheka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective</p><ol><li>clever, skilful, shrewd; skilled in (c. loc.) Vin.ii.96; MN.i.509; Ja.i.290 (anga-vijjāya); Ja.ii.161, Ja.ii.403, Ja.v.216, Ja.v.366 (˚pāpaka good &amp; bad); Ja.vi.294 (id.); Mil.293.; DN-a.i.90; Vv-a.36, Vv-a.215; Dhp-a.i.178.</li><li>genuine Vism.437 (opp. kūṭa).</li></ol>

chekatā|chekataa|chekata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chekataa</span></p><p>skill Vv-a.131.</p><p>cheka + tā</p>

cheppā|cheppaa|cheppa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cheppaa</span></p><p>the tail.</p>

cheppā|cheppaa|cheppa
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cheppaa</span></p><p>tail Vin.i.191; Vin.iii.21.</p><p>Sk. sépa</p>

cheta
<p>[Dhammika]</p><p></p><p>Asiatic Cheetah, <em>Acinonyx jabatus</em> <em>ventaicus</em> S.i.198. This large predatory cat has a lean body and small head, a creamy-yellow coat with black and brown spots and a white underside. In medieval times and even in the early 20<!-- raw HTML omitted -->th<!-- raw HTML omitted --> century cheetahs were captured and trained for hunting. The last sighting of a cheetah in India was in 1948 and now the animal is found only in Iran. The Indians have long confused the cheetah with the leopard and both the Hindi and Bengali word <em>cheeta</em> is used for both. Thus the Pāḷi word may refer to either creature also.</p>

cheta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://chetar">chetar</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chettar">chettar</a></p>

cheta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>an animal living in mountain cliffs, a sort of leopard SN.i.198.</p>

chetabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chettabba">chettabba</a></p>

chetar
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://chetar">chetar</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chettar">chettar</a></p>

chetta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://chettar">chettar</a></p><p>one who cuts; one who cuts off; one who cuts away.</p>

chettabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a></p>

chettar
