chida
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(always-˚) adjective breaking, cutting, destroying MN.i.386; SN.i.191 = Thag.1234; Thag.521; Thag.1143; Snp.87 (kankha˚), Snp.491, Snp.1021, Snp.1101 (taṇha˚); Vv-a.82 (id.).</p>

chidda
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. &amp; neuter</i></p><ol><li>(mfn.) having a hole or holes; split; having gaps; defective.</li><li>(n., pl. acc. <em>~ani</em>, <em>~e</em>) a hole; a split; an opening; a weak point.</li></ol>

chidda
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>(adj.) having rents or fissures, perforated SN.iv.316; Ja.i.419; (fig.) faulty, defective, Vin.i.290.</li><li>(nt.) a cutting, slit, hole aperture, SN.i.43; Ja.i.170 (eka˚), Ja.i.172, Ja.i.419, Ja.i.503; Ja.ii.244 Ja.ii.261; (kaṇṇa˚); Vism.171, Vism.172 (bhitti˚), Vism.174 (tāḷa˚) Snp-a.248 (akkhi˚); Dhp-a.iii.42; Vv-a.100 (bhitti˚) Pv-a.180 (kaṇṇa˚), Pv-a.253 (read chidde for chinde); fig a fault, defect, flaw Dhp.229 (acchidda-vutti faultless conduct) Mil.94.</li></ol><ul><li><em>-āvachidda</em> full of breaches and holes Ja.iii.491 Vism.252; Dhp-a.i.122, Dhp-a.i.284 (cp. ˚vichidda); Dhp-a.iii.151</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://k%C4%81rin">kārin</a></em> inconsistent AN.ii.187;</li><li><em>-vichidda</em> = ˚âvachidda Ja.i.419; Ja.v.163 (sarīraṃ chiddavichiddaṃ karoti to perforate a body).</li></ul><p>cp. Ohg. scetar. For suffix ˚ra, cp. rudhira, etc. Vedic <em>chid</em> + ra. Cp. Sk. chidra</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://kārin">kārin</a></p>

chiddaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective having holes or meshes (of a net) DN.i.45.</p>

chiddakarin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>making a split (in); making defective.</p>

chiddatā|chiddataa|chiddata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chiddataa</span></p><p>perforation, being perforated Ja.i.419.</p>

chiddava
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://chiddavat">chiddavat</a></p><p>having a hole; defective.</p>

chiddavant
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective having faults, full of defects MN.i.272.</p>

chiddavat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://chiddavat">chiddavat</a></p><p>having a hole; defective.</p>

chiddāvacchidda|chiddaavacchidda|chiddavacchidda
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chiddaavacchidda</span></p><p>full of holes; full of large or small holes.</p>

chief-elements
<p>[Nyana]</p><p></p><p><strong>Chief-elements:</strong> the 4: <em>mahā-bhūta</em> -d <em>hātu</em></p>

chiggala
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine neuter a</i></p><p>hole?</p>

chiggaḷa|chigga.la|chiggala
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chigga.la</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chiggala">chiggala</a></p>

chiggaḷa|chigga.la|chiggala
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chigga.la</span></p><p>hole, in eka˚-yuga MN.iii.169≈; tāḷa˚ key hole SN.iv.290; Vism.394.</p><p>cp. chidda</p>

chijjamāna|chijjamaana|chijjamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chijjamaana</span></p><p>of chijjati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chijjati">chijjati</a></p>

chijjatha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>of chijjati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chijjati">chijjati</a></p>

chijjati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>chijjati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>pr. 3 sg. of chindati; (quasi 4th class, in form identical with pass.; the meanings overlap), (intrans.) breaks, breaks off; dries up, comes to an end.</p><p>chijjati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>pass. pr. 3 sg. of chindati is cut; is cut off; is cut down; is destroyed; is brought to an end</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a>, <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a></p>

chinda
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://chindat">chindat</a></p><p>of chindati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a></p>

chindanaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective breaking, see *<a href="bword://pari">pari</a>*˚.</p><p>fr. chindati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://pari">pari</a></p>

chindanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mf</i></p><p>(~antī)n. of chindati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a></p>

chindat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://chindat">chindat</a></p><p>of chindati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a></p>

chindati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><ol><li>cuts; chops; cuts off; cuts out; inscribes.</li><li>cuts down; destroys; removes.</li><li>crosses (water)</li></ol>

chindati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to cut off, to destroy, to remove, both <em>lit.</em> (bandhanaṃ, pāsaṃ, pasibbakaṃ, jīvaṃ, gīvaṃ, sīsaṃ hatthapāde, etc.) and <em>fig.</em> (taṇhaṃ, mohaṃ, āsavā saṃyojanāni, vicikicchaṃ, vanathaṃ, etc.) Freq. in similes: see <em>J.P.T.S.</em> 1907, 88</p><h3>Forms</h3><ol><li><em>chid</em>: aor <em>acchidā</em> Snp.357, as acchidaṃ MN.ii.35, acchidda Dhp.351 (cp. agamā); Pass. pres. <em><a href="bword://chijjati">chijjati</a></em> (Sk. chidyate) Dhp.284; Iti.70; Ja.i.167; Thag.1055 = Mil.395; Mil.40; aor chijji Ja.iii.181 (dvidhā ch. broke in two)<br />fut <em>chijjissati</em> Ja.i.336<br />ger <strong>chijjitvā</strong> Ja.i.202; Ja.iv.120<br />pp <em>chijjita</em> Ja.iii.389; see also <em><a href="bword://chida">chida</a></em>, chidda, chinna.</li><li><em>chind</em>: Act. pres. <em><a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a></em> SN.i.149 = AN.v.174; Snp.657; Pv-a.4, Pv-a.114; Vv-a.123<br />imper chinda Snp.346; Ja.ii.153; <em>chindatha</em> Dhp.283<br />pot chinde Dhp.370<br />ppr <strong>chindamāna</strong> Ja.i.70, Ja.i.233<br />fut <em>chindissati</em> Dhp-a.ii.258<br />aor <em><a href="bword://acchindi">acchindi</a></em> Vin.i.88 &amp; chindi Ja.i.140<br />ger <em><a href="bword://chinditv%C4%81">chinditvā</a></em> Ja.i.222, Ja.i.254, Ja.i.326; Ja.ii.155.<br />inf <em>chindituṃ</em> Vin.i.206; Pv-a.253<br />grd <em><a href="bword://chindiya">chindiya</a></em> Ja.ii.139 (duc˚)<br />caus <em>chindāpeti</em> Ja.ii.104, Ja.ii.106; Vism.190 (rājāno core ch.)</li><li><em>ched</em>: fut. <em>checchati</em> (Sk chetsyati) MN.i.434; Dhp.350; Mil.391<br />aor <em><a href="bword://acchecchi">acchecchi</a></em> (Sk. acchaitsīt) SN.i.12; AN.ii.249; Snp.355 = Thag.1275; Ja.vi.261. <em>acchejji</em> (variant reading of acchecchi) is read at SN.iv.205, SN.iv.207, SN.iv.399; SN.v.441; AN.iii.246, AN.iii.444; Iti.47<br />inf <em>chetuṃ</em> Ja.iv.208; Pv.iv.3#28, &amp; chettuṃ Snp.28<br />ger <em><a href="bword://chetv%C4%81">chetvā</a></em> Snp.66, Snp.545, Snp.622; Dhp.283, Dhp.369; Ja.i.255; Cnd.245 &amp; <em><a href="bword://chetv%C4%81na">chetvāna</a></em> Snp.44; Dhp.346; Ja.iii.396<br />grd <em>chetabba</em> Vin.ii.110, &amp; <em><a href="bword://chejja">chejja</a></em> (often combined w. bhejja, torture &amp; maiming, as punishments) Vin.iii.47 (+ bh˚); Ja.v.444 (id.), Ja.vi.536; Mil.83, Mil.359. Also <em><a href="bword://chejja">chejja</a></em> in neg acchejja SN.vi.226<br />caus <em>chedeti</em> Vin.i.50, &amp; <em><a href="bword://ched%C4%81peti">chedāpeti</a></em> ib.; Ja.iv.154. See also cheda, chedana.</li></ol><p>Vedic <em>chid</em> in 3 forms viz. 1 (Perf.) base <em>chid</em>; 2 Act. (pres.) base w. nasal infix. <em>chind</em>; 3 Med (denom). base w. guṇa <em>ched</em>. Cp. the analagous formations of <em>cit</em> under cinteti<br />■ Idg.* <em>sk(h)eid</em>, Gr. σξίζω (E. schism); Lat. scindo (E. scissors); Ohg scīzan; Ags. scītan; cp. also Goth. skaidan, Ohg. sceidan Root <em>chid</em> is defined at Dhtp.382, Dhtp.406 as “dvedhākaraṇa”</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chijjati">chijjati</a>, chijjitvā, <a href="bword://chida">chida</a>, <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a>, chindamāna, <a href="bword://acchindi">acchindi</a>, <a href="bword://chinditvā">chinditvā</a>, <a href="bword://chindiya">chindiya</a>, <a href="bword://acchecchi">acchecchi</a>, <a href="bword://chetvā">chetvā</a>, <a href="bword://chetvāna">chetvāna</a>, <a href="bword://chejja">chejja</a>, <a href="bword://chejja">chejja</a>, <a href="bword://chedāpeti">chedāpeti</a></p>

chindi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>chindi<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>aor. 3 sg. of chindati</p><p>chindi<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>2 sg. of chindati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a>, <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a></p>

chindita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp neuter</i></p><p>cutting.</p>

chinditar
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://chinditar">chinditar</a></p><p>(from chindati) one who cuts.</p>

chindituṃ|chinditu.m|chinditum
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">inf.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chinditu.m</span></p><p>of chindati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a></p>

chinditvā|chinditvaa|chinditva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chinditvaa</span></p><p>of chindati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a></p>

chindiya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i></p><p>of chindati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a></p>

chindiṃsu|chindi.msu|chindimsu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 pl.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chindi.msu</span></p><p>of chindati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chindati">chindati</a></p>

chinna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn. &amp; neuter</i></p><ol><li>(mfn.) having broken; dried up; come to an end.</li><li>(mfn. &amp; n.) cut; cut off; cut away; cut down; destroyed; cutting.</li></ol>

chinna
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>cut off, destroyed Vin.i.71 (acchinna-kesa with unshaven hair); MN.i.430; DN.ii.8 (˚papañca); Ja.i.255; Ja.ii.155; Ja.iv.138; Dhp.338; Pv.i.11#2 (variant reading for bhinna), Pv.i.11#6; Dhp-a.iv.48. Very often in punishments of decapitation (sīsa˚) or mutilation (hatthapāda˚, etc.) e.g. Vin.i.91; Vin.iii.28; Pv.ii.2#4 (ghāna-sīsa˚); Mil.5. Cp. sañ˚. As first part of cpd. chinna˚ very frequently is to be rendered by “without”, e.g. <em>-āsa</em> without hope Ja.ii.230; Pv-a.22, Pv-a.174; <em>-<a href="bword://iriy%C4%81patha">iriyāpatha</a></em> unable to walk, i.e. a cripple Vin.i.91; <em>-<a href="bword://ka%E1%B9%87%E1%B9%87a">kaṇṇa</a></em> without ears Pv-a.151; <em>-<a href="bword://gantha">gantha</a></em> untrammelled, unfettered Snp.219; <em>-<a href="bword://pilotika">pilotika</a></em> with torn rags, or without rags SN.ii.28; Pv-a.171 (+ bhinna˚); <em>-<a href="bword://bhatta">bhatta</a></em> without food i.e. famished starved Ja.i.84; Ja.v.382; Dhp-a.iii.106 = Vv-a.76 <em>-<a href="bword://sa%E1%B9%83saya">saṃsaya</a></em> without doubt Snp.1112; Iti.96, Iti.97, Iti.123; Cnd.244. <em>-<a href="bword://s%C4%81%E1%B9%ADaka">sāṭaka</a></em> a torn garment Vism.51.</p><p>pp. of chindati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://iriyāpatha">iriyāpatha</a>, <a href="bword://kaṇṇa">kaṇṇa</a>, <a href="bword://gantha">gantha</a>, <a href="bword://pilotika">pilotika</a>, <a href="bword://bhatta">bhatta</a>, <a href="bword://saṃsaya">saṃsaya</a>, <a href="bword://sāṭaka">sāṭaka</a></p>

chinnababbhara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chinnabhabbhara">chinnabhabbhara</a></p>

chinnabhabbhara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not making the sound bharabhara?</p>

chinnaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>, mf(~ikā)n.</p><ol><li>(mfn.) cut; made up of cut pieces of cloth.</li><li>(mf. (~ikā) n.) wanton, shameless; of loose morals.</li></ol>

chinnaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective cut; <em>a˚</em>; uncut (of cloth) Vin.i.297.</p><p>fr. chinna</p>

chinnamūlaka|chinnamuulaka|chinnamulaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chinnamuulaka</span></p><p>with its root(s) cut away.</p>

chinnapapātaṃ|chinnapapaata.m|chinnapapatam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chinnapapaata.m</span></p><p>adverb falling as if cut down; or with a sudden steep fall; ? headlong, precipitately.</p>

chinnapilotika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>revealed; uncovered.</p>

chinnapātaṃ|chinnapaata.m|chinnapatam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chinnapaata.m</span></p><p>adverb of chinnapapātaṃ</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chinnapapātaṃ">chinnapapātaṃ</a></p>

chinnasassara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not making the sound <em>saṃsara</em>?</p>

chinnasota
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>who has crossed or cut off the stream, who has brought the flow to an end.</p>

chinnavaṭuma|chinnava.tuma|chinnavatuma
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chinnava.tuma</span></p><p>who has brought the path to an end; who has broken the cycle.</p>

chinnikā|chinnikaa|chinnika
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chinnikaa</span></p><p>deceitful, fraudulent, sly, only in combination w. <em>dhuttā</em> (dhuttikā) &amp; only applied to women Vin.iii.128 Vin.iv.61; Ja.ii.114; Mil.122.</p>

chinniriyāpatha|chinniriyaapatha|chinniriyapatha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chinniriyaapatha</span></p><p>whose movement is destroyed, who is unable to move; a cripple.</p>

chubhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>given as root <em>chubh</em> (for <em>kṣubh</em>) with def. “nicchubhe” at Dhtm.550. See khobha.</p>

chuddha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>thrown away, rejected, abandoned.</p>

chuddha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>thrown away, removed, rejected, contemptible Dhp.41 = Thig.468 (spelled chuṭṭha); Ja.v.302.</p><p>Sk. kṣubdha (?) <em>kṣubh</em>, perhaps better <em>ṣṭīv</em>, pp. ṣṭyūta (see <em><a href="bword://ni%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADhubhati">niṭṭhubhati</a></em>), cp. Pischel, <em>Prk. Gr.</em> §§ 66, 120 &amp; Trenckner; <em>Notes</em> p.75See also khipita</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://niṭṭhubhati">niṭṭhubhati</a></p>

chuddhūna|chuddhuuna|chuddhuna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chuddhuuna</span></p><p>indeclinable having thrown away, rejected, abandoned.</p>

chupana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>touching.</p>

chupana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>touching Vin.iii.121; Ja.vi.387.</p>

chupanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>of chupati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chupati">chupati</a></p>

chupati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>touches.</p>

chupati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to touch Vin.i.191; Vin.iii.37, Vin.iii.121; Ja.iv.82; Ja.vi.166; Vism.249; Dhp-a.i.166 (mā chupi)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://chupita">chupita</a></em>.</p><p>Dhtp.480 = samphasse</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chupita">chupita</a></p>

chupi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>of chupati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chupati">chupati</a></p>

chupita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>touched.</p>

chupita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>touched Vin.iii.37; Ja.vi.218.</p><p>pp. of chupati</p>

chupitabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chupati">chupati</a></p>

churikā|churikaa|churika
