chādeti|chaadeti|chadeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaadeti</span></p><p>chādeti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>covers, covers over; hides, conceals.</p><p>chādeti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>pr. 3 sg.</p><ol><li>seems good (to, dat., sometimes acc.), pleases, is enjoyable (esp. of food)</li><li>gratifies, pleases.</li></ol>

chādeti|chaadeti|chadeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaadeti</span></p><p>Chādeti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><ol><li>to cover, to conceal Vin.ii.211 (Pass. chādīyati); Snp.1022 (mukhaṃ jivhāya ch.); Dhp.252; Pv.iii.4#3</li><li>(of sound) to penetrate, to fill Ja.ii.253; Ja.vi.195</li></ol><p>pp <em>channa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></em> (q.v.).</p><p>Caus. of <em>chad</em>, Sk. chādayati</p><p>Chādeti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><ol><li>to seem good, to please, to give pleasure SN.ii.110; AN.iii.54; Dhp-a.iii.285 (bhattaṃ me na ch.).</li><li>to be pleased with, to delight in, to approve of (c acc.) esp. in phrase bhattaṃ chādeti to appreciate the meal Vin.ii.138; DN.i.72 (= rucceyya); DN.v.31 (chādayamāna), DN.v.33 (chādamana), DN.v.463; Thig.409; Pv.i.11#8 (nacchādimhamhase), pp. <em>channa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></em>. Chapa &amp; ka;</li></ol><p>for chandeti, cp. Sk. chandati &amp; chadayati; to <em>khyā</em>?</p>

chādetvā|chaadetvaa|chadetva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaadetvaa</span></p><p>of chādeti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://chādeti">chādeti</a></p>

chādi|chaadi|chadi
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaadi</span></p><p>shade Ja.iv.351.</p><p>chādeti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p>

chādiya|chaadiya|chadiya
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaadiya</span></p><p>covering (of a house or hut), thatch, straw, hay (for eating) Ja.vi.354 (= gehacchādana-tiṇa).</p>

