<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaahapa.ticchanna</span></p><p>concealed for six days.</p>

chāka|chaaka|chaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaaka</span></p><p>Chāpa &amp; ˚ka</p><p>the young of an animal MN.i.384 (˚ka); SN.ii.269 (bhinka˚); Ja.i.460; Ja.ii.439 (sakuṇa˚) Mil.402<br />■ f. <em>chāpī</em> Ja.vi.192 (maṇḍūka˚).</p><p>Sk. śāva</p>

chāpa|chaapa|chapa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaapa</span></p><p>the young of an animal; a chick.</p>

chāpa|chaapa|chapa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaapa</span></p><p>Chāpa &amp; ˚ka</p><p>the young of an animal MN.i.384 (˚ka); SN.ii.269 (bhinka˚); Ja.i.460; Ja.ii.439 (sakuṇa˚) Mil.402<br />■ f. <em>chāpī</em> Ja.vi.192 (maṇḍūka˚).</p><p>Sk. śāva</p>

chāpi|chaapi|chapi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaapi</span></p><p>the young of an animal; a chick.</p>

chāratta|chaaratta|charatta
