chārikā|chaarikaa|charika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaarikaa</span></p><p>ash; ashes.</p>

chārikā|chaarikaa|charika
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaarikaa</span></p><p>Ashes Vin.i.210; Vin.ii.220; DN.ii.164 = Ud.93; AN.i.209; AN.iv.103; Ja.iii.447; Ja.iv.88; Ja.v.144; Dhp-a.i.256 Dhp-a.ii.68; Vv-a.67; Pv-a.80 (chārikangāra).</p><p>Cp. kṣāyati to burn, kṣāra burning; Gr. ςηρός dry, Lat. serenus dry, clear. See also <em><a href="bword://kh%C4%81ra">khāra</a></em> bhasma.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://khāra">khāra</a></p>

chāta|chaata|chata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaata</span></p><p>hungry.</p>

chāta|chaata|chata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaata</span></p><p>adjective hungry Ja.i.338; Ja.ii.301; Ja.v.69; Pv.ii.1#13 (= bubhukkhita, khudāya abhibhūta Pv-a.72 Pv.ii.9#36 (jighacchita Pv-a.126); Pv-a.62; Vv-a.76; Mil.253; Mhvs.vii.24. Cp. pari˚.</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://ajjhatta">ajjhatta</a></em> with hungry insides Ja.i.345; Ja.ii.203; Ja.v.338 Ja.v.359; Dhp-a.i.125; Dhp-a.i.367 (chātak’); Dhp-a.iii.33, Dhp-a.iii.40.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://k%C4%81la">kāla</a></em> time of being hungry.</li></ul><p>cp. Sk. psāta from <em>bhas</em> (*bhsā), Gr. ψώξω; see Walde, <em>Lat. Wtb.</em> under sabulum &amp; cp. bhasman probably Non-Aryan</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ajjhatta">ajjhatta</a>, <a href="bword://kāla">kāla</a></p>

chātaka|chaataka|chataka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaataka</span></p><ol><li>adj. hungry Ja.i.245, Ja.i.266.</li><li>(nt.) hunger, famine Ja.i.266; Ja.ii.124, Ja.ii.149, Ja.ii.367; Ja.vi.487; Dhp-a.i.170.</li></ol><p>fr. prec.</p>

chātatā|chaatataa|chatata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaatataa</span></p><p>hunger (lit. hungriness) Dhp-a.i.170.</p><p>f. abstr. fr. chāta</p>

chāyā|chaayaa|chaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaayaa</span></p><ol><li>shade; shadow.</li><li>the shadow (e.g. of a measuring-stick) measuring the time; the length of shadow (at the time of a bhikkhu’s <em>upasampadā</em>)</li></ol>

chāyā|chaayaa|chaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chaayaa</span></p><p>shade, shadow SN.i.72, SN.i.93; MN.ii.235; MN.iii.164; AN.ii.114; Snp.1014; Dhp.2; Ja.ii.302 Ja.iv.304; Ja.v.445; Mil.90, Mil.298; Dhp-a.i.35; Pv-a.12, Pv-a.32, Pv-a.45 Pv-a.81, etc<br />■ Yakkhas have none; Ja.v.34; Ja.vi.337. chāyā is frequent in similes: see <em>J.P.T.S.</em> 1907, 87.</p><p>Vedic chāyā, light &amp; shade; <em>*skei</em> (cp. <em>(s)qait</em> σκιά &amp; σκοιόςskia/ &amp; skoio/s; Goth. skeinan See note on kāla, vol. ii. p. 38<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p>

chūrikā|chuurikaa|churika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">chuurikaa</span></p><p>dagger; a knife.</p>

ci
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(cid in Sandhi) indef. interr particle (always-˚), in koci (= Sk. kaścid) whoever kiñci (kincid-eva) whatever, kadāci at some time or any time, etc. (q.v.), see also <em><a href="bword://ca">ca</a></em>, cana, ce.</p><p>Vedic cid nom. nt. to interr. base <em>*qṷi</em> (as in Gr. τίς, Lat. quis, Goth. hvi-leiks, see <em>ki</em>˚, cp ka˚, ku˚), = Gr. τ ́δ, Lat. quid &amp; quid (d)em, Av. ciṭ (cp. tad, yad, kad beside taṃ, yaṃ, kiṃ)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ca">ca</a></p>

cicciṭi|cicci.ti|cicciti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cicci.ti</span></p><p>(onomat.) a hissing sound.</p>

cicciṭāti|cicci.taati|ciccitati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cicci.taati</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://cicciṭāyati">cicciṭāyati</a></p>

cicciṭāyana|cicci.taayana|ciccitayana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cicci.taayana</span></p><p>fizzing Vism.408 (˚sadda).</p>

cicciṭāyati|cicci.taayati|ciccitayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cicci.taayati</span></p><p>hisses; fizzes; makes the sound “chit-chit”; makes a hissing sound.</p>

cicciṭāyati|cicci.taayati|ciccitayati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cicci.taayati</span></p><p>to hiss, fizz, sizzle (always combined with ciṭiciṭāyati) Vin.i.225; SN.i.169 Snp.p.15; Pp.36; Mil.258 sq.</p><p>onomat. cp. ciṭiciṭāyati</p>

cihacihābhinadita|cihacihaabhinadita|cihacihabhinadita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cihacihaabhinadita</span></p><p>(onomat). the sound of cihaciha birds; or the sound of chirping.</p>

cikicchati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>usually tikicchati to reflect, think over, intend aim at. Pp. <em>cikicchita</em> Kp-a.188 (in expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n<!-- raw HTML omitted --> of vicikicchita q.v.).</p><p>Sk. cikitsati, Desid. of <em>cit</em>, cinteti. Cp. vicikicchā</p>

cikkhalla
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">m.n. &amp; mfn.</i></p><ol><li>(m. n.) mire; mud.</li><li>(mfn.) muddy.</li></ol>

cikkhalla
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>mud, mire, swamp; often with udaka˚. Vin.i.253; Vin.ii.120 Vin.ii.159, Vin.ii.291: Vin.iii.41; AN.iii.394; Ja.i.196; Mil.286, Mil.311, Mil.397; Pv-a.102, Pv-a.189, Pv-a.215<br />■ (adj.) Vin.ii.221; Vin.iv.312; Pv.iv.1#16; Mil.286.</p><p>Sk. cikkaṇa &amp; cikkala, slippery + ya</p>

cikkhallavant
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective muddy Pv-a.225.</p>

cikkhassati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to wish to drop, to ooze out Mil.152 (˚ssanto), see Kern.</p><blockquote><p>Toevoegselen</p></blockquote><p>ii.139 &amp; Morris, <em>J.P.T.S.</em> 1884, 87.</p><p>Desid. of <em>kṣar</em> = Sk. cikṣariṣati</p>

cikkhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>(cikkhanā, etc.) to tell, to announce: see *<a href="bword://%C4%81">ā</a>*˚ &amp; paṭisaṃ˚.</p><p>Freq. of <em>khyā</em>, Dhtp.19: <em>cikkh</em> = vacane</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ā">ā</a></p>

cilimikā|cilimikaa|cilimika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cilimikaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://cimilika">cimilika</a></p>

cilimikā|cilimikaa|cilimika
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cilimikaa</span></p><p>as <em><a href="bword://cimilik%C4%81">cimilikā</a></em> at Vin.ii.150; Vin.iv.40 a kind of cloth or carpeting, made from palmleaves bark, etc. Also at Pv-a.144 (doubtful reading).</p><p>Der. fr. cīra</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://cimilikā">cimilikā</a></p>

cillaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i></p><p>peg, post, pillar, in <em>dāruka˚</em>; Thig.390 (cp. Thag-a.257). Not with Kern <em>(Toev.)</em> “a wooden puppet,” as der. fr. citta.<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>kilaka or khīlaka, q.v.</p>

cimilika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i></p><p>strip of cloth; an (under-) mat of strips of cloth; ?</p>

cimilikā|cimilikaa|cimilika
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cimilikaa</span></p><p>see <em><a href="bword://cilimik%C4%81">cilimikā</a></em> Vin.ii.150; Vin.iv.40; Cp. <em>Vin. Texts</em> iii.167; <em>J.P.T.S.</em> 1885, 39.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://cilimikā">cilimikā</a></p>

cinitvā|cinitvaa|cinitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cinitvaa</span></p><p>having heaped up; having collected.</p>

cintaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective one who thinks out or invents, in <em>akkhara˚</em>; the grammarian Pv-a.120, <em>nīti˚</em>; the lawgiver ib. Pv-a.130; cp. Divy.212, Divy.451, “overseer.”</p><p>cp. cintin</p>

cintana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>= cintā Thag.695; Mil.233.</p>

cintanaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective thoughtful, considerate Ja.i.222.</p>

cintayamāna|cintayamaana|cintayamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">cintayamaana</span></p><p>of cinteti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://cinteti">cinteti</a></p>

cintayanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mf</i></p><p>(~ayantī)n. of cinteti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://cinteti">cinteti</a></p>

