dadeyyāsi|dadeyyaasi|dadeyyasi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">2 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dadeyyaasi</span></p><p>of dassati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://dassati">dassati</a></p>

dadhate
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://dahati">dahati</a></p>

dadhi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>sour, coagulated milk.</p>

dadhi
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>sour milk, curds junket Vin.i.244 (in enum<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n<!-- raw HTML omitted --> of 5-fold cow-produce, cp gorasa); DN.i.201 (id.); MN.i.316; AN.ii.95; Ja.ii.102 Ja.iv.140; Mil.41, Mil.48, Mil.63; Dhs.646, Dhs.740, Dhs.875; Vism.264 Vism.362.</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://gha%E1%B9%ADa">ghaṭa</a></em> a milk bowl Ja.ii.102;</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://ma%E1%B9%87%E1%B8%8Daka">maṇḍaka</a></em> whey SN.ii.111</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://m%C4%81la">māla</a></em> “the milk sea,” Name of an ocean Ja.iv.140;</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://v%C4%81raka">vāraka</a></em> a pot of milk-curds Ja.iii.52.</li></ul><p>Sk. dadhi, redpl. formation fr. dhayati to suck. Cp. also dhenu cow, dhīta, etc.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ghaṭa">ghaṭa</a>, <a href="bword://maṇḍaka">maṇḍaka</a>, <a href="bword://māla">māla</a>, <a href="bword://vāraka">vāraka</a></p>

dadhimaṇḍaka|dadhima.n.daka|dadhimandaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dadhima.n.daka</span></p><p>whey.</p>

dadhimukha
<p>[DPPN]</p><p></p><p>A Yakkha chieftain who should be invoked by disciples of the Buddha in times of need. DN.iii.205</p>

