devata
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective (-˚) having such &amp; such a god as one’s special divinity, worshipping, a worshipper of, devotee of Mil.234 (Brahma˚ + Brahma (garuka)<br />■ f.; <em><a href="bword://devat%C4%81">devatā</a></em> in pati “worshipping the husband,” i.e. a devoted wife Ja.iii.406; Vv-a.128.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://devatā">devatā</a></p>

