dussanīya|dussaniiya|dussaniya
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dussaniiya</span></p><p>adjective able to give offence, hateful, evil (always combined with rajanīya, cp. rāga dosa moha AN.iii.110 (dusanīye dussati, where Iti.84 has dosaneyye) Ja.vi.9; Mil.386.</p><p>cp. Sk. dveṣanīya, because of doṣa = dveṣa taken to <em>dus</em></p>

dussapallaṭṭhikā|dussapalla.t.thikaa|dussapallatthika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dussapalla.t.thikaa</span></p><p>posture held with the help of a cloth.</p>

dussapata
