dussati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>dussati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>pr. 3 sg.</p><ol><li>be comes dirtied or spoilt or damaged.</li><li>commits a fault, does wrong.</li></ol><p>dussati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>pr. 3 sg. is unfriendly or hostile towards.</p>

dussati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to be or become bad or cor rupted, to get damaged; to offend against, to do wrong Vin.ii.113; SN.i.13 = SN.i.164; Dhp.125 = Pv-a.116; Dhp.137; Iti.84 (dosancyye na d.) cp. AN.iii.110 (dussanīye d.) Ja.vi.9; Mil.101, Mil.386<br />pp <em><a href="bword://du%E1%B9%AD%E1%B9%ADha">duṭṭha</a></em> (q.v.)<br />caus <em><a href="bword://d%C5%ABseti">dūseti</a></em> (q.v.). See also dosa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --> &amp; dosaniya; &amp; pa˚.</p><p>Sk. duṣyati, Denom. fr. pref. duḥ (du˚); pp. duṣṭha, caus. dūṣayati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://duṭṭha">duṭṭha</a>, <a href="bword://dūseti">dūseti</a></p>

dussavaṭṭi|dussava.t.ti|dussavatti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dussava.t.ti</span></p><p>roll of cloth; fringe of a cloth.</p>

dussaveṇi|dussave.ni|dussaveni
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dussave.ni</span></p><p>twist of plait of a cloth.</p>

dussaṃhara|dussa.mhara|dussamhara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dussa.mhara</span></p><p>hard to collect hard; hard to gather together.</p>

dussi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>of dussati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://dussati">dussati</a></p>

dussika
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i></p><p>cloth merchant Ja.vi.276; Mil.262, Mil.331 sq.</p>

