<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dutiya.m</span></p><p>adverb a second time; again.</p>

dutiyya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>, m.f.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://dutiya">dutiya</a></p>

dutiyyatā|dutiyyataa|dutiyyata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dutiyyataa</span></p><p>companionship, friendship, help Ja.iii.169.</p>

duttakkita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>incorrectly conjectured; badly thought out.</p>

duttappaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>hard to satisfy.</p>

duttara
