<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective noun</p><ol><li>twofold Snp.886 (saccaṃ musā ti dvayadhammaṃ); Dhp.384; Pv.iv.1#29 (dvayaṃ vipākaṃ = duvidhaṃ Pv-a.228)- <em>advaya</em> single AN.v.46</li><li>false, deceitful Vin.iii.21-nt. a duality, a pair, couple SN.ii.17 (˚ṃ nissito loko) Ja.iii.395 (gātha˚); Pv-a.19 (māsa˚); Dhp-a.ii.93 (pada two lines, “couplet”).</li></ol><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://k%C4%81rin">kārin</a></em> “doing both,” i.e. both good &amp; evil deeds (su˚ &amp; duccaritaṃ) SN.iii.241, cp. SN.iii.247 sq.; DN.iii.96.</li></ul><p>Ved. dvaya; cp. dvi B I. 6</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://kārin">kārin</a></p>

