dvidhā|dvidhaa|dvidha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dvidhaa</span></p><p>numerical adverb in two parts, in two MN.i.114; Ja.i.253 (karoti), Ja.i.254 (chindati); Ja.i.298 (id.); Ja.iii.181; Ja.iv.101 (jāta disagreeing); Ja.vi.368 (bhindati). See also dvedhā &amp; dveḷhaka.</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://gata">gata</a></em> gone to pieces Ja.v.197;</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://patha">patha</a></em> a twofold way a crossing; only fig. doubt SN.iii.108; MN.i.142, MN.i.144; Ud.90. See also <em><a href="bword://dvedh%C4%81patha">dvedhāpatha</a></em>.</li></ul><p>Sk. dvidhā, see <em><a href="bword://dvi">dvi</a></em> B I. 2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->a<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://gata">gata</a>, <a href="bword://patha">patha</a>, <a href="bword://dvedhāpatha">dvedhāpatha</a>, <a href="bword://dvi">dvi</a></p>

