dvārika|dvaarika|dvarika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dvaarika</span></p><p>(-˚) adjective referring or belonging to the door of-; in cha ˚ā taṇhā, craving or fever, arising through the 6 doors (of the senses) Dhp-a.iv.221, &amp; <em>kāya˚</em><br />■ saṃvara control over the “bodily” door, i.e. over action (opp speech) Pv-a.10 (so read for kāyañ cārika˚).</p>

