<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dvaaviisatima</span></p><p>the 22nd.</p>

dvīha|dviiha|dviha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine &amp; neuter a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dviiha</span></p><p>period of two days.</p>

dvīha|dviiha|dviha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dviiha</span></p><p>adverb two days; dvīhena in 2 days SN.ii.192; dvīha-mata 2 days dead MN.i.88; MN.iii.91</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://t%C4%ABha">tīha</a></em> 2 or 3 days (˚ṃ adv.) (on meaning cp. dvi AN I.2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->b<!-- raw HTML omitted -->) DN.i.190 (˚assa accayena after a few days) Ja.ii.316; Dhp-a.iii.21 (˚accayena id., gloss: katipāh’ accayena); DN-a.i.190 (˚ṃ) 215; Vv-a.45</li></ul><p>Sk. dvis-ahnah; see <em><a href="bword://dvi">dvi</a></em> B I.2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->b<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://tīha">tīha</a>, <a href="bword://dvi">dvi</a></p>

dvīhapaṭicchanna|dviihapa.ticchanna|dvihapaticchanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dviihapa.ticchanna</span></p><p>concealed for two days.</p>

dvīhatīha|dviihatiiha|dvihatiha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine &amp; neuter a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">dviihatiiha</span></p><p>period of two or three days.</p>

