ekaccika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective single, not doubled (of cloth, opp. to diguṇa) Ja.v.216 (˚vasana = eka-paṭṭa-nivattha).</p><p>fr. ekacca</p>

ekacciya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>ekacciya<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>mfn. single, of a single thickness</p><p>ekacciya<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>mfn. a certain, a certain sort of; some.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekaccika">ekaccika</a></p>

ekacciya
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective = ekacca SN.i.199; Ja.iv.259; acc. as adv. <em>-ṃ</em> once, single Vin.i.289 (cp. <em>Vin Texts</em> ii.212).</p>

ekachiggala
