ekaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mf</i></p><p>(-ikā)n. &amp; masculine</p><ol><li><p>(mfn.)</p><ol><li>alone; by oneself; only…; a single; the only…</li><li>having one; having a single (verse)</li></ol></li><li><p>(m.)</p><ol><li>a group of one; a set consisting of a single item.</li><li>(or perhaps n.) a section dealing with groups of one.</li></ol></li></ol>

ekaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective single, alone, solitary Vin.ii.212; Ja.i.255; Ja.ii.234; Ja.iv.2<br />■ f. <em><a href="bword://ekik%C4%81">ekikā</a></em> Vin.iv.229; Ja.i.307; Ja.iii.139.</p><p>eka + ka</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekikā">ekikā</a></p>

ekakamma
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter &amp; mfn. a</i></p><p>single or the same official act (of the <em>saṅgha</em>)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekakuṭika|ekaku.tika|ekakutika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaku.tika</span></p><p>consisting of a single house</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekam antaṃ|ekam anta.m|ekam antam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">adv.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekam anta.m</span></p><p>(or eka-m-antaṃ)</p><ol><li>to one side (showing respect); at a respectful distance.</li><li>on one side, aside; out of the way; a little apart.</li><li>to one side, apart; at a distance; in private, on one’s own.</li><li>in one place; in a single place</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>fixing the mind upon one thing; attentive</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekamantaṃ|ekamanta.m|ekamantam
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekamanta.m</span></p><p>adverb on one side, apart, aside Vin.i.47, Vin.i.94 = Vin.ii.272; DN.i.106; Snp.p.13 (expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> at Snp-a.140 as follows: bhāvana-puṃsaka-niddeso, ek’okāsaṃ ekapassan ti vuttaṃ hoti, bhummatthe vā upayogavacanaṃ) Snp.580, Snp.1009, Snp.1017; Ja.i.291; Ja.ii.102, Ja.ii.111; Snp-a.314, Snp-a.456. Also in loc. <em>ekamante</em> on one side Dhp-a.i.40.</p><p>eka + anta, acc. in adv. function, cp. BSk. ekamante Mvu.i.35</p>

ekamaṃsakhala|ekama.msakhala|ekamamsakhala
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine neuter a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekama.msakhala</span></p><p>single mash or mass of flesh</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekameka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective one by one, each AN.v.173; Vv.78#2.</p><p>eka-m-eka, cp. BSk. ekameka Mvu.iii.358</p>

ekamūlaka|ekamuulaka|ekamulaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekamuulaka</span></p><p>(what is) based on one item; (a statement or exposition) concerned with one item</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekamūlika">ekamūlika</a>, <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekamūlika|ekamuulika|ekamulika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekamuulika</span></p><p>(what is) based on one item; (a statement or exposition) concerned with one item</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekamūlaka">ekamūlaka</a>, <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekanavuta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>91st</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekanavutikappa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>the 91st eon</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekanta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective one-sided, on one end, with one top, topmost (˚-) usually in function of an adv. as ˚-meaning “absolutely, extremely, extraordinary, quite” etc.</p><ol><li>(lit.) at one end, only in ˚lomin a woollen coverlet with a fringe at one end DN.i.7 (= ekato dasaṃ uṇṇāmay’ attharaṇaṃ keci ekato uggata-pupphan ti vadanti DN-a.i.87) Vin.i.192; Vin.ii.163, Vin.ii.169; AN.i.181.</li><li>(fig.) extremely very much, in freq. combinations; e.g. ˚kāḷaka AN.iii.406; AN.iv.11; ˚gata SN.v.225; AN.iii.326; ˚dukkha MN.i.74; SN.ii.173 SN.iii.70 (+ sukha); AN.v.289; ˚dussīlya Dhp-a.iii.153; ˚nibbida AN.iii.83; AN.iv.143; ˚paripuṇṇa SN.ii.219; SN.v.204; ˚manāpa SN.iv.238; ˚sukha AN.ii.231; AN.iii.409; ˚sukhin DN-a.i.119 etc.</li></ol><p>Sk. ekānta</p>

ekantarika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective with one in between, alternate Ja.iv.195, <em>-bhāvena</em> (instr. adv.) in alternation alternately Vism.374; ekantarikāya (adv.) with intervals Vism.244.</p><p>eka + antarika</p>

ekantarīka|ekantariika|ekantarika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekantariika</span></p><p>an interval of one; <em>aṃ</em>, <em>-āya</em>, with something between; with an interval of one (year); alternately</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekantarīkaṃ|ekantariika.m|ekantarikam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(?)</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekantariika.m</span></p><p>with something between; with an interval of one (year); alternately</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekantarīka">ekantarīka</a></p>

ekantarīyā|ekantariiyaa|ekantariya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(?)</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekantariiyaa</span></p><p>with something between; with an interval of one (year); alternately</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekantarīka">ekantarīka</a></p>

ekantaṃ|ekanta.m|ekantam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">acc. adv.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekanta.m</span></p><p>solely; exclusively; absolutely; wholly; invariably</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekantaṃgata|ekanta.mgata|ekantamgata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekanta.mgata</span></p><p>with utter devotion or certainty; taking one side; following one alternative</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekantaṃ">ekantaṃ</a></p>

ekantaṃgatalomi|ekanta.mgatalomi|ekantamgatalomi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekanta.mgatalomi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekantaṃgatalomin">ekantaṃgatalomin</a></p><p>(a bed with) a kind of rug or covering</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekantaṃgatalomī">ekantaṃgatalomī</a>, <a href="bword://ekantaṃgata">ekantaṃgata</a></p>

ekantaṃgatalomin|ekanta.mgatalomin|ekantamgatalomin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekanta.mgatalomin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekantaṃgatalomin">ekantaṃgatalomin</a></p><p>(a bed with) a kind of rug or covering</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekantaṃgatalomī">ekantaṃgatalomī</a>, <a href="bword://ekantaṃgata">ekantaṃgata</a></p>

ekantaṃgatalomī|ekanta.mgatalomii|ekantamgatalomi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekanta.mgatalomii</span></p><p>(also <em>ekantaṃgatalomi(n)</em>) (a bed with) a kind of rug or covering</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekantaṃgata">ekantaṃgata</a></p>

ekantaṃkusalāyatika|ekanta.mkusalaayatika|ekantamkusalayatika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekanta.mkusalaayatika</span></p><p>(according to commentary) coming from what is absolutely good, resulting form what is good; or perhaps; producing what is absolutely good in the future</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekantaṃ">ekantaṃ</a></p>

ekantika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter &amp; mfn.</i></p><p>invariability; certainty; invariable; certain</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekanāḷā|ekanaa.laa|ekanala
<p>[DPPN]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekanaa.laa</span></p><p>A brahmin village near Dakkhiṇāgiri, to the south of Rājagaha. Once, during the eleventh year of his ministry, the Buddha visited the village and preached to Kāsī-Bhāradvāja the sutta which bears his name and which converted him to the faith. Snp.p.12<em>ff.</em> SN.i.172<em>ff.</em></p><p>23.4834, 84.429932town</p>

ekapada
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>one word, a single word; a single expression</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekapalāsika|ekapalaasika|ekapalasika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekapalaasika</span></p><p>with a single layered sole</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekapariyākata|ekapariyaakata|ekapariyakata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekapariyaakata</span></p><p>wound around once</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekapassayika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>sleeping on one side only</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekapuṇḍarīka|ekapu.n.dariika|ekapundarika
<p>[DPPN]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekapu.n.dariika</span></p><p>Ekapuṇḍarīka<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>A monastery of the wanderers, the residence of Vacchagotta. MN.i.481<em>f.</em> It was near the Kūṭāgārasālā in the Mahāvana of Vesāli. The Buddha went there to see Vacchagotta, and it was on this occasion that the Tevijja-Vacchagotta Sutta was preached. MN.i.481<em>f.</em></p><p>25.990761,85.0863652non-Buddhist monasteryEkapuṇḍarīka<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>An elephant belonging to Pasenadi. It was while riding on this elephant that the king met Ānanda. The king followed the Elder to the monastery, and their conversation is recorded in the Bāhitika Sutta. MN.ii.112<em>f.</em></p>

ekarukkhika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>made from one tree</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekasata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>101 or 100</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekasattati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>71</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekasaṭṭhi|ekasa.t.thi|ekasatthi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">f.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekasa.t.thi</span></p><p>num. 61</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekaseyya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter \~ā, feminine</i></p><p>lying or sleeping alone; being alone; a solitary lodging; a single lodging</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekaso
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adverb singly, one by one Ja.iii.224 (an˚).</p><p>Sk. ekaśaḥ</p>

ekasālaka|ekasaalaka|ekasalaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekasaalaka</span></p><p>containing one hall</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekasālā|ekasaalaa|ekasala
<p>[DPPN]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekasaalaa</span></p><p>A Brahmin village in the Kosala kingdom. The Buddha once stayed there, and when a large congregation of the laity were listening to him, Māra, thinking to darken their intelligence, suggested to him that he should not teach others. The Buddha refuted the suggestion of Māra, who retired discomfited. SN.i.111</p><p>Kosala3town</p>

ekasārīrika|ekasaariirika|ekasaririka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(m)f(n).</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekasaariirika</span></p><p>relating to one body; connected with one body</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekatimsā|ekatimsaa|ekatimsa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekatimsaa</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekattimsā">ekattimsā</a></p><p>num. &amp; mfn. (also <em>eka(t)tiṃsa</em>)</p><ol><li>(num.) 31.</li><li>(mfn.) 31st</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekatiya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. a</i></p><p>certain; some.</p>

ekatiṃsa|ekati.msa|ekatimsa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekati.msa</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekattiṃsa">ekattiṃsa</a></p><p>num. &amp; mfn. (also <em>eka(t)timsā</em>)</p><ol><li>(num.) 31.</li><li>(mfn.) 31st</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekato
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i></p><ol><li>on one side, on one part; on each side; to one side; separately.</li><li>all on one side, in one body; together.</li></ol><p>ekato … ekato …</p><p>(?) on one side …; on the other side …</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekato">ekato</a></p>

ekato
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adverb</p><ol><li>on the one side (opp. on the other) Ja.iii.51; Ja.iv.141.</li><li>together Ja.ii.415; Ja.iii.57 (vasanto), Ja.iii.52 (sannipatanti) Ja.iii.391; Ja.iv.390; Dhp-a.i.18. ekato <em>karoti</em> to put together, to collect Vv-a.3. ekato <em>hutvā</em> “coming to one”, agreeing Dhp-a.i.102, cp. ekato ahesuṃ Ja.i.201.</li></ol><p>abl. formation fr. eka, cp. Sk. ekataḥ</p>

ekato-upasampanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>ekato-upasampanna</p><p>mfn. ordained in (only) one <em>saṅgha</em>)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekato">ekato</a></p>

ekatodhāra|ekatodhaara|ekatodhara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekatodhaara</span></p><p>with a single cutting edge</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekato">ekato</a></p>

ekatokāja|ekatokaaja|ekatokaja
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekatokaaja</span></p><p>carrying pole with a load at one end</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekato">ekato</a></p>

ekatopakkhika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>supporting one side, belonging to one party</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekato">ekato</a></p>

ekatovaṇṭikamālā|ekatova.n.tikamaalaa|ekatovantikamala
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekatova.n.tikamaalaa</span></p><p>garland with stalk(s) on one side</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekato">ekato</a></p>

ekatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>ekatta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>neuter abstr. the being one;</p><ol><li>oneness, unity; identity; integration; a collective idea; a single concept; the single number, the singular;</li><li>singleness, being alone, solitariness</li></ol><p>ekatta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>mfn. onl, being the only one; unique; of one nature, of a single kind, uniform</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a>, <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><ol><li>unity DN.i.31.</li><li>loneliness, solitude, separation Snp.718; Thag.49; Mil.162; Ja.vi.64; Vv-a.202 (= ekībhāva).</li></ol><p>abstr. fr. eka</p>

ekattakāya|ekattakaaya|ekattakaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekattakaaya</span></p><p>having bodies of the same nature, having uniform bodies</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekatta">ekatta</a></p>

ekattanirata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>(or n.) devoted to (or devotion to) solitariness or unity</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekatta">ekatta</a></p>

ekattasaññi|ekattasa~n~ni|ekattasanni
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekattasa~n~ni</span></p><p>Also written as: ekattasaññin<sup>1</sup></p><p>having a notion of unity or identity; (<em>ekattasaññi(n)</em>)</p><p>ekattasaññi(n)<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>mfn. having perceptions or notions of the same nature; (<em>ekattasaññi(n)</em>)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekatta">ekatta</a>, <a href="bword://ekatta">ekatta</a></p>

ekattasaññin|ekattasa~n~nin|ekattasannin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekattasa~n~nin</span></p><p>Also written as: ekattasaññin<sup>1</sup></p><p>having a notion of unity or identity; (<em>ekattasaññi(n)</em>)</p><p>ekattasaññi(n)<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>mfn. having perceptions or notions of the same nature; (<em>ekattasaññi(n)</em>)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekatta">ekatta</a>, <a href="bword://ekatta">ekatta</a></p>

ekattatā|ekattataa|ekattata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekattataa</span></p><p>unity, combination, unification, concentration Ne.4, Ne.72 sq, Ne.107 sq.</p><p>fr. ekatta</p>

ekattavāsa|ekattavaasa|ekattavasa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekattavaasa</span></p><p>living together</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekatta">ekatta</a></p>

ekattha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>ekattha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>ind. in one place; in one and the same place; in only one place.</p><p>ekattha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>mfn. having one meaning; having the same sense</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekaṭṭha">ekaṭṭha</a>, <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekattimsā|ekattimsaa|ekattimsa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekattimsaa</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekattimsā">ekattimsā</a></p><p>num. &amp; mfn. (also <em>eka(t)tiṃsa</em>)</p><ol><li>(num.) 31.</li><li>(mfn.) 31st</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekattiṃsa|ekatti.msa|ekattimsa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekatti.msa</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekattiṃsa">ekattiṃsa</a></p><p>num. &amp; mfn. (also <em>eka(t)timsā</em>)</p><ol><li>(num.) 31.</li><li>(mfn.) 31st</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekavaraka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>the one and only husband</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekavassa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>of one year’s standing; having been ordained for one year</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekavassaṃ|ekavassa.m|ekavassam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekavassa.m</span></p><p>for one year; in one year</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekavassa">ekavassa</a></p>

ekavatthuka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>having the same basis or ground; relating to the same matter</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekavidha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective of one kind, single, simple Vism.514; adv. <em>ekavidhā</em> singly, simply Vism.528.</p><p>eka + vidha</p>

ekavihāri|ekavihaari|ekavihari
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekavihaari</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekavihārin">ekavihārin</a></p><p>living alone; solitary</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekavihārin|ekavihaarin|ekaviharin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekavihaarin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekavihārin">ekavihārin</a></p><p>living alone; solitary</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekavācika|ekavaacika|ekavacika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter \~ā, feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekavaacika</span></p><p>single utterance; a single proclamation</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekavīsa|ekaviisa|ekavisa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaviisa</span></p><p>num. 21</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekavīsaṃ">ekavīsaṃ</a>, <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekavīsaṃ|ekaviisa.m|ekavisam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaviisa.m</span></p><p>num. 21</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekavīsa">ekavīsa</a>, <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekaṃsa|eka.msa|ekamsa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka.msa</span></p><p>ekaṃsa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>masculine</p><ol><li>one part.</li><li>certainty; absolute assurance</li></ol><p>ekaṃsa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>masculine &amp; mfn.</p><ol><li>(m.) one shoulder.</li><li>(mfn.) (or <em>ekaṃsaṃ</em>, ind.) on one shoulder, covering one shoulder (the left)</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a>, <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekaṃsa|eka.msa|ekamsa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka.msa</span></p><p>Ekaṃsa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>adjective belonging to one shoulder, on or with one shoulder; only in phṛase ekaṃsaṃ uttarāsangaṃ karoti to arrange the upper robe over one shoulder (the left) Vin.i.46; Vin.ii.188 &amp; passim.</p><p>eka + aṃsa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>Ekaṃsa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>“one part or point”, i.e. one-pointedness, definiteness; affirmation, certainty absoluteness DN.i.153; AN.ii.46; Snp.427, Snp.1027; Ja.iii.224 (ekaṃsatthe nipāto for “nūna”); Snp-a.414 (˚vacana for “taggha”)<br />■ Opp. <em>an˚</em>; Mil.225<br />■ instr. <em><a href="bword://eka%E1%B9%83sena">ekaṃsena</a></em> as adv. for certain, absolutely, definitely, inevitably DN.i.122 DN.i.161, DN.i.162; MN.i.393; SN.iv.326; AN.v.190; Ja.i.150; Ja.iii.224; Pv-a.11.</p><p>eka + aṃsa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --> or better aṃsa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekaṃsena">ekaṃsena</a></p>

ekaṃsabhavita|eka.msabhavita|ekamsabhavita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka.msabhavita</span></p><p>developed in one part; practiced for one aspect</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekaṃsa">ekaṃsa</a></p>

ekaṃsavacana|eka.msavacana|ekamsavacana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka.msavacana</span></p><p>an expression of certainty or affirmation</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekaṃsa">ekaṃsa</a></p>

ekaṃsavyākaraṇiya|eka.msavyaakara.niya|ekamsavyakaraniya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka.msavyaakara.niya</span></p><p>answerable; to be answered with certainty, or with an absolute affirmation</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekaṃsa">ekaṃsa</a></p>

ekaṃsavāda|eka.msavaada|ekamsavada
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka.msavaada</span></p><p>speaking with absolute certainty; having absolute views</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekaṃsa">ekaṃsa</a></p>

ekaṃsena|eka.msena|ekamsena
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">instr. adv.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka.msena</span></p><p>with certainty, with assurance; certainly, absolutely, definitely</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekaṃsa">ekaṃsa</a></p>

ekaṃsika|eka.msika|ekamsika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka.msika</span></p><p>determined; certain; assured</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekaṃsika|eka.msika|ekamsika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka.msika</span></p><p>adjective certain DN.i.189, DN.i.191; <em>an˚</em>; uncertain, indefinite DN.i.191.</p><p>fr. ekaṃsa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p>

ekaṃsikatā|eka.msikataa|ekamsikata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka.msikataa</span></p><p>as neg. <em>an˚</em>; indefiniteness Mil.93.</p><p>abstr. fr. ekaṃsika</p>

ekaṅga|eka"nga|ekanga
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka"nga</span></p><p>one part; one characteristic; one factor</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekaṅgadassi|eka"ngadassi|ekangadassi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka"ngadassi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekaṅgadassin">ekaṅgadassin</a></p><p>seeing only one part, one aspect</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekaṅga">ekaṅga</a></p>

ekaṅgadassin|eka"ngadassin|ekangadassin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka"ngadassin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekaṅgadassin">ekaṅgadassin</a></p><p>seeing only one part, one aspect</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekaṅga">ekaṅga</a></p>

ekaṅgahīna|eka"ngahiina|ekangahina
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka"ngahiina</span></p><p>deficient in one respect; lacking one attribute</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekaṅga">ekaṅga</a></p>

ekaṭṭha|eka.t.tha|ekattha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine &amp; mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">eka.t.tha</span></p><p>having one meaning; having the same sense</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekattha">ekattha</a>, <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekeka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pron. &amp; mfn.</i></p><p>one each; one … each; single</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekikā|ekikaa|ekika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekikaa</span></p><p>see <em><a href="bword://ekaka">ekaka</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekaka">ekaka</a></p>

ekindriya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>having only one sense faculty</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekodaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. &amp; neuter</i></p><p>all water; covered in water; nothing but water</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekodakībhhūta|ekodakiibhhuuta|ekodakibhhuta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. &amp; neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekodakiibhhuuta</span></p><p>being all water; covered in water; (a world) consisting of or covered in water, nothing but water</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekodi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>woven into one’, integrated, unified; withdrawn, apart.</p>

ekodi
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective concentrated attentive, fixed AN.iii.354; Mnd.478. Usually in comp<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with <em>kṛ &amp; bhū</em> (which points however to a form ekoda with the regular change of a to i in connection with these roots!), as ekodi <em>-<a href="bword://karoti">karoti</a></em> to concentrate MN.i.116; SN.iv.263; <em>-bhavati</em> to become settled SN.iv.196; SN.v.144; <em>-bhūta</em> concentrated Snp.975; <em>-bhāva</em> concentration, fixing one’s mind on one point DN.i.37; DN.iii.78, DN.iii.131; AN.i.254; AN.iii.24 Vism.156 (expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> as eko udeti); Dhs.161 (cp. <em>Dhs trsl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --></em> 46); Dhs-a.169; Ne.89.</p><p>most likely eka + odi for odhi, see *<a href="bword://avadhi">avadhi</a>*<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --> &amp; cp. avadahati, avadahana, lit. of one attention, limited to one point. Thus also suggested by Morris; J.P.T.S. 1885, 32 sq. The word was Sanskritised into ekoti, e.g. at Mvu.iii.212, Mvu.iii.213; Lal.147, Lal.439</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://karoti">karoti</a>, <a href="bword://avadhi">avadhi</a></p>

ekodibhāva|ekodibhaava|ekodibhava
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekodibhaava</span></p><p>integration, unification; apartness, withdrawal.</p>

ekodibhāvita|ekodibhaavita|ekodibhavita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekodibhaavita</span></p><p>made unified; brought to integration</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekodihoti">ekodihoti</a></p>

ekodibhūta|ekodibhuuta|ekodibhuta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekodibhuuta</span></p><p>integrated, unified; withdrawn, apart</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekodihoti">ekodihoti</a></p>

ekodihoti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>is or becomes integrated, unified; is apart.</p>

ekodikaroti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>integrates; unifies.</p>

ekodikatabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekodikātabba">ekodikātabba</a>, <a href="bword://ekodikaroti">ekodikaroti</a></p>

ekodikātabba|ekodikaatabba|ekodikatabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekodikaatabba</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekodikatabba">ekodikatabba</a>, <a href="bword://ekodikaroti">ekodikaroti</a></p>

ekuddesa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine &amp; mfn.</i></p><ol><li>(m.) a single or the same instruction; a single or the same recitation, a shared recitation (of the pātimokkha).</li><li>(mfn.) having a single recitation, coming together in one recitation (of the pātimokkha)</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekuddāniya|ekuddaaniya|ekuddaniya
<p>[DPPN]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekuddaaniya</span></p><p>EkuddāniyaEkuddāna</p><p>A monk whose verse in the Theragāthā says that one of higher mind will not sorrow. Thag.68</p><p>The verse attributed above to Ekuddāniya, occurs in the Vinaya Vin.iv.54 as having been constantly used by Cūḷapanthaka.</p>

ekuttarika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter \~ā, feminine</i></p><p>a section of sets increasing by one</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekuttariya">ekuttariya</a>, <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekuttariya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter \~ā, feminine</i></p><p>a section of sets increasing by one</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekuttariya">ekuttariya</a>, <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekādasa|ekaadasa|ekadasa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaadasa</span></p><p>num. n., &amp; mf(~ā &amp; ~ī)n.</p><ol><li>(num.) eleven.</li><li>(n.) an eleven; a group of eleven.</li><li>(mfn.) eleventh.</li></ol>

ekādasa|ekaadasa|ekadasa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaadasa</span></p><p>number eleven Vin.i.19<br />■ num. ord. <em>ekādasama</em> the eleventh Snp.111, Snp.113.</p><p>Sk. ekādaśa</p>

ekādasaka|ekaadasaka|ekadasaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaadasaka</span></p><p>section dealing with a group or groups of eleven.</p>

ekādasama|ekaadasama|ekadasama
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mf</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaadasama</span></p><p>(~ā &amp; ~ī)n. the eleventh.</p>

ekāhaṃ|ekaaha.m|ekaham
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">acc. adv.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaaha.m</span></p><p>for one day, during one day</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekāhena|ekaahena|ekahena
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">instr. adv.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaahena</span></p><p>in one day, in a single day; during that same day</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekāhenamata|ekaahenamata|ekahenamata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaahenamata</span></p><p>who has been dead for one day, being a day old corpse</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekāhena">ekāhena</a></p>

ekāhika|ekaahika|ekahika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaahika</span></p><ol><li>coming every other day, missing a day.</li><li>intermittent</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekāki|ekaaki|ekaki
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaaki</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekākin">ekākin</a></p><p>alone, solitary.</p>

ekākika|ekaakika|ekakika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaakika</span></p><p>alone, solitary</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekākiya">ekākiya</a></p>

ekākin|ekaakin|ekakin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaakin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekākin">ekākin</a></p><p>alone, solitary.</p>

ekākiya|ekaakiya|ekakiya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaakiya</span></p><p>alone, solitary</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekākika">ekākika</a></p>

ekākiya|ekaakiya|ekakiya
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaakiya</span></p><p>adjective alone, solitary Thag.541; Mil.398.</p>

ekālopika|ekaalopika|ekalopika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">m(fn).</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaalopika</span></p><p>living on only one portion of alms</p><p>See also: ekā</p>

ekānika|ekaanika|ekanika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaanika</span></p><p>adjective = <em><a href="bword://ek%C4%81kiya">ekākiya</a></em>; instr. ekānikena as adv. “by oneself” Mil.402.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekākiya">ekākiya</a></p>

ekārāmatā|ekaaraamataa|ekaramata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine abstr.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaaraamataa</span></p><p>delight in solitude</p><p>See also: ekā</p>

ekāsana|ekaasana|ekasana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaasana</span></p><ol><li>sitting alone; being alone, being separate.</li><li>one seat, a single seat; the same seat</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekāsanabhojana|ekaasanabhojana|ekasanabhojana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaasanabhojana</span></p><p>eating only a single meal (a day); food at only a single meal.</p>

ekāsani|ekaasani|ekasani
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaasani</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekāsanin">ekāsanin</a></p><p>eating only at one sitting each day; (or possibly: sitting alone)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekāsanik'anga|ekaasanik'anga|ekasanik'anga
<p>[Nyana]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaasanik'anga</span></p><p><strong>[[ekāsanik’anga]]Ekāsanik’anga:</strong> the exercise of eating at one sitting, is one of the ascetic practices; see: <em>dhutānga</em></p>

ekāsanika|ekaasanika|ekasanika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaasanika</span></p><p>one who eats each day only once, only at one sitting</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekāsanin|ekaasanin|ekasanin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaasanin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ekāsanin">ekāsanin</a></p><p>eating only at one sitting each day; (or possibly: sitting alone)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekāyana|ekaayana|ekayana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekaayana</span></p><p>narrow, passable by only one person; being the only way</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://eka">eka</a></p>

ekībhāva|ekiibhaava|ekibhava
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekiibhaava</span></p><p>becoming one; uniting, union; oneness.</p>

ekībhāva|ekiibhaava|ekibhava
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekiibhaava</span></p><p>being alone, loneliness, solitude DN.iii.245; MN.ii.250; AN.iii.289; AN.v.89, AN.v.164; Vism.34; Snp-a.92, Snp-a.93; Dhp-a.ii.103; Vv-a.202; DN-a.i.253, DN-a.i.309.</p><p>eka + bhāva, with ī for a in comp<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with <em><a href="bword://bh%C5%AB">bhū</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://bhū">bhū</a></p>

ekūnapaññāsa|ekuunapa~n~naasa|ekunapannasa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekuunapa~n~naasa</span></p><p>num. 49</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekūnapaṇṇāsa">ekūnapaṇṇāsa</a>, <a href="bword://ekūnapaññāsaṃ">ekūnapaññāsaṃ</a></p>

ekūnapaññāsaṃ|ekuunapa~n~naasa.m|ekunapannasam
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ekuunapa~n~naasa.m</span></p><p>num. 49</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ekūnapaṇṇāsa">ekūnapaṇṇāsa</a>, <a href="bword://ekūnapaññāsa">ekūnapaññāsa</a></p>

ekūnapaṇṇāsa|ekuunapa.n.naasa|ekunapannasa
