garukaronta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://garukaroti">garukaroti</a></p>

garukaroti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>honors; venerates; esteems; treats as important.</p>

garukarīyati|garukariiyati|garukariyati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pass. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">garukariiyati</span></p><p>of garukaroti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://garukaroti">garukaroti</a></p>

garukata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>of garukaroti honored, venerated, esteemed</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://garukaroti">garukaroti</a></p>

garukatvā|garukatvaa|garukatva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">garukatvaa</span></p><p>of garukaroti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://garukaroti">garukaroti</a></p>

garukāra|garukaara|garukara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">garukaara</span></p><p>(an act of) respect, veneration.</p>

garukātabba|garukaatabba|garukatabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">garukaatabba</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://garukaroti">garukaroti</a></p>

garutara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>heavier; more to be esteemed.</p>

garutta
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>the fact of being honoured or considered worthy of esteem, honourableness AN.v.164 sq.</p>

garuvacana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>an expression of respect or esteem.</p>

garuḷa|garu.la|garula
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">garu.la</span></p><p>Name of a mythical bird, a harpy Pts.ii.196 = Cnd.235, Cnd.3 q.; Vism.206; Vv-a.9 (= supaṇṇa) Dhp-a.i.144.</p><p>Derivation uncertain. Sk. garuḍa, Lat. volucer winged, volo to fly</p>

garuḷā|garu.laa|garula
