ghāyati|ghaayati|ghayati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ghaayati</span></p><p>Ghāyati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>to smell, always with gandhaṃ; ger. ghātvā SN.iv.71, SN.iv.74 or ghāyitvā Ja.i.210 (jālagandhaṃ); Ja.iii.52 (macchagandhaṃ); Mil.347. Cp. sāyati &amp; upagghāyati.</p><p>Sk. ghrāti &amp; jighrati, to; <em>ghrā</em>, cp. gandha</p><p>Ghāyati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>to be consumed, to be tormented by thirst Pv.i.11#10 (ghāyire = ghāyanti Pv-a.60 variant reading BB jhāyire &amp; jhāynati) Mil.397.</p><p>a variant of jhāyati</p>

ghāyita|ghaayita|ghayita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ghaayita</span></p><p>smelled.</p>

