giddha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>eagerly desiring; hungry, greedy (for, loc.)</p>

giddha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective greedy; greedy for, hankering after (with loc.) SN.i.74 (+ kāmesu mucchita); SN.ii.227; AN.ii.2; AN.iii.68; Snp.243 (rasesu), Snp.774 (kāmesu); Snp.809; Pv.iv.6#2 (sukhe); Pv-a.3 (+ rata (= gadhita), Pv-a.271 (āhāre = hungry; cp. giddhin). In series with similar terms of desire; giddha gathita (or gadhita) mucchita ajjhopanna Cnd.369 (nissita); Snp-a.286. Cp. gathita<br />■ <em>agiddha</em> without greed, desireless controlled Iti.92 (+ vītagedha); Snp.210 (do), Snp.845 Cp. pa˚.</p><p>pp. of gijjhati</p>

giddhi
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>greed, usually in compounds: ˚māna greed &amp; conceit Snp.328; <em>-lobha</em> g. desire MN.i.360, MN.i.362 (see <em>a˚ and giddhilobhin</em>); Ja.v.343 Der. giddhikatā (f. abstr. = Sk. gṛdhnutā) greed Vb.351 (variant reading gedhi˚).</p><p>cp. Sk. gṛdhyā or gṛdhnutā</p><p>See also: a˚ and giddhilobhin</p>

giddhilobha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>greed and covetousness; greedy desire.</p>

giddhilobhi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://giddhilobhin">giddhilobhin</a></p><p>greedy and covetous; greedily desiring</p><p>See also: also gedhin</p>

giddhilobhin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://giddhilobhin">giddhilobhin</a></p><p>greedy and covetous; greedily desiring</p><p>See also: also gedhin</p>

giddhimā|giddhimaa|giddhima
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">giddhimaa</span></p><p>adjective from giddhi greedy, full of greed Ja.v.464 (rasa˚).</p>

giddhimāna|giddhimaana|giddhimana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">giddhimaana</span></p><p>(or n.) greed and pride.</p>

giddhin
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adj. from preceding greedy, usually -˚ greedy for, desirous after Pv.iv.10#7 (āhāra˚) f. <em>giddhinī</em>: gāvī vaccha Vin.i.193; SN.iv.181. Cp. also paligedhin.</p>

