golomika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective like a cluster; in phrase <em>massuṃ golomikaṃ kārāpeti</em> “to have the beard trimmed into a ball-or cluster-shape Vin.ii.134. Bdhgh’s expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n<!-- raw HTML omitted --> “like a goat’s beard” (cp <em>Vin. Texts</em> iii.138) is based on pop. etym. go + loma ika “cow-hair-like,” the discrepancy being that go does <em>not</em> mean <em>goat.</em></p><p>inverted diaeretic form fr. Sk. gulma = P. gumba: viz. *golmika → *golmika → golomika</p>

