gopānasī|gopaanasii|gopanasi
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">gopaanasii</span></p><p>beam supporting the framework of a roof, shaped Λ; fig. of old people, bent by age (see ˚vanka) Vin.iii.65, Vin.iii.81; SN.ii.263; SN.iii.156; SN.v.43, SN.v.228; MN.i.80; AN.i.261; AN.iii.364; AN.v.21; Vism.320; Dhp-a.ii.190; Vv-a.188.</p><ul><li><em>-gaṇā</em> (pl.) a collection of beams, the rafters Vv.78#4</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://bhogga">bhogga</a></em> (-sama) bent like a rafter (nārī) Ja.iii.395</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://va%E1%B9%85ka">vaṅka</a></em> (gopānasi˚) as crooked as a rafter (of old people cp. BSk. gopānasī-vakra Avs.ii.25<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n5<!-- raw HTML omitted -->) SN.i.117; MN.i.88; AN.i.138.</li></ul><p>See also: <a href="bword://bhogga">bhogga</a>, <a href="bword://vaṅka">vaṅka</a></p>

