iddhimant
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective</p><ol><li>(lit.) successful, proficient, only in neg. <em>an˚</em>; unfortunate, miserable, poor Ja.vi.361.</li><li>(fig.) possessing psychic powers Vin.iii.67; Vin.iv.108; AN.i.23, AN.i.25; AN.ii.185; AN.iii.340; AN.iv.312; Snp.179; Ne.23 Sdhp.32, Sdhp.472.</li></ol><p>fr. iddhi</p>

iddhimat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mf(n).</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://iddhimat">iddhimat</a></p><p>of splendid power; (one) who possesses supernatural power(s)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://iddhi">iddhi</a></p>

