ijjhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter &amp;</i></p><p><em>-ā</em> (f.) success, carrying out successfully Pts.i.17 sq., Pts.i.74, Pts.i.181; Pts.ii.125, Pts.ii.143 sq., Pts.ii.161, Pts.ii.174, Vb.217 sq.; Vism.266, Vism.383 (˚aṭṭhena iddhi); Dhs-a.91 Dhs-a.118, Dhs-a.237.</p><p>fr. ijjhati</p>

ijjhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>prospers, succeeds; (impers., gen. personae, instr. rei) there is success, there is prosperity.</p>

ijjhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to have a good result, turn out a blessing. succeed prosper, be successful SN.i.175 (“work effectively trsl.; = samijjhati mahapphalaṃ hoti C.); SN.iv.303; Snp.461 Snp.485; Ja.v.393; Pv.ii.1#11; Pv.ii.9#13 (= samijjhati Pv-a.120) Pot. ijjhe Snp.458, Snp.459; pret. ijjhittha (= Sk. ṛdhyiṣṭha Vv.20#6 (= nippajjittha mahapphalo ahuvattha Vv-a.103). pp. <em><a href="bword://iddha">iddha</a></em>. See also aḍḍha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --> &amp; aḍḍhaka. Cp. sam˚.</p><p>Vedic ṛdhyate &amp; ṛdhnoti; Gr. α ̓́λχομαι to thrive, Lat. alo to nourish, also Vedic iḍā refreshment &amp; P. iddhi power</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://iddha">iddha</a></p>

ijjhiṃsu|ijjhi.msu|ijjhimsu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ijjhi.msu</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ijjhati">ijjhati</a></p>

ikka
<p>[Dhammika]</p><p></p><p>See <em>Acchaka</em>.</p><p>See also: Acchaka</p>

ikka
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i></p><p>bear Ja.vi.538 [= accha C.).</p><p>Sk. ṛkṣa, of which the regular representation is P. accha<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p>

ikkhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to look Ja.v.153; Thag-a.147; Dhs-a.172.</p><p>fr. <em>īkṣ</em></p>

