ill-will
<p>[Nyana]</p><p></p><p><strong>Ill-will:</strong> <em>vyāpāda</em> is a synonym of <em>dosa</em> see: <em>mūla</em> and <em>patigha</em> and is one of the 10 mental chains <em>samyojana</em>, 5 hindrances <em>nīvarana</em> and 10 disadvantageous courses of action see: <em>kamma -pat ha</em> I.</p>

illiyā|illiyaa|illiya
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">illiyaa</span></p><p>= illī Ja.v.259; Ja.vi.50.</p><p>fr. illī, cp. Sk. *īlikā</p>

illī|illii|illi
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">illii</span></p><p>sort of weapon, a short one-edged sword Ja.v.259.</p><p>cp. Vedic ilībiśa Np. of a demon</p>

illīyituṃ|illiiyitu.m|illiyitum
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">illiiyitu.m</span></p><p>variant reading for allīyituṃ at Ja.v.154.</p>

image
<p>[Nyana]</p><p></p><p><strong>Image:</strong> mental: see: <em>nimitta</em>, <em>samādhi</em>, <em>kasina</em>.</p>

iminā upāyena|iminaa upaayena|imina upayena
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(?)</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">iminaa upaayena</span></p><p>in this way, thus; by this means</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upāya">upāya</a></p>

