<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">jhaapeti</span></p><ol><li><p>to set fire to, to burn, to cook Vin.iv.265; Ja.i.255, Ja.i.294; Dhp-a.ii.66; Pv-a.62.</p></li><li><p>to destroy, to bring to ruin, to kill (see Kern,</p><blockquote><p>Toevoegselen</p></blockquote><p>, p. 37 sq. Ja.iii.441 (= ḍahati pīḷeti); Vv-a.38 (= jhāyati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted -->, connected w. jhāna: to destroy by means of jhāna)</p></li></ol><p>inf jhāpetuṃ Ja.vi.300 (+ ghātetuṃ hantuṃ);<br />ger <em><a href="bword://jhatv%C4%81">jhatvā</a></em> ref. SN.i.161 (<em>reads</em> chetvā) = Ne.145 (<em>reads</em> jhitvā, with variant reading chetvā) SN.i.19 (reads chetvā, vv.ll. ghatvā &amp; jhatvā) = Ja.iv.67 (T. jhatvā, variant reading chetvā; explained by kilametvā); SN.i.41 (variant reading for T. chetvā, Bdhgh says “jhatvā ti vadhitvā”) Ja.ii.262 (+ hantvā vadhitvā; explained by kilametvā), Ja.vi.299 (+ vadhitvā); also jhatvāna Ja.iv.57 (= hantvā)<br />pp <em>jhatta &amp; jhāpita</em>.</p><p>Caus. of jhāyati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://jhatvā">jhatvā</a></p>

