kasambu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>decomposed or rotten matter; refuse.</p>

kasambu
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>anything worthless, rubbish, filth, impurity; fig. low passions SN.i.166; Snp.281 = Mil.414 = AN.iv.172; Vism.258 (maṃsa˚), Vism.259 (parama˚).</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://j%C4%81ta">jāta</a></em> one whose nature is impurity, in comb. brahmacāripaṭiñño antopūti avassuto k˚ SN.iv.181; AN.ii.240; AN.iv.128, AN.iv.201; Vin.ii.236; Pp.27, Pp.34, Pp.36; Vism.57 (+ avassuta pāpa).</li><li><em>-ka</em> -jāta ibid. in vv.ll.</li></ul><p>Derivation uncertain</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://jāta">jāta</a></p>

kasambujāta|kasambujaata|kasambujata
