kiṇha|ki.nha|kinha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ki.nha</span></p><p>adjective black; in the stock phrase muṇḍakā samaṇakā ibbhā k˚ bandhupādâpaccā DN.i.90 = DN.i.116; SN.iv.117; MN.i.334; MN.ii.177; in a moral sense = bad, wicked, with nâlam-ariyā dhammā DN.i.163.</p><p>see kaṇha; DN-a.i.254 kiṇhā ti kaṇhā, kāḷakā ti attho</p>

