kākacchati|kaakacchati|kakacchati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">kaakacchati</span></p><p>to snore Vin.iv.355; AN.iii.299; Ja.i.61, Ja.i.160 (= ghurughurûpassāsa; cp. DN-a.i.42 ghurû-ghurûpassāsī); Ja.i.318 Ja.vi.57; Mil.85; Vism.311.</p><p>derived by Fausböll fr. <em>kās</em>, to cough; by Trenckner fr. <em>krath</em>; by Childers &amp; E. Müller fr.; <em>kath</em> should it not rather be a den. fr. kakaca a saw?</p>

kākapeyya|kaakapeyya|kakapeyya
