kāruṇika|kaaru.nika|karunika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">kaaru.nika</span></p><p>adjective compassionate, merciful Pv.ii.1#13; Pv-a.16; Bdhd 49; often with <em>mahā˚</em>: of great mercy Sdhp.330, Sdhp.557; so of the Buddha: mahākāruṇika nātha “the Saviour of great mercy” in introductory stanzas to Pv and Vv.</p><p>fr. karuṇa</p>

