kāyura|kaayura|kayura
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">kaayura</span></p><p>Kāyūra &amp; Kāyura</p><ol><li>an ornamental bracket or ring worn on the upper arm (bāh’âlankāra Pv; bhuj˚ Vv) or neck (gīvāya pilandhana Ja.iii.437); a bracelet or necklace Vin.ii.106; Ja.iii.437; Ja.iv.92; Pv.iii.9#3; Vv.36#2.</li><li>adj as sakāyura raṭṭha having the insignia “regis” Ja.v.289 = Ja.v.486.</li></ol><p>see also <em><a href="bword://key%C5%ABra">keyūra</a></em>, which is the only form in Sk.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://keyūra">keyūra</a></p>

kāyānupassana|kaayaanupassana|kayanupassana
