ni
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Ni˚</p><p>Nearly all (ultimately prob. all) words under this heading are compounds with the pref. ni.</p><h3>A. <em>Forms</em></h3><ol><li>Pāli <strong>ni˚</strong>; combines the two prefixes <em>ni</em>, <em>nis</em> (nir). They are outwardly to be distinguished inasmuch as <em>ni</em> is usually followed by a single consonant (except in forms where double cons. is usually restored in composition, like ni-kkhipati = ni + <em>kṣip</em>; nissita ni + <em>sri</em>. Sometimes the double cons. is merely graphic or due to analogy, esp. in words where ni-is contrasted with <em>ud-</em> (“up”), as nikkujja → ukkujja, niggilati → uggilati, ninnamati → unnamati). On the other hand a compound with <em>nis</em> is subject to the rules of assimilation viz. either <em>doubling</em> of cons. (nibbhoga = nir-bhoga where <em>vv</em> is represented by <em>bb</em> (nibbiṇṇa fr. nir-vindati) or lengthening of ni to <em>nī</em> (nīyādeti as well as niyy˚ nīharati = nir + <em>har</em>), or <em>single</em> cons. in the special cases of <em>r &amp; v;</em> (niroga besides nīroga for nirroga, cp. duratta → dūrakkha; niveṭheti = nibbeṭheti, nivāreti = *nivvāreti = nīvāreti). Before a vowel the sandhi-cons. <em>r</em> is restored: nir-aya, nir-upadhi etc.</li><li>Both ni &amp; nis are base-prefixes only, &amp; of stable, well-defined character i.e. never enter combinations with other prefixes as first (modifying) components in verb-function (like saṃ, vi etc.), although <em>nis</em> occurs in such combination in noun-cpds negating the <em>whole</em> term: nir-upadhi, nis-saṃsaya etc.</li><li><em>ni</em> is freq. emphasised by <em>saṃ</em> as saṃni˚ (tud, dhā pat, sad); <em>nis</em> most freq. by <em>abhi</em> as abhinis˚ (nam, pad vatt, har).</li></ol><h3>B. <em>Meanings</em></h3><ol><li><em>ni</em> (with secondary derivations like nīca “low”) is a verb-pref. only, i.e. it characterises action with respect to its direction, which is that of (a) a <em>downward</em> motion (opp. abhi &amp; ud); (b) often implying the aim (= down into, on to, cp. Lat. sub in subire, or pref. ad˚); or(c) the reverting of an upward motion = back (identical with b); e.g. (a) ni-dhā (put down), ˚kkhip (throw d.), ˚guh (hide d.), ˚ci (heap up) ˚pad (fall d.), ˚sad (sit d.); (b) ni-ratta (<em>at</em>-tached to) ˚mant (speak to); ˚yuj (ap-point), ˚ved (ad-dress), ˚sev (be devoted to) etc.; (c) ni-vatt (turn back).</li><li><em>nis</em><ol><li>as verb-pref. it denotes the directional “out” with further development to “away from, opposite, without, pointing out the finishing, completion or vanishing of an action &amp; through the latter idea often assuming the meaning of the reverse, disappearance or contrary of an action = “un” (Lat. dis-), e.g. nikkhamati (to go out from) opp. pavisati (to enter into), ˚ccharati (nis to <em>car</em> to go forth), ˚ddhamati (throw out), ˚pajjati (result from), ˚bbattati (<em>vatt</em> spring out from), nīharati (take out), nirodhati (break up, destroy)</li><li>as noun-pref it denotes “being without” or “not having” E. <em>-less</em>, e.g. niccola without clothes, ˚ttaṇha (without thirst), ˚ppurisa (without a man), ˚pphala (without fruit); niccala motion-less, ˚kkaruṇa (heartless), ˚ddosa (fault˚), ˚maṃsa (flesh˚), ˚saṃsaya (doubt˚) nirattha (useless), ˚bbhaya (fear˚)<br />■ Bdhgh evidently takes <em>ni-</em> in meaning of <em>nis</em> only, when defining: ni-saddo abhāvaṃ dīpeti Vism.495.</li></ol></li></ol><p>Sk. ni- &amp; nih-, insep. prefixes: (a) ni down = Av. ni, cp. Gr.; νειός lowland, νείατος the lowest, hindmost Lat. nīdus (*ni-zdos: place to sit down = nest); Ags nēol, nider = E. nether; Goth. nidar = Ohg. nidar; also Sk. nīca, nīpa etc (b) <em>niḥ</em> out, prob. fr. *seni &amp; to Lat. sine without</p><p>See also: ni˚</p>

nibaddha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective bound down to, i.e.</p><ol><li>fixed, stable, sure Ja.iv.134 (bhattavetana); Mil.398 (a˚ unstable, ˚sayana). At DN-a.i.243 two kinds of <em><a href="bword://c%C4%81rik%C4%81">cārikā</a></em> (wanderings, pilgrimages) are distinguished, viz. <em>nibaddha˚</em>; definite, regular and <em>anibaddha˚</em>; indefinite irregular pilgrimage</li><li>asked, pressed, urged Ja.iii.277</li><li><strong>nibaddhaṃ</strong> (nt. as adv.) constantly always, continually Ja.i.100, Ja.i.150; Ja.iii.325; Ja.v.95, Ja.v.459 Ja.vi.161; Pv-a.267 (˚vasanaka); Dhp-a.ii.41, Dhp-a.ii.52 sq.</li></ol><p>ni + baddha</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://cārikā">cārikā</a>, nibaddhaṃ</p>

nibaddhatelaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>dressed with oil?</p>

nibandha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>binding, bond; attachment, continuance, continuity SN.ii.17; Vv-a.259 Vv-a.260 (perseverance). acc. <em>nibandhaṃ</em> (often misspelt for <strong>nibaddhaṃ</strong>) continually Vv-a.75. Cp. vi˚.</p><p>Sk. nibandha, ni + bandha</p><p>See also: nibaddhaṃ</p>

nibandhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>tying, fastening; binding, bond; (adj.) tied to, fettered Snp.654 (kamma˚); Mil.78, Mil.80.</p><p>ni + bandhana</p>

nibandhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>binds, ties; fetters; fixes.</p>

nibandhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>to bind Mil.79.</li><li>to mix, apply, prepare Vin.ii.151 (anibandhanīya unable to be applied, not binding); Ja.i.201 (yāgubhattaṃ).</li><li>to press, urge, importune Ja.iii.277.</li></ol><p>ni + bandhati</p>

nibbahati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>tears out, plucks out.</p>

nibbahati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to stretch out Ja.iii.185 (asiṃ); to pull out Ja.v.269 (jivhaṃ = jivhaṃ balisena n. 275). See also nibbāheti &amp; nibbāhāpeti.</p><p>nis + bahati</p>

nibbajjaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://nibbajjayat">nibbajjayat</a></p><p>shunning; abandoning.</p>

nibbajjayat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://nibbajjayat">nibbajjayat</a></p><p>shunning; abandoning.</p>

nibbajjeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to throw away, to do without, to avoid Thag.1105.</p><p>nis + vajjeti</p>

nibbakosa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>the gutter, the edge, of the eaves; the shelter of the eaves; ?</p>

nibbana
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective</p><ol><li>without forest, woodless Ja.ii.358.</li><li>an abstr. fr. nibbāna, see <em><a href="bword://nibb%C4%81na">nibbāna</a></em> I. cp. vana<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->. Freq. nibbāna as variant reading instead of nibbana without cravings Snp.1131 (nikkāmo nibbano); Dhp.283 (nibbanā pl.) Vv.50#14 (better reading nibbāna, in phrase “vanā nibbānaṃ āgataṃ,” as found at AN.iii.346 Thag.691, although the latter has nibbanaṃ in text) explained by “nittaṇhabhāvaṃ nibbānam eva upagataṃ Vv-a.213.</li></ol><p>Sk. nirvana</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbāna">nibbāna</a></p>

nibbanatha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective free from lust or cravings SN.i.180, SN.i.186 (so ‘haṃ vane nibbanatho visallo); Thag.526; Dhp.344; Dāvs i.18.</p><p>nis + vanatha</p>

nibbandhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: nibhandati</p>

nibbasana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>worn out, cast off (of clothes)</p>

nibbasana
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective no longer worn, cast off (of cloth) SN.ii.202, SN.ii.221.</p><p>nis + vasana</p>

nibbatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>of nibbattati</p><ol><li>arisen; originated; come into being; developed.</li><li>removed?</li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbattati">nibbattati</a></p>

nibbatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>past participle existing, having existed, being reborn Vin.i.215 (n. bījaṃ phalaṃ fruit with seed); Ja.i.168; Ja.ii.111; Pv-a.10 (niraye), Pv-a.35 (petayoniyaṃ), Pv-a.100 (pubbe n<br />■ ṭhānato paṭṭhāya) Mil.268 (kamma˚, hetu˚ &amp; utu˚)<br />■ Cp. abhi˚.</p><p>Sk. nirvṛtta, nis + vaṭṭa, pp. of nibbattati</p>

nibbattabīja|nibbattabiija|nibbattabija
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn &amp; neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbattabiija</span></p><p>with the seed removed; (or with the seed fully developed?)</p>

nibbattaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective producing, yielding Pv-a.26 (phala ˚ṃ kusalakammaṃ), Pv-a.126 (= sukha˚ = sukhāvaha).</p><p>cp. nibbatta</p>

nibbattana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>growing, coming forth; (re)birth, existence, life Ja.ii.105; Pv-a.5 (devaloke n-araha deserving rebirth in the world of gods), Pv-a.9, Pv-a.67 etc.</p><p>abstr. fr. nibbattati</p>

nibbattanaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective</p><ol><li>arising, coming out, growing Thag-a.259 (akkhidalesu n. pīḷikā).</li><li>one destined to be reborn, a candidate of rebirth Ja.iii.304 (sagge).</li></ol><p>fr. nibbattana</p>

nibbattati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>arises; comes into being; appears; becomes.</p>

nibbattati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to come out from (cp. E. turn out), arise, become, be produced, result, come into being, be reborn, ex-ist (= nir-vatt) Dhp.338; Pv.i.1#1 (nibbattate); Thag-a.259 (= jāyati); Dhp-a.iii.173; Pv-a.8 (= uppajjati), Pv-a.71 (id.); ger. <em><a href="bword://nibbattitv%C4%81">nibbattitvā</a></em> Ja.ii.158 (kapiyoniyaṃ); Pv-a.68, Pv-a.78; aor. <em><a href="bword://nibbatti">nibbatti</a></em> Ja.i.221; Pv-a.14 (Avīcimhi), Pv-a.67 (petesu), Pv-a.73 (amaccakule)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://nibbatta">nibbatta</a></em> (q.v.). Caus. <em><a href="bword://nibbatteti">nibbatteti</a></em> (q.v.). Cp. abhi˚.</p><p>nis + vattati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbattitvā">nibbattitvā</a>, <a href="bword://nibbatti">nibbatti</a>, <a href="bword://nibbatta">nibbatta</a>, <a href="bword://nibbatteti">nibbatteti</a></p>

nibbattayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbatteti">nibbatteti</a></p>

nibbattetabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i></p><p>of nibbatteti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbatteti">nibbatteti</a></p>

nibbatteti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>produces; brings forth; brings into being</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbattati">nibbattati</a></p>

nibbatteti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to produce, bring forth; practise, perform; to bring to light, find something lost (at Mil.218) Nd ii.= jāneti (s. v.); Ja.i.66, Ja.i.140; Ja.iii.396 (jhānâbhiññaṃ); Pv-a.76 (jhānāni) 30; Mil.200; Sdhp.470<br />pp <em><a href="bword://nibbattita">nibbattita</a></em> (q.v.) second Caus. <em>nibbattāpeti</em> to cause rebirth Dhp-a.iii.484 see also <em><a href="bword://nibbatt%C4%81pana">nibbattāpana</a></em><br />■ Cp. abhi˚.</p><p>nis + vatteti, Caus. of nibbattati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbattita">nibbattita</a>, <a href="bword://nibbattāpana">nibbattāpana</a></p>

nibbattetuṃ|nibbattetu.m|nibbattetum
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbattetu.m</span></p><p>of nibbatteti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbatteti">nibbatteti</a></p>

nibbattetvā|nibbattetvaa|nibbattetva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">inf.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbattetvaa</span></p><p>of nibbatteti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbatteti">nibbatteti</a></p>

nibbatti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>nibbatti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>caus. pr. 3 sg. of nibbattati</p><p>nibbatti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>aor. 3 sg. coming into being; origination; appearance.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbattati">nibbattati</a></p>

nibbatti
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>constitution, product; rebirth Ja.i.47; Ne.28, Ne.79; Vism.199, Vism.649; Vv-a.10 Cp. abhi˚.</p><p>Sk. nirvṛtti, nis + vatti</p>

nibbattin
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective arising, having rebirth, in neg. <em>anibbattin</em> not to be born again Ja.vi.573.</p><p>fr. nibbatti</p>

nibbattita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective done, produced, brought forth Pv-a.150 (a˚kusalakamma = akata).</p><p>pp. of nibbatteti</p>

nibbattitvā|nibbattitvaa|nibbattitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbattitvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbattati">nibbattati</a></p>

nibbattāpana|nibbattaapana|nibbattapana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbattaapana</span></p><p>reproduction Mil.97.</p><p>fr. nibbattāpeti, see <em><a href="bword://nibbatteti">nibbatteti</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbatteti">nibbatteti</a></p>

nibbaṅka|nibba"nka|nibbanka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibba"nka</span></p><p>adjective not crooked, straight Dhp-a.i.288.</p><p>nis + vanka</p>

nibbaṭṭeti|nibba.t.teti|nibbatteti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibba.t.teti</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbatteti">nibbatteti</a></p>

nibbecikicchā|nibbecikicchaa|nibbecikiccha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbecikicchaa</span></p><p>= nibbicikicchā certainty, doubtlessness Cnd.185 (opp. savicikicchā).</p>

nibbedha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>penetration; insight.</p>

nibbedha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>penetration, insight; adj.: penetrating, piercing, scrutinising, sharp. Freq. in phrase <em>nibbedha-bhāgiya</em> (sharing the quality of penetration), with ref. to samādhi, saññā etc. [cp. BSk nirvedha˚ Divy.50; but also nirbheda˚ Avs.ii.181, of kusalamūlāni; explained as lobhakkhandhassa (etc.) nibbijjhanāni at Ne.274] DN.iii.251, DN.iii.277; AN.iii.427 Vb.330; Ne.21, Ne.48, Ne.143 sq., Ne.153 sq.; Vism.15, Vism.88; Dhs-a.162<br />■ Also in nibbedha-gāminī (paññā) Iti.35 &amp; <em>dunnibbedha</em> (hard to penetrate, difficult to solve Mil.155, Mil.233 (pañha); spelt <em>dunniveṭha</em> at Mil.90).</p><p>nis + vedha, to <em>vyadh</em></p>

nibbedhabhāgiya|nibbedhabhaagiya|nibbedhabhagiya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbedhabhaagiya</span></p><p>belonging to, conducing to, penetration.</p>

nibbedhaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective piercing, sharp, penetrating, discriminating; only in f. <em>nibbedhikā</em> (cp. āvedhikā), applied to <em><a href="bword://pa%C3%B1%C3%B1%C4%81">paññā</a></em> (wisdom) DN.iii.237, DN.iii.268; SN.v.197, SN.v.199; MN.i.356; AN.i.45; AN.ii.167 AN.iii.152; AN.iii.410 sq., AN.iii.416; AN.v.15; Pts.ii.201; Cnd.235, Cnd.3#2 (+ tikkha-paññā), Cnd.415, Cnd.689; Ja.ii.9, Ja.ii.297; Ja.iv.267.</p><p>nis + vedhaka, to <em>vyadh</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://paññā">paññā</a></p>

nibbedhika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>piercing, penetrating.</p>

nibbejaniya
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>at SN.i.124 should probably be read as <em>nibbeṭhaniya</em> (rejecting, evading).</p>

nibbematika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>not in doubt; certain, assured.</p>

nibbematika
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective not disagreeing, of one accord, unanimous Vin.ii.65; Dhp-a.i.34.</p><p>nis + vimati + ka</p>

nibbenjanīya|nibbenjaniiya|nibbenjaniya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbenjaniiya</span></p><p>connected with recoiling; connected with despondency; giving up.</p>

nibbesa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbisa">nibbisa</a></p>

nibbeṭhana|nibbe.thana|nibbethana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbe.thana</span></p><p>unwinding; disentanglement; rebuttal (one of the elements of a disputation)</p>

nibbeṭhana|nibbe.thana|nibbethana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbe.thana</span></p><p>unwinding, fig. explanation Mil.28.</p><p>Sk. nirveṣṭana, nis + veṭhana</p>

nibbeṭhayati|nibbe.thayati|nibbethayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbe.thayati</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbeṭheti">nibbeṭheti</a></p>

nibbeṭhenta|nibbe.thenta|nibbethenta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbe.thenta</span></p><p>of nibbeṭheti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbeṭheti">nibbeṭheti</a></p>

nibbeṭhetabba|nibbe.thetabba|nibbethetabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pass. part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbe.thetabba</span></p><p>of nibbeṭheti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbeṭheti">nibbeṭheti</a></p>

nibbeṭheti|nibbe.theti|nibbetheti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbe.theti</span></p><p>unwinds (trans. and intrans.), disentangles; explicates; disentangles oneself; answers, rebuts (a charge)</p>

nibbeṭheti|nibbe.theti|nibbetheti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbe.theti</span></p><ol><li>to unravel, untwist, unwind; to explain, make clear DN.i.54 (nibbeṭhiyamāna, variant reading BB nibbedh˚); Pv.iv.3#29 (˚ento = niveṭhīyamāna Pv-a.253 variant reading BB nibbedh˚) Mil.3; Sdhp.153.</li><li>to deny, reject Vin.ii.79; DN.i.3 (= apanetabba Com.); SN.iii.12 (variant reading BB ˚dh˚).</li><li>to give an evasive answer Vin.iii.162<br />■ See also nibbejaniya</li></ol><p>pp <em><a href="bword://nibbe%E1%B9%ADhita">nibbeṭhita</a></em>, q.v.</p><p>Sk. nirveṣṭate, nis + veṭheti, to twist round</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbeṭhita">nibbeṭhita</a></p>

nibbeṭhita|nibbe.thita|nibbethita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbe.thita</span></p><p>explained, unravelled, made clear Mil.123 (su˚).</p><p>pp. of nibbeṭheti</p>

nibbeṭhiyamāna|nibbe.thiyamaana|nibbethiyamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbe.thiyamaana</span></p><p>of nibbeṭheti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbeṭheti">nibbeṭheti</a></p>

nibbhacceti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to threaten, revile, scorn Ja.iii.338.</p><p>Sk. nirbhartsayati, nis + bhaccheti</p>

nibbhaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective free from fear or danger, fearless, unafraid Ja.i.274; Ja.iii.80; Ja.v.287; Vism.512.</p><p>nis + bhaya</p>

nibbhijjha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i></p><p>of nibbijjhati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbijjhati">nibbijjhati</a></p>

nibbhoga
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective deprived of enjoyment; deserted, being of no avail, useless Ja.vi.556; Pv.i.12. Cp. vi˚.</p><p>Sk. nirbhoga, nis + bhoga<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>Nibbhoga</p><p>bending, contortion Ja.ii.264 (oṭṭha˚).</p><p>ni + bhoga<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p>

nibbhujati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to twist round, bend, wind, contort oneself Mil.253. Cp. vi˚.</p><p>Sk. ni-or nirbhujati, nis + bhujati</p>

nibbicikicchā|nibbicikicchaa|nibbicikiccha
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbicikicchaa</span></p><p>surety, reliance, trust SN.ii.84; SN.v.221 (= nikkankhā); Vv-a.85 (= ekaṃsikā).</p><p>nis + vicikicchā</p>

nibbiddha
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>in phrase <em>-piṅgala</em> (with) disgustingly red (eyes) (perhaps = nibbiṇṇa?) Ja.v.42 (of a giant).</li><li>with ref. to a road: broken up, i.e. much frequented, busy street Ja.vi.276 (of vīthi, bazaar, in contrast with a-nibbiddha-raccha carriage-road, which is not a thoroughfare. The reading patatthiyo <em>at</em> Ja.vi.276, for which nibbiddha-vīthiyo is the C. expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n<!-- raw HTML omitted --> is to be corrected into pathaddhiyo).</li></ol><p>pp. of nibbijjhati</p>

nibbidā|nibbidaa|nibbida
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbidaa</span></p><p>weariness (of); disenchantment, dissatisfaction, disgust (with)</p>

nibbidā|nibbidaa|nibbida
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbidaa</span></p><p>weariness, disgust with worldly life, tedium, aversion, indifference, disenchantment N. is of the preliminary &amp; conditional states for the attainment of Nibbāna (see <em><a href="bword://nibb%C4%81na">nibbāna</a></em> II B 1) &amp; occurs frequently together with; <em>virāga, vimutti &amp; nibbāna;</em> in the formula: etaṃ ekanta-nibbidāya virāgāya nirodhāya… sambodhāya nibbānāya saṃvattati “this leads to being thoroughly tired (of the world), to dispassionateness to destruction (of egoism), to perfect wisdom, to Nibbāna,” e.g. at DN.i.189; SN.v.82, SN.v.179, SN.v.255 SN.v.361; AN.iii.83; AN.iv.143; AN.v.216<br />■ In other connections Vin.i.15 (nibbidāya cittaṃ saṇṭhāsi); DN.iii.130 sq. SN.ii.30; SN.iii.40; SN.iii.179, SN.iii.189; SN.iv.86, SN.iv.141 (read nibbidāya for nibbindāya?); AN.i.51, AN.i.64; AN.iii.19, AN.iii.200, AN.iii.325 sq.; AN.iv.99, AN.iv.336 AN.v.2 sq., AN.v.311 sq.; Ja.i.97; Ja.iv.471, Ja.iv.473; Snp.340; Pts.i.195 Pts.ii.43 sq.; Vb.330; Ne.27, Ne.29; Vism.650. Cp. abhi˚.</p><p>Sk. nirvid, f. (see [BSk. e.g. Lal.300](bword://BSk. e.g. Lal.300)) &amp; nirveda; to nibbindati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbāna">nibbāna</a>, BSk. e.g. Lal.300</p>

nibbijja
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i></p><p>having been disheartened or disgusted.</p>

nibbijjhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i></p><ol><li>pieces through; strikes.</li><li>having penetrated?</li></ol>

nibbijjhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to pierce, transfix, wound SN.v.88 (+ padāleti); Sdhp.153 (patodehi). ger <em>nibbijjha</em> Snp.940 (= paṭivijjhitvā Mnd.420)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://nibbiddha">nibbiddha</a></em>. Cp. abhi˚.</p><p>nis + vijjhati, <em>vyadh</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbiddha">nibbiddha</a></p>

nibbikappa
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>distinction, distinguishing Vism.193.</p><p>nis + vikappa</p>

nibbikāra|nibbikaara|nibbikara
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbikaara</span></p><p>adjective steady, unchanged, steadfast; persevering Ja.i.66; Pv-a.178, Pv-a.253 (+ nicca); Snp-a.189, Snp-a.497; Vism.311.</p><p>nis + vikāra</p>

nibbinda
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><ol><li>(mfn.) being dissatisfied or disgusted; weary; turning away.</li><li>(m.) dissatisfaction; disgust; turning away.</li></ol>

nibbindamāna|nibbindamaana|nibbindamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbindamaana</span></p><p>of nibbindati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbindati">nibbindati</a></p>

nibbindanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>of nibbindati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbindati">nibbindati</a></p>

nibbindat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn. &amp; masculine</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://nibbindat">nibbindat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nibbindati">nibbindati</a></p>

nibbindati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>is despondent; becomes wearied, fed up (with, loc., occasionally acc. or instr.), feels disenchantment or dissatisfaction or disgust (with, loc., occasionally acc. or instr.); gives up, turns away from (abl.)</p>

nibbindati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to get wearied of (c. loc.); to have enough of, be satiated, turn away from, to be disgusted with. In two roots:</p><ol><li><em>vind</em>: prs. nibbindati etc. usually in combination with <em>virajjati &amp; vimuccati;</em> (cp nibbāna III. 2). Vin.i.35; SN.ii.94; SN.iv.86, SN.iv.140; AN.v.3; Dhp.277 sq.; Iti.33; Ja.i.267; Mil.235, Mil.244; Sdhp.612 ppr. <em>nibbindaṃ</em> SN.iv.86; Pv-a.36 (nibbinda-mānasa) ger. <em>nibbindiya</em> Ja.v.121 (˚kārin)</li><li><em>vid</em>: Pot. <em>nibbide</em> (variant reading BB nibbije) Ja.v.368 (= nibbindeyya Com.); ger <strong>nibbijjitvā</strong> Ja.i.82, &amp; <em><a href="bword://nibbijja">nibbijja</a></em> Snp.448 = SN.i.124 (nibbijjâpema = nibbijja pakkameyya Snp-a.393)</li></ol><p>pp <em><a href="bword://nibbi%E1%B9%87%E1%B9%87a">nibbiṇṇa</a></em>. See also <em><a href="bword://nibbid%C4%81">nibbidā</a></em>.</p><p>nis + vindati, <em>vid<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></em></p><p>See also: nibbijjitvā, <a href="bword://nibbijja">nibbijja</a>, <a href="bword://nibbiṇṇa">nibbiṇṇa</a>, <a href="bword://nibbidā">nibbidā</a></p>

nibbinditvā|nibbinditvaa|nibbinditva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nibbinditvaa</span></p><p>having got wearied of; having been disgusted with.</p>

nibbinna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i></p><ol><li>disenchanted or dissatisfied or disgusted (with); weary (of)</li><li>which has caused dissatisfaction or disgust; given up, turned away from.</li></ol>

nibbinnarūpa|nibbinnaruupa|nibbinnarupa
