nigūhana|niguuhana|niguhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">niguuhana</span></p><p>covering, concealing, hiding Vv-a.71.</p><p>Sk. nigūhana, see <em><a href="bword://nig%C5%ABhati">nigūhati</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nigūhati">nigūhati</a></p>

nigūhati|niguuhati|niguhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">niguuhati</span></p><p>to cover up, conceal, hide Ja.i.286; Ja.iii.392; Ja.iv.203; Pv.iii.4#3 (≈ parigūhāmi variant reading SS guyhāmi). pp. <em><a href="bword://nig%C5%AB%E1%B8%B7ha">nigūḷha</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>Sk. nigūhati, ni + gūhati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nigūḷha">nigūḷha</a></p>

nigūḷha|niguu.lha|nigulha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">niguu.lha</span></p><p>hidden (down), concealed; (n.) a secret Ja.i.461; Dāvs iii.39.</p><p>Sk. nigūḍha, but BSk. nirgūḍha (Divy.256); ni + gūḷha</p>

