nihiniṃ|nihini.m|nihinim
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nihini.m</span></p><p>setting in motion; impelling.</p>

nihita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p></p><p>nihita<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>laid aside; (what is) deposited, stored; hidden; laid down</p><p>nihita<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>pp mfn. of nihi set in motion; impelled</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nidahati">nidahati</a>, <a href="bword://nihi">nihi</a></p>

nihita
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective put down, put into, applied, settled; laid down, given up renounced. As ˚-often in the sense of a prep. without, e.g. ˚daṇḍa ˚sattha without stick &amp; sword (see <em><a href="bword://da%E1%B9%87%E1%B8%8Da">daṇḍa</a></em>…) DN.i.70 (˚paccāmitta); Pv.iv.3#26 (su˚ well applied); Pv-a.252 (bhasma-nihita thrown into the ashes); Sdhp.311.</p><p>Sk. nihita, pp. of ni + <em>dhā</em>, see <em><a href="bword://dahati">dahati</a></em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://daṇḍa">daṇḍa</a>, <a href="bword://dahati">dahati</a></p>

nihitadaṇḍa|nihitada.n.da|nihitadanda
