nihuhuṅka|nihuhu"nka|nihuhunka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nihuhu"nka</span></p><p>adjective one who does not confide in the sound <em><a href="bword://hu%E1%B9%83">huṃ</a></em> Vin.i.3 (cp. <em>J.P.T.S.</em> 1901 42).</p><p>fr. <em>nī˚</em>; = nis + huhunka</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://huṃ">huṃ</a></p>

nihīna|nihiina|nihina
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 1 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nihiina</span></p><p>of nihīyati low, base, mean; inferior; deprived of, deficient</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nihīyati">nihīyati</a></p>

nihīna|nihiina|nihina
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nihiina</span></p><p>adjective lost; degraded, low, vile, base; inferior, little, insignificant SN.i.12; Snp.890; Mnd.105, Mnd.194; Pv-a.198 (jāti˚ low-born) Sdhp.86. Opp. to seyya Ja.vi.356 sq.</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://attha">attha</a></em> one who has lost his fortune, poor Pv.iv.1#5</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://kamma">kamma</a></em> of low action Snp.661 = Iti.43; Dhp.306; Ja.ii.417</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://citta">citta</a></em> low-minded Pv-a.107 (= dīna);</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://j%C4%81tika">jātika</a></em> of inferior birth or caste Pv-a.175;</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://pa%C3%B1%C3%B1a">pañña</a></em> of inferior wisdom Snp.890 (= paritta-pañña Mnd.299);</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://sevin">sevin</a></em> of vile pursuit AN.i.126.</li></ul><p>Sk. nihīna, pp. of nihīyati or nihāyati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://attha">attha</a>, <a href="bword://kamma">kamma</a>, <a href="bword://citta">citta</a>, <a href="bword://jātika">jātika</a>, <a href="bword://pañña">pañña</a>, <a href="bword://sevin">sevin</a></p>

nihīnasevi|nihiinasevi|nihinasevi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nihiinasevi</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://nihīnasevin">nihīnasevin</a></p><p>associating with inferior people.</p>

nihīnasevin|nihiinasevin|nihinasevin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nihiinasevin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://nihīnasevin">nihīnasevin</a></p><p>associating with inferior people.</p>

nihīnatā|nihiinataa|nihinata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nihiinataa</span></p><p>lowness, inferiority; vileness, baseness DN.i.98, DN.i.99.</p><p>abstr. to nihīna</p>

nihīyati|nihiiyati|nihiyati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nihiiyati</span></p><p>decreases, grows less; falls away, falls short (of); is deficient.</p>

nihīyati|nihiiyati|nihiyati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nihiiyati</span></p><p>to be left, to come to ruin, to be destroyed AN.i.126 = Ja.iii.324 (= vināsaṃ pāpuṇāti). pp. <em><a href="bword://nih%C4%ABna">nihīna</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>ni + hīyati, Pass. of <em><a href="bword://h%C4%81">hā</a></em>, see jahāti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nihīna">nihīna</a>, <a href="bword://hā">hā</a></p>

nija
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective own Dāvs ii.68. Cp. niya.</p><p>Sk. nija, wth dial. j. for nitya = P. nicca</p>

nijana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>washing, cleansing Vism.342 (variant reading nijj˚).</p><p>fr. <em>nij</em></p>

nijigiṃsana|nijigi.msana|nijigimsana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijigi.msana</span></p><p>wishing to acquire; coveting.</p>

nijigiṃsanaka|nijigi.msanaka|nijigimsanaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijigi.msanaka</span></p><p>wishing to acquire; covetous.</p>

nijigiṃsanatā|nijigi.msanataa|nijigimsanata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">f.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijigi.msanataa</span></p><p>, abstr. of nijigiṃsana the wish to acquire; covetousness for</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nijigiṃsana">nijigiṃsana</a></p>

nijigiṃsanatā|nijigi.msanataa|nijigimsanata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijigi.msanataa</span></p><p>covetousness Vism.23 sq. (defined), Vism.29 (id. = magganā), referring to Vb.353 where T has jigiṃsanatā, with variant reading nijigīsanatā.</p><p>fr. last</p>

nijigiṃsati|nijigi.msati|nijigimsati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijigi.msati</span></p><p>to desire ardently, to covet DN-a.i.92 (= maggeti pariyesati).</p><p>Sk. nijigīṣati, ni + jigiṃsati</p>

nijigiṃsita|nijigi.msita|nijigimsita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijigi.msita</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://nijigiṃsitar">nijigiṃsitar</a></p><p>one who wishes to acquire; who covets.</p>

nijigiṃsitar|nijigi.msitar|nijigimsitar
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijigi.msitar</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://nijigiṃsitar">nijigiṃsitar</a></p><p>one who wishes to acquire; who covets.</p>

nijigiṃsitar|nijigi.msitar|nijigimsitar
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijigi.msitar</span></p><p>noun adjective one who desires ardently, covetous, rapacious DN.i.8 (lābhaṃ) AN.iii.111 (id.).</p><p>n. ag. fr. prec.</p>

nijigīsana|nijigiisana|nijigisana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijigiisana</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nijigiṃsana">nijigiṃsana</a></p>

nijigīsanaka|nijigiisanaka|nijigisanaka
