nijjhapeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nijjhāpeti">nijjhāpeti</a></p>

nijjhatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective satisfied, pacified, appeased Ja.vi.414 (= khamāpita Com.); Vv.63#19 (= nijjhāpita Vv-a.265) Mil.209. See also paṭi˚</p><p>pp. of nijjhāpeti, *Sk. nidhyapta or nidhyāpita</p>

nijjhatti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>making scrutinize; making understand; convincing.</p>

nijjhatti
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i></p><p>conviction, understanding realization; favourable disposition, satisfaction MN.i.320; AN.iv.223; Pts.ii.171, Pts.ii.176; Mil.210.</p><p>abstr. to nijjhatta, cp. BSk. nidhyapti, formation like P. ñatti → Sk. jñapti</p>

nijjhattibala
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i></p><p>whose strength is making (someone) understand.</p>

nijjhāma|nijjhaama|nijjhama
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaama</span></p><p>burnt; burning.</p>

nijjhāma|nijjhaama|nijjhama
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaama</span></p><p>adjective noun burning away, wasting away, consuming or consumed AN.i.295; Ne.77, Ne.95 paṭipadā.</p><ul><li><em>-taṇha</em> (adj.) of consuming thirst, very thirsty Ja.i.44</li><li><em>-taṇhika = ˚taṇha</em> denoting a class of Petas (q.v. Mil.294, Mil.303, Mil.357.</li></ul><p>Sk. niḥkṣāma, cp. niḥkṣīṇa, nis + jhāma of jhāyati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --> = Sk. kṣāyati</p>

nijjhāna|nijjhaana|nijjhana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaana</span></p><p>looking; scrutiny; reflection, meditation.</p>

nijjhāna|nijjhaana|nijjhana
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaana</span></p><p>Nijjhāna<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>neuter understanding, insight, perception, comprehension; favour, indulgence (= nijjhāpana), pleasure, delight Ja.vi.207. Often as <em>-ṃ khamati</em>: to be pleased with, to find pleasure in SN.iii.225, SN.iii.228; MN.i.133, MN.i.480; Vv.84#17. Thus also diṭṭhinijjhāna-kkhanti delighting in speculation AN.i.189 sq. AN.ii.191. Cp. upa˚.</p><p>*Sk. nidhyāna, ni + jhāna<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>Nijjhāna<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>neuter conflagration, in anto˚ = nijjhāyana Pv-a.18 (cittasantāpa + in expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n<!-- raw HTML omitted --> of soka).</p><p>nis + jhāna<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p>

nijjhāpana|nijjhaapana|nijjhapana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaapana</span></p><p>making understand; convincing; winning over.</p>

nijjhāpana|nijjhaapana|nijjhapana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaapana</span></p><p>favourable disposition, kindness, indulgence Ja.iv.495 (˚ṃ karoti = khamāpeti Com.; text reads nijjhapana).</p><p>Sk. *nidhyāpana, ni + jhāpana, Caus. to jhāpeti</p>

nijjhāpaniya|nijjhaapaniya|nijjhapaniya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaapaniya</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nijjhāpeti">nijjhāpeti</a></p>

nijjhāpaya|nijjhaapaya|nijjhapaya
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaapaya</span></p><p>adjective to be discriminated or understood, in <em>dun˚</em>; hard to… Mil.141 (pañha).</p><p>Sk. *ni-dhyāpya, to nijjhāpeti</p>

nijjhāpayati|nijjhaapayati|nijjhapayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaapayati</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nijjhāpeti">nijjhāpeti</a></p>

nijjhāpetabba|nijjhaapetabba|nijjhapetabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaapetabba</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nijjhāpeti">nijjhāpeti</a></p>

nijjhāpeti|nijjhaapeti|nijjhapeti
