nijjhāpeti|nijjhaapeti|nijjhapeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaapeti</span></p><p>to make favourably disposed, to win somebody’s affection, or favour, to gain over Vin.ii.96; MN.i.321; Ja.iv.108; Ja.iv.414, Ja.iv.495; Ja.vi.516; Mil.264; Vv-a.265 (nijjhāpita = nijjhatta).</p><p>Sk. nidhāyayati, ni + jhāpeti, Caus. to jhāyati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted -->; cp. Sk. nididhyāsate</p>

nijjhāti|nijjhaati|nijjhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaati</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nijjhāyati">nijjhāyati</a></p>

nijjhāya|nijjhaaya|nijjhaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaaya</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://nijjhāyat">nijjhāyat</a></p><p>of nijjhāyati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nijjhāyati">nijjhāyati</a></p>

nijjhāyana|nijjhaayana|nijjhayana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaayana</span></p><p>burning away, consumption; fig. remorse, mortification in <em>anto˚</em>; Ja.i.168 (cp. nijjhāna<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted -->).</p><p>Sk. *niḥkṣāyana, nis + jhāyana of jhāyati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p>

nijjhāyanta|nijjhaayanta|nijjhayanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaayanta</span></p><p>of nijjhāyati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nijjhāyati">nijjhāyati</a></p>

nijjhāyat|nijjhaayat|nijjhayat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">nijjhaayat</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://nijjhāyat">nijjhāyat</a></p><p>of nijjhāyati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nijjhāyati">nijjhāyati</a></p>

