<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine &amp; neuter a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naamadheyya</span></p><p>name; naming.</p>

nāmagotta|naamagotta|namagotta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naamagotta</span></p><p>the personal name and clan name.</p>

nāmaka|naamaka|namaka
<p>[Dhammika]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naamaka</span></p><p>A type of bird Ja.vi.538.</p>

nāmaka|naamaka|namaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naamaka</span></p><p>having the name; having merely the name.</p>

nāmaka|naamaka|namaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naamaka</span></p><p>adjective</p><ol><li>(-˚) by name SN.ii.282 (Thera˚); Pv-a.67, Pv-a.96 (kaṇha˚).</li><li>consisting of a mere name i.e. mere talk, nonsense, ridiculous DN.i.240.</li></ol><p>fr. nāma</p>

nāmakamma|naamakamma|namakamma
