<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naamakaaya</span></p><p>the nama group, the group of non-material aspects (of an individual)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nama">nama</a></p>

nāmarūpa|naamaruupa|namarupa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naamaruupa</span></p><ol><li>name and form;<ol><li>individual person or identity; interpreted as the mental and physical aspects of an individual.</li><li>esp. in the <em>paṭiccasamuppāda</em> series: with <em>viññāṇa</em> furnishing (the possibility of) individual identity (conditioned by <em>avijjā</em> and <em>saṅkhārā</em>) and experience (by means of the senses)</li></ol></li></ol><p>See also: <a href="bword://nāma">nāma</a></p>

nāmarūpajātika|naamaruupajaatika|namarupajatika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naamaruupajaatika</span></p><p>born from name and form.</p>

nāmato gaṇhāti|naamato ga.nhaati|namato ganhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naamato ga.nhaati</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://nāmaṃ gaṇhāti">nāmaṃ gaṇhāti</a></p>

nāmayati|naamayati|namayati
