nānatta|naanatta|nanatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naanatta</span></p><p>nānatta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>neuter various; different; separated.</p><p>nānatta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>neuter abstr. diversity, variety; difference.</p>

nānatta|naanatta|nanatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naanatta</span></p><p>(nt. m.) diversity, variety, manifoldness, multiformity, distraction; all sorts of (opp. ekatta, cp. MN.i.364: “the multiformity of sensuous impressions,” M.A.). Enum<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n<!-- raw HTML omitted --> of diversity as nānattā, viz. dhātu˚ phassa˚ vedanā˚ saññā˚ sankappa chanda˚ pariḷāha˚ pariyesanā˚ lābha˚ DN.iii.289; SN.ii.140 sq., cp. SN.iv.113 sq., SN.iv.284 sq.; Pts.i.87<br />■ AN.iv.385; Pts.i.63 sq., Pts.i.88 sq.; SN.ii.115 (vedanā˚); Pts.i.91 (samāpatti &amp; vihāra˚); Ja.ii.265. In composition, substituted sometimes for <em>nāna</em>. Cp. <em>Dialogues</em> i.14, <em>n.</em> 2.</p><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://kath%C4%81">kathā</a></em> desultory talk, gossip DN.i.8; (= niratthakakathā DN-a.i.90); SN.v.420;</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://k%C4%81ya">kāya</a></em> (adj.) having a variety of bodies or bodily states (combined with or opp. to ekatta˚, nānatta-saññin, &amp; ekatta-saññin), appl. to manussā, devā, vinipātikā (cp. nava sattâvāsā) AN.iv.39 sq. = Cnd.570#2; DN.iii.253, DN.iii.263, DN.iii.282;</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://sa%C3%B1%C3%B1%C4%81">saññā</a></em> consciousness of diversity (Rh. D.: “idea of multiformity, <em>Dial.</em> ii.119; Mrs. Rh. D. “consciousness of the manifold”) MN.i.3; SN.iv.113 sq.; DN.iii.224, DN.iii.262 sq., DN.iii.282; AN.i.41, AN.i.267; AN.ii.184; AN.iii.306; Pts.ii.172; Dhs.265 (cp trsl. p. 72); Vb.342, Vb.369;</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://sa%C3%B1%C3%B1in">saññin</a></em> having a varying consciousness (cp. ˚kāya), DN.i.31 (cp. DN-a.i.119), DN.i.183 DN.iii.263.</li></ul><p>Sk. nānatva; abstr. fr. nānā</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://kathā">kathā</a>, <a href="bword://kāya">kāya</a>, <a href="bword://saññā">saññā</a>, <a href="bword://saññin">saññin</a></p>

nānattakathā|naanattakathaa|nanattakatha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naanattakathaa</span></p><p>various sorts of talk, tale, trivial conversation.</p>

nānattakāya|naanattakaaya|nanattakaya
