nānattasaññin|naanattasa~n~nin|nanattasannin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naanattasa~n~nin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://nānattasaññin">nānattasaññin</a></p><p>having different perceptions or notions.</p>

nānattatā|naanattataa|nanattata
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naanattataa</span></p><p>= nānatta, diversity (of states of mind). Seven sorts at Vb.425: ārammaṇa manasikāra˚ chanda˚ paṇidha˚ adhimokkha˚ abhinīhāra paññā˚.</p><p>second abstr. to nānā</p>

nānattavaṇṇi|naanattava.n.ni|nanattavanni
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naanattava.n.ni</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://nānattavaṇṇin">nānattavaṇṇin</a></p><p>of various colors or appearance.</p>

nānattavaṇṇin|naanattava.n.nin|nanattavannin
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">naanattava.n.nin</span></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://nānattavaṇṇin">nānattavaṇṇin</a></p><p>of various colors or appearance.</p>

