ohiyyaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective noun one who is left behind (in the house as a guard) Vin.iii.208; Vin.iv.94; SN.i.185 (vihārapāla).</p><p>fr. ohīyati, avahiyyati</p>

ohiyyati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>is left behind; falls behind; falls back; hangs back;</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ohīyati">ohīyati</a></p>

ohiyyati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Ohīyati &amp; ohiyyati</p><ol><li>to be left behind, to stay behind Ja.v.340 (avahīyati ohiyyati C.).</li><li>to stay behind, to fall out (in order to urinate or defecate); ger. <em><a href="bword://oh%C4%AByitv%C4%81">ohīyitvā</a></em> Vin.iv.229; Dhp-a.ii.21 (cp. ohanati). See also <em><a href="bword://ohiyyaka">ohiyyaka</a></em>.</li></ol><p>ava + hīyati, Pass. of <em><a href="bword://ha">ha</a></em>, see avajahāti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ohīyitvā">ohīyitvā</a>, <a href="bword://ohiyyaka">ohiyyaka</a>, <a href="bword://ha">ha</a></p>

ohāra|ohaara|ohara
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ohaara</span></p><p>see <em><a href="bword://avah%C4%81ra">avahāra</a></em> &amp; cp.; <em><a href="bword://voh%C4%81ra">vohāra</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://avahāra">avahāra</a>, <a href="bword://vohāra">vohāra</a></p>

ohārapetvā|ohaarapetvaa|oharapetva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ohaarapetvaa</span></p><p>having caused to be removed, having had removed</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://oharati">oharati</a></p>

ohārayitvā|ohaarayitvaa|oharayitva
