ohīyati|ohiiyati|ohiyati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ohiiyati</span></p><p>Ohīyati &amp; ohiyyati</p><ol><li>to be left behind, to stay behind Ja.v.340 (avahīyati ohiyyati C.).</li><li>to stay behind, to fall out (in order to urinate or defecate); ger. <em><a href="bword://oh%C4%AByitv%C4%81">ohīyitvā</a></em> Vin.iv.229; Dhp-a.ii.21 (cp. ohanati). See also <em><a href="bword://ohiyyaka">ohiyyaka</a></em>.</li></ol><p>ava + hīyati, Pass. of <em><a href="bword://ha">ha</a></em>, see avajahāti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ohīyitvā">ohīyitvā</a>, <a href="bword://ohiyyaka">ohiyyaka</a>, <a href="bword://ha">ha</a></p>

ohīyi|ohiiyi|ohiyi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ohiiyi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ohīyaka">ohīyaka</a></p>

