ottāpin|ottaapin|ottapin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ottaapin</span></p><p>Ottappin &amp; Ottāpin</p><p>adjective afraid of wrong, conscientious, scrupulous</p><ol><li>ottappin DN.iii.252, DN.iii.282; Iti.28, Iti.119</li><li>ottāpin MN.i.43 sq.; SN.ii.159 sq., SN.ii.196 SN.ii.207; SN.iv.243 sq.; AN.ii.13 sq.; AN.iii.3 sq., AN.iii.112; AN.iv.1 sq. AN.v.123, AN.v.146. <em>Anottappin</em> bold, reckless, unscrupulous Pp.20 (+ ahirika). <em>anottāpin</em> at SN.ii.159 sq., SN.ii.195, SN.ii.206; SN.iv.240 sq.; Snp.133 (ahirika +).</li></ol><p>fr. ottappa</p>

otāpaka|otaapaka|otapaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaapaka</span></p><p>adjective drying or dried (in the sun), with ref. to food Snp-a.35 (parivāsika-bhattaṃ bhuñjati hatth’otāpakaṃ khādati).</p><p>fr. otāpeti</p>

otāpayamāna|otaapayamaana|otapayamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaapayamaana</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://otāpeti">otāpeti</a></p>

otāpayati|otaapayati|otapayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaapayati</span></p><p>warms; warms in the sun, dries; puts (in the sun) to dry</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://otāpeti">otāpeti</a></p>

otāpenta|otaapenta|otapenta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaapenta</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://otāpeti">otāpeti</a></p>

otāpetabba|otaapetabba|otapetabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaapetabba</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://otāpeti">otāpeti</a></p>

otāpeti|otaapeti|otapeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaapeti</span></p><p>warms; warms in the sun, dries; puts (in the sun) to dry</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://otāpayati">otāpayati</a></p>

otāpeti|otaapeti|otapeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaapeti</span></p><p>to dry in the sun Vin.ii.113; Vin.iv.281; Mil.371 (kummo udakato nikkhamitvā kāyaṃ o. fig applied to mānasa).</p><p>o + tāpeti</p>

otāpetvā|otaapetvaa|otapetva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaapetvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://otāpeti">otāpeti</a></p>

otāra|otaara|otara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaara</span></p><p>entrance, way in; opening, opening for attack; weak point.</p>

otāra|otaara|otara
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaara</span></p><ol><li>descent to, i.e. approach to, access, fig. chance, opportunity <em>otāraṃ</em> labhati. Only in the Māra myth. He, the tempter, ʻgets his chance’ to tempt the Buddha or the disciples, MN.i.334; SN.i.122; SN.iv.178, SN.iv.185; Dhp-a.iii.121. (avatāraṃ labhati Divy.144, Divy.145) <em>ot˚ adhigacchati</em>, to find a chance Snp.446. [Fausböll here translates ʻdefect’. This is fair as exegesis. Every moral or intellectual defect gives the enemy a chance. But otāra does not mean defect]. <em>Ot gavesati</em> to seek an opportunity, Dhp-a.iii.21. <em>Otārāpekkha</em> watching for a chance, SN.i.122. At one passage, AN.iii.67 = AN.iii.259, it is said that constant association leads to agreement, agreement to trust, and trust to otāra. The Com. has nothing. ʻCarelessness’ would suit the context o. gavesati to look for an opportunity Dhp-a.iii.21, and otāraṃ labhati to get a chance SN.i.122; SN.iv.178, SN.iv.185; MN.i.334; Dhp-a.iii.21 (gloss okāra &amp; okāsa); cp. avatāraṃ labhati Divy.144, Divy.145 etc.</li><li>access, fig. inclination to, being at home with, approach, familiarity (cp. otiṇṇa and avacara adj.) AN.iii.67, AN.iii.259.</li><li>(influenced by ocarati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --> and ociṇṇa) being after something, spying, finding out; hence: fault, blame, defect, flaw Snp.446 (= randha vivara Snp-a.393); also in phrase <em>otārāpekkha</em> spying faults SN.i.122 (which may be taken to meaning 1, but meaning 3 is accredited by BSk. avatāraprekṣin Divy.322) Mrs. Rh. D. translates the latter passage by “watching for access”.</li></ol><p>fr. otarati, BSk. avatāra. The Sk. avatāra is centuries later and means ʻincarnation’</p>

otārayati|otaarayati|otarayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaarayati</span></p><p>causes to descend, makes go down (into), fetches down; lets down, lowers, puts down; takes down, removes; makes appear, puts forward; makes alight</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://otāreti">otāreti</a>, <a href="bword://otarati">otarati</a></p>

otārayitabba|otaarayitabba|otarayitabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaarayitabba</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://otārayati">otārayati</a></p>

otāretabba|otaaretabba|otaretabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaaretabba</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://otāreti">otāreti</a></p>

otāreti|otaareti|otareti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaareti</span></p><p>causes to descend, makes go down (into), fetches down; lets down, lowers, puts down; takes down, removes; makes appear, puts forward; makes alight</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://otārayati">otārayati</a>, <a href="bword://otarati">otarati</a></p>

otāreti|otaareti|otareti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaareti</span></p><p>to cause to come down, to bring down, take down Ja.i.426; Ja.iv.402; Ne.21, Ne.22; Dhp-a.ii.81.</p><p>Caus. of otarati</p>

otāriyamāna|otaariyamaana|otariyamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pass. part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaariyamaana</span></p><p>being made to descend, being brought down; being tested as to fitness; being collated</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://otārayati">otārayati</a></p>

otārāpekkha|otaaraapekkha|otarapekkha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">otaaraapekkha</span></p><p>looking for an opening; longing for a weak point</p><p>See also: otārā</p>

ovada
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ovadat">ovadat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovadati">ovadati</a></p>

ovadanta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mf</i></p><p>(~antī)n.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovadati">ovadati</a></p>

ovadat
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i></p><p>Also written as: <a href="bword://ovadat">ovadat</a></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovadati">ovadati</a></p>

ovadati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>instructs; admonishes; counsels</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovadati">ovadati</a></p>

ovadati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to give advice, to admonish exhort, instruct, usually comb<!-- raw HTML omitted -->d.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> with <em><a href="bword://anus%C4%81sati">anusāsati</a></em><br />pres <em><a href="bword://ovadati">ovadati</a></em> Vin.iv.52 sq.; Dhp-a.i.11, Dhp-a.i.13;<br />imper ovadatu MN.iii.267<br />pot <em>ovadeyya</em> Vin.iv.52 (= aṭṭhahi garudhammehi ovadati); Snp.1051 (= anusāseyya)<br />aor <strong>ovadi</strong> Dhp-a.i.397<br />inf <em>ovadituṃ</em> Vin.i.59 (+ anusāsituṃ)<br />grd <em><a href="bword://ovaditabba">ovaditabba</a></em> Vin.ii.5; and <em><a href="bword://ovadiya">ovadiya</a></em> (see sep.)<br />pass <em>avadiyati</em>; ppr. <em>-iyamāna</em> Pp.64 (anusāsiyamāna).</p><p>o + vadati. The Sk. avavadati is some centuries later and is diff. in meaning</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anusāsati">anusāsati</a>, <a href="bword://ovadati">ovadati</a>, ovadi, <a href="bword://ovaditabba">ovaditabba</a>, <a href="bword://ovadiya">ovadiya</a></p>

ovaddheyya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter a</i></p><p>patch, patching.</p>

ovaddheyya
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i></p><p>process to be carried out with the kaṭhina robes. The meaning is obscure Vin.i.254. See the note at <em>Vin. Texts</em> ii.154; Vin.i.254 is not clear (see expl<!-- raw HTML omitted -->n.<!-- raw HTML omitted --> by C. on p. 388). The vv.ll. are ovadeyya˚ ovadheyya ovaṭṭheyya˚.</p>

ovadeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>instructs; admonishes; counsels</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovadati">ovadati</a></p>

ovadita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>instructed; admonished</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovadati">ovadati</a></p>

ovaditabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovadati">ovadati</a></p>

ovaditvā|ovaditvaa|ovaditva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovaditvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovadati">ovadati</a></p>

ovadiya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovadati">ovadati</a></p>

ovadiya
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>adjective who or what can be advised, advisable Vin.i.59 (+ anusāsiya); Vv.84#36 (ovāda-vasena vattabbaṃ Vv-a.345).</p><p>grd. of ovadati</p>

ovadiyamāna|ovadiyamaana|ovadiyamana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">par. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovadiyamaana</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovadati">ovadati</a></p>

ovadiṃsu|ovadi.msu|ovadimsu
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">3 plural</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovadi.msu</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovadati">ovadati</a></p>

ovadī|ovadii|ovadi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovadii</span></p><p>gave advice; admonished.</p>

ovahati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to carry down<br />pass <em><a href="bword://ovuyhati">ovuyhati</a></em> Iti.114 (ind. &amp; pot. ovuyheyya).</p><p>o + vahati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovuyhati">ovuyhati</a></p>

ovaja
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>at SN.i.212 read <em>ojava</em>.</p>

ovamati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to throw up, vomit Ud.78.</p><p>o + <em>vam</em></p>

ovamitvā|ovamitvaa|ovamitva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovamitvaa</span></p><p>spewing out.</p>

ovaraka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine neuter</i></p><p>an inner apartment.</p>

ovaraka
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>an inner room Vin.i.217; MN.i.253; Ja.i.391 (jāto varake T. to be read as jāt’ovarake i.e. the inner chamber where he was born, thus also at Vv-a.158); Vism.90, Vism.431; Vv-a.304 (= gabbha).</p><p>Deriv. uncertain. The Sk. apavaraka is some centuries later. The Sk. apavaraka forbidden or secret room, Halāyudha “lying-in chamber”</p>

ovaraṇa|ovara.na|ovarana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovara.na</span></p><p>covering, protection.</p>

ovarenta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. part.pr. mfn.</i></p><p>obstructing; covering, concealing.</p>

ovariyāna|ovariyaana|ovariyana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovariyaana</span></p><p>covered; checked; hindered, obstructed.</p>

ovariyāna|ovariyaana|ovariyana
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovariyaana</span></p><p>forbidding, obstructing, holding back, preventing Thig.367 (variant reading ovadiyāna, thus also Thag-a.250 explained “maṃ gacchantiṃ avaditvā gamanaṃ nisedhetvā”). Ovassa &amp; ka;</p><p>ger. of o + <em>vṛ</em>.</p>

ovassa
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Ovassa &amp; ˚ka</p><p>see <em><a href="bword://anovassa">anovassa</a></em>(ka).</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anovassa">anovassa</a></p>

ovassaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Ovassa &amp; ˚ka</p><p>see <em><a href="bword://anovassa">anovassa</a></em>(ka).</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://anovassa">anovassa</a></p>

ovassate
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>rains upon.</p>

ovassati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pass. pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>is rained upon; is exposed to rain</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovassate">ovassate</a></p>

ovassati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to rain down on, to make wet. - Pass. <em><a href="bword://ovassati">ovassati</a></em> to become wet through rain Vin.ii.121.</p><p>o + vassati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovassati">ovassati</a></p>

ovassāpenta|ovassaapenta|ovassapenta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">part. pr. mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovassaapenta</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovassāpeti">ovassāpeti</a></p>

ovassāpeti|ovassaapeti|ovassapeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovassaapeti</span></p><p>lets be rained upon; exposes to the rain</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovassāyati">ovassāyati</a>, <a href="bword://ovassate">ovassate</a></p>

ovassāyati|ovassaayati|ovassayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovassaayati</span></p><p>lets be rained upon; exposes to the rain</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovassāpeti">ovassāpeti</a>, <a href="bword://ovassate">ovassate</a></p>

ovaṭa|ova.ta|ovata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ova.ta</span></p><p>checked; prevented.</p>

ovaṭa|ova.ta|ovata
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ova.ta</span></p><p>obstructed, prevented Vin.ii.255 = Vin.iv.52; AN.iv.277 (variant reading ovāda); also <em>an˚</em>; ibid.</p><p>o + vaṭa, pp. of <em>vṛ</em>; another form of ovuta = ophuta, q.v.</p>

ovaṭṭa|ova.t.ta|ovatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ova.t.ta</span></p><p>rained upon; exposed to the rain</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovaṭṭha">ovaṭṭha</a>, <a href="bword://ovuṭṭha">ovuṭṭha</a></p>

ovaṭṭha|ova.t.tha|ovattha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ova.t.tha</span></p><p>rained upon; exposed to the rain</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovaṭṭa">ovaṭṭa</a>, <a href="bword://ovuṭṭha">ovuṭṭha</a></p>

ovaṭṭika|ova.t.tika|ovattika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ova.t.tika</span></p><p>what is rolled up or round; a fold, a tuck; a hem; a seam; a girdle, a waist cloth, a fold of material at the waist (in which objects were carried); perhaps also a bracelet</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovaṭṭikā">ovaṭṭikā</a>, <a href="bword://ovaṭṭiya">ovaṭṭiya</a></p>

ovaṭṭika|ova.t.tika|ovattika
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ova.t.tika</span></p><ol><li>girdle, waistband MN.ii.47; Ja.iii.285 (variant reading ovaddhi˚); Vism.312; Dhp-a.ii.37 Dhp-a.iv.206; DN-a.i.218 (Morris, J.P.T.S. 1887, 156: a kind of bag).</li><li>a bracelet Vin.ii.106 (= vaḷayaṃ C.).</li><li>a patch, patching (˚karaṇa), darning (?) Vin.i.254 (vv ll. ovaṭṭiya˚, ovadhita˚ ovadhīya˚); Ja.ii.197 (variant reading ovaddhi˚) See also <em><a href="bword://ovaddheyya">ovaddheyya</a></em> (ava˚).</li></ol><p>fr. ava + <em>vṛt</em></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovaddheyya">ovaddheyya</a></p>

ovaṭṭikā|ova.t.tikaa|ovattika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ova.t.tikaa</span></p><p>what is rolled up or round; a fold, a tuck; a hem; a seam; a girdle, a waist cloth, a fold of material at the waist (in which objects were carried); perhaps also a bracelet</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovaṭṭika">ovaṭṭika</a>, <a href="bword://ovaṭṭiya">ovaṭṭiya</a></p>

ovaṭṭiya|ova.t.tiya|ovattiya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ova.t.tiya</span></p><p>what is rolled up or round; a fold, a tuck; a hem; a seam; a girdle, a waist cloth, a fold of material at the waist (in which objects were carried); perhaps also a bracelet</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovaṭṭika">ovaṭṭika</a>, <a href="bword://ovaṭṭikā">ovaṭṭikā</a></p>

ovijjhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to pierce through Vism.304.</p><p>ava + <em>vyadh</em></p>

ovuta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i></p><p>covered; encompassed; checked, obstructed</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovuta">ovuta</a></p>

ovuta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>see <em>ophuta</em>.</p>

ovuyhati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>is carried down.</p>

ovuyhati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to be carried down (a river) Iti.114.</p><p>Pass. of ovahati</p>

ovuṭa|ovu.ta|ovuta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovu.ta</span></p><p>covered; encompassed; checked, obstructed</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovuta">ovuta</a></p>

ovuṭṭha|ovu.t.tha|ovuttha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovu.t.tha</span></p><p>rained upon; exposed to the rain</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovaṭṭa">ovaṭṭa</a>, <a href="bword://ovaṭṭha">ovaṭṭha</a></p>

ovāda|ovaada|ovada
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovaada</span></p><p>admonishing; instructions; counsel.</p>

ovāda|ovaada|ovada
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovaada</span></p><p>advice, instruction, admonition, exhortation Vin.i.50 = Vin.ii.228; Vin.ii.255 Vin.iv.52; DN.i.137 (˚paṭikara, function of a king); Ja.iii.256 (anovādakara one who cannot be helped by advice, cp ovadaka); Ne.91, Ne.92; Dhp-a.i.13, Dhp-a.i.398 (dasavidha o.) Vv-a.345<br />■ ovādaṃ <em><a href="bword://deti">deti</a></em> to give advice Pv-a.11, Pv-a.12, Pv-a.15,</p><p>BSk. avavāda in same sense as P.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://deti">deti</a></p>

ovādaka|ovaadaka|ovadaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovaadaka</span></p><p>(one) who admonishes; instructs, counsels</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovādikā">ovādikā</a></p>

ovādaka|ovaadaka|ovadaka
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovaadaka</span></p><p>adjective noun admonishing (act.) or being admonished (pass.); giving or taking advice; a spiritual instructor or adviser. MN.i.145 AN.i.25 SN.v.67 Iti.107<br />■ <em>anovādaka</em> one who cannot or does not want to be advised, incorrigible Ja.i.159; Ja.iii.256, Ja.iii.304; Ja.v.314.</p><p>fr. ovāda; cp. BSk. avavādaka in same meaning, e.g. Divy.48, Divy.254, Divy.385</p>

ovādakara|ovaadakara|ovadakara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovaadakara</span></p><p>following advice; obeying instructions</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovāda">ovāda</a></p>

ovādaṭhapita|ovaada.thapita|ovadathapita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovaada.thapita</span></p><p>from whom instruction has been withdrawn</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovāda">ovāda</a></p>

ovādikā|ovaadikaa|ovadika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovaadikaa</span></p><p>(one) who admonishes; instructs, counsels</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ovādaka">ovādaka</a></p>

ovādin|ovaadin|ovadin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">ovaadin</span></p><p>adjective noun = ovādaka MN.i.360 (anovādin).</p><p>fr. ovāda</p>

ovādita|ovaadita|ovadita
