oḍḍeti|o.d.deti|oddeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">o.d.deti</span></p><p>ties, strings up; lays out, fixes (a snare or noose or net); lays out, presents (as a trap, or to mislead)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://oḍḍayati">oḍḍayati</a>, <a href="bword://uḍḍeti">uḍḍeti</a></p>

oḍḍeti|o.d.deti|oddeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">o.d.deti</span></p><p>to throw out (a net), to lay snares AN.i.33 = Ja.ii.37, Ja.ii.153; Ja.iii.184 and passim; Thag-a.243<br />pp oḍḍita (q.v.).</p><p>for uḍḍeti (?). See further under uḍḍeti</p>

oḍḍetvā|o.d.detvaa|oddetva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">o.d.detvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://oḍḍeti">oḍḍeti</a></p>

oḍḍha|o.d.dha|oddha
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">o.d.dha</span></p><p>carried away, appropriated, only in cpd. <em>sah-oḍhā</em> corā thieves with their plunder Vism.180 (cp. Sk. sahoḍha Manu ix.270).</p><p>better spelling <em>oḍha</em>, pp. of ā + <em>vah</em></p>

oḍḍi|o.d.di|oddi
