sapati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to swear, curse SN.i.225; Ja.v.104, Ja.v.397; Mhvs.25, Mhvs.113; Vv-a.336<br />pp <em>satta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->3<!-- raw HTML omitted --></em>.</p><p><em>śap</em>, cp. Dhtp.184 “akkose”</p>

sapatikā|sapatikaa|sapatika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">sapatikaa</span></p><p>adjective having a husband, a woman whose husband is alive Ja.vi.158; Pv-a.86.</p>

sapatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>hostile, rival Thig.347; Thag-a.242; sapattarājā a rival king Ja.i.358; Ja.ii.94; Ja.iii.416; asapatta without enmity Snp.150; sapatta (m.) a rival, foe, Iti.83; AN.iv.94 sq.; Ja.i.297.</p><p>Sk. sapatna</p>

sapattabhāra|sapattabhaara|sapattabhara
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">sapattabhaara</span></p><p>with the weight of the wings, carrying one’s wings with oneself DN.i.71; MN.i.180 MN.i.268; AN.ii.210; Pp.58.</p><p>sa<!-- raw HTML omitted -->3<!-- raw HTML omitted --> + patta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --> + bhāra</p>

