sappadāsa|sappadaasa|sappadasa
<p>[DPPN]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">sappadaasa</span></p><p>Overmastered by corrupt habits of mind and character, for twenty five years he was unable to develop concentration. This so distressed him that he was about to commit suicide, when, inward vision suddenly expanding, he attained arahantship. Thag.405–410</p>

sappana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>gliding on Dhs-a.133.</p><p>fr. sappati</p>

sappasoṇḍikapabbhāra|sappaso.n.dikapabbhaara|sappasondikapabbhara
<p>[DPPN]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">sappaso.n.dikapabbhaara</span></p><p>SappasoṇḍikapabbhāraSappasoṇḍika</p><p>A mountain cave in the Sītavana, near Rājagaha. DN.ii.116 A conversation which took place there between Sāriputta and Upasena, just before the latter’s death, is recorded in the Saṃyutta Nikāya. Upasena died of snake bite. SN.iv.40 The cave was used as a residence by monks who come to Rājagaha from afar. Vin.ii.76</p><p>in the Sītavana, near Rājagaha3cave</p>

