satti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Satti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>feminine ability, power Dhtp.508 Usually in phrase <em>yathā satti</em> as much as one can do according to one’s ability Cp.i.10#6; Dhp-a.i.399; or <em>yathā sattiṃ</em> DN.i.102, or <em>y. sattiyā</em> Dhp-a.i.92.</p><p>fr. <em>śak</em>, cp. Vedic śakti</p><p>Satti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>feminine</p><ol><li>knife, dagger, sword AN.iv.130; Ja.ii.153; Vism.313 (dīgha-daṇḍa˚ with a long handle); Dhp-a.i.189; Dhp-a.ii.134 (tikhiṇa˚ a sharp knife). <em>mukha˚</em>; piercing words Ja.i.341.</li><li>a spear, javelin SN.i.13; AN.ii.117; Ja.i.150.</li></ol><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://pa%C3%B1jara">pañjara</a></em> lattice work of spears DN.ii.164.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://la%E1%B9%85ghana">laṅghana</a></em> javelin dance Ja.i.430.</li><li><em>-simbali-vana</em> the forest of swords (in purgatory) Ja.v.453.</li><li><em>-<a href="bword://s%C5%ABla">sūla</a></em> a sword stake often in simile <em>˚ûpamā kāmā</em> SN.i.128; AN.iii.97; Vism.341 Also Name of a purgatory Ja.v.143 sq.</li></ul><p>cp. Vedic śakti, orig. identical with satti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://pañjara">pañjara</a>, <a href="bword://laṅghana">laṅghana</a>, <a href="bword://sūla">sūla</a></p>

