thūṇa|thuu.na|thuna
<p>[DPPN]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">thuu.na</span></p><p>A brahmin village on the western boundary of Majjhimadesa. Vin.i.197 It was in the Kosala country and belonged to the Mallas, and was once visited by the Buddha. Ud.vii.9</p><p>on the western boundary of Majjhimadesa, in the Kosala country, of the Mallas2town</p>

thūṇa|thuu.na|thuna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">thuu.na</span></p><p>post, a stake, a pillar; the trunk of a tree.</p>

thūṇeyyakā|thuu.neyyakaa|thuneyyaka
<p>[DPPN]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">thuu.neyyakaa</span></p><p>The people of Thūṇa.</p>

thūṇikā|thuu.nikaa|thunika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">thuu.nikaa</span></p><p>roof plate.</p>

