udakavāhanarajju|udakavaahanarajju|udakavahanarajju
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">udakavaahanarajju</span></p><p>rope used when drawing water</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://udaka">udaka</a></p>

udakecara
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mf(n.)</i></p><p>who moves or lives in water; an aquatic creature.</p>

udakorohaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>(one) who goes down into the water (for ritual bath)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://udaka">udaka</a></p>

udakorohana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i></p><p>going down into the water; a ritual bath</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://udakorohaṇa">udakorohaṇa</a>, <a href="bword://udaka">udaka</a></p>

udakorohaṇa|udakoroha.na|udakorohana
