udakorohaṇanuyoga|udakoroha.nanuyoga|udakorohananuyoga
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">m</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">udakoroha.nanuyoga</span></p><p>the practice of ritual bathing</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://udakorohaṇa">udakorohaṇa</a></p>

udakukkhepa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i></p><p>(the are defined by) a throw of water (or sand, to determine a sīma)</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://udaka">udaka</a></p>

udakumbha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine a</i></p><p>water jar.</p>

udakumbha
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i></p><p>water jug Ja.i.20; Dhp.121, Dhp.122; Pv.i.12#9.</p><p>uda + kumbha</p>

udakumbhaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine a</i></p><p>water jar.</p>

udakupasaṭṭhā|udakupasa.t.thaa|udakupasattha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(m)f(n).</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">udakupasa.t.thaa</span></p><p>let go, handed over (in marriage) with (the pouring of) water</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://udakupassaṭṭhā">udakupassaṭṭhā</a>, <a href="bword://udaka">udaka</a></p>

udakupassaṭṭhā|udakupassa.t.thaa|udakupassattha
