udakādhāna|udakaadhaana|udakadhana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">udakaadhaana</span></p><p>container for water</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://udaka">udaka</a></p>

udapajjatha
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uppajjati">uppajjati</a></p>

udapatta
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine (n.) a</i></p><p>bowl of water.</p>

udapatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>Udapatta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>risen, flying up sprung up Ja.iii.484 (= uppatita C.); Ja.v.71 (= uṭṭhita C.).</p><p>ụda for ud, and <em><a href="bword://patta">patta</a></em>, pp. of pat, for patita? Kern,</p><blockquote><p>Toevoegselen</p></blockquote><p>s. v. takes it as udak-prāpta</p><p>Udapatta<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>a bowl of water, a water-jug, ewer MN.i.100; SN.v.121; AN.iii.230 sq., AN.iii.236, AN.v.92, AN.v.94, AN.v.97 sq.</p><p>uda + patta; Sk. udapātra</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://patta">patta</a></p>

udappatta
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>see <em><a href="bword://udapatta">udapatta</a></em>.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://udapatta">udapatta</a></p>

udapādi|udapaadi|udapadi
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">aor. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">udapaadi</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uppajjati">uppajjati</a></p>

udapādi|udapaadi|udapadi
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">udapaadi</span></p><p>3<!-- raw HTML omitted -->rd<!-- raw HTML omitted --> sg. aor. of <em><a href="bword://uppajjati">uppajjati</a></em> to arise, originate, become DN.i.110, DN.i.180, DN.i.185; SN.ii.273; Iti.52, Iti.99; Snp-a.346, Snp-a.462.</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uppajjati">uppajjati</a></p>

udapāna|udapaana|udapana
