upaneti
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><p>to bring up to, conduce, adduce; to present, give Ja.i.200; Mil.396; DN-a.i.276; Pv-a.39, Pv-a.43 Pv-a.49, Pv-a.53, Pv-a.74<br />pass <em><a href="bword://upan%C4%AByati">upanīyati</a></em> (˚niyyati)</p><ol><li>to be brought (up to) Ja.iv.398; ppr. ˚nīyamāna Ja.i.200; Pv-a.5.</li><li>to be brought to conclusion, or to an end (of life) MN.ii.68; SN.i.2.</li><li>to be carried along or away AN.i.155</li></ol><p>pp <em><a href="bword://upan%C4%ABta">upanīta</a></em> (q.v.)<br />ger upanīya (q.v.).</p><p>upa + neti</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://upanīyati">upanīyati</a>, <a href="bword://upanīta">upanīta</a></p>

