uttarasve
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">ind.</i></p><p>the day after tomorrow</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uttarasuve">uttarasuve</a>, <a href="bword://uttara">uttara</a></p>

uttarasīsaka|uttarasiisaka|uttarasisaka
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">uttarasiisaka</span></p><p>with its head to the north</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uttara">uttara</a></p>

uttarati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i></p><p>climbs out, emerges (esp. from water); escapes (from); comes out; boils up, overflows; crosses, passes over (to).</p>

uttarati
<p>[PTS]</p><p></p><ol><li>to come out of (water) Vin.ii.221 (opp. otarati); Ja.i.108 (id.).</li><li>to go over, to flow over (of water), to boil over Mil.117, Mil.118, Mil.132 Mil.260, Mil.277.</li><li>to cross over, to go beyond MN.i.135 aor. <em><a href="bword://udat%C4%81ri">udatāri</a></em> Snp.471 (oghaṃ).</li><li>to go over, to overspread Ja.v.204 (ger. uttariyāna = avattharitvā C.)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://oti%E1%B9%87%E1%B9%87a">otiṇṇa</a></em> (q.v.)</li></ol><p>caus <em>uttareti</em> (q.v.). Uttari (-) &amp; Uttarim</p><p>ud + tarati<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://udatāri">udatāri</a>, <a href="bword://otiṇṇa">otiṇṇa</a></p>

uttarato
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">(?)</i></p><p>in a north direction; to the north (of).</p>

uttaraṇa|uttara.na|uttarana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">uttara.na</span></p><p>coming out of; crossing over.</p>

uttaraṇa|uttara.na|uttarana
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">uttara.na</span></p><p>bringing or moving out, saving, delivery Thag.418; Ja.i.195. In BSk. uttaraṇa only in sense of crossing, overcoming, e.g. Jtm.31 <!-- raw HTML omitted -->8<!-- raw HTML omitted --> (˚setu). Cp. <em><a href="bword://uttara">uttara</a></em>.</p><p>fr. uttarati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uttara">uttara</a></p>

uttaraṇī|uttara.nii|uttarani
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">uttara.nii</span></p><p>the upper of the two pieces of wood used for kindling fire</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://uttara">uttara</a></p>

uttarena
