<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aahaarayati</span></p><p>eats</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://āhāreti">āhāreti</a>, <a href="bword://āharati">āharati</a></p>

āhāraṭṭhika|aahaara.t.thika|aharatthika
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aahaara.t.thika</span></p><p>dependent upon food or sustenance</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://āhāra">āhāra</a></p>

āhāre patikkūla-saññā|aahaare patikkuula-sa~n~naa|ahare patikkula-sanna
<p>[Nyana]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aahaare patikkuula-sa~n~naa</span></p><p><strong>[[āhāre patikkūla-saññā]]Āhāre-patikkūla-saññā:</strong> ‘reflection on the disgusting aspects of food’, fully described in Vis.M XI, l.</p>

