ājīvikapakata|aajiivikapakata|ajivikapakata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aajiivikapakata</span></p><p>induced by (the necessity of) obtaining a living</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ājīvikāpakata">ājīvikāpakata</a></p>

ājīvikābhaya|aajiivikaabhaya|ajivikabhaya
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aajiivikaabhaya</span></p><p>danger to one’s livelihood; fear concerning livelihood</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ājīvikabhaya">ājīvikabhaya</a></p>

ājīvikāpakata|aajiivikaapakata|ajivikapakata
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aajiivikaapakata</span></p><p>induced by (the necessity of) obtaining a living</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ājīvikapakata">ājīvikapakata</a></p>

ājīvin|aajiivin|ajivin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aajiivin</span></p><p>adjective noun having one’s livelihood, finding one’s subsistence, living, leading a life of (-˚) DN.iii.64; AN.v.190 (lūkha˚)</p><p>fr. ājīva</p>

ākampita|aakampita|akampita
