ākappa|aakappa|akappa
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">masculine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aakappa</span></p><p>dress, appearance, guise; outward sign; deportment; (good) behavior.</p>

ākappa|aakappa|akappa
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aakappa</span></p><ol><li>attire, appearance, Vin.i.44 (an˚) = Vin.ii.213; Ja.i.505.</li><li>deportment Dhs.713 (ā˚ gamanādi-ākāro Dhs-a.321).</li></ol><ul><li><em>-<a href="bword://sampanna">sampanna</a></em>, suitably attired, well dressed, AN.iii.78; Ja.iv.542; <em>an˚ sampanna</em>, ill dressed, Ja.i.420.</li></ul><p>cp. Sk. ākalpa ā + kappa</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://sampanna">sampanna</a></p>

ākappasampanna|aakappasampanna|akappasampanna
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aakappasampanna</span></p><p>of good deportment or appearance; decorous</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ākappa">ākappa</a></p>

ākara|aakara|akara
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">a</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aakara</span></p><p>mine, usually in cpd. <em>ratan-ākara</em> a mine of jewels Thag.1049; Ja.ii.414; Ja.vi.459; Dpvs.i.18<br />■ Cp. also Mil.356; Vv-a.13.</p><p>cp. Sk. ākara</p>

ākassati|aakassati|akassati
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aakassati</span></p><p>to draw along, draw after, plough, cultivate Mnd.428.</p><p>ā + kassati</p>

ākaḍḍhana|aaka.d.dhana|akaddhana
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter \~ā, feminine</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aaka.d.dhana</span></p><p>(from ākaḍḍhati) dragging to, drawing towards; pulling, pulling about; drawing out; bending (a bow).</p>

ākaḍḍhana|aaka.d.dhana|akaddhana
