ālassa|aalassa|alassa
<p>[PTS]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">neuter</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aalassa</span></p><p>sloth, idleness, laziness SN.i.43; DN.iii.182; AN.iv.59; AN.v.136; Sdhp.567. Spelling also <em><a href="bword://%C4%81lasya">ālasya</a></em> SN.i.43 (variant reading BB); Vb.352; Mil.289, and <em><a href="bword://%C4%81lasiya">ālasiya</a></em> Ja.i.427; DN-a.i.310; Dhp-a.i.299; Vv-a.43. Alana &amp; Alana;</p><p>Der. fr. alasa</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ālasya">ālasya</a>, <a href="bword://ālasiya">ālasiya</a></p>

ālasya|aalasya|alasya
