ālimpeti|aalimpeti|alimpeti
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aalimpeti</span></p><p>Ālimpeti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->1<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>to smear, anoint Vin.ii.107; SN.iv.177 (vaṇaṃ)<br />caus 2 <em>ālimpāpeti</em> Vin.iv.316<br />pass <em>ālimpīyati</em> Mil.74 &amp; <em>ālippati</em> Dhp-a.iv.166 (variant reading for lippati)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://%C4%81litta">ālitta</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>Sk. ālimpayati or ālepayati. ā + <em>lip</em> or <em>limp</em></p><p>Ālimpeti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p><p>to kindle, ignite set fire to Vin.ii.138 (dāyo ālimpetabbo); Vin.iii.85; DN.ii.163 (citakaṃ); AN.i.257; Dhp-a.i.177 (āvāsaṃ read āvāpaṃ), Dhp-a.i.225; Pv-a.62 (kaṭṭhāni)<br />pp <em><a href="bword://%C4%81limpita">ālimpita</a></em> (q.v.).</p><p>for Sk. ādīpayati, with change of d to l over ḷ and substitution of limp for ḷīp after analogy of roots in ˚mp, like lup → lump, lip → limp</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ālitta">ālitta</a>, <a href="bword://ālimpita">ālimpita</a></p>

ālimpetvā|aalimpetvaa|alimpetva
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">absol.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aalimpetvaa</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ālimpeti">ālimpeti</a></p>

ālimpita|aalimpita|alimpita
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pp mfn.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aalimpita</span></p><p>kindled; set on fire</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ālimpeti">ālimpeti</a></p>

ālimpita|aalimpita|alimpita
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">aalimpita</span></p><p>ignited, lit. AN.iv.102 (variant reading ālepita).</p><p>pp. of ālimpeti<!-- raw HTML omitted -->2<!-- raw HTML omitted --></p>

