ṭhāpeti|.thaapeti|thapeti
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">caus. pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">.thaapeti</span></p><p>of tiṭṭhati</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://tiṭṭhati">tiṭṭhati</a></p>

ṭhātabba|.thaatabba|thatabba
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">fpp mfn. &amp; impers.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">.thaatabba</span></p><p>of ṭhita</p><p>See also: <a href="bword://ṭhita">ṭhita</a></p>

ṭhāti|.thaati|thati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">.thaati</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://tiṭṭhati">tiṭṭhati</a></p>

ṭhāyati|.thaayati|thayati
<p>[NCPED]</p><p><i style="color: #448C19;">pr. 3 sg.</i> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">.thaayati</span></p><p>See also: <a href="bword://tiṭṭhati">tiṭṭhati</a></p>

ṭhāyika|.thaayika|thayika
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">.thaayika</span></p><p>adjective at Mil.201 “one who gains his living or subsists on” (instr.) is doubtful reading.</p>

ṭhāyin|.thaayin|thayin
<p>[PTS]</p><p> | <span style="color: #0B4A72;">.thaayin</span></p><p>adjective noun standing, being in, being in a state of (-˚), staying with, dependent on (with gen.) pariyuṭṭhaṭṭhāyin “being in a state of one to whom it has arisen,” i.e. one who has got the idea of… or one who imagines SN.iii.3 sq.; arūpa-ṭṭhāyin Iti.62 Yamassa ṭhāyino being under the rule of Yama Pv.i.11#9.</p><p>from tiṭṭhati</p>

